2026-10-13 03:58:04,649 - voice_bot.livekit - INFO - Search packages by name response: [{'id': 'PKG015059', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015059', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Scenic Scandinavia (Winter)', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'On Board Silja Or Viking', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Geilo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Fjord Line Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the Ice bar Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery'], 'pdfName': 'PKG004841_0_20211130183554.pdf', 'price': 411783, 'packageSummary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia (Winter)\' package is an 11-day tour covering Bergen, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Geilo, Oslo, and Stockholm, as well as scenic journeys on the Fjord Line Cruise and On Board Silja or Viking. The itinerary offers a range of memorable experiences, including the breathtaking "Norway in a Nutshell" tour, a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, and a unique drink at the Ice bar. Additionally, participants will enjoy a beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery, making this winter journey a perfect blend of scenic sightseeing and local culinary delights.', 'images': ['Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'Talllin.jpg', 'Helsnki-fery-iti.jpg', 'Stockholm.jpg', 'Karstad_753_Adobe.jpg', 'VigelandParkMuseumOsloNorway.jpg', 'Gudvangen_Norway_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Bergen_Funicular_Train_753_Adobe.jpg', 'AArhus.jpg', 'Little_Mermaid_Copenhagen_753_Adobe.jpg', 'Copenhagen_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 411783, 'thumbnailImage': 'Ganla_Stan_Stockholm_267_Adobe.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015059 is named 'Scenic Scandinavia (Winter)' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Helsinki, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Helsinki! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Tallinn – Guided city tour of Tallinn Today, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we see the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - On Board Silja Or Viking, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm. Today, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar Today, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern Today, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Geilo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park – Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Travel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’ Today, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen. NOTE: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Fjord Line Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum Onto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable stayed bridge across the Oresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Flights Important notes : Flights are subject to change, once the group materializes on a first come first basis, alternative flight options will be offered. Round trip Flights included for EX-India passengers Airfare not included for joining direct passengers, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 411783.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n, \n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunch.\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches. , \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline And Airfare The Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July,2026 Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers. Passengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves. For Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents. Passengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To/ From The Hub City At Their Own Expense. Joining Direct Clients Main Sector Air Tickets To Reach The First Overnight City And Last Departure City Is Not Included In The Joining Direct Package Price. Arrival And Departure Transfers Are Not Included In The Package Price. The Tour Manager Shall Meet The Clients Directly At The Hotel. Hotels All Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts. The Hotel Room Size In Europe Would Be Up To 16 – 18 Sq. Mts. Most Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size. As A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And The Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room. For Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room. A Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult. Hotel Rooms May Not Be Air-Conditioned / Air Cooled, Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions. Functioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority. During Heat Waves In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures. Most Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms. Due To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As The Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City. Any Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers. We Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary. In Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast. Coaches Most Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean. Due To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives. Eating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach. One Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach. In Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. The Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop. Coaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach. Due To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities, As Per Eu Norms, To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And On Foot. Meals Meals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible. On Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided. Sightseeing On Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same. Generally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible. General On Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members. A Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour. Arrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary, To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer About The Group Flight Timings. Security Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary. Please Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage. Disabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client. Tcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour. Normal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges. The Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services. The Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same. There Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour. All Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted). Optional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non-Cancellation Policy. Gst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India. In Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed. The Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only. Tours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At The Prevailing Rate Of Exchange. Please Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the Ice bar Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE215', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia (Winter)\' package is an 11-day tour covering Bergen, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Geilo, Oslo, and Stockholm, as well as scenic journeys on the Fjord Line Cruise and On Board Silja or Viking. The itinerary offers a range of memorable experiences, including the breathtaking "Norway in a Nutshell" tour, a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, and a unique drink at the Ice bar. Additionally, participants will enjoy a beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery, making this winter journey a perfect blend of scenic sightseeing and local culinary delights.', 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Helsinki!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Hotel Clarion Helsinki\xa0/ Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nDay trip to Tallinn – Guided city tour of Tallinn\nToday, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we see the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Hotel Clarion Helsinki\xa0/\xa0Radisson Seaside\xa0or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm.\nToday, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'On board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar\nToday, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern\nToday, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park – Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum\xa0\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nTravel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’\nToday, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen.\nNOTE: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Quality Edward Grieg / ComfortBergen Air port / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum\nOnto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable stayed bridge across the Oresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky /\xa0Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen\xa0or similar in Copenhagen,\xa0Denmark'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\xa0\nFlights Important notes :\n\nFlights are subject to change, once the group materializes on a first come first basis, alternative flight options will be offered.\nRound trip Flights included for EX-India passengers\nAirfare not included for joining direct passengers\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n', '2': '\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DK', 'countryName': 'Denmark', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EE', 'countryName': 'Estonia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EURP', 'countryName': 'Europe', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 411800.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunch.\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches. ', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', 'Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Finland\nRovaniemi \n\nVisit Arktikum\nMidnight Sun Tour\nVisit Reindeer Farm\nVisit Husky Farm\nVisit Santa Village\nArctic Crossing Certificate\n\nHelsinki \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center With Chocolate Tasting\n\nEstonia \nTallinn\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm Concert Hall\nVisit The Vasa Ship Museum\n\nNorway\nOslo \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nVisit The Fram Museum\nPhotostop At Holmenkollen Ski Jump\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour: A Unique To Bergen\n\nBergen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride – Floybanen\n\nDenmark\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy Canal Cruise\nRide On The Oresund Bridge\n', 'Finland\nHelsinki\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center\n\nEstonia \nTallinn \n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm City Hall\nVisit The Viking Museum\nVisit The Icebar\n\nKarlstad\n\nPhoto Stop At Lake Vanern\xa0\n\nNorway\nOslo\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nEntrance To Holmenkollen Ski Museum\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour\n\nBergen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride - Mt Floyen\n\nDenmark\nAarhus\n\nOrientation City Tour\nPhoto Stop At Infinite Bridge\n\nOdense\n\nVisit H C Andersen Museum\n\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Carlsberg Brewery\nPhoto Stop At Oresund Bridge\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\xa0\nAirline And Airfare\n\nThe Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July,2026\nAny Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers.\nPassengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves.\xa0\nFor Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents.\xa0\nPassengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To/ From The Hub City At Their Own Expense.\n\nJoining Direct Clients\n\nMain Sector Air Tickets To Reach The First Overnight City And Last Departure City Is Not Included In The Joining Direct Package Price.\nArrival And Departure Transfers Are Not Included In The Package Price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager Shall Meet The Clients Directly At The Hotel.\n\nHotels\xa0\n\nAll Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts.\xa0\nThe Hotel Room Size In Europe Would Be Up To 16 – 18 Sq. Mts.\nMost Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size.\xa0\nAs A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And The Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room.\xa0\nFor Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room.\xa0\nA Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel Rooms May Not Be Air-Conditioned / Air Cooled, Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority.\xa0\nDuring Heat Waves In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms.\xa0\nDue To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As The Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City.\xa0\nAny Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers.\xa0\nWe Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary.\xa0\nIn Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches\xa0\n\nMost Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean.\xa0\nDue To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives.\xa0\nEating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach.\xa0\nOne Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach.\xa0\nIn Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. The Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop.\nCoaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach.\xa0\nDue To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities, As Per Eu Norms, To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And On Foot.\n\nMeals\xa0\n\nMeals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible.\xa0\nOn Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nGenerally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible.\n\nGeneral\xa0\n\nOn Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members.\xa0\nA Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour.\xa0\nArrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary, To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer About The Group Flight Timings.\nSecurity Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary.\xa0\nPlease Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage.\xa0\nDisabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client.\xa0\nTcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour.\xa0\nNormal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges.\xa0\nThe Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nThere Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour.\xa0\nAll Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted).\nOptional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non-Cancellation Policy.\nGst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed.\xa0\nThe Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only.\xa0\nTours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At The Prevailing Rate Of Exchange.\xa0\nPlease Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/Ganla_Stan_Stockholm_267_Adobe.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Talllin.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Helsnki-fery-iti.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Stockholm.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Karstad_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/VigelandParkMuseumOsloNorway.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Gudvangen_Norway_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Bergen_Funicular_Train_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/AArhus.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Little_Mermaid_Copenhagen_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015059/itinerary/Copenhagen_753.jpg']}, 'score': 7.285092, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015169', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015169', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026'], 'packageName': 'Scenic Scandinavia With Rovaniemi (Winter)', 'days': 13, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'On Board Silja Or Viking', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Geilo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Fjord Line Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Get the Arctic crossing certificate Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the ice bar. Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery'], 'pdfName': 'PKG004841_0_20211130183554.pdf', 'price': 502075, 'packageSummary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia With Rovaniemi (Winter)\' package is a 13-day tour covering Stockholm, Geilo, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Rovaniemi, Bergen, and Oslo, alongside scenic cruises on the Fjord Line and Silja or Viking lines. Throughout this winter journey, participants will enjoy key highlights such as receiving an official Arctic crossing certificate, indulging in a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, and sipping a drink at an authentic ice bar. Additionally, travelers will experience the breathtaking "Norway in a Nutshell" tour and enjoy a beer tasting at the historic Carlsberg Brewery.', 'images': ['Romaniemi_7532.jpg', 'Rovaniemi7531.jpg', 'Kuopio_Finland_753_Adobe.jpg', 'Helsinki7534.jpg', 'Tallinn753.jpg', 'Silja753.jpg', 'VasaMuseum.jpg', 'Karlstad753.jpg', 'VigelandSculpturePark753.jpg', 'Norway753.jpg', 'FunicularRailwayBergenNorwayshutterstock_57936379.jpg', 'Copenhagen.jpg', 'Copenhagen_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 502075, 'thumbnailImage': 'Rovaniemi_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015169 is named 'Scenic Scandinavia With Rovaniemi (Winter)' and spans 13 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Rovaniemi! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Reindeer farm – Visit husky Farm – Visit Santa village - Northern Lights Tour Today, we visit the reindeer and husky farms. Meet the authentic reindeer herder and take photos of the reindeer. Next, we visit the Santa Claus Village and the numerous souvenir shops, Santa's Post Office and surely, we get to meet the man himself in his office. Santa Claus Village in Lapland is a popular place to cross the Arctic Circle: here you will get a certificate confirming the feat. Tonight, we either experience Midnight Sun tour (Jun-Aug) OR we experience the Northern Lights (Sep-Oct) phenomenon depending upon the departure date. Ride around the surroundings of Lapland to observe the Midnight sun OR the auroras. Our driving guide will take you to several different spots to give you the best chance to see the Midnight sun OR to chase the northern lights. (Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Midnight sun/Northern Lights, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Midnight sun/Northern Lights tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the midnight sun or the lights)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly to Helsinki Today, we check out and we take a flight to Helsinki. Upon arrival, we check in to the hotel. Note: Today the group will be joining the Scenic Scandinavia guests., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Tallinn – Guided City Tour of Tallinn Today, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we visit the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - On Board Silja Or Viking, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm. Today, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar Today, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern Today, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Geilo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park – Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Travel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’ Today, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen. NOTE: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Fjord Line Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum Onto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable-stayed bridge across the Øresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. International connection may be from Delhi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 502075.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights at Santa hotel / Scandic Rovaniemi City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen,\xa0\n, \n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunch.\n09 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinner.\n\n\xa0\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches., Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 13 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 39 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 15th November 2023. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided Sightseeing: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. (Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Northern lights OR Midnight sun, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Northern Lights OR Midnight Sun tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the lights). General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Get the Arctic crossing certificate Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the ice bar. Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE221', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia With Rovaniemi (Winter)\' package is a 13-day tour covering Stockholm, Geilo, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Rovaniemi, Bergen, and Oslo, alongside scenic cruises on the Fjord Line and Silja or Viking lines. Throughout this winter journey, participants will enjoy key highlights such as receiving an official Arctic crossing certificate, indulging in a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, and sipping a drink at an authentic ice bar. Additionally, travelers will experience the breathtaking "Norway in a Nutshell" tour and enjoy a beer tasting at the historic Carlsberg Brewery.', 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Rovaniemi!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Santa / Scandic Rovaniemi City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Reindeer farm – Visit husky Farm – Visit Santa village - Northern Lights Tour\nToday, we visit the reindeer and husky farms. Meet the authentic reindeer herder and take photos of the reindeer. Next, we visit the Santa Claus Village and the numerous souvenir shops, Santa's Post Office and surely, we get to meet the man himself in his office. Santa Claus Village in Lapland is a popular place to cross the Arctic Circle: here you will get a certificate confirming the feat. Tonight, we either experience Midnight Sun tour (Jun-Aug) OR we experience the Northern Lights (Sep-Oct) phenomenon depending upon the departure date. Ride around the surroundings of Lapland to observe the Midnight sun OR the auroras. Our driving guide will take you to several different spots to give you the best chance to see the Midnight sun OR to chase the northern lights. (Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Midnight sun/Northern Lights, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Midnight sun/Northern Lights tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the midnight sun or the lights).", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Santa / Scandic\xa0Rovaniemi\xa0City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi,\xa0Finland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nFly to Helsinki\xa0\nToday, we check out and we take a flight to Helsinki. Upon arrival, we check in to the hotel.\nNote: Today the group will be joining the Scenic Scandinavia guests.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Hotel Radisson Blu Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nDay trip to Tallinn – Guided City Tour of Tallinn\nToday, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we visit the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki.\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Hotel Radisson Blu Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm.\nToday, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Board ferry (Inside Cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm.'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar\nToday, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Strawberry Arena / Hotel Scandic Infra City / Hotel Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOnto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern\nToday, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Thon Oslo Fjord / Hotel Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park – Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Vestlia Resort / Hotel Highland Lodge / Hotel Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nTravel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’\nToday, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen.  \n\xa0NOTE: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Edvard Grieg / Hotel Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Hotel Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Board ferry (Inside Cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum\xa0\nOnto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky / Hotel Crowne Plaza / Hotel Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery\xa0\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable-stayed bridge across the Øresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky / Hotel Crowne Plaza / Hotel Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nInternational connection may be from Delhi.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'NA'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Santa hotel / Scandic Rovaniemi City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen,\xa0\n', '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights at Santa hotel / Scandic Rovaniemi City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen,\xa0\n', '1': '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DK', 'countryName': 'Denmark', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EURP', 'countryName': 'Europe', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EE', 'countryName': 'Estonia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 502100.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Santa hotel / Scandic Rovaniemi City / Scandic Pohjanhovi or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen,\xa0\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunch.\n09 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinner.\n\n\xa0\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.', 'Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', 'Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Finland\nRovaniemi \n\nVisit Arktikum\nMidnight Sun Tour\nVisit Reindeer Farm\nVisit Husky Farm\nVisit Santa Village\nArctic Crossing Certificate\n\nHelsinki \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center With Chocolate Tasting\n\nEstonia \nTallinn\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm Concert Hall\nVisit The Vasa Ship Museum\n\nNorway\nOslo \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nVisit The Fram Museum\nPhotostop At Holmenkollen Ski Jump\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour: A Unique To Bergen\n\nBergen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride – Floybanen\n\nDenmark\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy Canal Cruise\nRide On The Oresund Bridge\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'Finland\nRovaniemi \n\nVisit Reindeer Farm\nVisit Husky Farm\nVisit Santa Village\nArctic Crossing Certificate\xa0\nExperience The Midnight Sun (June To Aug) Or Experience The Northern Lights Phenomenon (Sept To Oct)\xa0\n\n\xa0\nHelsinki\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center\n\nEstonia \nTallinn \n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm City Hall\nVisit The Viking Museum\nVisit The Icebar\n\n\xa0\nKarlstad\n\nPhoto Stop At Lake Vanern\n\nNorway\n\nOslo\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nEntrance To Holmenkollen Ski Museum\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nBergen \n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride –\xa0Floibanen\n\n\xa0\nDenmark\nAarhus \n\nOrientation City Tour\nPhoto Stop At Infinite Bridge\n\n\xa0\nOdense\n\nVisit H C Andersen Museum\n\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Carlsberg Brewery\nPhoto Stop At Oresund Bridge\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 13 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 39 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 15th November 2023.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\xa0\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided\n\nSightseeing:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\n(Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Northern lights OR Midnight sun, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Northern Lights OR Midnight Sun tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the lights).\n\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/Rovaniemi_267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Romaniemi_7532.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Rovaniemi7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Kuopio_Finland_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Helsinki7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Tallinn753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Silja753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/VasaMuseum.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Karlstad753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/VigelandSculpturePark753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Norway753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/FunicularRailwayBergenNorwayshutterstock_57936379.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Copenhagen.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015169/itinerary/Copenhagen_753.jpg']}, 'score': 7.285092, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015151', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015151', 'availableMonths': ['march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Scenic Scandinavia With Iceland (Winter)', 'days': 14, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'On Board Silja Or Viking', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Geilo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Fjord Line Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the ice bar Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery A cup of tomato soup at the Tomato farm'], 'pdfName': 'PKG004841_0_20211130183554.pdf', 'price': 552494, 'packageSummary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia With Iceland (Winter)\' package is a 14-day tour covering Copenhagen, Stockholm, Oslo, Reykjavik, Bergen, Geilo, and Helsinki, alongside memorable journeys on the Silja or Viking and Fjord Line cruises. Throughout this extensive itinerary, participants will enjoy unique experiences such as a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, a refreshing drink at an ice bar, and the incredibly scenic "Norway in a Nutshell" tour. Additionally, travelers will get to experience a beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery and savor a warm cup of tomato soup at a local tomato farm.', 'images': ['Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'Talllin.jpg', 'Helsnki-fery-iti.jpg', 'Stockholm.jpg', 'Karstad_753_Adobe.jpg', 'VigelandParkMuseumOsloNorway.jpg', 'Gudvangen_Norway_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Bergen_Funicular_Train_753_Adobe.jpg', 'AArhus.jpg', 'Little_Mermaid_Copenhagen_753_Adobe.jpg', 'Reyjavik_753.jpg', 'Iceland_7532.jpg', 'Iceland_Waterfall_7531.jpg', 'Iceland_Iceberg_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 552494, 'thumbnailImage': 'Iceland_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015151 is named 'Scenic Scandinavia With Iceland (Winter)' and spans 14 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Helsinki, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Helsinki! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Tallinn – Guided city tour of Tallinn Today, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we see the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - On Board Silja Or Viking, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm. Today, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar Today, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th-century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern Today, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Geilo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park – Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Travel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’ Today, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen. Note: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Fjord Line Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum Onto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable stayed bridge across the Oresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Copenhagen - Fly to Reykjavik, Iceland –Orientation Tour of Reykjavik Today, we check out and proceed to take a flight to Reykjavik. On arrival, proceed for an Orientation Tour of Reykjavik: see the Hallgrimskirkja (Church), Rainbow Street and many more interesting sites., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Golden Circle tour (Thingvellir – Geysir – Gullfoss) Today, we proceed for a Golden Circle Tour where we first Visit the Thingvellir national park. Here, we walk through the rift valley. This is the only place in the world where separation between the North American and European geological rift (tectonic plates) are above sea level, and nowhere in the world are the edges of both plates as clearly visible than the rift valley in Thingvellir National Park. Here, you can stand on two continents at the same time! Then, we proceed to Visit the Geysir where we take a Stop at the hot springs. Next, we will see the famous Gullfoss waterfall and take a few pictures. Later we visit the Tomato farm where we taste a cup of their tomato soup., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: South Island Tour (Visit Eyjafjallajokull Volcano - Visit Seljalandsfoss - Skogafoss waterfalls – Photo stop at Plane Wreck – Photo stop at Black Sand Beach Today, we take a scenic drive to South Island where we first stop and see the Eyjafjallajokull Volcano. Next we proceed to the famous Seljalandsfoss and Skogafoss. Take photos of the waterfall where you see the maximum rainbows at once. These were the locations of a famous Bollywood song. Seljalandsfoss cascades over steep cliffs, which make it possible for people to walk behind the waterfall, offering a spectacular view of the waterfall itself and the surroundings. Skogafoss stands at 60 meters tall. Later, proceed to take a photo-stop at the Black Sand beach and we Visit the Iconic plane wreck site., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 14 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity to India from Reykjavik, there is a possibility that you may have to stay an additional night in Copenhagen, Denmark for your flight back home. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Flights Important notes : Flights are subject to change, once the group materializes on a first come first basis, alternative flight options will be offered. Round trip Flights included for EX-India passengers Airfare not included for joining direct passengers, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 552494.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n, \n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n03 nights at Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik, Iceland.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 14 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 42 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeings: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue. There are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided. General: In case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Chocolate tasting at Fazer Experience Enjoy drink at the ice bar Enjoy the most scenic “Norway in a Nutshell” tour Beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery A cup of tomato soup at the Tomato farm.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE220', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': 'The \'Scenic Scandinavia With Iceland (Winter)\' package is a 14-day tour covering Copenhagen, Stockholm, Oslo, Reykjavik, Bergen, Geilo, and Helsinki, alongside memorable journeys on the Silja or Viking and Fjord Line cruises. Throughout this extensive itinerary, participants will enjoy unique experiences such as a chocolate tasting at the Fazer Experience, a refreshing drink at an ice bar, and the incredibly scenic "Norway in a Nutshell" tour. Additionally, travelers will get to experience a beer tasting at the Carlsberg Brewery and savor a warm cup of tomato soup at a local tomato farm.', 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Helsinki!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nDay trip to Tallinn – Guided city tour of Tallinn\nToday, we drive to the pier to take a ferry to Tallinn, Estonia's capital on the Baltic Sea. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Tallinn: See the Toompea Hill, Parliament building, Dome Church, St. Nicholas Church, Town Hall Square. Next, we see the Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Later, we drive to the pier to take the ferry back to Helsinki.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion Helsinki\xa0/\xa0Radisson Seaside\xa0or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Fazer experience - Guided city tour of Helsinki - Board Cruise to Stockholm.\nToday, visit Fazer experience centre and learn the art of chocolate making including chocolate tasting. Next, we proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki: See the Senate Square, visit Lutheran Tempelliauki Church, Sibelius Park and many more interesting sights. Later, we board the cruise across the Baltic Sea to Stockholm.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'On board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided city tour of Stockholm – Visit Stockholm City Hall – Visit Viking Museum – Visit the Icebar\nToday, we proceed on a guided city tour of Stockholm: See the Opera House, Alfred Nobel's House and the Royal Palace. Also, we visit the Stockholm City Hall - the seat of Stockholm Municipality. Next, we visit Viking Museum - Museum displaying wooden, 9th-century Viking ships, plus artifacts recovered from burial tombs. Later, we visit the Icebar where you see the interior, bars & glasses carved from ice. In the evening, we spend some free time in Gamla Stan – the old Town.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Oslo – Photo stop at Lake Vanern\nToday, we drive to Oslo. Enroute, we visit the town of Karlstad, for a photo stop at Lake Vanern – the largest lake of Sweden.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided Tour of Oslo – Entrance to Vigeland Sculpture Park –\xa0Entrance to Holmenkollen Ski Jump Area & Museum\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Oslo: See the Parliament Square, National Galleries, Karl Johan shopping street, the Royal Palace and Akhershus Fortress. Next, we visit Vigeland Sculpture Park. Later we visit the Holmenkollen Ski Museum: the world's oldest ski museum. Later we drive to Geilo.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nTravel on one of Norway’s most popular trips ‘Norway in a nutshell’\nToday, we board our train from Geilo to Myrdal, change to the Flam railway line, for a scenic travel to Flam. We wander around the idyllic countryside, before embarking on a boat ride through the Aurlandsfjord into the Naeroyfjord, one of the narrowest fjords in Europe, surrounded by mountains of up to 1800 meters. On arrival at scenic Gudvangen, we board the coach and travel through the impressive Norwegian landscape to Bergen.  \nNote: Due to weather conditions, at times the cruise or the trains might not operate. In such situations, we shall try to re-route the journey and shall try to cover maximum of the landscapes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Bergen – Ride on the Funicular train – Board Cruise to Hirtshals\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Bergen: Visit the Hanseatic wharf Bryggen with its pastel – coloured wooden houses, winding cobblestone streets and old Bergen. Next, we take a ride on the Funicular train, to the top of the Mount Floyen for an aerial view of Bergen. Later, we board the cruise to Hirtshals.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation city tour of Aarhus – Photo stop at Infinite Bridge - Visit H C Andersen Museum\nOnto arrival at Hirtshals, we proceed to the old town of Aarhus for an Orientation city tour: See the Aarhus cathedral and the old town. Next, we take a photo stop at the Scenic Infinite bridge. Later we proceed to Odense. On arrival, we visit H C Andersen Museum dedicated to the famous author Hans Christian Andersen. Later we depart for Copenhagen.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Copenhagen – Photo stop at Oresund bridge – Visit Carlsberg Brewery\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Copenhagen: See the Parliament building, Amalienborg Palace, Gefion fountain, Little Mermaid statue and many other interesting sights. Next, we take a photo stop at the Oresund bridge: a combined railway and motorway cable stayed bridge across the Oresund strait between Denmark and Sweden Later we visit the famous Carlsberg Brewery with beer tasting.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC Bella Sky /\xa0Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen\xa0or similar in Copenhagen,\xa0Denmark'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nCopenhagen - Fly to Reykjavik, Iceland –Orientation Tour of Reykjavik\nToday, we check out and proceed to take a flight to Reykjavik. On arrival, proceed for an Orientation Tour of Reykjavik: see the Hallgrimskirkja (Church), Rainbow Street and many more interesting sites.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik, Iceland'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nGolden Circle tour (Thingvellir – Geysir – Gullfoss)\nToday, we proceed for a Golden Circle Tour where we first Visit the\xa0Thingvellir\xa0national park. Here, we walk through the rift valley. This is the only place in the world where separation between the North American and European geological rift (tectonic plates) are above sea level, and nowhere in the world are the edges of both plates as clearly visible than the rift valley in Thingvellir National Park. Here, you can stand on two continents at the same time! Then, we proceed to Visit the Geysir where we take a Stop at the hot springs. Next, we will see the famous Gullfoss waterfall and take a few pictures. Later we visit the Tomato farm where we taste a cup of their tomato soup.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik,\xa0Iceland'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nSouth Island Tour (Visit Eyjafjallajokull Volcano - Visit Seljalandsfoss - Skogafoss waterfalls – Photo stop at Plane Wreck – Photo stop at Black Sand Beach\nToday, we take a scenic drive to South Island where we first stop and see the Eyjafjallajokull Volcano. Next we proceed to the famous Seljalandsfoss and Skogafoss. Take photos of the waterfall where you see the maximum rainbows at once. These were the locations of a famous Bollywood song. Seljalandsfoss cascades over steep cliffs, which make it possible for people to walk behind the waterfall, offering a spectacular view of the waterfall itself and the surroundings. Skogafoss stands at 60 meters tall. Later, proceed to take a photo-stop at the Black Sand beach and we Visit the Iconic plane wreck site.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik,\xa0Iceland'}, {'day': 14, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nDue to flight connectivity to India from Reykjavik, there is a possibility that you may have to stay an additional night in Copenhagen, Denmark for your flight back home.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n\n\xa0\nFlights Important notes :\n\nFlights are subject to change, once the group materializes on a first come first basis, alternative flight options will be offered.\nRound trip Flights included for EX-India passengers\nAirfare not included for joining direct passengers\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n03 nights at Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik, Iceland.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n03 nights at Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik, Iceland.\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n01 Night at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n02 Nights at Scandic Rovaniemi / Scandic Pohjanhovi\xa0 or similar in Rovaniemi\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Marina / Clarion Helsinki or similar in Helsinki.\n01 night on board ferry (outside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Hotel Quality Friends/ Scandic or similar in Stockholm\n02 night at Thon Oslo Fjord/ Radisson blu Nydalen or similar in Oslo\n01 night at Magic Hotel Kloverhuset/ Quality Edvard Grieg/ Clarion Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen\n02 nights at Hotel Bella Sky/ Cornwell Portside/ Crowne Plaza Towers or similar in Copenhagen\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EURP', 'countryName': 'Europe', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DK', 'countryName': 'Denmark', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IS', 'countryName': 'Iceland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'EE', 'countryName': 'Estonia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 552500.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Clarion Helsinki / Radisson Seaside or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n01 night on board ferry (Inside cabin) from Helsinki to Stockholm\n01 night at Quality Strawberry Arena / Scandic Infra City / Quality Globe or similar in Stockholm, Sweden.\n01 night at Thon Oslo Fjord / Thon Arena or similar in Oslo, Norway.\n01 night at Vestlia / Highland Lodge / Bardola or similar in Geilo, Norway.\n01 night at Quality Edward Grieg / Comfort Hotel Bergen Airport / Thon Bergen Airport or similar in Bergen, Norway.\n01 night on board ferry (inside cabin) from Bergen to Hirtshals.\n02 nights at Hotel AC Bella Sky / Crowne Plaza / Scandic Sydhavnen or similar in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n03 nights at Hotel Grand Reykjavik or similar in Reykjavik, Iceland.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast.\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches including local meals.\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners including local meals.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.', 'Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n03 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', 'Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', '\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Finland\nRovaniemi \n\nVisit Arktikum\nMidnight Sun Tour\nVisit Reindeer Farm\nVisit Husky Farm\nVisit Santa Village\nArctic Crossing Certificate\n\nHelsinki \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center With Chocolate Tasting\n\nEstonia \nTallinn\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm Concert Hall\nVisit The Vasa Ship Museum\n\nNorway\nOslo \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nVisit The Fram Museum\nPhotostop At Holmenkollen Ski Jump\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour: A Unique To Bergen\n\nBergen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride – Floybanen\n\nDenmark\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy Canal Cruise\nRide On The Oresund Bridge\n', 'Finland\nHelsinki \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Lutheran Temppeliaukio Church Or ‘Rock Church Helsinki’\nVisit Fazer Experience Center\n\nEstonia \nTallinn \n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSweden\nStockholm \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Stockholm City Hall\nVisit The Viking Museum\nVisit The Icebar\n\nKarlstad\n\nPhoto Stop At Lake Vanern\n\nNorway\nOslo\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit The Vigeland Sculpture Park\nEntrance To Holmenkollen Ski Museum\n‘Norway In A Nutshell’ Tour\n\nBergen\n\nGuided City Tour\nEnjoy A Scenic Funicular Train Ride – Mt Floyen\n\xa0\n\n\nDenmark\nAarhus\n\nOrientation City Tour\nPhoto Stop At Infinite Bridge\n\nOdense \n\nVisit H C Andersen Museum\n\nCopenhagen\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Carlsberg Brewery\nPhoto Stop At Oresund Bridge\n\nIceland\nReykjavik\n\nReykjavik Orientation Tour\nGolden Circle Tour\nVisit The Site Of Eyjafjallajokull Volcano\nVisit Seljalandsfoss And Skogafoss Waterfalls\nPhotostop At Black Sand Beach & Plane Wreck\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 14 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 42 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021.\xa0 Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\xa0\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot.\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain Days packed lunch will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeings:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue.\nThere are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nIn case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses\xa0 to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”.\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/Iceland_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Talllin.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Helsnki-fery-iti.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Stockholm.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Karstad_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/VigelandParkMuseumOsloNorway.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Gudvangen_Norway_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Bergen_Funicular_Train_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/AArhus.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Little_Mermaid_Copenhagen_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Reyjavik_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Iceland_7532.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Iceland_Waterfall_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015151/itinerary/Iceland_Iceberg_753.jpg']}, 'score': 7.285092, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015024', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015024', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Europe (Winter)', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lausanne', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lausanne', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Illumination tour of Paris. Fondue lunch at Glacier 3000 Chocolate tasting at Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Champagne lunch at Top of Jungfraujoch.'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 401645, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering London, Paris, Lausanne, and Zurich. The itinerary features a variety of memorable experiences, including an illumination tour of Paris, a delicious fondue lunch at Glacier 3000, and a sweet chocolate tasting at Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Additionally, participants will enjoy a luxurious champagne lunch at the Top of Jungfraujoch, making this winter journey truly magical.", 'images': ['House_Of_Parliament_London1_753.jpg', 'LondonEye753.jpg', 'Oxford_London_753_Adobe.jpg', 'Paris_Champs_Elyees_753.jpg', 'Eiffel_Tower_SienRiver_Cruise_753.jpg', 'Disneylandparis3.jpg', 'Flower_Clock_geneva_753.jpg', 'Glacier_3000_7531.jpg', 'Lucern_Lake_Cruise_753.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'Zurich_Downtown_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 401645, 'thumbnailImage': 'London_Bridge_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015024 is named 'Magical Europe (Winter)' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - London, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to London! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside London Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of London – Visit Tower of London – Madame Tussauds Wax Museum – Ride on the London Eye Today, we proceed on a guided City Tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. After the city tour, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh i Noor Diamond. Next, we visit the famous Madame Tussauds Wax Museum. Later, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Oxford – Lords Cricket Ground Today, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”. Later, we drive back to London and enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground. Note: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Le shuttle / Ferry to Paris Today, we proceed to Calais by the Le Shuttle / Ferry and onwards drive to Paris., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Versailles Palace - Visit Fragonard - Guided city tour of Paris Today, we proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. Next, we visit the Famous French perfume museum – Fragonard. Later, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) – Seine River Cruise – Eiffel Tower Level 3 – Illumination Tour of Paris Today, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park (Up to 5 Hours). Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland. Next, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River. Later in the evening, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level and we proceed for an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up. Note: Visiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue. Due to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Lausanne, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Swiss - Orientation Tour of Geneva Today, we drive to Geneva in Switzerland. On arrival, we enjoy an orientation tour: see the Palais des Nations - the European arm of the United Nations. Later, see the Jet d’eau - Geneva’s famous fountain, the Floral Clock., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Lausanne, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Glacier 3000 - Orientation tour of Gstaad – Golden Pass Train Today, we proceed on an excursion to Glacier 3000. Enjoy breath- taking views of the iconic mountains such as Mont-Blanc, the Matterhorn, Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau from the Tissot Peak Walk. Next, we enjoy an orientation tour of Gstaad - a shooting location for Indian films. Later, we board the scenic Golden Pass train and enjoy panoramic views as we journey through alpine forest and picturesque villages. Note: On the days, Mt Glacier 3000 is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to an alternate excursion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour of Lucerne - Lake Lucerne Cruise – Orientation tour of Zurich – Visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate Today, we proceed to Lucerne. On arrival we enjoy an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument, and Kapel Brucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Also, we enjoy a cruise on Lake Lucerne. Next, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Zurich where we explore the historic Old Town with its winding streets and iconic churches. Later, we visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate; where we get to discover Switzerland’s oldest chocolate brands and get to learn the art of chocolate making. Note: If Lindt is not available, we shall take the group to an alternate Chocolate experience., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Excursion to Jungfraujoch with Lunch & Interlaken Today, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We take the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Enjoy lunch on Top. Later, descend and visit Interlaken., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to Zurich airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Frankfurt or Milan instead of Zurich. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 401645.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Holiday Inn Bath Road / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Central Residence / Eurotel Victoria / Novotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n, \n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Radisson LHR / Crown Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n, \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen + UK visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers. Important Notes : Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st September, 2023. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, city tours may not take place for several groups in case of road closures for rehearsals / events that would be taking place from 11th July, 2024 to 23rd September, 2024. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Illumination tour of Paris. Fondue lunch at Glacier 3000 Chocolate tasting at Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Champagne lunch at Top of Jungfraujoch..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE214', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering London, Paris, Lausanne, and Zurich. The itinerary features a variety of memorable experiences, including an illumination tour of Paris, a delicious fondue lunch at Glacier 3000, and a sweet chocolate tasting at Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Additionally, participants will enjoy a luxurious champagne lunch at the Top of Jungfraujoch, making this winter journey truly magical.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to London!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside London Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Hilton Heathrow / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of London – Visit Tower of London – Madame Tussauds Wax Museum – Ride on the London Eye\nToday, we proceed on a guided City Tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. After the city tour, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh i Noor Diamond. Next, we visit the famous Madame Tussauds Wax Museum. Later, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Hilton Heathrow / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided Tour of Oxford – Lords Cricket Ground\nToday, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”. Later, we drive back to London and enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground.\nNote: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Hilton Heathrow / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nLe shuttle / Ferry to Paris\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Calais by the Le Shuttle / Ferry and onwards drive to Paris.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Mercure Orly / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\n\n\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Versailles Palace - Visit Fragonard - Guided city tour of Paris\xa0\nToday, we proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. Next, we visit the Famous French perfume museum – Fragonard. Later, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris:\xa0 See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Mercure Orly / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDisneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) – Seine River Cruise – Eiffel Tower Level 3 – Illumination Tour of Paris\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park (Up to 5 Hours). Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland. Next, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River. Later in the evening, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level and we proceed for an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up.\nNote:\xa0\n\nVisiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level.\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue.\nDue to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Mercure Orly / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Swiss - Orientation Tour of Geneva\nToday, we drive to Geneva in Switzerland. On arrival, we enjoy an orientation tour: see the Palais des Nations - the European arm of the United Nations. Later, see the Jet d’eau - Geneva’s famous fountain, the Floral Clock.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Agora by Fassbind / Central Residence / Eurotel Victoria / Novotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGlacier 3000 - Orientation tour of Gstaad – Golden Pass Train\nToday, we proceed on an excursion to Glacier 3000. Enjoy breath- taking views of the iconic mountains such as Mont-Blanc, the Matterhorn, Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau from the Tissot Peak Walk. Next, we enjoy an orientation tour of Gstaad - a shooting location for Indian films. Later, we board the scenic Golden Pass train and enjoy panoramic views as we journey through alpine forest and picturesque villages.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0\nOn the days, Mt Glacier 3000 is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to an alternate excursion.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Agora by Fassbind /\xa0Central Residence\xa0/ Eurotel Victoria\xa0/ Novotel\xa0or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation Tour of Lucerne - Lake Lucerne Cruise – Orientation tour of Zurich – Visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate\nToday, we proceed to Lucerne. On arrival we enjoy an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument, and Kapel Brucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Also, we enjoy a cruise on Lake Lucerne. Next, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Zurich where we explore the historic Old Town with its winding streets and iconic churches. Later, we visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate; where we get to discover Switzerland’s oldest chocolate brands and get to learn the art of chocolate making.\xa0\nNote: If Lindt is not available, we shall take the group to an alternate Chocolate experience.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick /\xa0 Courtyard by Marriott \xa0or similar in Zurich, Switzerland'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with Lunch & Interlaken\nToday, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We take the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Enjoy lunch on Top. Later, descend and visit Interlaken.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick /\xa0\xa0Courtyard by Marriott\xa0\xa0or similar in Zurich,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to Zurich airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\n\nDue to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Frankfurt or Milan instead of Zurich. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Holiday Inn Bath Road / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Central Residence / Eurotel Victoria / Novotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n', '\n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Radisson LHR / Crown Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Holiday Inn Bath Road / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Central Residence / Eurotel Victoria / Novotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n', '1': '\n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Radisson LHR / Crown Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GB', 'countryName': 'United Kingdom', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 401600.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott LHR / Holiday Inn Bath Road / Crowne Plaza LHR or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Central Residence / Eurotel Victoria / Novotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Novotel Zurich Messe /Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n', '\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nMultiple entry Schengen + UK visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0 \xa0\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['United Kingdom\n\nGuided city tour of London\nEntrance to Madame Tussauds Wax Museum\nVisit Tower of London - see the famous Koh i Noor Diamond\nRide on the London Eye\nGuided tour of Oxford\nVisit the Lords Cricket Ground\n\nFrance\n\nGuided city tour of Paris\nSeine river cruise\nGuided Tour of Versailles Palace\nVisit Fragonard - French Perfume Museum\nVisit 3rd level of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\nIllumination Tour of Paris\n\nSwitzerland\n\nOrientation tour of Geneva\nVisit Glacier 3000\nOrientation Tour of Gstaad\nRide on the Scenic Golden Pass Train\nOrientation tour of Lucerne\nCruise on Lake Lucerne\nOrientation tour of Zurich\nVisit Lindt: Home of Chocolate\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\n', 'UNITED KINGDOM :\n\nGuided city tour of London\nEntrance to Madame Tussauds Wax Museum\nRide on the London Eye\n\nFRANCE :\n\nGuided city tour of Paris\nVisit 2nd level of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Fragonard – French Perfume Museum\nIllumination Tour of Paris\xa0\nSeine river cruise\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\xa0\n\n\nSWITZERLAND :\n\nVisit Glacier 3000\xa0\nRide on the Scenic Golden Pass Train\nOrientation tour of Geneva\nOrientation Tour of Gstaad\nOrientation tour of Montreux\nOrientation tour of Lucerne\nCruise on Lake Lucerne\nVisit Lindt Home of Chocolate\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0 \nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0 \nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen + UK visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nNote:\xa0Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers.\nImportant Notes :\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st September, 2023.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\nOn certain days a packed lunch will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nDue to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, city tours may not take place for several groups in case of road closures for rehearsals / events that would be taking place from 11th July, 2024 to 23rd September, 2024.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/London_Bridge_267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/House_Of_Parliament_London1_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/LondonEye753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Oxford_London_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Paris_Champs_Elyees_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Eiffel_Tower_SienRiver_Cruise_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Disneylandparis3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Flower_Clock_geneva_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Glacier_3000_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Lucern_Lake_Cruise_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015024/itinerary/Zurich_Downtown_753.jpg']}, 'score': 6.785142, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015085', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015085', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026'], 'packageName': 'Sensational Europe (Winter) ', 'days': 15, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rhineland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Laax', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Laax', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Wattens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Padova', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Indian dinners in the comforts of your hotel in most cities Illumination tour of Paris. Beer tasting at the Beer Museum in Brussels. Exclusive lunch inside Mini Europe. Enjoy Tea, Coffee or Beer on the Rhine River cruise. Enjoy Black Forest cake in Titisee – Heart of Black Forest. Champagne lunch at Jungfraujoch Authentic local Italian meal in Florence. Ice cream in Italy.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG000642_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 452059, 'packageSummary': "The 'Sensational Europe (Winter)' package is a 15-day tour covering Padova, Paris, Eindhoven, Central Switzerland, Florence, Laax, Rhineland, and Wattens. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy key highlights such as an illumination tour of Paris, beer tasting at the Beer Museum in Brussels, an exclusive lunch inside Mini Europe, and a scenic Rhine River cruise with tea, coffee, or beer. The itinerary also features delicious culinary experiences, including Black Forest cake in Titisee, a Champagne lunch at Jungfraujoch, an authentic local Italian meal in Florence, and traditional ice cream in Italy, alongside the comfort of Indian dinners served at hotels in most cities.", 'images': ['Rome753.jpg', 'StPeterBasilica753.jpg', 'Pisa753.jpg', 'StMarkVenice.jpg', 'SwarovskiMuseumInnsbruck753.jpg', 'StMoritz753.jpg', 'Titles753.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'RhineFallsSchaffhausen753.jpg', 'Cologne753.jpg', 'Amsterdam753.jpg', 'Atomuim753.jpg', 'EiffelTower753.jpg', 'Disneyland75345.jpg', 'Paris75390.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 452059, 'thumbnailImage': 'Lucerne_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015085 is named 'Sensational Europe (Winter) ' and spans 15 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Paris! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City tour of Paris – Fragonard Museum – Seine River Cruise – Eiffel Tower 3rd Level – Illumination Tour of Paris Today, proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees including a visit to the famous Fragonard perfume museum. Next, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River. Later, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level. In the evening, proceed for an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up. Overnight in Paris (CDG Area), France Note: Visiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue. Due to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) Today, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland. Overnight in Paris (CDG Area), France, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Brussels – Visit Beer Museum - Visit Mini Europe with Exclusive Lunch – Photo stop at Atomium Today, we proceed to Brussels for an orientation tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with free time in the city. Next, we visit the Beer Museum with beer tasting. Later we visit Mini Europe – Europe in Miniature. Next, proceed for a photo stop at Atomuim. Overnight in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands/ Belgium, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Cheese farm and Wooden Shoe factory – Amsterdam canal cruise – Visit Dam Square Today, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Next, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass topped boat. Later we spent some free time at Dam Square. Overnight in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands/ Belgium, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Rhineland, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Photo stop at the Cologne Cathedral – Rhine River cruise Today, we drive to Cologne and take a photo stop at the Cologne Cathedral, which is the largest Gothic church in northern Europe and features immense twin towers that stand 515 feet (157 metres) tall. Next, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the River Rhine. Overnight in Rhineland, Germany., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Central Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Black Forest – Cuckoo Clock Demonstration – Orientation tour of Lucerne Today we drive in the heart of the Black Forest region, known for its dense, evergreen forests and picturesque villages. Here, we also get to see how the famous Cuckoo Clocks are made. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Lucerne: See the Lion Monument, and Kapellbrucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Overnight in Central Switzerland, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Central Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Excursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken Today, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken. Overnight in Central Switzerland, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Laax, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Mt. Titlis – Proceed to Laax Today, we visit Mt Titlis. Our cable car ride includes the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair – to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis. Next, we drive to Laax and have some free time in the city where we see Switzerland’s most scenic sights & lakes. Overnight in Laax, Switzerland., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Laax, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Cable car to Flims - Rhine Gorge train – Orientation tour of Chur Today, we take a cable car to proceed to Flims: a pioneering, on demand gondola system that transports you from the village up to the UNESCO World Heritage Tectonic Arena Sardona. Next, we take a Scenic train journey through the Rhine Gorge. Here, we have some free time for shopping at Landquart Fashion Outlet (Subject to time permitting). Later, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Chur: the oldest city of Switzerland., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Wattens, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Vaduz – Orientation tour of Innsbruck – Swarovski Crystal Worlds Today, proceed to Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz, and you also have free time to shop at the Huber watch store. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse. Later, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens. Overnight in Innsbruck/ Wattens, Austria., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Padova, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Private boat to St. Mark’s Square – Orientation tour of Venice Today, we drive to Italy and proceed to the pier to take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs. Overnight in Padova / Ferrara, Italy, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided walking tour of Florence Today, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria. Overnight in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme, Italy, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 14 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Rome - Panoramic guided tour of Rome and Vatican City on an open roof bus Today we proceed towards Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a panoramic guided city tour of Rome & Vatican City (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed) on an open roof top bus where we see Colosseum, Piazza Venezia, Circus Maximus, Castel Angelo and Piazza Barberini. Next, we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square with a photo stop of Colosseum. Overnight in Chianciano Terme, Italy, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 15 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: See Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to Pisa to see the world famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 452059.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Van der Valk / NH or similar in Belgium / Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Intercity Frankfurt / Best Western Frankfurt or similar in Germany.\n02 nights at Hotel Central / Terrace / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Engelberg / Zurich, Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Laudinella / Reine Victoria or similar in St. Moritz, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Alp / Alpenkoning / Waldhotel / Park Hotel Hall Tirol or similar in Innsbruck / Seefeld / Tirol, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra Ferrara / AC / Orologio / Best Western or similar in Ferrara, Italy.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme, Italy.\n, \n03 nights at Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Dorint or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n02 nights at Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Dion / Seelos / Harry’s home or similar in Innsbruck / Wattens, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra / Best Western / Four Points by Sheraton or similar in Ferrara/ Padova, Italy.\n02 night at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch.\n13 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches., \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk and coffee)\n11 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch.\n14 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen Visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 15 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 45 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: Airline And Airfare The Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July, 2026. Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers. Passengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves. For Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents. Passengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To / From The Hub City At Their Own Expense. Joining Direct Clients Main Sector Air Tickets To Reach The First Overnight City And Last Departure City Is Not Included In The Joining Direct Package Price. Arrival And Departure Transfers Are Not Included In The Package Price. The Tour Manager Shall Meet The Clients Directly At The Hotel. Hotels All Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts. The Hotel Room Size In Europe Would Be Up To 16 – 18 Sq. Mts. Most Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size. As A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room. For Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room. A Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult. Hotel Rooms May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions. Functioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority. During Heat Wave In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures. Most Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms. Due To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As The Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City. In Switzerland The Stay May Be Split In Two Hotels. Any Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers. We Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary. In Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast. Coaches Most Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean. Due To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives. Eating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach. One Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach. In Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop. Coaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach. Due To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities, As Per Eu Norms To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And On Foot. Meals Meals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible. On Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided. Sightseeing On Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same. Generally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible. The Eiffel Tower On Certain Days Due To Strong Wind Conditions Or Being Overcrowded Or For Security Reasons May Be Closed. The Lifts At The Eiffel Tower Are Currently Closed Due To Safety. Hence The Visit To The Tower Is Only Allowed By Climbing The Staircase. In Case There Is No Change In The Same On Tour Customers Will Be Refunded The Amount For The Same If They Chose Not To Climb The Stairs. Due To Stringent Security Checks At The Eiffel Tower, It May Take Up To 4-5 Hours In The Queue. No Refund Will Be Provided In Case The Group Is Unable To Visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level Due To Weather Conditions / Operational Closures. General On Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members. A Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour. Arrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer For The Group Flight Timings. Security Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary. Please Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage. Disabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client. Tcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour. Normal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges. The Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services. The Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same. There Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour. All Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted). Optional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy. Gst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India. In Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed. The Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only. Tours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange. Please Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Indian dinners in the comforts of your hotel in most cities Illumination tour of Paris. Beer tasting at the Beer Museum in Brussels. Exclusive lunch inside Mini Europe. Enjoy Tea, Coffee or Beer on the Rhine River cruise. Enjoy Black Forest cake in Titisee – Heart of Black Forest. Champagne lunch at Jungfraujoch Authentic local Italian meal in Florence. Ice cream in Italy..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE219', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Sensational Europe (Winter)' package is a 15-day tour covering Padova, Paris, Eindhoven, Central Switzerland, Florence, Laax, Rhineland, and Wattens. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy key highlights such as an illumination tour of Paris, beer tasting at the Beer Museum in Brussels, an exclusive lunch inside Mini Europe, and a scenic Rhine River cruise with tea, coffee, or beer. The itinerary also features delicious culinary experiences, including Black Forest cake in Titisee, a Champagne lunch at Jungfraujoch, an authentic local Italian meal in Florence, and traditional ice cream in Italy, alongside the comfort of Indian dinners served at hotels in most cities.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Paris!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City tour of Paris – Fragonard Museum – Seine River Cruise – Eiffel Tower 3rd Level – Illumination Tour of Paris\xa0\nToday, proceed for a guided city tour of Paris:\xa0 See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees including a visit to the famous Fragonard perfume museum. Next, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River. Later, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level. In the evening, proceed for an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up.\xa0\nOvernight in Paris (CDG Area), France\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nVisiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level.\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue.\nDue to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDisneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\nToday, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland.\nOvernight in Paris (CDG Area), France\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Brussels – Visit Beer Museum - Visit Mini Europe with Exclusive Lunch – Photo stop at Atomium\nToday, we proceed to Brussels for an orientation tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with free time in the city. Next, we visit the Beer Museum with beer tasting. Later we visit Mini Europe – Europe in Miniature.\nNext, proceed for a photo stop at Atomuim.\xa0\nOvernight in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands/ Belgium\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Cheese farm and Wooden Shoe factory – Amsterdam canal cruise – Visit Dam Square\xa0\nToday, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Next, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass topped boat. Later we spent some free time at Dam Square.\nOvernight in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands/ Belgium\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nPhoto stop at the Cologne Cathedral – Rhine River cruise\xa0\nToday, we drive to Cologne and take a photo stop at the Cologne Cathedral, which is the largest Gothic church in northern Europe and features immense twin towers that stand 515 feet (157 metres) tall. Next, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the River Rhine.\xa0\nOvernight in Rhineland, Germany.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn / Dorint or similar in Rhineland, Germany.'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Black Forest – Cuckoo Clock Demonstration – Orientation tour of Lucerne\nToday we drive in the heart of the Black Forest region, known for its dense, evergreen forests and picturesque villages. Here, we also get to see how the famous Cuckoo Clocks are made. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Lucerne: See the Lion Monument, and Kapellbrucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates.\nOvernight in Central Switzerland\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\nToday, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken.\nOvernight in Central Switzerland\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Mt. Titlis – Proceed to Laax\nToday, we visit Mt Titlis. Our cable car ride includes the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair – to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis. Next, we drive to Laax and have some free time in the city where we see Switzerland’s most scenic sights & lakes.\nOvernight in Laax, Switzerland.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\xa0'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nCable car to Flims - Rhine Gorge train – Orientation tour of Chur\xa0\nToday, we take a cable car to proceed to Flims: a pioneering, on demand gondola system that transports you from the village up to the UNESCO World Heritage Tectonic Arena Sardona. Next, we take a Scenic train journey through the Rhine Gorge. Here, we have some free time for shopping at Landquart Fashion Outlet (Subject to time permitting). Later, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Chur: the oldest city of Switzerland.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\xa0'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Vaduz – Orientation tour of Innsbruck – Swarovski Crystal Worlds\nToday, proceed to Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz, and you also have free time to shop at the Huber watch store. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse. Later, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens.\nOvernight in Innsbruck/ Wattens, Austria.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Dion / Seelos / Harry’s home or similar in Innsbruck / Wattens, Austria.'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nPrivate boat to St. Mark’s Square – Orientation tour of Venice\xa0\nToday, we drive to Italy and proceed to the pier to take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs.\xa0\nOvernight in Padova / Ferrara, Italy\xa0\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Astra / Best Western / Four Points by Sheraton or similar in Ferrara/ Padova, Italy.'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided walking tour of Florence\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria.\xa0\nOvernight in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme, Italy\xa0\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.'}, {'day': 14, 'description': '\xa0\nDay trip to Rome - Panoramic guided tour of Rome and Vatican City on an open roof bus\xa0\nToday we proceed towards Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a panoramic guided city tour of Rome & Vatican City (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed) on an open roof top bus where we see Colosseum, Piazza Venezia, Circus Maximus, Castel Angelo and Piazza Barberini. Next, we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square with a photo stop of Colosseum.\xa0\nOvernight in Chianciano Terme, Italy\xa0\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.'}, {'day': 15, 'description': '\xa0\nSee Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories!\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Pisa to see the world famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Van der Valk / NH or similar in Belgium / Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Intercity Frankfurt / Best Western Frankfurt or similar in Germany.\n02 nights at Hotel Central / Terrace / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Engelberg / Zurich, Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Laudinella / Reine Victoria or similar in St. Moritz, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Alp / Alpenkoning / Waldhotel / Park Hotel Hall Tirol or similar in Innsbruck / Seefeld / Tirol, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra Ferrara / AC / Orologio / Best Western or similar in Ferrara, Italy.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme, Italy.\n', '\n03 nights at Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Dorint or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n02 nights at Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Dion / Seelos / Harry’s home or similar in Innsbruck / Wattens, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra / Best Western / Four Points by Sheraton or similar in Ferrara/ Padova, Italy.\n02 night at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n03 nights at Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Dorint or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n02 nights at Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Dion / Seelos / Harry’s home or similar in Innsbruck / Wattens, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra / Best Western / Four Points by Sheraton or similar in Ferrara/ Padova, Italy.\n02 night at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.\n', '1': '\n03 nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Van der Valk / NH or similar in Belgium / Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Intercity Frankfurt / Best Western Frankfurt or similar in Germany.\n02 nights at Hotel Central / Terrace / Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Engelberg / Zurich, Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Laudinella / Reine Victoria or similar in St. Moritz, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Alp / Alpenkoning / Waldhotel / Park Hotel Hall Tirol or similar in Innsbruck / Seefeld / Tirol, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra Ferrara / AC / Orologio / Best Western or similar in Ferrara, Italy.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme, Italy.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IT', 'countryName': 'Italy', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'VA', 'countryName': 'Vatican City', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DE', 'countryName': 'Germany', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NL', 'countryName': 'Netherlands', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'BE', 'countryName': 'Belgium', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'LCH', 'countryName': 'Liechtenstein', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 452100.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at Courtyard by Marriott / Hilton CDG / Hyatt CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n02 nights at Holiday Inn / Novotel / Den’s Hertogenbosch or similar in Eindhoven/ Antwerp, Netherlands / Belgium.\n01 night at Holiday Inn / Dorint or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n02 nights at Movenpick / Courtyard by Marriott / Intercity or similar in Central Switzerland.\n02 nights at Hotel Signina / Rock resort or similar in Laax, Switzerland.\n01 night at Hotel Dion / Seelos / Harry’s home or similar in Innsbruck / Wattens, Austria.\n01 night at Hotel Astra / Best Western / Four Points by Sheraton or similar in Ferrara/ Padova, Italy.\n02 night at Hotel Grand Fonti / Excelsior or similar in Arezzo / Chianciano Terme/ Florence, Italy.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n12 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch.\n13 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.', '\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk and coffee)\n11 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch.\n14 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n'], 'visa': ['\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nMultiple entry Schengen Visa.\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0 \xa0\n', '\nMultiple entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['France :\n\nGuided city tour of Paris\nVisit 3rd level of Eiffel Tower\xa0\nVisit Fragonard Museum\nSeine river cruise\nIllumination tour of Paris\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\nBelgium :\n\nMini Europe\nOrientation tour of Brussels\nPhoto Stop at Atomium\n\nNetherlands :\n\nVisit Keukenhof (Till 11th May, 2024)\nVisit Zaanse Schans (Windmills, Cheese Farm and Wooden Shoe making) (From 12th May 2025)\nEnjoy Amsterdam canal cruise\nVisit Dam Square\n\nGermany :\n\nVisit the Cologne Cathedral\nEnjoy River Rhine cruise\nVisit Black Forest\nCuckoo clock demonstration\n\nSwitzerland :\n\nView the Rhine Falls\xa0\nChance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional)\nVisit Mt. Titlis\xa0\nOrientation tour of Lucerne\xa0\nTravel on the famous Bernina railway route\xa0\nVisit to Mt. Diavolezza via train and cable car in St Moritz\nHorse carriage ride in St Moritz\n\nAustria :\n\nVisit the Swarovski Crystal\xa0Worlds\nOrientation tour of Innsbruck\n\nItaly :\nVenice :\n\nVisit St. Mark’s square on a private boat\nOrientation tour of Venice\n\nFlorence :\n\nGuided Walking Tour of Florence\n\nRome :\n\nGuided city tour of Rome\n\nVatican City :\n\nVisit the St. Peter’s Basilica and Square\n\nPisa :\n\nVisit the Field of Miracles – See the Leaning Tower of Pisa\n', 'FRANCE\n\nGuided city tour of Paris\nVisit 3rd level of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Fragonard Museum\nSeine river cruise\nIllumination tour of Paris\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\n\xa0\nBELGIUM\n\nVisit Mini Europe\nOrientation tour of Brussels\nPhoto stop at Atomuim\nVisit Beer Museum\n\nNETHERLANDS\n\nVisit Cheese farm & Wooden Shoe Factory\nEnjoy Amsterdam canal cruise\nVisit Dam Square\n\n\xa0\nGERMANY\xa0\n\nPhoto stop at the Cologne Cathedral\nEnjoy River Rhine cruise\nVisit Black Forest\nCuckoo clock demonstration\n\n\xa0\nSWITZERLAND\n\nOrientation tour of Lucerne\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\nVisit Mt. Titlis\nCable car to Flims\nScenic Rhine Gorge Train\nOrientation tour of Chur\n\n\xa0\nLEICHTENSTIEN\n\nOrientation tour of Vaduz\n\n\xa0\nAUSTRIA\n\nVisit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds\nOrientation tour of Innsbruck\n\n\xa0\nITALY\nVENICE\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 \n\nVisit St. Mark’s square on a private boat\nOrientation tour of Venice\n\nFLORENCE\xa0\xa0 \n\nGuided walking tour of Florence\n\n\xa0\nPISA\n\nVisit the Field of Miracles – See the Leaning Tower of Pisa\n\n\xa0\nROME\n\nPanoramic guided tour of Rome on an open roof bus \n\n\xa0\nVATICAN CITY\n\nVisit the St. Peter’s Basilica and Square\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0 \nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0 \nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\n\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 15 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 45 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\nAirline And Airfare\n\nThe Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July, 2026.\nAny Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers.\nPassengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves.\xa0\nFor Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents.\xa0\nPassengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To / From The Hub City At Their Own Expense.\n\n\xa0\nJoining Direct Clients\n\nMain Sector Air Tickets To Reach The First Overnight City And Last Departure City Is Not Included In The Joining Direct Package Price.\nArrival And Departure Transfers Are Not Included In The Package Price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager Shall Meet The Clients Directly At The Hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\xa0\n\nAll Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts.\xa0\nThe Hotel Room Size In Europe Would Be Up To 16 – 18 Sq. Mts.\nMost Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size.\xa0\nAs A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room.\xa0\nFor Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room.\xa0\nA Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel Rooms May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority.\xa0\nDuring Heat Wave In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms.\xa0\nDue To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As The Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City.\xa0\nIn Switzerland The Stay May Be Split In Two Hotels.\nAny Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers.\xa0\nWe Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary.\xa0\nIn Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches\xa0\n\nMost Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean.\xa0\nDue To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives.\xa0\nEating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach.\xa0\nOne Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach.\xa0\nIn Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop.\nCoaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach.\xa0\nDue To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities, As Per Eu Norms To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And On Foot.\n\nMeals\xa0\n\nMeals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible.\xa0\nOn Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nGenerally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower On Certain Days Due To Strong Wind Conditions Or Being Overcrowded Or For Security Reasons May Be Closed.\xa0\nThe Lifts At The Eiffel Tower Are Currently Closed Due To Safety. Hence The Visit To The Tower Is Only Allowed By Climbing The Staircase. In Case There Is No Change In The Same On Tour Customers Will Be Refunded The Amount For The Same If They Chose Not To Climb The Stairs.\xa0\nDue To Stringent Security Checks At The Eiffel Tower, It May Take Up To 4-5 Hours In The Queue.\nNo Refund Will Be Provided In Case The Group Is Unable To Visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level Due To Weather Conditions / Operational Closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral\xa0\n\nOn Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members.\xa0\nA Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour.\xa0\nArrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer For The Group Flight Timings.\nSecurity Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary.\xa0\nPlease Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage.\xa0\nDisabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client.\xa0\nTcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour.\xa0\nNormal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges.\xa0\nThe Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nThere Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour.\xa0\nAll Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted).\nOptional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy.\nGst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed.\xa0\nThe Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only.\xa0\nTours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange.\xa0\nPlease Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/Lucerne_267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Rome753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/StPeterBasilica753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Pisa753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/StMarkVenice.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/SwarovskiMuseumInnsbruck753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/StMoritz753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Titles753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/RhineFallsSchaffhausen753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Cologne753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Amsterdam753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Atomuim753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/EiffelTower753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Disneyland75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015085/itinerary/Paris75390.jpg']}, 'score': 6.785142, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015036', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015036', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Fusion Europe (Winter)', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Basel', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Basel', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seefeld', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Padova', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chianciano Terme', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chianciano Terme', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pisa', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014256_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 301151, 'packageSummary': "The 'Fusion Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering Paris, Basel, Pisa, Padova, Chianciano Terme, Zurich, and Seefeld. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the famous Leaning Tower of Pisa, and the historic streets of Padova, alongside scenic stops in Basel and Zurich. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing, scenic drives through the snow-capped Swiss and Austrian Alps, relaxing thermal experiences in Chianciano Terme, and exploring the charming winter wonderland of Seefeld.", 'images': ['Paris7533.jpg', 'VersaillesPalace.jpg', 'Disneyland75345.jpg', 'Switzerland7537.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'Titles753.jpg', 'SwarovskiMuseumInnsbruck753.jpg', 'PiazzaSanMarcDogePalaceVenice753.jpg', 'FlorenceandDuomo753.jpg', 'StPeterBasilica753.jpg', 'Pisa753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 301151, 'thumbnailImage': 'Rome.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015036 is named 'Fusion Europe (Winter)' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Paris! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Paris – Visit Fragonard - Guided tour of Versailles Palace– River Seine Cruise Today, we proceed on a guided tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House and Les Invalides. Next, we visit the Famous French perfume museum – Fragonard. Later, we proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, Opera Hall, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. In the evening, we take a scenic cruise on river Seine., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) - Eiffel Tower (2nd Level) – Illumination Tour Today, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris (Upto 5 hrs), where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Disneyland® Studios. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland. In the evening, we visit the Eiffel tower 2nd level and we enjoy ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights light up. Note: Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue. Due to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Basel, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Onto Scenic Switzerland Today, we enjoy a scenic drive to Switzerland. On arrival, check in to the hotel. Overnight in Basel/Central Switzerland, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Basel, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at leisure OR Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional) Today, the day is at leisure OR you can join us for a visit to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cog-wheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken. Overnight in Basel/Central Switzerland Note: Guests who do not opt for this Optional excursion will get packed dinner delivered at the hotel when the group arrives., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mt. Titlis – Orientation tour of Lucerne Today, we drive to Lucerne for an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument and Kapellbrucke. Next, we enjoy some free time to explore the town and shop for Swiss watches, knives, chocolates and souvenirs. Later, we proceed to Mt. Titlis where you will take cable car rides including the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair - to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” - a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis.” Note: On the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Seefeld, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Vaduz – Swarovski Crystal Worlds – Orientation tour of Innsbruck Today, we drive to Innsbruck. En route, visit Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz. Here you get some free time to shop at the Huber watch store Next, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens. Later, proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Padova, Meals: Breakfast,Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Venice Today, we proceed to the pier and take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs. Later, spend time to explore the city on your own. Overnight in Padova / Bologna / Ferrara, Italy., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Chianciano Terme, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided walking tour of Florence Today, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Chianciano Terme, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Rome: Guided tour of Rome and Vatican City Today we go on a day trip to Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vatican City: the smallest country in the world (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed), where we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square. Next, we continue for a guided city tour of Rome: See Circus Maximus and photo-stop at Colosseum & Arc of Constantine., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Pisa, Meals: Breakfast, Description: See Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to Pisa to see the world famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Rome instead of Milan. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 301151.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 nights at Clarion CDG / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n03 nights at Ibis style / HI Express / Prizeotel or similar in Basel/ Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Olympia / Lizumerhof / Kirchdach or similar in Seefeld, Austria.\n01 night at Four Point / Unaway / SHG / Radisson or similar in Padova/ Bologna / Ferrara, Italy.\n02 nights at Hotel Fortuna / Alexandre Palme / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee).\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n09 Indian Jain / vegetarian /non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeings: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue. There are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided. General: In case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE764', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Fusion Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering Paris, Basel, Pisa, Padova, Chianciano Terme, Zurich, and Seefeld. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the famous Leaning Tower of Pisa, and the historic streets of Padova, alongside scenic stops in Basel and Zurich. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing, scenic drives through the snow-capped Swiss and Austrian Alps, relaxing thermal experiences in Chianciano Terme, and exploring the charming winter wonderland of Seefeld.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Paris!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Clarion CDG\xa0 / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Paris – Visit Fragonard - Guided tour of Versailles Palace– River Seine Cruise\nToday, we proceed on a guided tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House and Les Invalides. Next, we visit the Famous French perfume museum – Fragonard. Later, we proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, Opera Hall, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. In the evening, we take a scenic cruise on river Seine.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Clarion CDG\xa0 / City Residence or similar in Paris\xa0(CDG Area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDisneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) - Eiffel Tower (2nd Level) – Illumination Tour\nToday, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris (Upto 5 hrs), where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Disneyland® Studios. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventureland. In the evening, we visit the Eiffel tower 2nd level and we enjoy ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights light up.\nNote:\n\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue.\nDue to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process.\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Clarion CDG\xa0 / City Residence or similar in Paris\xa0(CDG Area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Scenic Switzerland\nToday, we enjoy a scenic drive to Switzerland. On arrival, check in to the hotel.\nOvernight in Basel/Central Switzerland', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis style Basel / HI Express Basel or similar in Basel, Switzerland'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nDay at leisure OR Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional)\nToday, the day is at leisure OR you can join us for a visit to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cog-wheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken.\xa0\nOvernight in Basel/Central Switzerland\nNote: Guests who do not opt for this Optional excursion will get packed dinner delivered at the hotel when the group arrives.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis style Basel / HI Express Basel or similar in Basel,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Mt. Titlis – Orientation tour of Lucerne\nToday, we drive to Lucerne for an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument and Kapellbrucke. Next, we enjoy some free time to explore the town and shop for Swiss watches, knives, chocolates and souvenirs. Later, we proceed to Mt. Titlis where you will take cable car rides including the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair - to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” - a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis.”\nNote:\xa0\n\nOn the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis style / HI Express / Harry’s Home or similar in Zurich, Switzerland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Vaduz – Swarovski Crystal Worlds – Orientation tour of Innsbruck\nToday, we drive to Innsbruck. En route, visit Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz. Here you get some free time to shop at the Huber watch store Next, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens. Later, proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Olympia / Lizumerhof / Kirchdach or similar in Seefeld, Austria'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Venice\nToday, we proceed to the pier and take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs. Later, spend time to explore the city on your own.\xa0\nOvernight in Padova / Bologna / Ferrara, Italy.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast,Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Four Point / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova/ Bologna, Italy'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided walking tour of Florence\nToday, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Fortuna / Alexandre Palme / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nDay trip to Rome: Guided tour of Rome and Vatican City\nToday we go on a day trip to Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vatican City: the smallest country in the world (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed), where we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square. Next, we continue for a guided city tour of Rome: See Circus Maximus and photo-stop at Colosseum & Arc of Constantine.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Fortuna\xa0/ Alexandre Palme / Planet\xa0or similar in\xa0Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo,\xa0Italy'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nSee Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to Pisa to see the world famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote:\n\nDue to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Rome instead of Milan. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n03 nights at Clarion CDG / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n03 nights at Ibis style / HI Express / Prizeotel or similar in Basel/ Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Olympia / Lizumerhof / Kirchdach or similar in Seefeld, Austria.\n01 night at Four Point / Unaway / SHG / Radisson or similar in Padova/ Bologna / Ferrara, Italy.\n02 nights at Hotel Fortuna / Alexandre Palme / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n03 nights at Clarion CDG / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n03 nights at Ibis style / HI Express / Prizeotel or similar in Basel/ Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Olympia / Lizumerhof / Kirchdach or similar in Seefeld, Austria.\n01 night at Four Point / Unaway / SHG / Radisson or similar in Padova/ Bologna / Ferrara, Italy.\n02 nights at Hotel Fortuna / Alexandre Palme / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IT', 'countryName': 'Italy', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'VA', 'countryName': 'Vatican City', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'LCH', 'countryName': 'Liechtenstein', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 301200.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at Clarion CDG / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\n03 nights at Ibis style / HI Express / Prizeotel or similar in Basel/ Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Olympia / Lizumerhof / Kirchdach or similar in Seefeld, Austria.\n01 night at Four Point / Unaway / SHG / Radisson or similar in Padova/ Bologna / Ferrara, Italy.\n02 nights at Hotel Fortuna / Alexandre Palme / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee).\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n09 Indian Jain / vegetarian /non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\xa0\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0 \n\n\xa0'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', 'France\n\nGuided City Tour Of Paris\nGuided Tour Of Versailles Palace\nVisit 2nd Level Of Eiffel Tower\xa0\nVisit Fragonard – French Perfume Museum\nEnjoy Illumination Tour Of Paris\nSeine River Cruise\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\nSwitzerland\n\nVisit Mt. Titlis\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Lucerne\nChance to visit to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional)\xa0\n\n\xa0\nLiechtenstein\xa0\n\nOrientation Tour Of Vaduz\n\n\xa0\nAustria\n\nOrientation Tour Of Innsbruck\nVisit The Swarovski Crystal Worlds\n\nItaly\nVenice\n\nVisit St. Mark’s Square On A Private Boat\nOrientation Tour Of Venice\n\n\xa0\nFlorence \n\nGuided Walking Tour Of Florence\n\nRome\n\nGuided City Tour Of Rome\n\nVatican City\n\nVisit St. Peter’s Basilica And Square\n\nPisa\n\nVisit Field Of Miracles - See The Leaning Tower Of Pisa\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0 \nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0 \nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021.\xa0 Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\xa0\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot.\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain Days packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeings:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue.\nThere are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided.\n\nGeneral:\n\nIn case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses\xa0 to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”.\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/Rome.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/Paris7533.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/VersaillesPalace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/Disneyland75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/Switzerland7537.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/Titles753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/SwarovskiMuseumInnsbruck753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/PiazzaSanMarcDogePalaceVenice753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/FlorenceandDuomo753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/StPeterBasilica753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015036/itinerary/Pisa753.jpg']}, 'score': 6.785142, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015055', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015055', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026'], 'packageName': 'Enchanting East Europe (Winter)', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Berlin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Berlin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Krakow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Krakow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Beer tasting at the Brewery Local lunch at Hungarian Horsemanship Show Knight tournament in Visegard Local Lunch at the Renaissance restaurant in Visegrad'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 326235, 'packageSummary': "The 'Enchanting East Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering the historic and scenic cities of Budapest, Vienna, Prague, Krakow, and Berlin. Throughout this winter journey, participants will enjoy unique cultural and culinary experiences, including a beer tasting at a local brewery, a traditional lunch at a Hungarian Horsemanship Show, and an exciting knight tournament in Visegrad paired with a local lunch at the Renaissance restaurant.", 'images': ['brandenburg-gate.jpg', 'Berlinwall.jpg', 'wawelKrakow.jpg', 'Wieliczka_salt_mine_Krakow_753.jpg', 'PragueCityPrague.jpg', 'PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'Cesky_Crumlov_753.jpg', 'SchonbrunnPalace1.jpg', 'ChainBridgeHungary.jpg', 'DanubeCruise.jpg', 'budapest1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 326235, 'thumbnailImage': 'BrandenburgGate.bmp', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015055 is named 'Enchanting East Europe (Winter)' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Berlin, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Berlin! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Berlin, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Potsdam - Entrance to Sanssouci Gardens - Guided tour of Berlin – Visit Topography of Terror Museum Today, we proceed for a guided tour of Potsdam with entrance to Sanssouci Gardens. We also take a Photo stop at Glienicke - Bridge of Spies. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Berlin: Visit the Berlin tower, See the famous Berlin Wall, the Reichstag, visit the Alexander Platz, where you will see the World Time Clock. Later, we visit the Topography of Terror, an indoor and open air museum where between 1933 and 1945 the principal instruments of Nazi persecution and terror were located., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Krakow, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Proceed to Krakow – Horse Carriage ride Today, we drive to Krakow. Upon arrival, we proceed for a Horse Carriage ride in the old town., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Krakow, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Auschwitz Concentration Camp - Wieliczka Salt mines Today we proceed for a guided tour of the Auschwitz Concentration Camp of WW II. A sombre experience that highlights the atrocities that occurred here between 1939 - 1945. Later we visit to Wieliczka Salt mines - one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Brewery with beer tasting - Onto Prague Today, we proceed to Brno and visit a local brewery to taste their famous beers. We also spend some free time in the city. Next, we drive to Prague., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane Today, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided Walking tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Vienna Today we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. We also see the Church of St Vitus & the clock bridge. Next, we proceed to Vienna. Upon arrival, we have some free time for shopping at the Swarovski outlet (Subject to time permitting), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Vienna – Visit the glorious Schonbrunn Palace – Orientation city tour of Bratislava Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, Parliament building, Hofburg Palace and many more interesting monuments. Next, we visit the famous Schonbrunn Palace - a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site and experience the grand tour. Later we proceed to Bratislava for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Later, we drive to Budapest., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Budapest – Hungarian Horsemanship show Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Budapest: Visit the Citadel, Fisherman’s Bastion Heroes Square, see the Chain Bridge that connects the cities of Buda and Pest. Next, we proceed to enjoy a show of Hungarian Horsemanship., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: See the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre – Farewell dinner on Danube River Cruise Today, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes. In the evening, we enjoy a farewell dinner on board the Danube River Cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 326235.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 night at Courtyard by Marriott Berlin City Centre/ Berlin Berlin/ AC by Hilton Berlin similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at International Royal Prague / Courtyard by Marriott Prague airport or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n02 night at Q+ Krakow / Novotel / Swing or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n01 night at Double Tree by Hilton / Austria Trend / Event Hotel Pyramide / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Park Inn / Novotel / Danubius / Holiday Inn Budaors or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n, \n02 night at Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at Hotel Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n02 night at Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n01 night at Senator / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Intercity / Danubius or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non-vegetarian lunches.\n02 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non vegetarian lunches.\n03 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline And Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Joining Direct Clients: Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. No refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Beer tasting at the Brewery Local lunch at Hungarian Horsemanship Show Knight tournament in Visegard Local Lunch at the Renaissance restaurant in Visegrad.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE218', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Enchanting East Europe (Winter)' package is an 11-day tour covering the historic and scenic cities of Budapest, Vienna, Prague, Krakow, and Berlin. Throughout this winter journey, participants will enjoy unique cultural and culinary experiences, including a beer tasting at a local brewery, a traditional lunch at a Hungarian Horsemanship Show, and an exciting knight tournament in Visegrad paired with a local lunch at the Renaissance restaurant.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Berlin!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport or\xa0 similar in Berlin, Germany'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Potsdam - Entrance to Sanssouci Gardens - Guided tour of Berlin – Visit Topography of Terror Museum\nToday, we proceed for a guided tour of Potsdam with entrance to Sanssouci Gardens. We also take a Photo stop at Glienicke - Bridge of Spies. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Berlin: Visit the Berlin tower, See the famous Berlin Wall, the Reichstag, visit the Alexander Platz, where you will see the World Time Clock. Later, we visit the Topography of Terror, an indoor and open air museum where between 1933 and 1945 the principal instruments of Nazi persecution and terror were located.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport or\xa0 similar in Berlin,\xa0Germany'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nProceed to Krakow – Horse Carriage ride\nToday, we drive to Krakow. Upon arrival, we proceed for a Horse Carriage ride in the old town.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum\xa0or similar in Krakow, Poland'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nAuschwitz Concentration Camp - Wieliczka Salt mines\nToday we proceed for a guided tour of the Auschwitz Concentration Camp of WW II. A sombre experience that highlights the atrocities that occurred here between 1939 - 1945. Later we visit to Wieliczka Salt mines - one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum\xa0or similar in\xa0Krakow,\xa0Poland'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Brewery with beer tasting - Onto Prague\nToday, we proceed to Brno and visit a local brewery to taste their famous beers. We also spend some free time in the city. Next, we drive to Prague.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague\xa0\xa0or similar in Prague, Czech Republic'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane\nToday, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague\xa0\xa0or similar in\xa0Prague,\xa0Czech Republic'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided Walking tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Vienna\nToday we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. We also see the Church of St Vitus & the clock bridge. Next, we proceed to Vienna. Upon arrival, we have some free time for shopping at the Swarovski outlet (Subject to time permitting)', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel\xa0Senator / Holiday Inn\xa0or similar in Vienna, Austria'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Vienna – Visit the glorious Schonbrunn Palace – Orientation city tour of Bratislava\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, Parliament building, Hofburg Palace and many more interesting monuments. Next, we visit the famous Schonbrunn Palace - a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site and experience the grand tour. Later we proceed to Bratislava for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Later, we drive to Budapest.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Intercity / Danubius\xa0or similar in Budapest, Hungary'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Budapest – Hungarian Horsemanship show\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Budapest: Visit the Citadel, Fisherman’s Bastion Heroes Square, see the Chain Bridge that connects the cities of Buda and Pest. Next, we proceed to enjoy a show of Hungarian Horsemanship.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Intercity / Danubius\xa0or similar in Budapest,\xa0Hungary'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nSee the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre – Farewell dinner on Danube River Cruise\nToday, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes. In the evening, we enjoy a farewell dinner on board the Danube River Cruise.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Intercity / Danubius\xa0or similar in Budapest,\xa0Hungary'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 night at Courtyard by Marriott Berlin City Centre/ Berlin Berlin/ AC by Hilton Berlin similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at International Royal Prague / Courtyard by Marriott Prague airport or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n02 night at Q+ Krakow / Novotel / Swing or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n01 night at Double Tree by Hilton / Austria Trend / Event Hotel Pyramide / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Park Inn / Novotel / Danubius / Holiday Inn Budaors or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n', '\n02 night at Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at Hotel Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n02 night at Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n01 night at Senator / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Intercity / Danubius or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n02 night at Courtyard by Marriott Berlin City Centre/ Berlin Berlin/ AC by Hilton Berlin similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at International Royal Prague / Courtyard by Marriott Prague airport or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n02 night at Q+ Krakow / Novotel / Swing or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n01 night at Double Tree by Hilton / Austria Trend / Event Hotel Pyramide / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Park Inn / Novotel / Danubius / Holiday Inn Budaors or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n', '2': '\n02 night at Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at Hotel Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n02 night at Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n01 night at Senator / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Intercity / Danubius or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DE', 'countryName': 'Germany', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CZ', 'countryName': 'Czech Republic', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'HU', 'countryName': 'Hungary', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SK', 'countryName': 'Slovakia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'PL', 'countryName': 'Poland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 326200.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 night at Intercity Airport North/Holiday Inn Airport similar in Berlin, Germany.\n02 night at Hotel Conrad Comfort/Hotel Centrum/Novotel City West/Hotel Centrum or similar in Krakow, Poland.\n02 night at Clarion Congress/Hotel Occidental Prague or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n01 night at Senator / Holiday Inn or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n03 night at Intercity / Danubius or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non-vegetarian lunches.\n02 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non vegetarian lunches.\n03 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-\xa0conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['GERMANY\nBerlin:\n\nGuided city tour\xa0\nEntrance to Topography of Terror Museum\n\nDresden:\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nPrague:\n\nGuided city tour\nEntrance to the Prague Castle\xa0\nVisit St. Vitus Cathedral\xa0\nGolden Lane\nHistoric Tram Experience\nVisit Brewery with beer tasting\n\nPOLAND\nKrakow:\n\nHorse Carriage ride\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Wieliczka Salt mines\nAuschwitz concentration camp\n\nAUSTRIA\nVienna: \n\nGuided city tour\nVisit Schonbrunn Palace\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSLOVAKIA\nBratislava:\n\nOrientation city tour\n\n\xa0\nHUNGARY\nVisegrad:\n\nVisit Visegrad castle\nSee the Knight tournament\xa0\n\n\xa0\nBudapest:\n\nGuided city tour\nHungarian Horsemanship show\nEnjoy the Danube river cruise\n', 'GERMANY\nBerlin:\n\nGuided city tour of Berlin\nEntrance to Topography of Terror Museum\nVisit Berlin Tower\n\n\xa0\nPotsdam:\n\nGuided Tour of Potsdam\nEntrance to Sanssouci Gardens\n\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nPrague: \n\nGuided city tour\nEntrance to the Prague Castle\xa0\nVisit St. Vitus Cathedral\xa0\nGolden Lane\xa0\n\nBrno:\n\nVisit brewery with beer tasting\n\nCesky Crumlov:\n\nGuided Walking tour\n\n\xa0\nPOLAND\nKrakow:\n\nVisit Wieliczka Salt mines\nAuschwitz concentration camp\nHorse Carraige Ride\n\n\xa0\nWroclaw\n\nOrientation city tour of Wroclaw\n\nAUSTRIA\nVienna:\n\nGuided city tour\nVisit Schonbrunn Palace\n\n\xa0\nSLOVAKIA\nBratislava \n\nOrientation city tour\n\nHUNGARY\nVisegrad\n\nVisit Visegrad castle\nSee the Knight tournament\n\nBudapest:\n\nGuided city tour\nHungarian Horsemanship show\nEnjoy the Danube river cruise\nVisit Szentendre\n\nEsztergom\n\nSee the Basilica Esztergom\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\nAirline And Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nJoining Direct Clients:\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches\xa0\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\n\nMeals:\xa0\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing:\xa0\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/BrandenburgGate.bmp', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/brandenburg-gate.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/Berlinwall.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/wawelKrakow.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/Wieliczka_salt_mine_Krakow_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/PragueCityPrague.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/Cesky_Crumlov_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/SchonbrunnPalace1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/ChainBridgeHungary.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/DanubeCruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015055/itinerary/budapest1.jpg']}, 'score': 6.2883325, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015020', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015020', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Europe For All (Winter)', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015020_0_20260901183227', 'price': 230731, 'packageSummary': "The 'Europe For All (Winter)' package is an 8-day tour covering Zurich, Paris, and Eindhoven. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre Museum, and the scenic shores of Lake Zurich, alongside exploring the modern charm of Eindhoven. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing, a romantic cruise along the Seine River, and opportunities to experience local winter markets, Swiss chocolate tastings, and vibrant cultural highlights across these beautiful European destinations.", 'images': ['Zurich753.jpg', 'Titles753.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'Paris7536.jpg', 'Paris7533.jpg', 'Atomuim753.jpg', 'RoyalPalace753.jpg', 'Amsterdam7531.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 230731, 'thumbnailImage': 'Lucerne26778.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015020 is named 'Europe For All (Winter)' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Zurich, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Zurich! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Mt. Titlis – Orientation Tour of Lucerne Today, we proceed to Mt Titlis where you will take cable car rides including the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair - to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” - a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis.” Next, we proceed for an Orientation Tour of Lucerne: See the Lion Monument, Kapellbrucke. Also, enjoy some free time to explore the town and shop for Swiss knives, Chocolates and Souvenirs. Note: On the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at leisure OR Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional) Today, the day is at leisure OR you can join us for a visit to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cog wheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken. Note: Guests who do not opt for this Optional excursion will get packed dinner delivered at the hotel when the group arrives., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Onto Paris Today, we take a scenic drive to Paris. Upon arrival we check in to the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Paris - Eiffel Tower (2nd Level) – Visit Fragonard - Seine River Cruise with Illumination Tour of Paris (Optional) Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Les Invalides and Champs Elysees. Next, we visit the Eiffel Tower (2nd level). Later we visit Fragonard Museum and learn the art of Perfume making. The evening is at leisure, or you can enjoy an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ on Seine River Cruise and see Paris by night, with some of the City’s famous monuments / sights lit up (Optional). Note: Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue. Due to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Brussels – Photo stop at Atomium Today, we drive to Brussels, and we proceed for an orientation tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with free time in the city. Later we take a photo stop at Atomium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Till 17th March: Visit Madurodam - Visit Wooden shoe and Cheese farm Factory – Orientation City Tour of Amsterdam Today, we proceed to Madurodam: Holland in Miniature. Next, we proceed to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, we proceed for an orientation city tour of Amsterdam: See the Royal Palace, Nieuwmarkt. In the evening, we have some free time at Dam Square. Or From 18th March: Keukenhof - Visit Wooden shoe and Cheese farm Factory – Orientation City Tour of Amsterdam Today, we proceed to Keukenhof – the largest spring garden in the world. Next, we proceed to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, we proceed for an orientation city tour of Amsterdam: See the Royal Palace, Nieuwmarkt. In the evening, we have some free time at Dam Square., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with Pleasant Memories! Today, we proceed to Amsterdam Airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. OPTIONAL TOUR ADULT (EUR) CHILD (EUR) Visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken 180 130 Seine River Cruise with Illumination tour of Paris 50 50, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 230731.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 nights at BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch/ Prizeotel or similar in Switzerland.\n02 nights at Moxy / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area), France.\n01 night at B&B / Ibis or similar in Brussels, Belgium.\n01 night at Fletcher / Twenty Three / Best Western or similar in Rotterdam / Eindhoven / Amsterdam (Airport Area), Netherlands.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 08 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 24 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026. Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Airline and Airfare The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Joining Direct Clients Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. Hotels All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. No refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures. General On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE157', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Europe For All (Winter)' package is an 8-day tour covering Zurich, Paris, and Eindhoven. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre Museum, and the scenic shores of Lake Zurich, alongside exploring the modern charm of Eindhoven. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing, a romantic cruise along the Seine River, and opportunities to experience local winter markets, Swiss chocolate tastings, and vibrant cultural highlights across these beautiful European destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Zurich!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Zurich Airport/BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Zurich, Switzerland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Mt. Titlis – Orientation Tour of Lucerne\nToday, we proceed to Mt Titlis where you will take cable car rides including the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair - to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” - a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis.” Next, we proceed for an Orientation Tour of Lucerne:\xa0 See the Lion Monument, Kapellbrucke. Also, enjoy some free time to explore the town and shop for Swiss knives, Chocolates and Souvenirs.\nNote:\xa0On the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Zurich Airport/BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Zurich,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDay at leisure OR Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken (Optional)\nToday, the day is at leisure OR you can join us for a visit to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cog wheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken.\xa0 \nNote: Guests who do not opt for this Optional excursion will get packed dinner delivered at the hotel when the group arrives.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Zurich Airport/BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Zurich,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Paris\nToday, we take a scenic drive to Paris. Upon arrival we check in to the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Moxy CDG / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Paris - Eiffel Tower (2nd Level) – Visit Fragonard - Seine River Cruise with Illumination Tour of Paris (Optional)\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Les Invalides and Champs Elysees. Next, we visit the Eiffel Tower (2nd level). Later we visit Fragonard Museum and learn the art of Perfume making. The evening is at leisure, or you can enjoy an ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ on Seine River Cruise and see Paris by night, with some of the City’s famous monuments / sights lit up (Optional).\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue.\nDue to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Moxy CDG / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Brussels – Photo stop at Atomium\nToday, we drive to Brussels, and we proceed for an orientation tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with free time in the city. Later we take a photo stop at Atomium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0NH / Best Western or similar in Eindhoven,\xa0Netherlands'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nTill 17th March:\xa0 Visit Madurodam - Visit Wooden shoe and Cheese farm Factory – Orientation City Tour of Amsterdam\nToday, we proceed to Madurodam: Holland in Miniature. Next, we proceed to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, we proceed for an orientation city tour of Amsterdam:\xa0 See the Royal Palace, Nieuwmarkt. In the evening, we have some free time at Dam Square.\nOr\n\xa0\nFrom 18th March:\xa0 Keukenhof - Visit Wooden shoe and Cheese farm Factory – Orientation City Tour of Amsterdam\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Keukenhof – the largest spring garden in the world. Next, we proceed to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, we proceed for an orientation city tour of Amsterdam:\xa0 See the Royal Palace, Nieuwmarkt. In the evening, we have some free time at Dam Square.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0NH / Best Western or similar in Eindhoven,\xa0Netherlands'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with Pleasant Memories!\nToday, we proceed to Amsterdam Airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nOPTIONAL TOUR\n\n\nADULT  (EUR)\n\n\nCHILD  (EUR)\n\n\n\n\nVisit Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\n\n\n180\n\n\n130\n\n\n\n\nSeine River Cruise with Illumination tour of Paris \n\n\n50\n\n\n50\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch/ Prizeotel or similar in Switzerland.\n02 nights at Moxy / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area), France.\n01 night at B&B / Ibis or similar in Brussels, Belgium.\n01 night at Fletcher / Twenty Three / Best Western or similar in Rotterdam / Eindhoven / Amsterdam (Airport Area), Netherlands.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n03 nights at BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch/ Prizeotel or similar in Switzerland.\n02 nights at Moxy / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area), France.\n01 night at B&B / Ibis or similar in Brussels, Belgium.\n01 night at Fletcher / Twenty Three / Best Western or similar in Rotterdam / Eindhoven / Amsterdam (Airport Area), Netherlands.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NL', 'countryName': 'Netherlands', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'BE', 'countryName': 'Belgium', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 230700.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch/ Prizeotel or similar in Switzerland.\n02 nights at Moxy / ACE / Ibis or similar in Paris (CDG area), France.\n01 night at B&B / Ibis or similar in Brussels, Belgium.\n01 night at Fletcher / Twenty Three / Best Western or similar in Rotterdam / Eindhoven / Amsterdam (Airport Area), Netherlands.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0 \n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Switzerland\n\nVisit Mt. Titlis\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Lucerne\n\nFrance\n\nGuided City Tour Of Paris\nVisit 2nd Level Of Eiffel Tower\xa0\nVisit Fragonard\n\nBelgium\n\nOrientation Tour Of Brussels\nPhoto Stop At Atomium\n\nNetherlands\n\nVisit Madurodam (Till 17th March)\nVisit Keukenhof (from 18th March)\nOrientation tour of Amsterdam\nVisit Cheese Farm And Wooden Shoe Factory\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory.</p>\n<p>(Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)&nbsp;</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0 \nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 08 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 24 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026.\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nAirline and Airfare\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJoining Direct Clients\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. \n\n\xa0\nCoaches\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. \n\n\xa0\nMeals\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. \n\n\xa0\nSightseeing\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/Lucerne26778.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Zurich753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Titles753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Paris7536.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Paris7533.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Atomuim753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/RoyalPalace753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015020/itinerary/Amsterdam7531.jpg']}, 'score': 6.2883325, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013070', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013070', 'availableMonths': ['march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of East Europe (Winter)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Krakow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Krakow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 250653, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of East Europe (Winter)' package is a 9-day tour covering Prague, Krakow, Baku, Budapest, and Vienna. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Prague Castle, the medieval Old Town of Krakow, the modern Flame Towers of Baku, the grand Parliament Building in Budapest, and the imperial palaces of Vienna. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, exploring vibrant winter markets, and experiencing the rich cultural heritage and scenic beauty of these diverse destinations.", 'images': ['Krakow00.jpg', 'Krakow02.jpg', 'Budapest00.avif', 'Budapest033.jpg', 'Budapest78.jpg', 'Vienna123.jpg', 'Prague_jp.jpg', 'Prague000.jpg', 'Prague_2jp.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 250653, 'thumbnailImage': 'PragueCastle26789.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG013070 is named 'Highlights Of East Europe (Winter)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Krakow, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Krakow The Tour Manager or Station Manager will meet you outside the airport. Proceed for dinner and then to the hotel and check in., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Krakow, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Krakow and Wieliczka Salt Mines Proceed for a guided tour of Krakow where we see the UNESCO listed Old Town Wawel Castle the historic Jewish Quarter and nearby poignant memorials. Later visit the Wieliczka Salt Mines one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Budapest – Danube River Cruise Today, we drive towards Budapest. Upon arrival, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the Danube river which offers spectacular, illuminated views of the UNESCO World Heritage listed riverfront, including the Hungarian Parliament Building and Buda Castle., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Budapest – Shopping at Vaci Utca Today proceed for a Guided tour of Budapest: See the equestrian statue of St. Stephen and experience the domination of the seven turrets at Fisherman’s Bastion, visit the Heroes Square and see more interesting sights. Later we have free time for shopping at Vaci Utca., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: See the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre Today, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Bratislava – Guided City Tour of Vienna Today we drive towards Bratislava. Upon arrival, we proceed for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Next we proceed to Vienna for a Guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, St. Stephen’s Church and many more interesting monuments of this beautiful city., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Prague Today we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. Later, we drive to Prague – the city of hundred spires, built at the meandering Vltava River., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane Today, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Baku, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity, a few groups may depart out of Vienna instead of Prague. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 250653.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n2 nights at Ibis Styles/ Q Hotel in Krakow, Poland.\n3 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n, \n2 nights in Krakow, Poland (Ibis Styles / Q Hotel)\n3 nights in Budapest, Hungary (Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar)\n1 night in Vienna, Austria (Senator / B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar)\n2 nights in Prague, Czech Republic (Hotel Duo / Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar)\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental breakfast (bread, butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, coffee)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners\n01 local lunch\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners\nNote:\xa0Packed meals if applicable will be Jain / vegetarian\n, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non-vegetarian lunches.\n02 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per itinerary All local taxes and services as of 1st July 2026 Cost of visa and medical insurance for tour duration Sightseeing and accommodation as per itinerary All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified) by deluxe air conditioned coach Services of a professional multilingual Tour Manager or local representative (subject to minimum 15 customers) Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 09 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: AIRLINE AND AIRFAREThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. HOTELS All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 - 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. COACHES Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. MEALS Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. SIGHTSEEING On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. GENERAL On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE803', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of East Europe (Winter)' package is a 9-day tour covering Prague, Krakow, Baku, Budapest, and Vienna. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Prague Castle, the medieval Old Town of Krakow, the modern Flame Towers of Baku, the grand Parliament Building in Budapest, and the imperial palaces of Vienna. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, exploring vibrant winter markets, and experiencing the rich cultural heritage and scenic beauty of these diverse destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Krakow\xa0\xa0\nThe Tour Manager or Station Manager will meet you outside the airport. Proceed for dinner and then to the hotel and check in.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Styles/ Q Hotel or similar in Krakow, Poland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Krakow and Wieliczka Salt Mines\xa0\nProceed for a guided tour of Krakow where we see the UNESCO listed Old Town Wawel Castle the historic Jewish Quarter and nearby poignant memorials. Later visit the Wieliczka Salt Mines one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Styles/ Q Hotel or similar in Krakow, Poland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Budapest – Danube River Cruise\xa0\nToday, we drive towards Budapest. Upon arrival, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the Danube river which offers spectacular, illuminated views of the UNESCO World Heritage listed riverfront, including the Hungarian Parliament Building and Buda Castle.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Budapest – Shopping at Vaci Utca\nToday proceed for a Guided tour of Budapest: See the equestrian statue of St. Stephen and experience the domination of the seven turrets at Fisherman’s Bastion, visit the Heroes Square and see more interesting sights. Later we have free time for shopping at Vaci Utca.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nSee the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Bratislava – Guided City Tour of Vienna\nToday we drive towards Bratislava. Upon arrival, we proceed for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Next we proceed to Vienna for a Guided city tour of Vienna:\xa0 See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, St. Stephen’s Church and many more interesting monuments of this beautiful city.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Prague\nToday we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. Later, we drive to Prague – the city of hundred spires, built at the meandering Vltava River.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane\xa0\nToday, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nProceed to the airport for your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nDue to flight connectivity, a few groups may depart out of Vienna instead of Prague. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights at Ibis Styles/ Q Hotel in Krakow, Poland.\n3 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n', '\n2 nights in Krakow, Poland (Ibis Styles / Q Hotel)\n3 nights in Budapest, Hungary (Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar)\n1 night in Vienna, Austria (Senator / B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar)\n2 nights in Prague, Czech Republic (Hotel Duo / Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar)\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n2 nights at Ibis Styles/ Q Hotel in Krakow, Poland.\n3 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n', '1': '\n2 nights in Krakow, Poland (Ibis Styles / Q Hotel)\n3 nights in Budapest, Hungary (Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar)\n1 night in Vienna, Austria (Senator / B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar)\n2 nights in Prague, Czech Republic (Hotel Duo / Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar)\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CZ', 'countryName': 'Czech Republic', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'HU', 'countryName': 'Hungary', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'PL', 'countryName': 'Poland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SK', 'countryName': 'Slovakia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AZ', 'countryName': 'Azerbaijan', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 250700.0, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights in Krakow, Poland (Ibis Styles / Q Hotel)\n3 nights in Budapest, Hungary (Hotel Amadeus / Lifehotel / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar)\n1 night in Vienna, Austria (Senator / B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar)\n2 nights in Prague, Czech Republic (Hotel Duo / Ibis Praha / Zleep / Olympik or similar)\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental breakfast (bread, butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, coffee)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners\n01 local lunch\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners\nNote:\xa0Packed meals if applicable will be Jain / vegetarian\n', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfasts. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, tea, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits).\n07 Indian Jain / vegetarian/ non-vegetarian lunches.\n02 Local Lunches.\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n'], 'visa': ['Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nDeluxe air conditioned coach for transfers and excursions\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Poland\nKrakow \n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\nVisit Wieliczka Salt Mines\n\n\xa0\nHungary\nBudapest \n\nGuided City Tour\nDanube River Cruise\xa0\nSee The Basilica Esztergom\xa0\nVisit Szentendre\n\n\xa0\nVisegrad\n\nVisit Visegrad Castle\nSee The Knight Tournament\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSlovakia\nBratislava\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\xa0\n\nOrientation Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nAustria\nVienna \n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nCesky Krumlov\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCzech Republic\nPrague \n\nGuided City Tour\nEntrance To The Prague Castle\xa0\nVisit St. Vitus Cathedral\xa0\nGolden Lane\n', 'GERMANY\nBerlin:\n\nGuided city tour\xa0\nEntrance to Topography of Terror Museum\n\nDresden:\n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nPrague: \n\nGuided city tour\nEntrance to the Prague Castle\xa0\nVisit St. Vitus Cathedral\xa0\nGolden Lane\nHistoric Tram Experience\nVisit Brewery with beer tasting\n\nPOLAND\nKrakow: \n\nHorse Carriage ride\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Wieliczka Salt mines\nAuschwitz concentration camp\n\n\xa0\nAUSTRIA\nVienna:\n\nGuided city tour\nVisit Schonbrunn Palace\xa0\n\nSLOVAKIA\nBratislava \n\nOrientation city tour\n\nHUNGARY\nVisegrad\n\nVisit Visegrad castle\nSee the Knight tournament\n\nBudapest:\n\nGuided city tour\nHungarian Horsemanship show\nEnjoy the Danube river cruise\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per itinerary\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July 2026\nCost of visa and medical insurance for tour duration\nSightseeing and accommodation as per itinerary\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified) by deluxe air conditioned coach\nServices of a professional multilingual Tour Manager or local representative (subject to minimum 15 customers)\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.\xa0 \xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 09 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'IMPORTANT NOTES:\n\xa0AIRLINE AND AIRFAREThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. \nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. \nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\xa0\nHOTELS \nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. \nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 - 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. \nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. \nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. \nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. \nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. \nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. \nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. \nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. \nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. \nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. \nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. \nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. \n\xa0\nCOACHES \nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. \nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. \nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. \nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. \nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. \nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. \n\xa0\nMEALS \nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. \nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. \n\xa0\nSIGHTSEEING \nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. \nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. \nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. \nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. \nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\n\xa0\nGENERAL \nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. \nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. \nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. \nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. \nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. \nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. \nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. \nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. \nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. \nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. \nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0\xa0 \nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. \nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. \nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. \nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/PragueCastle26789.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Krakow00.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Krakow02.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Budapest00.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Budapest033.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Budapest78.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Vienna123.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Prague_jp.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Prague000.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013070/itinerary/Prague_2jp.jpg']}, 'score': 5.875377, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014932', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014932', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'East Europe - Private Journeys (Winter)', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014932_0_20260910115457.pdf', 'price': 367303, 'packageSummary': "The 'East Europe - Private Journeys (Winter)' package is an 8-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Budapest, Vienna, and Prague. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the majestic Buda Castle, the grand Schönbrunn Palace, and the historic Prague Castle. Participants will enjoy private guided city tours, scenic walks through festive winter markets, and opportunities to explore charming old towns and stunning architectural marvels across these three beautiful capitals.", 'images': ['Prague-Castle.jpg', 'VLTAVA_RIVER2_C.jpg', 'vienna-city.jpg', 'SchonbrunnPalace.jpg', 'Vienna.jpg', 'Budapest-Hungary.jpg', 'Budapest-Danube-Cruise-.jpg', 'Budapest.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 367303, 'thumbnailImage': 'Krumlov_SRP.png', 'packageTheme': ['Private Journeys'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014932 is named 'East Europe - Private Journeys (Winter)' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Prague, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Prague, Czech Republic Transfers: Upon your arrival at Prague International Airport, you will have a private transfer to the hotel. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vltava River Cruise & Prague Castle Entrance Ticket Prague Castle Tour: Today you will visit Prague Castle’s spectacular beauty. The world’s largest castle complex crowns the city’s skyline. Explore its courtyards, Old Royal Palace, St. Vitus Cathedral, St. George’s Basilica, and stroll the charming Golden Lane. Vltava River Cruise: Enjoy Prague on a one-hour Vltava River cruise through the historic center. Continue by air conditioned boat with guided views of Prague Castle, St. Vitus Cathedral, Charles Bridge, and the National Theatre. Special Note: There will be Vehicle at disposal for 10 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague To Vienna - Enroute Cesky Krumlov Transfers: Travel from Prague to Vienna on private basis. Enroute Cesky Krumlov: Enjoy enroute trip to the fairy tale town of Cesky Krumlov, a UNESCO World Heritage site in Southern Bohemia. Discover its medieval streets, historic houses, scenic Vltava views, and grand castle with baroque gardens and a unique rotating auditorium theatre. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion Vehicle will be at disposal for 10 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna – Visit Schonbrunn Palace Panoramic drive through the city of Vienna (Optional): Enjoy a panoramic drive through Vienna with free time to explore. Your driver guide highlights key sights along the Ringstrasse, including the State Opera, Hofburg, Parliament, Museums Quarter, Belvedere Palace, and other grand landmarks. Schonbrunn Palace Tour (Audio Guide): Schonbrunn Palace, a Baroque masterpiece in Vienna, rose to prominence under Maria Theresa as the center of court life. Today, this UNESCO World Heritage Site is one of the city’s most popular historical attractions, famed for its palace and gardens. Special Note: Vehicle will be at disposal for 10 hrs. Entrance to Schonbrunn Palace will be with Imperial Ticket., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna: Visit To Salzburg Day trip to Salzburg: Explore Salzburg on a day trip from Vienna, visiting Mirabell Gardens and the UNESCO listed Old Town. Enjoy Alpine scenery, lakes, and “Sound of Music” sites, with free time for lunch, shopping, or visiting Mozart's Museum and Hohensalzburg Fortress. Special Note: Vehicle will be at disposal for 10 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna To Budapest - Enroute Bratislava Transfers: Travel from Vienna to Budapest enroute Bratislava on private basis. Enroute Visit to Bratislava: Just an hour from Vienna, discover Bratislava, one of Europe’s smallest capitals. Explore its colorful Old Town, lively cafés, modern skyline, and hilltop castle. Enjoy free time before continuing on to Budapest. Danube on a Boat Cruise: Enjoy a Danube River cruise through Budapest, dividing hilly Buda from lively Pest. Admire UNESCO listed waterfront landmarks including Chain Bridge, Buda Castle, Parliament, Matthias Church, and Margaret Island. Special Note: Vehicle will be at disposal for 10 hrs. Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Trip To Danube Bend & Szentendre Day Trip to Danube Bend & Szentendre: Experience the Danube Bend on a private drive north of Budapest. Visit charming Szentendre with its old town and cafés, then explore medieval Visegrád Castle, enjoying scenic river views and included admission as you discover Hungary’s history and landscapes. Special Note: Vehicle will be at disposal for 10 hrs. Danube Boat Cruise Included, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Budapest Transfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. STANDARD Travel Validity from 1 JULY – 31 OCTOBER 2026 NOTE: ADULT & CHILD COSTING WILL BE THE SAME FOR PRIVATE JOURNEYS Package Cost on 3* (Standard) Hotels: Based on Per Person Per Slab Starting From 8 – 9 Guests 10 – 11 Guests 12 Guests € 1,710 + INR 2250 € 1,510 + INR 2250 € 1,340 + INR 2250 VALUE Travel Validity from 1 JULY – 31 OCTOBER 2026 NOTE: ADULT & CHILD COSTING WILL BE THE SAME FOR PRIVATE JOURNEYS Package Cost on 4* (Value) Hotels: Based on Per Person Per Slab Starting From 8 – 9 Guests 10 – 11 Guests 12 Guests € 2,055 + INR 2250 € 1,790 + INR 2250 € 1,675 + INR 2250, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 367303.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza /\xa0 Galileo Hotel /\xa0 Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel / Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nPrague\xa0\n\n\nHotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\xa0\n\n\nHotel\xa0Zeitgeist\xa0Vienna,\xa0Mercure\xa0Wien\xa0Westbahnhof,\xa0Mercure\xa0Wien\xa0City\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\xa0\n\n\nRoyal\xa0Park\xa0Boutique\xa0Hotel\xa0/\xa0\xa0Corvin\xa0Center\xa0Suites\xa0/\xa0City\xa0Inn\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Prague based on the hotel category selected or similar 3 Nights’ accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Budapest based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transfers: [Includes Point to Point Transfer with limited waiting hours] Arrival Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel on private basis Departure transfer from Budapest Hotel to Budapest Airport Vehicle at disposal for 10 hrs. as mentioned in the itinerary Sightseeing: [Tour timing will have to be decided at the time of booking] Prague Vltava River cruise ticket Prague castle entrance ticket Vienna panoramic sightseeing drive through Day Excursion to Salzburg Budapest boat cruise ticket Budapest panoramic sightseeing drive through Day trip to Danube Bend & Szentendre - explore on own Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Meals other than those specified (if any). Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 5/ CHF 5 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: General Notes: Quote for 2 guests is based on standard car like Toyota Prius or similar, Quote for 4 – 8 guests is based on Van like VW/Opel/Vito or similar, Quote from 10 guests it will be 14/16/19-seater vehicle or similar. If the guests exceed the seating capacity of the vehicle, then the rate will change based on a real-time basis as it will fall under coach packages For 2 to 6 guests, Vehicle is with driver cum guide. No separate guide If there are 5A + 3C or 6A + 2C or 4A + 4C etc. or similar, then we will have to check rates on real time basis. Blocking must be done a minimum 45 days prior to travel date with re-confirmation before 30 - 25 days of travel date unless there is an event then the booking has to be made on an immediate basis and the rate will be based on real-time availability If the travel date is during any festival, Sporting / Cultural / State or Government Event, Exhibition, Trade fairs etc. then the rate will change based on a real-time basis. IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 1 July – 31 October 2026 // Except Blackout Period Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '