Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Budapest\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Budapest to Salzburg\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Salzburg to Vienna\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague – City Tour including Prague Castle\nBudapest City Tour\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nSalzburg - Sound of Music Tour\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n\n\xa0', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/vienna-city.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/497110_Prague_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/23139_Charles_Bridge_Prague_Czech_Republic_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/61588_Budapest_Danube_Cruise_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/107107_Hungalian_Parliament_and_Danube_River_Budapest_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/FestungHohensalzburg_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/Salzburg_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/Vienna_City_Hall_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/Schonbrunnpalace753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014515/itinerary/Vienna_753.jpg']}, 'score': 4.988437, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014516', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014516', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'East European Explorer', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014516_0_20260916125632.pdf', 'price': 114702, 'packageSummary': "The 'East European Explorer' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Budapest, Vienna, and Prague. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hungarian Parliament Building, the majestic Schönbrunn Palace, Prague Castle, and the famous Charles Bridge. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic cruise along the Danube River, and ample opportunities to immerse themselves in the rich history, stunning architecture, and vibrant local culture of these imperial capitals.", 'images': ['Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg', 'PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'Viena_20.jpeg', 'SchonbrunnPalace.jpg', 'Budapest_Hungary.jpg', 'DanubeCruise.jpg', 'Budapest.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 114702, 'thumbnailImage': 'Budapest_3.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Budget Friendly', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014516 is named 'East European Explorer' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Prague, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Prague Transfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague City Tour Prague City Tour: Prague Castle! St. Vitus Cathedral! Charles Bridge! Visit the most significant Czech monument - an ancient symbol of the Czech State with a tradition of more than 1000 years. Learn about its history and the most important monarchs who ruled the Czech Lands from the heights of the Prague Castle. See St. Vitus Cathedral, Old Royal Palace, St. George’s Basilica, and much more. Enjoy panoramic views over Prague - all this with a knowledgeable guide! (Duration of the tour: 3 hrs), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague To Vienna Via Train (Approx 4 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Vienna! Upon your arrival at Vienna train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed) Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna City Tour Vienna City Tour: Take a tour of the main sights within the city centre and visit the magnificently decorated rooms of Schonbrunn Palace. This city tour will introduce you to the the most important sights of the Austrian capital. As we drive around the famous 'Ringstrasse', Vienna's main boulevard, we pass by the State Opera, the Museums of Fine Art and Natural History, the Parliament building, the Burgtheater (National Theatre), the City Hall and the University. The highlight of this programme is the visit to Schonbrunn Palace where we take a tour of some of the most magnificently decorated rooms. (Duration of the Tour: 3 hours), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna To Budapest Via Train (Approx 3 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Budapest! Upon your arrival at Budapest train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Budapest City Tour Budapest City Tour: On this tour you will be passing by the Parliament building before crossing the Danube on the Margaret Bridge and drive to the Royal Castle on the Buda side of the city. Here you will have some free time to yourself to visit the Fishermen's Bastion which offers stunning views over the city and the Mathias Church. Your tour will continue to the Gillert Hill before crossing the Elisabeth Bridge from where you will drive towards the Heroes' Square. Passing by the Opera and St Stephen's Basilica you reach the Hotel Intercontinental where your tour ends. [Duration of this tour: Approx. 3 hrs.], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Budapest Transfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 