local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\nAirline And Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJoining Direct Clients:\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\xa0\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they choose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\xa0\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n\n\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/Prague_260.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Vienna9.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/PearlofDanube_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Slovakia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Czech-Republic-Cesky-Krumlov.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Prague1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg']}, 'score': 4.6572304, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014892', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014892', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)   ', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014892_0_20260609125554.pdf', 'price': 114252, 'packageSummary': "The 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Prague, Budapest, and Vienna. Throughout this captivating journey, participants will immerse themselves in the rich cultural heritage of Eastern Europe, enjoying guided city tours of majestic palaces, scenic walks through medieval old towns, and breathtaking views along the Danube River. This specially curated holiday offers a perfect blend of sightseeing, local experiences, and festive celebrations, making it an unforgettable holiday experience.", 'images': ['Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg', 'PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'Viena_20.jpeg', 'SchonbrunnPalace.jpg', 'Budapest_Hungary.jpg', 'DanubeCruise.jpg', 'Budapest.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 114252, 'thumbnailImage': 'Budapest_3.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Durga Puja Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Budget Friendly', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014892 is named 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)   ' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Prague, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Prague Transfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague City Tour Prague City Tour: Prague Castle! St. Vitus Cathedral! Charles Bridge! Visit the most significant Czech monument - an ancient symbol of the Czech State with a tradition of more than 1000 years. Learn about its history and the most important monarchs who ruled the Czech Lands from the heights of the Prague Castle. See St. Vitus Cathedral, Old Royal Palace, St. George’s Basilica, and much more. Enjoy panoramic views over Prague - all this with a knowledgeable guide! (Duration of the tour: 3 hrs), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague To Vienna Via Train (Approx 4 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Vienna! Upon your arrival at Vienna train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed) Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna City Tour Vienna City Tour: Take a tour of the main sights within the city centre and visit the magnificently decorated rooms of Schonbrunn Palace. This city tour will introduce you to the the most important sights of the Austrian capital. As we drive around the famous 'Ringstrasse', Vienna's main boulevard, we pass by the State Opera, the Museums of Fine Art and Natural History, the Parliament building, the Burgtheater (National Theatre), the City Hall and the University. The highlight of this programme is the visit to Schonbrunn Palace where we take a tour of some of the most magnificently decorated rooms. (Duration of the Tour: 3 hours), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna To Budapest Via Train (Approx 3 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Budapest! Upon your arrival at Budapest train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Budapest City Tour Budapest City Tour: On this tour you will be passing by the Parliament building before crossing the Danube on the Margaret Bridge and drive to the Royal Castle on the Buda side of the city. Here you will have some free time to yourself to visit the Fishermen's Bastion which offers stunning views over the city and the Mathias Church. Your tour will continue to the Gillert Hill before crossing the Elisabeth Bridge from where you will drive towards the Heroes' Square. Passing by the Opera and St Stephen's Basilica you reach the Hotel Intercontinental where your tour ends. [Duration of this tour: Approx. 3 hrs.], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Budapest Transfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 114252.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza / Galileo Hotel / Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel/ Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\n\xa0Hotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nHotel Zeitgeist Vienna, Mercure Wien Westbahnhof, Mercure Wien City or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nRoyal Park Boutique Hotel /\xa0 Corvin Center Suites / City Inn or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Prague based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Budapest based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel Departure Airport transfer from Budapest Hotel to Budapest Airport Train Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Vienna 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Vienna to Budapest Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Prague - City Tour including Prague Castle Vienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace Budapest City Tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Prague, Budapest, and Vienna. Throughout this captivating journey, participants will immerse themselves in the rich cultural heritage of Eastern Europe, enjoying guided city tours of majestic palaces, scenic walks through medieval old towns, and breathtaking views along the Danube River. This specially curated holiday offers a perfect blend of sightseeing, local experiences, and festive celebrations, making it an unforgettable holiday experience.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Prague\nTransfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel St. George (Standard) / Carlton (Value) or similar in Prague'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nPrague City Tour\nPrague City Tour: Prague Castle! St. Vitus Cathedral! Charles Bridge! Visit the most significant Czech monument - an ancient symbol of the Czech State with a tradition of more than 1000 years. Learn about its history and the most important monarchs who ruled the Czech Lands from the heights of the Prague Castle. See St. Vitus Cathedral, Old Royal Palace, St. George’s Basilica, and much more. Enjoy panoramic views over Prague - all this with a knowledgeable guide! (Duration of the tour: 3 hrs)\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel St. George (Standard) / Carlton (Value) or similar in Prague'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPrague To Vienna Via Train (Approx 4 Hrs)\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station to board the train to Vienna!\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Vienna train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed)\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Art Vienna (Standard) / Zeitgeist (Value) or similar in Vienna'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nVienna City Tour\nVienna City Tour: Take a tour of the main sights within the city centre and visit the magnificently decorated rooms of Schonbrunn Palace. This city tour will introduce you to the the most important sights of the Austrian capital. As we drive around the famous 'Ringstrasse', Vienna's main boulevard, we pass by the State Opera, the Museums of Fine Art and Natural History, the Parliament building, the Burgtheater (National Theatre), the City Hall and the University. The highlight of this programme is the visit to Schonbrunn Palace where we take a tour of some of the most magnificently decorated rooms. (Duration of the Tour: 3 hours)\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Art Vienna (Standard) / Zeitgeist (Value) or similar in Vienna'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVienna To Budapest Via Train (Approx 3 Hrs)\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station to board the train to Budapest!\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Budapest train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Benczur (Standard) / Royal Park Boutique (Value) or similar in Budapest'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nBudapest City Tour\nBudapest City Tour: On this tour you will be passing by the Parliament building before crossing the Danube on the Margaret Bridge and drive to the Royal Castle on the Buda side of the city. Here you will have some free time to yourself to visit the Fishermen's Bastion which offers stunning views over the city and the Mathias Church. Your tour will continue to the Gillert Hill before crossing the Elisabeth Bridge from where you will drive towards the Heroes' Square. Passing by the Opera and St Stephen's Basilica you reach the Hotel Intercontinental where your tour ends. [Duration of this tour: Approx. 3 hrs.]\n\xa0\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Benczur (Standard) / Royal Park Boutique (Value) or similar in Budapest'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Depart Budapest\nTransfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer.\xa0\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\xa