st\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Budapest to Salzburg\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Salzburg to Vienna\xa0\xa0\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague - City Tour including Prague Castle\nBudapest City Tour\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nSalzburg - Sound of Music Tour\n\n\xa0', 'Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague – City Tour including Prague Castle\nBudapest City Tour\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nSalzburg - Sound of Music Tour\n\n\xa0'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Prague based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Budapest based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Salzburg based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\nTransfers: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Vienna Hotel to Vienna Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Budapest\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Budapest to Salzburg\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Salzburg to Vienna\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague - City Tour including Prague Castle\nBudapest City Tour\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nSalzburg - Sound of Music Tour\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n\n\xa0', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/vienna-city.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/497110_Prague_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/23139_Charles_Bridge_Prague_Czech_Republic_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/61588_Budapest_Danube_Cruise_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/107107_Hungalian_Parliament_and_Danube_River_Budapest_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/FestungHohensalzburg_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/Salzburg_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/Vienna_City_Hall_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/Schonbrunnpalace753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014870/itinerary/Vienna_753.jpg']}, 'score': 3.9505892, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015139', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015139', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Denmark Adventure', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012446_0_20240410184106.pdf', 'price': 209531, 'packageSummary': "The 'Denmark Adventure' package is a 6-day tour dedicated entirely to exploring the beautiful city of Copenhagen. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Nyhavn waterfront, the majestic Amalienborg Palace, the famous Little Mermaid statue, and the enchanting Tivoli Gardens. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a scenic canal cruise, and ample opportunities to experience the local culture, shopping, and world-class Danish cuisine.", 'images': ['Copenhagen1.jpg', 'Copenhagen2.jpg', 'Copenhagen3.jpg', 'Copenhagen4.jpg', 'Copenhagen5.jpg', 'return-flight.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 209531, 'thumbnailImage': 'Borsen_Christiansborg_slot_palace_sotsholmen_Copenhagen.avif', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015139 is named 'Denmark Adventure' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Copenhagen, Meals: NA, Description: Transfers: Upon your arrival at Copenhagen Airport, you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Copenhagen Small Group Walking Tour: Explore Copenhagen on a small-group walking tour inspired by hygge. See top sights like Nyhavn, Amagertorv, and Christiansborg Palace, while discovering hidden gems and learning about the city’s history and culture from an expert guide., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day trip to Roskilde, Frederiksborg & Kronborg (On shared basis/SIC): Visit the royal castles of Frederiksborg and Kronborg, and Denmark’s old capital of Roskilde on an 8-hour minibus tour from Copenhagen. Enjoy the scenic landscape of North Zealand, and the history of the Vikings at the Viking Ship Museum., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Guided Classic Canal Tour: Join a classic canal tour through Copenhagens harbor and canals. Pass landmarks like the Royal Opera, Black Diamond, BLOX, and Borsen, while enjoying colorful Christianshavn and lively quays filled with cafes and local charm. Festive Tivoli Gardens Tour: Visit Tivoli Gardens for fun and entertainment for all ages. Enjoy thrilling rollercoasters, exciting rides, cozy cafes, great restaurants, and beautiful seasonal decorations that make the park magical year round., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hygge & Food Tour: Discover the essence of hygge on a Copenhagen stroll with a local and see why Danes are so happy. Then enjoy a food tour, tasting Danish specialties from Torvehallerne to cozy taverns, while learning the stories, culture, and traditions behind each bite., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Transfers: You will be transferred from Copenhagen hotel to the Airport on private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email, as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 209531.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue Category\n\n\n\n\nCopenhagen\n\n\nScandic Copenhagen\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0, \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nHelsinki\n\n\nHotel Haaga Central Park / Hotel Anna / Hotel Arthur / Scandic Kallio or similar\n\n\n\n\nRovaniemi\n\n\nScandic Grand Marina /\xa0 Scandic Meilahti\xa0 / Scandic Marski / Valo Hotel Helsinki \xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n, \n1 dinner included at Northern Lights Village Saariselka Resort\n5 lunches included (days 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 of the program)\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 5 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis] Arrival & Departure Transfers from Copenhagen Airport to the Hotel and back Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Copenhagen Small Group Walking Tour Day trip to Roskilde, Frederiksborg & Kronborg (On shared basis/SIC) Guided Classic Canal Tour Festive Tivoli Gardens Tour Hygge & Food Tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Black out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 – 10 January’27. Product Terms and Conditions: Special Note: The itinerary and sightseeing may vary based on availability and seasonality Please note that should the Covid-19 pandemic necessitate further protocols as mandated by the Government and/or the individual properties in the future which results in an increase in our standard tour operator rates, then Thomas Cook India reserves the right to adjust the above quoted rates accordingly. This may lead to an increase in prices quoted. Certain Activities are subject to weather conditions and protocols. Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and Conditions: Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. TCS & GST would be levied as applicable The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Denmark Adventure' package is a 6-day tour dedicated entirely to exploring the beautiful city of Copenhagen. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Nyhavn waterfront, the majestic Amalienborg Palace, the famous Little Mermaid statue, and the enchanting Tivoli Gardens. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a scenic canal cruise, and ample opportunities to experience the local culture, shopping, and world-class Danish cuisine.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at Copenhagen Airport, you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\xa0\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'NA', 'overnightStay': 'Scandic Copenhagen or similar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nCopenhagen Small Group Walking Tour: Explore Copenhagen on a small-group walking tour inspired by hygge. See top sights like Nyhavn, Amagertorv, and Christiansborg Palace, while discovering hidden gems and learning about the city’s history and culture from an expert guide.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Scandic Copenhagen or similar'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDay trip to Roskilde, Frederiksborg & Kronborg (On shared basis/SIC): Visit the royal castles of Frederiksborg and Kronborg, and Denmark’s old capital of Roskilde on an 8-hour minibus tour from Copenhagen. Enjoy the scenic landscape of North Zealand, and the history of the Vikings at the Viking Ship Museum.\xa0 \xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Scandic Copenhagen or similar'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided Classic Canal Tour: Join a classic canal tour through Copenhagens harbor and canals. Pass landmarks like the Royal Opera, Black Diamond, BLOX, and Borsen, while enjoying colorful Christianshavn and lively quays filled with cafes and local charm.\xa0\xa0\nFestive Tivoli Gardens Tour: Visit Tivoli Gardens for fun and entertainment for all ages. Enjoy thrilling rollercoasters, exciting rides, cozy cafes, great restaurants, and beautiful seasonal decorations that make the park magical year round.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Scandic Copenhagen or similar'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nHygge & Food Tour: Discover the essence of hygge on a Copenhagen stroll with a local and see why Danes are so happy. Then enjoy a food tour, tasting Danish specialties from Torvehallerne to cozy taverns, while learning the stories, culture, and traditions behind each bite.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Scandic Copenhagen or similar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Copenhagen hotel to the Airport on private transfer.\xa0\xa0\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email, as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'NA'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue Category\n\n\n\n\nCopenhagen\n\n\nScandic Copenhagen\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', '\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nHelsinki\n\n\nHotel Haaga Central Park / Hotel Anna / Hotel Arthur / Scandic Kallio or similar\n\n\n\n\nRovaniemi\n\n\nScandic Grand Marina /\xa0 Scandic Meilahti\xa0 / Scandic Marski / Valo Hotel Helsinki \xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue Category\n\n\n\n\nCopenhagen\n\n\nScandic Copenhagen\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': '\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nHelsinki\n\n\nHotel Haaga Central Park / Hotel Anna / Hotel Arthur / Scandic Kallio or similar\n\n\n\n\nRovaniemi\n\n\nScandic Grand Marina /\xa0 Scandic Meilahti\xa0 / Scandic Marski / Valo Hotel Helsinki \xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DK', 'countryName': 'Denmark', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 209500.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue Category\n\n\n\n\nCopenhagen\n\n\nScandic Copenhagen\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n', '\n1 dinner included at Northern Lights Village Saariselka Resort\n5 lunches included (days 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 of the program)\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nRental of winter thermal clothing from day 2 to day 7 of the program\xa0\nDay 2: Visit to a husky dog farm & Santa Claus Village\nDay 3 - 3h30m cruise on the icebreaker ship Sampo & Visit to the Ice Castle in Kemi\nDay 5 - 2-hour snowmobile safari &\nVisit to a Sami farm including a short ride on a reindeer sleigh &\xa0\nNight Safari "Aurora Borealis" with grilled sausages and hot drinks\nDay 6 – 4-hour visit to Ranua Zoo\n', 'Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\xa0\n\nCopenhagen Small Group Walking Tour\xa0\xa0\nDay trip to Roskilde, Frederiksborg & Kronborg (On shared basis/SIC)\xa0\nGuided Classic Canal Tour\xa0\xa0\nFestive Tivoli Gardens Tour\xa0\xa0\nHygge & Food Tour\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\xa0\n\n5 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\xa0\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\xa0\xa0\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis]\xa0\n\nArrival & Departure Transfers from Copenhagen Airport to the Hotel and back\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\xa0\n\nCopenhagen Small Group Walking Tour\xa0\xa0\nDay trip to Roskilde, Frederiksborg & Kronborg (On shared basis/SIC)\xa0\nGuided Classic Canal Tour\xa0\xa0\nFestive Tivoli Gardens Tour\xa0\xa0\nHygge & Food Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\xa0\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\xa0\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\xa0\nDrinks during meals\xa0\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\xa0\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\xa0\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\xa0\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\xa0\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\xa0\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\xa0\nBlack out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 – 10 January’27\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\n\xa0Special Note:\n\nThe itinerary and sightseeing may vary based on availability and seasonality\nPlease note that should the Covid-19 pandemic necessitate further protocols as mandated by the Government and/or the individual properties in the future which results in an increase in our standard tour operator rates, then Thomas Cook India reserves the right to adjust the above quoted rates accordingly. This may lead to an increase in prices quoted. Certain Activities are subject to weather conditions and protocols.\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/Borsen_Christiansborg_slot_palace_sotsholmen_Copenhagen.avif', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/Copenhagen1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/Copenhagen2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/Copenhagen3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/Copenhagen4.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/Copenhagen5.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015139/itinerary/return-flight.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014676', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014676', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Istanbul With Cappadocia - PVT Tour', 'days': 5, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014676_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 81828, 'packageSummary': "The 'Istanbul With Cappadocia - PVT Tour' package is a 5-day tour covering the historic and scenic destinations of Istanbul and Cappadocia. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia, the Blue Mosque, Topkapi Palace, and the unique fairy chimneys and underground cities of Cappadocia. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a scenic Bosphorus cruise, and the unforgettable experience of a hot air balloon ride over the volcanic landscapes.", 'images': ['Istanbul753.jpg', 'GrandBazar.jpg', 'Cappadocia7532.jpg', 'Cappadocia7531.jpg', 'Cappodocia753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 81828, 'thumbnailImage': 'Istanbul2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014676 is named 'Istanbul With Cappadocia - PVT Tour' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Istanbul, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Istanbul Transfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion Optional Activity: Bosphorus Dinner Cruise Enjoy an enchanting evening on the Bosphorus Strait with a leisurely dinner cruise that showcases Istanbuls beauty by night. Sail between Europe and Asia as you pass iconic landmarks such as the Bosphorus Bridge, Dolmabahce Palace, and the illuminated waterfront mansions. The experience is complemented by a delicious Turkish dinner and live entertainment, often including traditional music and folk dance performances, making it a memorable blend of scenic views, culture, and cuisine. [The supplement cost for this activity will be approx. USD 80 per adult & USD 55 for children below 6 years], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full-Day Guided Tour Of Istanbul On Private Basis Istanbul City Tour : Between 07:30 and 09:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel (pickup time subject to hotel location) for a full day guided city tour. The tour includes visits to the Hagia Sophia Mosque (entrance not included), the pride of Byzantine architecture the Byzantine Hippodrome, once the venue for ancient chariot races and the Blue Mosque, renowned for its exquisite blue Iznik tiles. You will also visit the Topkapi Palace (entrance not included), the former residence of the Ottoman Sultans, followed by time at the Grand Bazaar, Turkeys largest covered market with over 4,000 shops. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary. Entrance to the Hagia Sophia Mosque and Topkapi Palace is available at an additional supplement. Supplement costs: Hagia Sophia: USD 35 - 40 Per adult (Under 8 years Free) Topkapi Palace USD 65 Per adult (Under 6 years Free), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Istanbul To Cappadocia Transfers: Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight Upon arrival at Cappadocia, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the Hotel. Special Note: Please note that the domestic flight from Istanbul to Cappadocia is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast and Local Lunch, Description: Explore Cappadocia Optional Activity: Hot Air Balloon If a hot air balloon ride is on your bucket list, Cappadocia offers one of the most iconic experiences in the world. Drift gently at sunrise above a surreal, lunar like landscape of volcanic rock formations, fairy chimneys, and honeycombed valleys, as dozens of vibrantly colored balloons rise alongside you. This unforgettable experience offers breathtaking panoramic views and spectacular photo opportunities. [The supplement cost for this activity will be upon On Request Basis] Please Note: Children below 6 years of age or under 120 cm in height are not permitted to participate in the hot air balloon ride. Cappadocia Sightseeing on Private Basis: After breakfast, between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel to begin a full day tour of Cappadocia. The first stop is Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley), known for its spectacular fairy chimneys and uniquely shaped rock formations set amidst beautiful landscape.You will then visit Pasabag (Monks Valley), famous for its remarkable double and triple headed rock formations, once used as hermit dwellings by monks. Lunch will be served in Avanos, a town renowned for its traditional pottery craftsmanship and located along the Red River. After lunch, continue to the Goreme Open Air Museum, the heart of Cappadocia, celebrated for its rock cut churches adorned with wall paintings dating back to the 10th century, depicting scenes from the life of Jesus and early Christian monastic life.The tour concludes with a photo stop at Uchisar Castle, a natural rock citadel and one of the largest fairy chimney formations in the region, offering panoramic views of Cappadocia. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Cappadocia Transfers: From Cappadocia hotel to Kayseri Airport in private transfer. Special Note: Please note that the domestic flight from Cappadocia to Istanbul is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 81828.0. Hotels envisaged include:  \n\n\n\n\nPREMIUM CATEGORY (5* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\n\n \n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n \n\n\nThe Elysium Taksim / Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa Hotel or similar\n\n\nHanedan Cave Suites /\n Acer Cave Hotel or similar\n\n \n\n, \n\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY (4* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\n\n\nFour Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy Hotel/ Konak Taksim\xa0or similar\n\n\nDedeli Cave / Sunak Cave Hotel\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n2 Local Lunches as a part of the itinerary\n, Breakfast Included, \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\xa0\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Istanbul based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: Private Airport Transfer from Istanbul Airport to Hotel Private transfer from Istanbul hotel to Istanbul Airprort Private Airport Transfer from Kayseri Airport to Cappadocia Hotel Private Airport transfer from Cappadocia Hotel to Kayseri Airport Sightseeing: (Sightseeing is provided on a private basis only. The vehicle is available strictly as per the sightseeing itinerary and is not available at disposal) Full Day Guided Tour of Istanbul on private basis (SIC) Cappadocia Sightseeing Tour on private basis (SIC) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Blackout Dates: HOLIDAY DATE National Sovereignty and Children’s Day 23-04-2026 Labor and Solidarity Day 01-05-2026 Commemoration of Atatürk, Youth and Sports Day 19-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 1st day 27-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 2nd day 28-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 3rd day 29-05-2026 Eid al-Adha last day 30-05-2026 Democracy and National Unity Day 15-07-2026 Victory Day 30-08-2026 Republic Day 29-10-2026. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the ti