s visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia, the Blue Mosque, Topkapi Palace, and the unique fairy chimneys and underground cities of Cappadocia. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a scenic Bosphorus cruise, and the unforgettable experience of a hot air balloon ride over the volcanic landscapes.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive Istanbul\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: Bosphorus Dinner Cruise\nEnjoy an enchanting evening on the Bosphorus Strait with a leisurely dinner cruise that showcases Istanbuls beauty by night. Sail between Europe and Asia as you pass iconic landmarks such as the Bosphorus Bridge, Dolmabahce Palace, and the illuminated waterfront mansions. The experience is complemented by a delicious Turkish dinner and live entertainment, often including traditional music and folk dance performances, making it a memorable blend of scenic views, culture, and cuisine. [The supplement cost for this activity will be approx. USD 80 per adult & USD 55 for children below 6 years]', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy / Konak Taksim (Value) / The Elysium Taksim / Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa or similar (Premium) in Istanbul'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFull-Day Guided Tour Of Istanbul On Private Basis\n\xa0\nIstanbul City Tour : Between 07:30 and 09:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel (pickup time subject to hotel location) for a full day guided city tour. The tour includes visits to the Hagia Sophia Mosque (entrance not included), the pride of Byzantine architecture the Byzantine Hippodrome, once the venue for ancient chariot races and the Blue Mosque, renowned for its exquisite blue Iznik tiles. You will also visit the Topkapi Palace (entrance not included), the former residence of the Ottoman Sultans, followed by time at the Grand Bazaar, Turkeys largest covered market with over 4,000 shops.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Notes:\xa0\n\nSightseeing will be conducted on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary.\nEntrance to the Hagia Sophia Mosque and Topkapi Palace is available at an additional supplement.\n\n\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\nSupplement costs:\n\nHagia Sophia: USD 35 - 40 Per adult (Under 8 years Free)\xa0 \xa0\nTopkapi Palace USD 65 Per adult (Under 6 years Free)\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy / Konak Taksim (Value) / The Elysium Taksim / Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa or similar (Premium) in Istanbul'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nIstanbul To Cappadocia\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nToday you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight\nUpon arrival at Cappadocia, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the Hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note that the domestic flight from Istanbul to Cappadocia is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Dedeli Cave / Sunak Cave (Value) / Hanedan Cave Suites / Acer Cave or similar (Premium) in Cappadocia\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExplore Cappadocia\xa0\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: Hot Air Balloon\n\xa0\nIf a hot air balloon ride is on your bucket list, Cappadocia offers one of the most iconic experiences in the world. Drift gently at sunrise above a surreal, lunar like landscape of volcanic rock formations, fairy chimneys, and honeycombed valleys, as dozens of vibrantly colored balloons rise alongside you. This unforgettable experience offers breathtaking panoramic views and spectacular photo opportunities. [The supplement cost for this activity will be upon On Request Basis]\n\xa0\nPlease Note:\xa0 Children below 6 years of age or under 120 cm in height are not permitted to participate in the hot air balloon ride.\n\xa0\nCappadocia Sightseeing on Private Basis: After breakfast, between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel to begin a full day tour of Cappadocia. The first stop is Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley), known for its spectacular fairy chimneys and uniquely shaped rock formations set amidst beautiful landscape.You will then visit Pasabag (Monks Valley), famous for its remarkable double and triple headed rock formations, once used as hermit dwellings by monks. Lunch will be served in Avanos, a town renowned for its traditional pottery craftsmanship and located along the Red River.\n\xa0\nAfter lunch, continue to the Goreme Open Air Museum, the heart of Cappadocia, celebrated for its rock cut churches adorned with wall paintings dating back to the 10th century, depicting scenes from the life of Jesus and early Christian monastic life.The tour concludes with a photo stop at Uchisar Castle, a natural rock citadel and one of the largest fairy chimney formations in the region, offering panoramic views of Cappadocia.\n\xa0\nSpecial Notes:\xa0\n\nSightseeing will be conducted on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Local Lunch', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Dedeli Cave / Sunak Cave (Value) / Hanedan Cave Suites / Acer Cave or similar (Premium) in Cappadocia\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart Cappadocia\n\xa0\nTransfers: From Cappadocia hotel to Kayseri Airport in private transfer.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note that the domestic flight from Cappadocia to Istanbul is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with 