ill be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2 - 3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/St.Petersburg_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/650718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/Petersburg7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/12117_Hermitage_Museum_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/Church_of_the_Saviour_on_Blood_St._Petersburg_Russia_753.jpgiti6.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015026/itinerary/MoscowRussia7534.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014720', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014720', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Complete Iceland - Fixed Departures', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Hofn', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Egilsstadir', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Akureyri', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Borgarnes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Borgarnes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG013109_0_20250313144409.pdf', 'price': 395001, 'packageSummary': "The 'Complete Iceland - Fixed Departures' package is a 9-day tour covering Reykjavik, Borgarnes, Akureyri, Egilsstadir, and Hofn. The itinerary includes exploring the famous Golden Circle, marveling at the stunning Jökulsárlón Glacier Lagoon, and visiting the majestic Goðafoss waterfall. Participants will enjoy guided sightseeing tours of historic towns, scenic drives through the dramatic East Fjords, and relaxing visits to geothermal hot springs.", 'images': ['03286_reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', '61166_Seljalandsfoss_waterfall_Iceland_753.jpg', 'Jokulsarlon.jpg', 'LakeMyvatn.avif', 'WhaleWatching.avif', 'Hraunfossar.avif', 'Snaefellsness.avif', 'BlueLagoon.avif', 'Reykjavik_City.png'], 'minimumPrice': 395001, 'thumbnailImage': 'SRP_blue-lagoon.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014720 is named 'Complete Iceland - Fixed Departures' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Reykjavik, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Reykjavik Transfers: Upon arrival in Keflavik Airport, you will meet the representative and get transferred to the hotel on private basis, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Hofn, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reykjavik To South Coast Transfers: There will be a pick-up from the scheduled meeting point near the hotel starts around 08:30. South Coast Tour: Enjoy the South Coast's tour including Stunning waterfalls of Seljalandsfoss and Skogafoss, secret waterfall Gljufrabui. Visit Vatnajokull, the largest glacier in Europe. Unique black beach Reynisfjara near the village of Vík., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Egilsstadir, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Glacier Lagoon, Diamond Beach & Adventure In The East Transfers: Drive from South Iceland towards the East of Iceland. Glacier Lagoon, Diamond Beach & East Iceland: Visit at Jokulsarlon Glacier Lagoon – world-famous glacial lake filled with floating icebergs falling from the biggest glacier in Europe – Vatnajökull. Visit Djupivogur, located in Berufjordur – a long and narrow fjord rich in birdlife. This day ends at Egillsstadir – the capital of East Iceland. Special Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Akureyri, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Lake Myvatn And Waterfall Transfers: Continue the journey from East to North Iceland. Lake Myvatn and Waterfall: Visit Lake Mývatn, formed by a lava eruption 2300 years ago. See Dettifoss and hike to Selfoss. Explore Hverir, Grjótagjá, Dimmuborgir, and Krafla. Finish at Goðafoss before driving to Akureyri, the capital of North Iceland. Special Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Borgarnes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Whale Watching & Journey To West Iceland Transfers: Continue the journey from North to West Iceland. Whale Watching & Journey to West Iceland: Explore Northern Iceland and continue towards the West. Take a short tour of Akureyri, then visit Dalvík, a small fishing village, for a 3 hour whale safari. Continue to the unique dinosaur like Hvítserkur rock and the stunning Kolugljufur Canyon with its spectacular waterfall. Proceed to the west part of Iceland. Special Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Borgarnes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Silver Circle And Lava Cave Silver Circle and Lava Cave: Enjoy the drive to the Silver Circle and visit Bifröst’s Elves & Waterfalls, Deildartunguhver, Reykholt, Hraunfossar, Barnafoss and Húsafell, ending with a 1–1.5hr guided Lava Cave expedition. Special Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Snaefellsnes National Park Snaefellsnes National Park: See Snæfellsjökull volcano, visit Ytri Tunga’s seal beach, Arnarstapi and Hellnar. Explore the black beach Djúpalónssandur, iconic Kirkjufell mountain, Barnafoss, and Húsafell. Special Note: Transfer back to Reykjavik Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Golden Circle, Kerid Crater & Blue Lagoon Golden Circle, Kerid Crater, Blue Lagoon: Explore the Golden Circle, including Geysers, Gullfoss, Thingvellir, and the Kerid Crater. Then unwind at the Blue Lagoon with 2 hours of relaxation in its natural hot waters before returning to Reykjavik. This Multi-City Small Group tour ends with drop off in Reykjavík between 20-20:30 (8-8:30 PM)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: From Reykjavik hotel to the Keflavik Airport in private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 395001.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nREYKJAVIK\n\n\nFosshotel Baron /center Klopp/Foss Lind / Hotel Foss Lind / Hotel 22 Hill / Klettur/ or similar\n\n\n\n\nHÖFN\n\n\nHotel Smylabjor or similar\n\n\n\n\nEGILSSTAÐIR\n\n\nBerjaya Hotel Herad or similar\n\n\n\n\nAKUREYRI\n\n\nKea Hotel Akureyri or similar\n\n\n\n\nBORGARNES\n\n\nHotel Borgarnes or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik\n\n\nHotel Cabin standard room or Similar\n\n\n\n\nHella\n\n\nStracta hotel standard room or Similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 3 Nights’ Split accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Höfn area based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Egilsstaðir based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Akureyri based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Night accommodation in Borgarnes based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Private airport transfer upon arrival at KEF Airport Private airport transfer upon departure from KEF Airport Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) South Coast Tour on shared basis (SIC Tour) Glacier Lagoon, Diamond Beach & East Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour) Lake Myvatn and Waterfall on shared basis (SIC Tour) Whale Watching & Journey to West Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour) Silver Circle and Lava Cave on shared basis (SIC Tour) Snaefellsnes National Park on shared basis (SIC Tour) Golden Circle, Kerid Crater, Blue Lagoon on shared basis (SIC Tour) Entry fee to the Geothermal Park with tasting of geothermal bread (Hverabrauð) 45-minute Amphibian Boat Tour at Jökulsárlón (available from May to October) among floating icebergs. Vidgelmir Lava Cave Tour - 1-1 ½ hour Lava Caving Expedition to see one of the largest lava caves in Iceland with its stunning lava stalactites and stalagmites. 3-Hour Whale Watching Boat Tour in Dalvik during fixed departure tour. Entry to Kerid Volcano Crater on shared basis (SIC Tour) Blue Lagoon on Comfort ticket. Includes: Entrance to the Blue Lagoon, Silica mud mask, Use of towel and Welcome drink. Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: SPECIAL NOTES: Reykjavik down town has restrictions for vehicles. For drop offs and pickups, nearest authorised stops will be used in case the hotel location is within the No driving zone (these can be in the range of average 300-700 meters from the hotels). Price subject to availability and confirmation. prices may change in case of special events/low availability/holiday season. Mandatory age to join the Fixed Departure tour: minimum 8yrs old It can happen that the activities can be cancelled because of weather and/or safety reasons. Then we will find other activities when possible and refund the amount paid for the cancelled activities or the price difference between new activity and cancelled one Luggage Capacity: 1 small item (like a backpack or cabin luggage) + 1 big piece of luggage (no more than 22 inches) per person. Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and conditions: Travel Validity: FIXED DEPARTURES (May – October 2026) Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', '