al lake filled with floating icebergs falling from the biggest glacier in Europe – Vatnajökull. Visit Djupivogur, located in Berufjordur – a long and narrow fjord rich in birdlife. This day ends at Egillsstadir – the capital of East Iceland.\nSpecial Note:\xa0Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Berjaya Herad or similar\xa0Egillsstadir'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nLake Myvatn And Waterfall\nTransfers: Continue the journey from East to North Iceland.\nLake Myvatn and Waterfall: Visit Lake Mývatn, formed by a lava eruption 2300 years ago. See Dettifoss and hike to Selfoss. Explore Hverir, Grjótagjá, Dimmuborgir, and Krafla. Finish at Goðafoss before driving to Akureyri, the capital of North Iceland.\nSpecial Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Kea Akureyri or similar in\xa0Akureyri'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nWhale Watching & Journey To West Iceland\nTransfers: Continue the journey from North to West Iceland.\nWhale Watching & Journey to West Iceland: Explore Northern Iceland and continue towards the West. Take a short tour of Akureyri, then visit Dalvík, a small fishing village, for a 3 hour whale safari. Continue to the unique dinosaur like Hvítserkur rock and the stunning Kolugljufur Canyon with its spectacular waterfall. Proceed to the west part of Iceland.\nSpecial Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Borgarnes or similar in\xa0Borgarnes'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nSilver Circle And Lava Cave\nSilver Circle and Lava Cave: Enjoy the drive to the Silver Circle and visit Bifröst’s Elves & Waterfalls, Deildartunguhver, Reykholt, Hraunfossar, Barnafoss and Húsafell, ending with a 1–1.5hr guided Lava Cave expedition.\xa0\nSpecial Note: Sightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Borgarnes or similar in\xa0Borgarnes'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nSnaefellsnes National Park\nSnaefellsnes National Park: See Snæfellsjökull volcano, visit Ytri Tunga’s seal beach, Arnarstapi and Hellnar. Explore the black beach Djúpalónssandur, iconic Kirkjufell mountain, Barnafoss, and Húsafell.\nSpecial Note:\n\nTransfer back to Reykjavik\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Fosshotel Baron / center Klopp / Foss Lind / Hotel Foss Lind / Hotel 22 Hill / Klettur/\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nGolden Circle, Kerid Crater & Blue Lagoon\nGolden Circle, Kerid Crater, Blue Lagoon: Explore the Golden Circle, including Geysers, Gullfoss, Thingvellir, and the Kerid Crater. Then unwind at the Blue Lagoon with 2 hours of relaxation in its natural hot waters before returning to Reykjavik. This Multi-City Small Group tour ends with drop off in Reykjavík between 20-20:30 (8-8:30 PM).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Fosshotel Baron / center Klopp / Foss Lind / Hotel Foss Lind / Hotel 22 Hill / Klettur/\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\nTransfers: From Reykjavik hotel to the Keflavik Airport in private transfer.\nSpecial Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\