nated point)\n\nSouth Coast Tour on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nGlacier Lagoon, Diamond Beach & East Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nLake Myvatn and Waterfall on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nWhale Watching & Journey to West Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nSilver Circle and Lava Cave on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nSnaefellsnes National Park on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nGolden Circle, Kerid Crater, Blue Lagoon on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nEntry fee to the Geothermal Park with tasting of geothermal bread (Hverabrauð)\n45-minute Amphibian Boat Tour at Jökulsárlón (available from May to October) among floating icebergs.\nVidgelmir Lava Cave Tour - 1-1 ½ hour Lava Caving Expedition to see one of the largest lava caves in Iceland with its stunning lava stalactites and stalagmites.\xa0\n3-Hour Whale Watching Boat Tour in Dalvik during fixed departure tour.\xa0\nEntry to Kerid Volcano Crater on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nBlue Lagoon on Comfort ticket.\xa0 Includes: Entrance to the Blue Lagoon, Silica mud mask, Use of towel and Welcome drink.\xa0\n', '\n3 days escorted tour with private English-speaking guide/driver-guide\nNorthern Lights program during two evenings\nReykjavik City Tour, Reykjanes Peninsula & Northern Lights\xa0\nSouth Iceland & Northern Lights\xa0\nGolden circle tour\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n3 Nights’ Split accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Höfn area based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Egilsstaðir based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Akureyri based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Night accommodation in Borgarnes based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nPrivate airport transfer upon arrival at KEF Airport\xa0\nPrivate airport transfer upon departure from KEF Airport\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nSouth Coast Tour on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nGlacier Lagoon, Diamond Beach & East Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nLake Myvatn and Waterfall on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nWhale Watching & Journey to West Iceland on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nSilver Circle and Lava Cave on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nSnaefellsnes National Park on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nGolden Circle, Kerid Crater, Blue Lagoon on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nEntry fee to the Geothermal Park with tasting of geothermal bread (Hverabrauð)\n45-minute Amphibian Boat Tour at Jökulsárlón (available from May to October) among floating icebergs.\nVidgelmir Lava Cave Tour - 1-1 ½ hour Lava Caving Expedition to see one of the largest lava caves in Iceland with its stunning lava stalactites and stalagmites.\xa0\n3-Hour Whale Watching Boat Tour in Dalvik during fixed departure tour.\xa0\nEntry to Kerid Volcano Crater on shared basis (SIC Tour)\nBlue Lagoon on Comfort ticket.\xa0 Includes: Entrance to the Blue Lagoon, Silica mud mask, Use of towel and Welcome drink.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'SPECIAL NOTES:\n\nReykjavik down town has restrictions for vehicles. For drop offs and pickups, nearest authorised stops will be used in case the hotel location is within the No driving zone (these can be in the range of average 300-700 meters from the hotels).\xa0\nPrice subject to availability and confirmation. prices may change in case of special events/low availability/holiday season.\nMandatory age to join the Fixed Departure tour: minimum 8yrs old\nIt can happen that the activities can be cancelled because of weather and/or safety reasons. Then we will find other activities when possible and refund the amount paid for the cancelled activities or the price difference between new activity and cancelled one\nLuggage Capacity: 1 small item (like a backpack or cabin luggage) + 1 big piece of luggage (no more than 22 inches) per person.\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: FIXED DEPARTURES (May – October 2026)\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/SRP_blue-lagoon.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/03286_reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/61166_Seljalandsfoss_waterfall_Iceland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/Jokulsarlon.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/LakeMyvatn.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/WhaleWatching.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/Hraunfossar.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/Snaefellsness.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/BlueLagoon.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014720/itinerary/Reykjavik_City.png']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014876', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014876', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Best Of Spain (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seville', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seville', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Free upgrade to 1st class Train sector tickets'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014876_0_20260609183303.pdf', 'price': 169543, 'packageSummary': "The 'Best Of Spain (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 9-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Madrid, Valencia, Barcelona, and Seville. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will explore the rich culture, stunning architecture, and historic landmarks of these iconic Spanish destinations. A key highlight of this special holiday package is a complimentary upgrade to first-class train sector tickets, ensuring comfortable and scenic travel between cities.", 'images': ['Madrid2.jpg', 'MadridRoyalPalace.jpg', 'seville1.jpg', 'Seville.jpg', 'Valencia2.jpg', 'Valencia.jpg', 'Barcelona.jpg', 'BarcelonaSpain.jpg', 'BarcelonaCIty.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 169543, 'thumbnailImage': 'BArcelona_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Durga Puja Special', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014876 is named 'Best Of Spain (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Madrid, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Madrid Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Madrid airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid: Panoramic City Bus Tour Madrid Panoramic City Bus Tour: Route 1 (Blue) will take you to discover Historical Madrid. This circular route takes you through a complete historical, artistic, and monumental circuit featuring the city’s key landmarks. Travel along the beautiful tree lined Paseo del Prado and admire the magnificent architectural treasures of the Habsburg royal legacy. Discover parts of Madrid’s Art Triangle and enjoy stunning views from the Royal Palace to the Temple of Debod. Route 2 (Green) will take you to discover Modern Madrid. Explore the city beyond its historical landmarks and royal monuments. From Atocha Station to Nuevos Ministerios, and from the iconic Puerta de Alcala to Puerta del Sol. Admire the most contemporary architectural works in the capital, including the imposing KIO Towers, the modern sculptures of the Public Art Museum, and Real Madrid's Santiago Bernabéu Stadium. Discover Madrid’s vibrant life, art, and modern customs on this itinerary., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Seville, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid To Seville By Train Transfer: Make your way to the Madrid train station for your onward journey to Seville. Upon arrival at Seville train station make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Seville, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Seville: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Later enjoy Seville Hop on Hop off sightseeing. This tour is operated by double decker buses you can make a route through more emblematic places of the city of Seville, with commentaries in 16 different languages, which make possible to know the history, culture and heritage of the city, which origin goes back to Old Age, that way this city is a cultures mixing . This service is valid for 24 (basic) or 48 hours (Experience) with a hop on / hop off system , so during this period you can get on and get off of the bus such times as you want in any bus stop. The ticket can be purchase as in the bus as in any of two main bus stop, furthermore in any official sales point. Multilingual Audio System: 16 languages. Panoramic route on double decker buses with 14 stops at the most important locations of the city: Paseo Colon, Plaza de Espana, 1929 Exhibition, Triana San Jacinto, Triana Castilla, 1992 Universal Exhibition, Isla Magica, Macarena, Torre de los Perdigones, Alameda de Hercules, Plaza del Duque, Plaza de Armas, plaza de Cuba y Acuario de Sevilla. Hop on , hop off. Individual headsets. Free Entrance: El Salvador Church, Museo de Carruajes, Pabellon de la Navegacion, Casa de la Ciencia, Torre de los Perdigones, Iglesia de Santa Ana and Hospital de la Caridad., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Seville To Valencia Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the Seville train station for your onward journey to Valencia. Upon your arrival at Valencia train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Valencia: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Today enjoy Valencia Tourist Bus sightseeing. Get to know Valencia in a comfortable, rigorous and enjoyable way. You will be able to hop on and off the bus all day along the route of your choice or change to another, admiring the architectural and cultural magnificence of Valencia, with the commentaries offered through a headphones audio system in seven different languages (Spanish, English, French, German, Italian, Portuguese and Japanese). The tour offers you 2 Hop on Hop off routes (90 minutes duration each) to customise your own tour of Valencia. Route A (red colour) you will meet the city from a historical and monumental viewpoint and the route B (blue colour) you will know the Mediterranean Sea influence on the city of Valencia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Valencia To Barcelona Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Barcelona. Upon your arrival at Barcelona train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Barcelona: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Hop aboard the Barcelona Bus Turistic, and discover the best of the city aboard a panoramic double decker bus. Not only can you hop on and off as you wish, but you have the freedom to explore the beautiful city of Barcelona at your own leisure. Highlights - See the most iconic landmarks of the city - Hop on and off as you wish at conveniently located route stops - Learn about the city with a fascinating audioguide available in 16 languages The Barcelona Bus Turístic is the city’s official sightseeing hop on, hop off tour. The red route and the blue route take approximately two hours to complete. Others Both routes depart between 9 am and 9:30 am from any stop. The last departures leave at 7pm during the winter months and 8pm in summer. Depending on the season, the bus frequency varies, between 5 and 25 minutes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Barcelona Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Barcelona hotel to the airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant me