 Eye for panoramic city views, and guided walking tours through the city's historic royal parks and bustling West End district.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'Arrive London\nTransfer: Arrival in London Airport (LHR), you will be met by the representative and have a private transfer to the hotel.\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Earls Court\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Park Plaza\xa0(Value) Or Similar in\xa0London'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nLondon\nLondon Sightseeing: This tour combines the flexibility of a hop-on hop-off bus with a ride on the London Eye. You can explore London's famous landmarks like the Tower of London and Buckingham Palace at your own pace by getting on and off the open-top bus as you please, while the bus tour itself provides commentary. The package also includes a 30-minute ride on the London Eye, giving you panoramic views of the city from a unique perspective.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Earls Court\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Park Plaza\xa0(Value) Or Similar in\xa0London'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nLondon - Free Day\nChanging of the Guard Guided Tour at Buckingham Palace (Optional Activity)\nWalking Tour - English 09:00 [Duration approx. 90 mins]\nBegin this regal tour at the Duke of York Column in St. James's. Greet the guide and don a personal headset for a historical overview of the iconic Changing of the Guard ceremony. Unlike typical tours that gather outside Buckingham Palace, this experience utilizes handpicked vantage points to guarantee the best views of the royal tradition. Listen to expert commentary explaining each part of the performance as you admire the shimmering Household Cavalry and capture photographs of the King's foot soldiers in their iconic red and black attire. The tour concludes outside of Buckingham Palace (Spur Road, London, United Ki