gory selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nPrivate Airport Transfer from Vienna Airport to Vienna Hotel\nPrivate Airport transfer from Vienna Hotel to Vienna Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional]\n\nVienna to Salzburg with sector ticket\nSalzburg to Innsbruck with sector ticket\nInnsbruck to Vienna with sector ticket\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nVienna City Tour with Schönbrunn Palace\nThe Sound of Music and Salt Mines Visit in Salzburg - Seat in Coach Basis\nEntrance ticket to Swarovski Kristallwelten\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/Viena_20.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/ViennaOperaHouse_108156170.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Schonbrunnpalace753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Salzburg_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Innsbruck_cityscape_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Swarovski_Museum_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Vienna_City_Hall_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014508/itinerary/Vienna_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014510', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014510', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Beautiful Benelux', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Brussels', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Brussels', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amsterdam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amsterdam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014510_0_20260919032509', 'price': 179514, 'packageSummary': "The 'Beautiful Benelux' package is an 8-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Brussels, Paris, and Amsterdam. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Grand Place and Atomium in Brussels, the majestic Eiffel Tower and Louvre Museum in Paris, and the historic Dam Square in Amsterdam. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic cruise along the River Seine, and a traditional canal cruise in Amsterdam, offering a perfect blend of culture, history, and breathtaking sights across these European destinations.", 'images': ['Brussels_Grand_Palace_753.jpg', 'Atomuim_753.jpg', 'Amsterdam6.jpg', 'Amsterdam_753.jpeg', 'Paris_City_new753.jpeg', 'Eiffeltowerwithseinecruise_753.jpeg', 'VersaillesPalace_new_753.jpg', 'Paris_new_753.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 179514, 'thumbnailImage': 'Belgium2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014510 is named 'Beautiful Benelux' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Brussels, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Brussels Transfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Brussels, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Brussels: Hop on Hop off & Mini Europe Brussels City Tour: Get in a red open top double deck bus and take a ride on one of the 2 lines with 24 hours pass. With this Hop-on Hop-off tour you can get on and off at any stop an unlimited number of times for a full day's sightseeing. The coach passes all the main sights in the city, including St Michael Cathedral, the Congress Column, the Atomium, Grand Place, Palace of Justice, the Royal Museum of Art and History and the Royal Palace, so you'll be able to see as much as you like in your own time. Mini Europe: Located at the foot of the Atomium, MINI-EUROPE is the only park where you can have a whitlestop tour around Europe in a few short hours. A truly unique voyage! Stroll amid the typical ambiance of the most beautiful towns of the Old Continent. The incomparable chimes of Big Ben welcome you to the heart of London. The gondolas and mandolins will invite you to discover the charms of Venice. Follow the T.G.V. from Paris to the other end of France. You can make the models work yourself: the eruption of Vesuvius, the fall of the Berlin Wall, the bullfight in Seville and many more. In total see 300 models and sites in a quite unequalled craftmanship. [Open Ticket for 24 hrs] Special Note: You can use the Atomium LINE of the hop on hop off route to help you reach the next famous attraction - Mini Europe (Entrance Ticket)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Amsterdam, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Brussels To Amsterdam By Train Transfers: Board the train from Brussels for Amsterdam (Approx. 3 Hrs)! Upon your arrival at Amsterdam train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Canal Cruise: By 1500 hrs make your way to Lindbergh Excursions Departure Point to Enjoy a marvellous canal cruise in Amsterdam. Enjoy a marvellous canal cruise in Amsterdam on board of a semi open electric boat with zero emissions. Discover Amsterdam's Canal Ring on a unique semi open boat (which can be closed for rain) and cruise down some of the hidden corners of the historic city center. Thanks to its diminutive size, the boat can access places that regular canal cruise boats can't. You will cruise the wide channels of the Amstel River in the 17th-century center, as well as some of the narrow canals of the infamous Red-Light District of De Wallen. Special Note: Please note cost of the train ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in at the hotel will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Amsterdam, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Amsterdam: Hop on Hop Off Tour Amsterdam City Tour: Choose a hop on hop off style to see the major attractions and enjoy the beauty of Amsterdam with a 1 Day valid ticket. Enjoy great panoramic views while following the carefully designed route passing all the major landmarks that Amsterdam has to offer. The specially designed glass roofs of the buses enable you to enjoy this beautiful and multi-faceted city to the full. Admire the famous canals with their beautiful, elegant canal houses, towers and bridges. You will also pass by interesting sites, such as the Wester Church, the Skinny Bridge, Amsterdam's tallest windmill and the major museums and attractions. You can get on and off as often as you like. [Open Ticket 1 Day], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Amsterdam to Paris via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train for Paris (Approx. 4 Hrs.). Upon your arrival at Paris train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in at the hotel will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour Paris City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour-long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time. Special Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris Day Free At Lerisure (Optional Activities) Louvre Museum Tour (Optional): Discover the world's largest museum. No need to stand in line! This guided tour offers the perfect opportunity to learn about the museum's huge collection and its greatest works of art, such as the Mona Lisa, the Venus de Milo, and the Coronation of Napoleon. OR Versailles Palace Tour (Optional): You can visit the huge Palace of Versailles by joining the guide on site. He will introduce you to the superb royal apartments while telling you about the life of the Kings of France of that time, from Francis I to Louis XVI. After this guided visit, which will immerse you in the history of France, you will have time to stroll through the Palace's gardens and visit the estate of Trianon by yourself., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Paris Transfers: From Paris hotel to the Airport in Private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 179514.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels envisaged or similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nBrussels\n\n\nBest Western City Centre / Floris Arlequin Grand Place / Ibis Brussels Centre Gare Midi or similar / B&b Hotel Brussels Centre Gare Du Midi\n\n\n\n\nAmsterdam\n\n\nHotel Prinsen Hotel / Ibis Amsterdam City West / Ibis Styles Amsterdam Amstel / Ibis Styles Amsterdam City or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hôtel Champerret-Elysées / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels envisaged or similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nBrussels\n\n\nThe President Brussels Hotel / Mercure Brussels Centre Midi / Hilton Garden Inn Brussels City Centre / Hotel Avenue Louise Brussels - Trademark Collection By Wyndham / Thon Hotel Brussels City Centre or similar\n\n\n\n\nAmsterdam\n\n\nXo Hotels Blue Tower / Olympic Hotel / Leonardo Royal Hotel Amsterdam / Mercure Amsterdam City Hotel / Tribe Amsterdam City / Hotel Arena / Leonardo Hotel Amsterdam City Center or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Brussels based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Amsterdam based on the hotel category selected or similar 3 Nights’ accommodation in Paris based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Brussels Airport to Brussels Hotel Departure Airport transfer from Paris Hotel to Paris Airport Train Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Brussels to Amsterdam 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Amsterdam to Paris Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Brussels - Hop on Hop off (24 hours) Brussels - Mini Europe -Entrance Ticket Amsterdam - Hop on Hop off (1 Day) Amsterdam - Canal Cruise with Semi Open Boat Paris - Paris Interactive City Tour + River Seine Cruise + 2nd Level Eiffel Tower Tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Beautiful Benelux' package is an 8-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Brussels, Paris, and Amsterdam. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Grand Place and Atomium in Brussels, the majestic Eiffel Tower and Louvre Museum in Paris, and the historic Dam Square in Amsterdam. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic cruise along the River Seine, and a traditional canal cruise in Amsterdam, offering a perfect blend of culture, history, and breathtaking sights across these European destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'Arrive Brussels\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Best Western City Centre (Standard) / The President Brussels (Value) or similar in Brussels'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "Brussels:\xa0Hop on Hop off & Mini Europe\n\xa0\nBrussels City Tour: Get in a red open top double deck bus and take a ride on one of the 2 lines with 24 hours pass. With this Hop-on Hop-off tour you can get on and off at any stop an unlimited number of times for a full day's sightseeing. The coach passes all the main sights in the city, including St Michael Cathedral, the Congress Column, the Atomium, Grand Place, Palace of Justice, the Royal Museum of Art and History and the Royal Palace, so you'll be able to see as much as you like in your own time.\xa0\n\xa0\nMini Europe: Located at the foot of the Atomium, MINI-EUROPE is the only park where you can have a whitlestop tour around Europe in a few short hours. A truly unique voyage! Stroll amid the typical ambiance of the most beautiful towns of the Old Continent. The incomparable chimes of Big Ben welcome you to the heart of London. The gondolas and mandolins will invite you to discover the charms of Venice. Follow the T.G.V. from Paris to the other end of France. You can make the models work yourself: the eruption of Vesuvius, the fall of the Berlin Wall, the bullfight in Seville and many more. In total see 300 models and sites in a quite unequalled craftmanship. [Open Ticket for 24 hrs]\n\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: You can use the Atomium LINE of the hop on hop off route to help you reach the next famous attraction - Mini Europe (Entrance Ticket).\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Best Western City Centre (Standard) / The President Brussels (Value) or similar in Brussels'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "Brussels To Amsterdam By Train \n\xa0\nTransfers:\n\nBoard the train from Brussels for Amsterdam (Approx. 3 Hrs)!\nUpon your arrival at Amsterdam train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nCanal Cruise: By 1500 hrs make your way to Lindbergh Excursions Departure Point to Enjoy a marvellous canal cruise in Amsterdam. Enjoy a marvellous canal cruise in Amsterdam on board of a semi open electric boat with zero emissions. Discover Amsterdam's Canal Ring on a unique semi open boat (which can be closed for rain) and cruise down some of the hidden corners of the historic city center. Thanks to its diminutive size, the boat can access places that regular canal cruise boats can't. You will cruise the wide channels of the Amstel River in the 17th-century center, as well as some of the narrow canals of the infamous Red-Light District of De Wallen.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the train ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed.\xa0\nCheck in at the hotel will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Prinsen\xa0 (Standard) / Xo Hotels Blue Tower (Value) or similar in Amsterdam\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "Amsterdam: Hop on Hop Off Tour\nAmsterdam City Tour: Choose a hop on hop off style to see the major attractions and enjoy the beauty of Amsterdam with a 1 Day valid ticket. Enjoy great panoramic views while following the carefully designed route passing all the major landmarks that Amsterdam has to offer. The specially designed glass roofs of the buses enable you to enjoy this beautiful and multi-faceted city to the full. Admire the famous canals with their beautiful, elegant canal houses, towers and bridges. You will also pass by interesting sites, such as the Wester Church, the Skinny Bridge, Amsterdam's tallest windmill and the major museums and attractions. You can get on and off as often as you like. [Open Ticket 1 Day]", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Prinsen\xa0 (Standard) / Xo Hotels Blue Tower (Value) or similar in Amsterdam\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': 'Amsterdam to Paris via Train\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station to board the train for Paris (Approx. 4 Hrs.).\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Paris train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed.\nCheck in at the hotel will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "Paris City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour\nParis City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour-long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 7, 'description': "Paris Day Free At Lerisure (Optional Activities)\n\xa0\nLouvre Museum Tour (Optional): Discover the world's largest museum. No need to stand in line! This guided tour offers the perfect opportunity to learn about the museum's huge collection and its greatest works of art, such as the Mona Lisa, the Venus de Milo, and the Coronation of Napoleon.\n\xa0\nOR\n\xa0\nVersailles Palace Tour (Optional): You can visit the huge Palace of Versailles by joining the guide on site. He will introduce you to the superb royal apartments while telling you about the life of the Kings of France of that time, from Francis I to Louis XVI. After this guided visit, which will immerse you in the history of France, you will have time to stroll through the Palace's gardens and visit the estate of Trianon by yourself.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Paris\n\xa0\nTransfers: From Paris hotel to the Airport in Private transfer.\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\n\xa0\n\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels envisaged or similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nBrussels\n\n\nBest Western City Centre / Floris Arlequin Grand Place / Ibis Brussels Centre Gare Midi or similar / B&b Hotel Brussels Centre Gare Du Midi\n\n\n\n\nAmsterdam\n\n\nHotel Prinsen Hotel / Ibis Amsterdam City West / Ibis Styles Amsterdam Amstel / Ibis Styles Amsterdam City or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hôtel 