or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/Belgium2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Brussels_Grand_Palace_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Atomuim_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Amsterdam6.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Amsterdam_753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Paris_City_new753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Eiffeltowerwithseinecruise_753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/VersaillesPalace_new_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014510/itinerary/Paris_new_753.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014806', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014806', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special with Icebreaker Cruise', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stokmarknes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Narvik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kiruna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG009291_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 505129, 'packageSummary': "The 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special with Icebreaker Cruise' package is a 9-day tour covering Stokmarknes, Kemi, Helsinki, Narvik, Kiruna, Tromso, and Rovaniemi. Throughout this Arctic adventure, participants will chase the mesmerizing Northern Lights, embark on a thrilling icebreaker cruise, and enjoy guided city sightseeing across these iconic Nordic destinations.", 'images': ['Tromso_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Northern_Lights_Tromso_753_Adobe.jpg', 'ArcticDay3.jpg', 'ArcticDay4.jpg', 'ArcticDay5.jpg', 'Rovaniemi2.jpg', 'ArcticIce.jpg', 'Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'Helsinki1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 505129, 'thumbnailImage': 'Arctic267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014806 is named 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special with Icebreaker Cruise' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tromso, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Tromso! The Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local representative will meet you outside the airport. Proceed to the hotel and check–in. Spend some free time on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Tromso - Fjellheisn Cable Car – Northern Lights Hunting Tour Today, we proceed for an orientation tour of Tromsø known for its role as a gateway to the Arctic. Next, we take a cable car to Fjellheisen and enjoy a spectacular view of Tromsø and its beautiful surroundings from above. Later in the evening, we proceed on a Northern Lights Hunting Tour. Tromsø is famous for being one of the best places in the world to see the Northern Lights., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Stokmarknes, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Polaria - Express Ferry to Harstad Today, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Narvik, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Sea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum Today, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today. Next, we proceed to Narvik., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kiruna, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda Today, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Arktikum Museum - Visit Santa Claus Village – Northern Lights Hunting tour Today, we proceed to Rovaniemi. Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus. Upon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Next, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Kemi, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Ice Breaker Cruise Today, we experience the unique Sampo Icebreaker Cruise in Lapland on the frozen sea in Kemi, Finland. Here we float and walk on the Ice. Later we drive to Kemi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Fly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church Today, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Return back home with pleasant memories! Today, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give us your suggestions. Till we meet again! Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 505129.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n01 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 nights at Scandic or similar in Kemi, Finland\n01 night at Scandic / Clarion or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n03 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 01st Apr 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g. Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of Euro 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour which is 9 Days, the total Tips amount is Euros 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 01st Apr, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that what is mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Services of our Thomas Cook Tour Manager or local representatives will be not be available while on land tour. He will not be there onboard the cruise. Thomas Cook tour manager will only be available if the group size is a minimum of 15 passengers. As a third person in a Triple room, no extra bed or cot will be provided. Instead a room with two queen beds will be provided. On days when you are taking internal flights, there is a possibility that we might provide packed meal in case the flight timing does not suit the meal time. All transfers and extensive sightseeing with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. All local taxes and services (Presently calculated as prevailing on 20th October 2021). A person below 12 years of age on date of return flight will be considered a child Infants are not allowed on this cruise On certain departure dates the tour routing could change. In some tours, there is also a possibility that the tour could operate in reverse itinerary. However you will not miss any sightseeing or excursions that are mentioned in the itinerary. Please check with your sales representative for final details. Certain sightseeing and excursions may not operate on public holidays. In some cities, there is a possibility that you may have to wait at the airport (in the terminal as would have been informed to you before departure by your booking office) for multiple flight arrivals/departures of different groups. Group transfer from the airport to the hotel on a day prior to departure Group transfer to the ship on day of embarkation All scheduled landings/excursions (subject to weather and ice conditions) Leadership throughout the voyage by our experienced Expedition Leader & Expedition Team Points to be Noted: It is advisable to book more than 120 days prior to the tour departure date as the internal ticket rate might increase closer to the departure date, resulting in an increase in the Tour cost The cabin category on the cruise is Deluxe Stateroom The airfare is based on the existing fare structure (Presently calculated as prevailing on 20th October 2021). Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in fuel price, change in government regulations, ticket taxes etc. charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passenger. Thomas Cook (I) Ltd will not be held responsible for the same Any damage caused to the hotel rooms or coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. Thomas Cook (I) Ltd will not be liable for the same The management reserves the right to claim from the passengers, any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in the schedule of trains, flights, coach, cruise or other services We reserve the right to amend, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursions advertised or substitute a hotel of similar class if deemed necessary We reserve the right to use alternate cruise liner for any particular departure, excursions advertised or substitute a cruise of similar class if deemed necessary Due to high occupancy on the cruise, it is possible that the cabins provided would be of alternate category The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only A date change fee, as applicable, will be levied on passengers who change their date of travel For the convenience of our passengers, we may sometimes will have to amend the itinerary. However all services will remain the same The company reserves the right to alter the order of the itinerary. The same will be informed to the client before departure Due to Trade Fairs and conventions in the cities, it is possible that the hotel accommodation provided would be outside the city. The same will be informed in advance Passengers can board the tour from the hub city. Those boarding from any other city can do so, however all expenses to/from the hub city is to be borne by the passengers Attractions in the theme parks may not operate/may change/entry restricted/closed without notice Other applicable taxes will be extra The company shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, injury, accident, death, delay, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out of the tour arrangement due to weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expenses must be borne by the passenger For all Joining Direct/deviating clients, there would be airport transfers. Tours operated subject to RBI/GOI regulations Part of the tour cost is payable in USD out of your BTQ. The foreign exchange component will be payable as per the rate of exchange prevailing on the date of payment of foreign exchange When the outbound sector of an Ex-India ticket is not utilized, the return segment cannot be utilized for one-way travel and there will be no refund for non-utilisation Please refer to the booking form for detailed “Terms & Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE212', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE212', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE212', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'Z