erry to Harstad\nToday, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum\nToday, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today.\xa0 Next, we proceed to Narvik.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda\nToday, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Arktikum Museum - Visit Santa Claus Village – Northern Lights Hunting tour \nToday, we proceed to Rovaniemi. Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus.\nUpon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Next, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\nIce Breaker Cruise \nToday, we experience the unique Sampo Icebreaker Cruise in Lapland on the frozen sea in Kemi, Finland. Here we float and walk on the Ice. Later we drive to Kemi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic or similar in Kemi, Finland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\nToday, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic / Clarion or similar in Helsinki, Finland'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nReturn back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give\xa0us your suggestions. Till we meet again!\xa0\n\xa0\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n01 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 nights at Scandic or similar in Kemi, Finland\n01 night at Scandic / Clarion or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n01 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 nights at Scandic or similar in Kemi, Finland\n01 night at Scandic / Clarion or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 505100.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n01 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 nights at Scandic or similar in Kemi, Finland\n01 night at Scandic / Clarion or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n03 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', '\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'NORWAY:\nTromso:\n\nOrientation Tour\xa0\nWhale Watching Cruise\nFjellheisen Cable Car\xa0\nVisit Polaria\xa0\nGuided Northern Lights Tour\xa0\nExpress Ferry to Harstad\n\nNarvik:\n\nVsist the Narvik War Museum\n\nStokmarknes:\n\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat\nVisit Hurtigruten Museum\n\nSWEDEN:\nJukkasjarvi:\n\nVisit the Ice Hotel with lunch\n\nKiruna:\n\nOrientation tour\nVisit Nuti Sami Silda with Reindeer Feeding\n\nFINLAND:\nRovaniemi:\n\nVisit the Santa Claus Village\xa0\nArctic Crossing with Certificate\xa0\n\nSaariselka:\n\nVisit Husky Farm and Enjoy a Forest Walk (NOV)\nOR\nVisit Husky Farm and Enjoy a Husky Ride (DEC)\xa0\n\nHelsinki:\n\nGuided City Tour of Helsinki\xa0\nVisIt Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\xa0\nVisit Sibelius Park and Sibelius Monument\n', 'NORWAY\nTromso\n\nOrientation tour\xa0\nFjellheisen Cable Car\xa0\nNorthern Lights Hunting Tour\xa0\nVisit Polaria\xa0\nExpress Ferry to Harstad\n\nStokmarknes\n\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat\nVisit Hurtigruten Museum\n\nSWEDEN\nJukkasjarvi\xa0\n\nVisit Narvik War Museum\nVisit the Ice Hotel with lunch\n\nKiruna\n\nVisit Nuti Sami Silda\n\nFINLAND\nRovaniemi\xa0\n\nVisit Arktikum\nVisit the Santa Claus Village\xa0\nNorthern Lights Hunting tour\xa0\n\nKemi\n\nIce Breaker Cruise\n\nHelsinki:\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour of Helsinki\xa0\nVisit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<div>Rest assured, Thomas Cook\'s experienced &amp; knowledgeable&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it\'s a question or a challenge, our&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Manager</span>&nbsp;is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</div>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 01st Apr 2026.\xa0\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g. Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of Euro 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour which is 9 Days, the total Tips amount is Euros 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 01st Apr, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that what is mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note:\n\nServices of our Thomas Cook Tour Manager or local representatives will be not be available while on land tour. He will not be there onboard the cruise. Thomas Cook tour manager will only be available if the group size is a minimum of 15 passengers.\nAs a third person in a Triple room, no extra bed or cot will be provided. Instead a room with two queen beds will be provided.\nOn days when you are taking internal flights, there is a possibility that we might provide packed meal in case the flight timing does not suit the meal time.\nAll transfers and extensive sightseeing with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nAll local taxes and services (Presently calculated as prevailing on 20th October 2021).\nA person below 12 years of age on date of return flight will be considered a child\nInfants are not allowed on this cruise\nOn certain departure dates the tour routing could change. In some tours, there is also a possibility that the tour could operate in reverse itinerary. However you will not miss any sightseeing or excursions that are mentioned in the itinerary. Please check with your sales representative for final details.\nCertain sightseeing and excursions may not operate on public holidays.\nIn some cities, there is a possibility that you may have to wait at the airport (in the terminal as would have been informed to you before departure by your booking office) for multiple flight arrivals/departures of different groups.\nGroup transfer from the airport to the hotel on a day prior to departure\nGroup transfer to the ship on day of embarkation\nAll scheduled landings/excursions (subject to weather and ice conditions)\nLeadership throughout the voyage by our experienced Expedition Leader & Expedition Team\n\n\xa0\nPoints to be Noted:\n\nIt is advisable to book more than 120 days prior to the tour departure date as the internal ticket rate might increase closer to the departure date, resulting in an increase in the Tour cost\nThe cabin category on the cruise is Deluxe Stateroom\nThe airfare is based on the existing fare structure (Presently calculated as prevailing on 20th October 2021). Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in fuel price, change in government regulations, ticket taxes etc. charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passenger. Thomas Cook (I) Ltd will not be held responsible for the same\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms or coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. Thomas Cook (I) Ltd will not be liable for the same\nThe management reserves the right to claim from the passengers, any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in the schedule of trains, flights, coach, cruise or other services\nWe reserve the right to amend, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursions advertised or substitute a hotel of similar class if deemed necessary\nWe reserve the right to use alternate cruise liner for any particular departure, excursions advertised or substitute a cruise of similar class if deemed necessary\nDue to high occupancy on the cruise, it is possible that the cabins provided would be of alternate category\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only\nA date change fee, as applicable, will be levied on passengers who change their date of travel\nFor the convenience of our passengers, we may sometimes will have to amend the itinerary. However all services will remain the same\nThe company reserves the right to alter the order of the itinerary. The same will be informed to the client before departure\nDue to Trade Fairs and conventions in the cities, it is possible that the hotel accommodation provided would be outside the city. The same will be informed in advance\nPassengers can board the tour from the hub city. Those boarding from any other city can do so, however all expenses to/from the hub city is to be borne by the passengers\nAttractions in the theme parks may not operate/may change/entry restricted/closed without notice\nOther applicable taxes will be extra\nThe company shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, injury, accident, death, delay, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out of the tour arrangement due to weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expenses must be borne by the passenger\nFor all Joining Direct/deviating clients, there would be airport transfers.\nTours operated subject to RBI/GOI regulations\nPart of the tour cost is payable in USD out of your BTQ. The foreign exchange component will be payable as per the rate of exchange prevailing on the date of payment of foreign exchange\nWhen the outbound sector of an Ex-India ticket is not utilized, the return segment cannot be utilized for one-way travel and there will be no refund for non-utilisation\nPlease refer to the booking form for detailed “Terms & Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/Arctic267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/Tromso_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/Northern_Lights_Tromso_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/ArcticDay3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/ArcticDay4.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/ArcticDay5.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/Rovaniemi2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/ArcticIce.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014806/itinerary/Helsinki1.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014750', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014750', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Greece: The Eternal Escape - Honeymoon Special', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Mykonos', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Mykonos', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Santorini', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Santorini', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014750_0_20260826044338', 'price': 226600, 'packageSummary': "The 'Greece: The Eternal Escape - Honeymoon Special' package is an 8-day romantic getaway covering the historic capital of Athens and the picturesque islands of Santorini and Mykonos. Designed specifically for couples, this itinerary offers a perfect blend of ancient history and island relaxation, featuring guided tours of the iconic Acropolis in Athens, scenic sunset cruises along the caldera in Santorini, and leisurely strolls through the charming, whitewashed streets and vibrant beach clubs of Mykonos. Participants will enjoy intimate candlelit dinners, wine tastings at local vineyards, and breathtaking views of the Aegean Sea, making it an unforgettable honeymoon experience.", 'images': ['Athens.jpg', 'AcropolisinAthens.avif', 'AdobeStock_67990916.jpeg', 'Mykons753.jpg', 'Santorini_1.jpeg', 'SunsetonthefamousOiacityGreece.jpeg', 'Athense_4.jpeg', 'Athens_5.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 226600, 'thumbnailImage': 'OiaVillageduringsunset.GreeceSantorini.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Honeymoon'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Honeymoon Special', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014750 is named 'Greece: The Eternal Escape - Honeymoon Special' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Athens, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Athens Transfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion Timeless Romance Under the Acropolis Enjoy a leisurely 2 hour walking tour through the charming Plaka district with a private expert guide, bringing Athens’ myths and history to life. After your stroll, indulge in a romantic 3 course dinner with breathtaking Acropolis views. Round trip transfers are included for a seamless and memorable evening, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half-Day Guided Tour Of Athens On Shared Basis (SIC) Athens Sightseeing - The Acropolis & Acropolis Museum: Step into history on a half-day guided tour of Athens. The morning begins at the Panathenaic Stadium, birthplace of the modern Olympic Games, then past the Temple of Olympian Zeus and the elegant Athens Trilogy — University, Academy, and National Library. Ascend to the legendary Acropolis to explore the Parthenon, Erechtheion, and Temple of Athena Nike. End your morning at the Acropolis Museum, where ancient treasures are brought to life. [Entrance fees to Acropolis & Museum is included] Special Note: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick up for the same will be from selected central points., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Mykonos, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Athens To Mykonos & Evening Walking Tour Transfers: Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Port for the ferry to Mykonos. Upon arrival at Mykonos there will be a shared transfer from the port to the Hotel. Complimentary Guided walking tour of Mykonos: In the evening, enjoy a guided walking tour of Mykonos’ Chora, discovering hidden alleys, historic windmills, Little Venice, and Panagia Paraportiani Church., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Mykonos, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Free At Leisure Mykonos Lighthouse Sunset Experience {Optional Activity} Enjoy private round trip transfers to the iconic Mykonos Lighthouse for sweeping Aegean sunset views with an idyllic backdrop for romantic photos and quiet moments together. The evening continues with a delightful 3 course dinner overlooking the shimmering sea and the famous Mykonos windmills. [The supplement cost of € 190/- Per person covering transfers hotel-lighthouse-restaurant-hotel and 3-course dinner with sea view] Private or Semi Private Catamaran Cruise to Delos & Rhenia {Optional Activity} Sail aboard a modern Lagoon catamaran for a five hour journey through turquoise waters, secluded coves, and iconic Aegean landscapes. Enjoy onboard lunch, refreshing drinks, and seamless round trip transfers: “The perfect blend of privacy, comfort, and timeless island beauty” [The supplement cost of €550 per person for private, €215 per person for semi-private (covering cruise and Return transfers)], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Santorini, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mykonos To Santorini Transfers: Today you will have a shared transfer from the hotel to the Port for the ferry to Santorini. Upon arrival at Santorini there will be a shared transfer from the port to the Hotel. Special Note: The check in at the hotel will be as per the standard hotel time. The Ultimate Honeymoon Stage – Flying Dress Photoshoot Experience Capture iconic Santorini moments with a professional flying dress photoshoot in Imerovigli or Oia’s breathtaking caldera setting. Enjoy expert guidance, 30–40 fully edited images, and seamless round trip transfers: “A Timeless Keepsake Of Your Honeymoon”, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Santorini, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Volcanic Adventure & Sunset In Oia Transfers: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick-up for the same will be from selected central points Volcanic Adventure & Sunset in Oia: Today Embark on a guided tour to Santorini’s volcano and hot springs, then sail to Thirassia island for a glimpse into traditional island life. Conclude with a magical sunset in Oia. Cruise around the volcanic islands of Santorini's Caldera on a unique Greek traditional boat. First, sail to Nea Kameni lava islet. Guided walking tour through an ascending path to reach its top where the crater of the still active volcano lies. Enjoy incredible sights of Santorini from a different angle. Return to the boat and continue to the second lava islet called Palea Kameni, also known as the Hot Springs. Jump off the boat and dive into green sulfur thermal waters. Next is the traditional island of Thirassia where you will enjoy some free time. You can relax at the picturesque small port of Thirassia, have lunch (on your own) or visit the village of Manolas, accessed by winding stairs, either by walking or riding a donkey., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Santorini For Athens Transfers: Shared transfer from the island hotel to the port, followed by a speed ferry back to Athens A private transfer from Athens Port to Athens hotel Hammam – Exclusive Private Couple’s Experience {Optional Activity} Indulge in a luxurious 90 minute private hammam ritual designed exclusively for two, complete with refreshing juices, fine wine, and curated delicacies. Enjoy full privacy, serene wellness moments, and seamless round trip transfers: “The perfect intimate escape for honeymooners” [The supplement cost of € 250/- Per person covering return transfers & the 90' hammam treatment], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Athens Transfers: Private transfer will take you to Athens International Airport Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 226600.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nPREMIUM CATEGORY (5* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nWyndham Grand Athens or similar\n\n\nRoyal Myconian or similar\n\n\nApeiron Blue Santorini or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0STANDARD CATEGORY (3* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nCentral Hotel or similar\n\n\nErato Hotel or similar\n\n\nMakris Beach Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY (4* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nAthens Avenue or similar\n\n\nAeolos Resort Mykonos or similar\n\n\nDaedalus Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\nTimeless Romance Under the Acropolis (3 course dinner in Athens)\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Athens based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Mykonos based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Santorini based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Athens based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Timeless Romance Under the Acropolis (3 course dinner in Athens) Transportation: Private Airport Transfer from Athens Airport to Hotel Private transfer from Athens hotel to Port for the ferry to Mykonos Shared transport from Mykonos Port to the hotel and back to port Shared transport from Santorini port to hotel Shared transport from Santorini Hotel to Santorini Port Private transfer from Athens Port to Athens Hotel Private Airport Transfer from Athens Hotel to Athens Airport Ferry Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] Normal Ferry ticket – Economy class from Athens to Mykonos Speed Ferry ticket - Economy class from Mykonos to Santorini Speed Ferry ticket - Economy class from Santorini to Athens Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis * from a designated point) Timeless Romance Under the Acropolis Athens City Tour with Acropolis Museum on sharing basis tour coach. Walking tour in Mykonos Town (Complimentary Gesture) The Ultimate Honeymoon Stage – Flying Dress Photoshoot Experience in Mykonos Volcanic Islands Cruise on sharing basis with transportation from/to meeting point - clients need to go by themselves to the pick-up point for the tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 May 2026 – 15 October 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Greece: The Eternal Escape - Honeymoon Special' package is an 8-day romantic getaway covering the historic capital of Athens and the picturesque islands of Santorini and Mykonos. Designed specifically for couples, this itinerary offers a perfect blend of ancient history and island relaxation, featuring guided tours of the iconic Acropolis in Athens, scenic sunset cruises along the caldera in Santorini, and leisurely strolls through the charming, whitewashed streets and vibrant beach clubs of Mykonos. Participants will enjoy intimate candlelit dinners, wine tastings at local vineyards, and breathtaking views of the Aegean Sea, making it an unforgettable honeymoon experience.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Athens\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion\n\xa0\nTimeless Romance Under the Acropolis\nEnjoy a leisurely 2 hour walking tour through the charming Plaka district with a private expert guide, bringing Athens’ myths and history to life. After your stroll, indulge in a romantic 3 course dinner with breathtaking Acropolis views. Round trip transfers are included for a seamless and memorable evening', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Central\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Athens Avenue\xa0(Value) /\xa0Wyndham Grand\xa0(Premium) or similar\xa0in Athens'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nHalf-Day Guided Tour Of Athens On Shared Basis (SIC)\nAthens Sightseeing - The Acropolis & Acropolis Museum: Step into history on a half-day guided tour of Athens. The morning begins at the Panathenaic Stadium, birthplace of the modern Olympic Games, then past the Temple of Olympian Zeus and the elegant Athens Trilogy — University, Academy, and National Library. Ascend to the legendary Acropolis to explore the Parthenon, Erechtheion, and Temple of Athena Nike. End your morning at the Acropolis Museum, where ancient treasures are brought to life. [Entrance fees to Acropolis & Museum is included]\nSpecial Note: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick up for the same will be from selected central points.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Central\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Athens Avenue\xa0(Value) /\xa0Wyndham Grand\xa0(Premium) or similar\xa0in Athens'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nAthens To Mykonos\xa0& Evening Walking Tour\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nToday you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Port for the ferry to Mykonos.\nUpon arrival at Mykonos there will be a shared transfer from the port to the Hotel.\n\n\xa0\nComplimentary Guided walking tour of Mykonos: In the evening, enjoy a guided walking tour of Mykonos’ Chora, discovering hidden alleys, historic windmills, Little Venice, and Panagia Paraportiani Church.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Erato\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Aeolos Resort\xa0(Value) /\xa0Royal Myconian\xa0(Premium) or similar in Mykonos'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay Free At Leisure\xa0\n\xa0\nMykonos Lighthouse Sunset Experience {Optional Activity}\nEnjoy private round trip transfers to the iconic Mykonos Lighthouse for sweeping Aegean sunset views with an idyllic backdrop for romantic photos and quiet moments together. The evening continues with a delightful 3 course dinner overlooking the shimmering sea and the famous Mykonos windmills.\xa0\n[The supplement cost of € 190/- Per person covering transfers hotel-lighthouse-restaurant-hotel and 3-course dinner with sea view]\n\xa0\nPrivate or Semi Private Catamaran Cruise to Delos & Rhenia {Optional Activity}\nSail aboard a modern Lagoon catamaran for a five hour journey through turquoise waters, secluded coves, and iconic Aegean landscapes. Enjoy onboard lunch, refreshing drinks, and seamless round trip transfers: “The perfect blend of privacy, comfort, and timeless island beauty” [The supplement cost of €550 per person for private, €215 per person for semi-private (covering cruise and Return transfers)]', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Erato\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Aeolos Resort\xa0(Value) /\xa0Royal Myconian\xa0(Premium) or similar in Mykonos'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nMykonos To Santorini\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nToday you will have a shared transfer from the hotel to the Port for the ferry to Santorini.\nUpon arrival at Santorini there will be a shared transfer from the port to the Hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nThe check in at the hotel will be as per the standard hotel time.\n\nThe Ultimate Honeymoon Stage – Flying Dress Photoshoot Experience\nCapture iconic Santorini moments with a professional flying dress photoshoot in Imerovigli or Oia’s breathtaking caldera setting. Enjoy expert guidance, 30–40 fully edited images, and seamless round trip transfers: “A Timeless Keepsake Of Your Honeymoon”', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Makris Beach (Standard) /\xa0Daedalus\xa0(Value) /\xa0Apeiron Blue\xa0(Premium) or similar in Santorini'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nVolcanic Adventure & Sunset In Oia\nTransfers: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick-up for the same will be from selected central points\nVolcanic Adventure & Sunset in Oia: Today Embark on a guided tour to Santorini’s volcano and hot springs, then sail to Thirassia island for a glimpse into traditional island life. Conclude with a magical sunset in Oia. Cruise around the volcanic islands of Santorini's Caldera on a unique Greek traditional boat. First, sail to Nea Kameni lava islet. Guided walking tour through an ascending path to reach its top where the crater of the still active volcano lies. Enjoy incredible sights of Santorini from a different angle. Return to the boat and continue to the second lava islet called Palea Kameni, also known as the Hot Springs. Jump off the boat and dive into green sulfur thermal waters. Next is the traditional island of Thirassia where you will enjoy some free time. You can relax at the picturesque small port of Thirassia, have lunch (on your own) or visit the village of Manolas, accessed by winding stairs, either by walking or riding a donkey.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Makris Beach\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Daedalus\xa0(Value) /\xa0Apeiron Blue\xa0(Premium) or similar in Santorini'}, {'day': 7, 'description': "\xa0\nDepart\xa0Santorini For Athens\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nShared transfer from the island hotel to the port, followed by a speed ferry back to Athens\nA private transfer from Athens Port to Athens hotel\xa0\n\nHammam – Exclusive Private Couple’s Experience {Optional Activity}\nIndulge in a luxurious 90 minute private hammam ritual designed exclusively for two, complete with refreshing juices, fine wine, and curated delicacies. Enjoy full privacy, serene wellness moments, and seamless round trip transfers: “The perfect intimate escape for honeymooners”\n[The supplement cost of € 250/- Per person covering return transfers & the 90' hammam treatment]", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Central\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Athens Avenue\xa0(Value) /\xa0Wyndham Grand\xa0(Premium) or similar\xa0in Athens'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Athens\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0Private transfer will take you to Athens International Airport\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nPREMIUM CATEGORY (5* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nWyndham Grand Athens or similar\n\n\nRoyal Myconian or similar\n\n\nApeiron Blue Santorini or similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0STANDARD CATEGORY (3* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nCentral Hotel or similar\n\n\nErato Hotel or similar\n\n\nMakris Beach Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY (4* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nAthens Avenue or similar\n\n\nAeolos Resort Mykonos or similar\n\n\nDaedalus Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n\n\n\nPREMIUM CATEGORY (5* HOTELS OR SIMILAR)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nMykonos\n\n\nSantorini\n\n\n\n\nWyndham Grand Athens or similar\n\n\nRoyal Myconian or similar\n\n\nApeiron Blue Santorini or similar\n\n\n\n', '0': '\n\n\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0