 in coach basis & from a designated point)\n\nHalf-day City tour of Athens with new Acropolis Museum\xa0 on sharing basis tour coach.\nThe Saronic Islands Cruise on shared basis (SIC)\nPanoramic city tour of Thessaloniki on shared basis (SIC)\nMeteora Excursion on shared basis (SIC)\nHalkidiki & Sithonia Excursion on shared basis (SIC)\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Insurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n\n\xa0\nAdd On - Athens (1 Night Extension)\n\nPrivate transfers from airport-hotel-airport\n1 Night accommodation in Athens as per hotels mentioned on Bed & Breakfast basis\n\n\xa0\nPlease Refer to the below pricing for the Supplement Cost\n\n\n\n\nHOLIDAY PRICE (PER PERSON) IN EUR + INR (INSURANCE)\n\n\n\n\nTravel Validity:\n\n\nAverage Pricing based on 6 Months (Apr - Sep 2026)\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n\n\nTWIN\nSHARE\n\n\nTRIPLE SHARE\n\n\nSINGLE ROOMING\n\n\nCHILD WITH BED (06 - 11.99 YRS)\n\n\nCHILD W/O BED (02 – 05.99 YRS)\n\n\n\n\n3\n\n\nEuro\xa0345\n\n\nEuro\xa0310\n\n\nEuro 500\n\n\nEuro295\n\n\nEuro\xa0295\n\n\n\n\n4\n\n\nEuro\xa0\xa0355\n\n\nEuro 295\n\n\nEuro\xa0485\n\n\nEuro\xa0\xa0305\n\n\nEuro\xa0305\n\n\n\n\n5\n\n\nEuro\xa0360\n\n\nEuro\xa0300\n\n\nEuro\xa0510\n\n\nEuro\xa0340\n\n\nEuro 340\n\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\xa0\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 15 October 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/Thessaloniki.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Athens.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/AcropolisinAthens.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Image_3.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Thessaloniki_1.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Metoro.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Halkidiki.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014606/itinerary/Thessaloniki.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG011764', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG011764', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Explore Georgia', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bakuriani', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bakuriani', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batumi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG011764_0_20260817113815.pdf', 'price': 84483, 'packageSummary': "The 'Explore Georgia' package is an 8-day tour covering the historic capital of Tbilisi, the scenic mountain resort of Bakuriani, and the vibrant coastal city of Batumi. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, the charming Old Town of Tbilisi, the stunning alpine landscapes of Bakuriani, and the scenic Batumi Boulevard along the Black Sea coast. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, cable car rides offering panoramic mountain views, outdoor alpine activities, and opportunities to experience traditional Georgian wine tasting and local cuisine.", 'images': ['Tibilisi_753.jpg', 'Anauri_753.jpg', 'Mtskheta.jpg', 'Borjomi Central Park.jpg', 'batumi-it.jpg', 'Batumi-image.jpg', 'Ananuri.jpg', 'Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 84483, 'thumbnailImage': 'SRP_Georgia.png', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG011764 is named \'Explore Georgia\' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival Tbilisi Welcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel. Go for Tbilisi City Tour. Start with the world largest orthodox Holy Trinity cathedral, Continue to Rike Park and then cross the Bridge of Peace. Proceed to the clock tower of famous Rezo Gabriadze Theatre, Anchiskhati basilica, visit Sioni Cathedral. Walk down to the district of Sulfur bath houses passing by the only mosque in Tbilisi. Stroll through the Sharden area full of narrow streets with cozy cafés, wine tasting bars, souvenir shops, and breathe in the living past. Continue to Metekhi church and monument to Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi. There we will take Cable car to Narikala Fortress. The best place to release adrenaline, dopamine, oxytocin, serotonin, endorphins and just feel happy. Charge with emotions and unforgettable memories., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mtskheta – Gori Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Our road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord, is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people. Gori is one of the important cities on the Silk Road, during the tour you will see museum of the Joseph Stalin. Georgia dedicated to the life of Joseph Stalin, the leader of the Soviet Union, who was born in Gori. The Museum retains its Soviet-era characteristics. The museum has three sections, all located in the town\'s central square. It was officially dedicated to Stalin in 1957. With the downfall of the Soviet Union and independence movement of Georgia, the museum was closed in 1989, but has since been reopened, and is a popular tourist attraction., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Borjomi Tour - Bakuriani (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel. Modern Borjomi is one of the popular resorts in Georgia, which is suitable for ecotourism and family holidays. Its convenient location in the beautiful mountains of the Lesser Caucasus attracts many tourists all year round with its landscapes, the opportunity to relax and improve your health. There are dozens of mineral springs in Borjomi. The main mineral spring is located in the Central Park of Borjomi. Visit to the city park Borjomi. Borjomi Central Park is a well-groomed place with a lot of vegetation, clean air, which is considered healing here, and a pleasant atmosphere where residents and guests of the city like to relax. Central Park gained its fame thanks to the city’s main hot spring of mineral water, which anyone can try for free. The source is located in the park in a beautiful blue pavilion with a dome with a glass roof. The main ally of the Central Park stretches along the Borjomula River passing here, over which bridges are installed, the length of the park itself is about a kilometer., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bakuriani, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bakuriani - Batumi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Check out from the hotel and we will start the tour by driving to the western part of Georgia to Batumi, Check-in and rest of the day at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bakuriani, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Batumi City Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Piazza and St. Nicholas Church - anyone visiting Batumi will sooner or later end up at the Piazza. The square is located in the heart of Batumi. Unlike several more pleasant parks in Batumi, chaotic traffic dominates the square. While you will be able to relax here, there are some sights around the square worth visiting. The one of the famous landmark dominating Piazza is St. Nicholas Church, which is still worth to visit. Seaside Park - forms an important part of the urban landscape of Batumi. The Park was constricted in several phases by central government initiative as infrastructure improvements but are very much associated with strolling and leisurely enjoyment in the minds of Georgians. Miracle Park - Located in Batumi Boulevard. Park is an incredible family destination, which offers to residents and tourists entertainment activities like: yacht club, Ferris wheel, souvenir shops, a romantic statue coffee for two in the park, to rotating statue "Ali and Nino". Statue “Ali and Nino” - which is located in the “Miracle Park”, invites every tourist to the show. It\'s a mechanical statue about love were Ali and Nino merge into each other. Boulevard - This large boulevard is one of the longest in Batumi. But it is also one of the most luxurious! The most famous places can be found there: statue Ali and Nino, Bamboo square, fountains, summer theatre, zoo corner and more. The best moment to walk in the Batumi Boulevard is an evening while it is all illuminated. That is definitely the best way to enjoy the “most famous boulevard in Batumi”. Symbolizing the distinctiveness of the Georgian alphabet and people, this is an interesting take on the city’s evolving architecture. Designed in the shape of a DNA, in its familiar double helix pattern, the two helix bands ascend the tower holding 33 letters of the Georgian alphabet, each being 4 meters tall. These alphabets made of aluminum are a sight in their own!, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Batumi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Batumi – Ananuri & Gudauri Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Ananuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round tower, is mostly in ruins. Gudauri Ski Resort - is a small touristic settlement and ski mountain resort located at the altitude of 3,000m on the southern slopes of the Lesser Caucasus range of Georgia. Gudauri is situated 120 km from Tbilisi. You can reach it by the Georgian Military Road for about 2 hours by car. It has served as an important link between Europe and Asia since ancient times, though it was only after Russia’s annexation of east Georgia in the 19th century and the subsequent improvement of the track for troop movements that it became known as the “Military Highway”. Today it serves as the best route via which we can enjoy the dramatic scenery, crystal-clear air and indescribable grandeur of the mighty Caucasus Mountains. Vicinity of Stepantsminda is picturesque. There is a river Thergi running below the town, with snowed peaks of Caucasus rising among which the Mount Kazbek standing out, with its 5033m height. There are quite a few valley glaciers and forests, both deciduous and coniferous. Fresh mountain air and mineral springs of Stepantsminda are considered to be the main therapy for breathing or eating disorders., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice Other SLAB PRICES:VALID FROM 01 AUG 2026 - 23 MAR 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-10 PAX STANDARD 685 685 831 VALUE 749 813 895 PREMIUM 923 987 1069, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 84483.0. Hotels envisaged include: \nHotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard) or similar in Bakuriani\nHotel New Wave Batumi (Standard) in or similar Batumi\n, \nHotel\xa0Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Value) or similar in Bakuriani\nHotel\xa0New Wave Batumi (Value) or similar in Batumi\n, \nHotel\xa0Pullman Axis Tower Tbilisi (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Premium) or similar in Bakuriani\nHotel\xa0New Wave Batumi (Premium) or similar in Batumi\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n. Inclusions: 04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi 01 night stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Bakuriani 02 night stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Batumi Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Mtskheta – Gori Tour (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Borjomi Tour - Bakuriani (PVT Basis) Bakuriani - Batumi (PVT Basis) Batumi City Tour (PVT Basis) Batumi – Ananuri & Gudauri Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Entrance fee for, Cab