ld Town of Tbilisi, the stunning alpine landscapes of Bakuriani, and the scenic Batumi Boulevard along the Black Sea coast. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, cable car rides offering panoramic mountain views, outdoor alpine activities, and opportunities to experience traditional Georgian wine tasting and local cuisine.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival Tbilisi\nWelcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.).', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Pullman Axis Tower Tbilisi (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.\n\xa0\nGo for Tbilisi City Tour. Start with the world largest orthodox Holy Trinity cathedral, Continue to Rike Park and then cross the Bridge of Peace. Proceed to the clock tower of famous Rezo Gabriadze Theatre, Anchiskhati basilica, visit Sioni Cathedral. Walk down to the district of Sulfur bath houses passing by the only mosque in Tbilisi. Stroll through the Sharden area full of narrow streets with cozy cafés, wine tasting bars, souvenir shops, and breathe in the living past.\nContinue to Metekhi church and monument to Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi.\xa0\nThere we will take Cable car to Narikala Fortress. The best place to release adrenaline, dopamine, oxytocin, serotonin, endorphins and just feel happy. Charge with emotions and unforgettable memories.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Pullman Axis Tower Tbilisi (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nMtskheta – Gori Tour (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nOur road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord, is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people.\n\xa0\nGori is one of the important cities on the Silk Road, during the tour you will see museum of the Joseph Stalin. Georgia dedicated to the life of Joseph Stalin, the leader of the Soviet Union, who was born in Gori. The Museum retains its Soviet-era characteristics. The museum has three sections, all located in the town\'s central square. It was officially dedicated to Stalin in 1957. With the downfall of the Soviet Union and independence movement of Georgia, the museum was closed in 1989, but has since been reopened, and is a popular tourist attraction.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Pullman Axis Tower Tbilisi (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Borjomi Tour - Bakuriani (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.\nModern Borjomi is one of the popular resorts in Georgia, which is suitable for ecotourism and family holidays. Its convenient location in the beautiful mountains of the Lesser Caucasus attracts many tourists all year round with its landscapes, the opportunity to relax and improve your health. There are dozens of mineral springs in Borjomi. The main mineral spring is located in the Central Park of Borjomi.\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit to the city park Borjomi. Borjomi Central Park is a well-groomed place with a lot of vegetation, clean air, which is considered healing here, and a pleasant atmosphere where residents and guests of the city like to relax. Central Park gained its fame thanks to the city’s main hot spring of mineral water, which anyone can try for free. The source is located in the park in a beautiful blue pavilion with a dome with a glass roof. The main ally of the Central Park stretches along the Borjomula River passing here, over which bridges are installed, the length of the park itself is about a kilometer.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Pullman Axis Tower Tbilisi (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nBakuriani - Batumi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nCheck out from the hotel and we will start the tour by driving to the western part of Georgia to Batumi, Check-in and rest of the day at leisure.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard) / (Value) / (Premium) or similar in Bakuriani'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nBatumi City Tour (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nPiazza and St. Nicholas Church\xa0-\xa0anyone visiting Batumi will sooner or later end up at the Piazza. The square is located in the heart of Batumi. Unlike several more pleasant parks in Batumi, chaotic traffic dominates the square. While you will be able to relax here, there are some sights around the square worth visiting. The one of the famous landmark dominating Piazza is St. Nicholas Church, which is still worth to visit.\xa0\n\xa0\nSeaside Park - forms an important part of the urban landscape of Batumi. The Park was constricted in several phases by central government initiative as infrastructure improvements but are very much associated with strolling and leisurely enjoyment in the minds of Georgians.\xa0\n\xa0\nMiracle Park - Located in Batumi Boulevard. Park is an incredible family destination, which offers to residents and tourists entertainment activities like: yacht club, Ferris wheel, souvenir shops, a romantic statue coffee for two in the park, to rotating statue "Ali and Nino".\n\xa0\nStatue “Ali and Nino” - which is located in the “Miracle Park”, invites every tourist to the show. It\'s a mechanical statue about love were Ali and Nino merge into each other.\n\xa0\nBoulevard - This large boulevard is one of the longest in Batumi. But it is also one of the most luxurious! The most famous places can be found there: statue Ali and Nino, Bamboo square, fountains, summer theatre, zoo corner and more. The best moment to walk in the Batumi Boulevard is an evening while it is all illuminated. That is definitely the best way to enjoy the “most famous boulevard in Batumi”.\n\xa0\nSymbolizing the distinctiveness of the Georgian alphabet and people, this is an interesting take on the city’s evolving architecture. Designed in the shape of a DNA, in its familiar double helix pattern, the two helix bands ascend the tower holding 33 letters of the Georgian alphabet, each being 4 meters tall. These alphabets made of aluminum are a sight in their own!', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Wave Batumi (Standard) / (Value) / (Premium) or similar in Batumi'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nBatumi – Ananuri & Gudauri Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nAnanuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round t