Fragonard – French Perfume Museum\nIllumination Tour of Paris\xa0\nSeine River Cruise\xa0\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\nSwitzerland:\n\nVisit Glacier 3000\xa0\nRide on the Scenic Golden Pass Train\nOrientation tour of Geneva\nOrientation Tour of Gstaad\nOrientation Tour of Montreux\nOrientation Tour of Lucerne\nCruise on Lake Lucerne\nVisit Lindt Home of Chocolate\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 08 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 24 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\nAIRLINE AND AIRFARE:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJOINING DIRECT CLIENTS:\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHOTELS:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCOACHES:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\n\n\xa0\nMEALS:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSIGHTSEEING:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGENERAL:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/Switzerland567.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/Zurich_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/Zurich753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/9063_Lucerne_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/Golden_Pass_Train.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/EiffelTower_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/VersaillesPalace_new_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/DisneylandParis.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015029/itinerary/Paris_new_753.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014552', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014552', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Swiss Special', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Moritz', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Montreux', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Montreux', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Montreux', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014552_0_20260916160450.pdf', 'price': 194909, 'packageSummary': "The 'Swiss Special' package is an 8-day tour covering St Moritz, Central and Southern Switzerland, Montreux, and Zurich. The itinerary includes visits to the glamorous resort town of St Moritz, the scenic shores of Lake Geneva in Montreux, and the bustling streets of Zurich. Participants will enjoy breathtaking alpine train journeys, guided city sightseeing, cable car rides to stunning mountain peaks, and opportunities to explore historic castles and local Swiss chocolate shops.", 'images': ['Zurich_1.jpg', '9063_Lucerne_Switzerland_753.jpg', '89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', '77233_Matterhorn_slopes_Zermatt_Switzerland_753.jpg', '62869_Lake_Geneva_Montreux_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'Glacier.jpg', 'Montreux.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 194909, 'thumbnailImage': 'Glacier.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014552 is named \'Swiss Special\' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Zurich, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zurich Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Zurich airport, you will walk across to the Flughafen station (located adjacent to the airport) for your train to Central Switzerland. From train station transfer on your own to the hotel. Local Sightseeing (Optional): Explore Lucerne with a Swiss Pass. Discover Lucerne’s highlights within walking distance, including the iconic Chapel Bridge and Water Tower – Switzerland’s most photographed landmark. Zurich Airport Observation Deck (Optional): Stop by before your shuttle for close-up views of aircraft. Deck B: Public area with insights into airport operations. Deck E: Free for passengers with boarding pass. Lindt Home of Chocolate (Optional): Enjoy an interactive chocolate tour, the world’s largest Lindt shop (500 m²), and a spectacular chocolate fountain. Stoos Funicular Adventure (Optional): Ride the world’s steepest funicular (110% gradient) to Stoos village. Free with Swiss Half Fare Card. Swiss National Museum, Zurich (Optional): Explore Swiss history in a modern extension behind century-old walls. Discounted with Swiss Half Fare Card. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - St Moritz, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zurich To Central Switzerland By Train Zurich City Tour: This panoramic tour takes you across the famous Bahnhofstrasse and the banking center of the lake with a view of the snow-capped mountains, part of the old town with its magnificent guild houses and the churches St. Peter, Grossmünster and Fraumünster. You’ll see the university quarter and the residential area Zürichberg, the National Museum and the Kunsthaus. Transfers: Make your way to the Zurich train station for your onward journey to Central Switzerland. Upon arrival at train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mt. Titlis Excursion Mt. Titlis Excursion: Don\'t miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier\'s deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10\'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe\'s highest suspension bridge. (In conjunction with Swiss Pass) Swiss Museum of Transport (Optional): Today Sweet Chocolate Adventure awaits you at the famous Swiss Museum of Transport - Use the entrance ticket to head inside the Swiss Chocolate Adventure, a new attraction located at the Swiss Museum of Transport. Take your seat on a traveling cart to embark on a multimedia journey about Swiss chocolate. Listen to commentary on your audio guide as you pull up to 10 different displays to learn about the history of Swiss chocolate and how it has produced, transported and sold. [50% Discount with Swiss Pass] Convertible style cable car ‘CabriO’ (Optional): Later “Feel the wind in your hair in a convertible style cable car (CabriO)". Ride the unique double-decker cable car with an open upper deck to Mount Stanserhorn (1,900 m). Enjoy fresh air and stunning 360° views as you ascend. [Free with Swiss Pass], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Jungfraujoch Excursion Jungfraujoch Excursion: Don\'t miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world-famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Mt. Matterhorn Excursion: The Matterhorn – mystical, majestic, the mountain of mountains. No one can escape its fascination. Neither locals nor guests. Triangular. A cragged rock “tooth” ranging into the heavens. Standing alone on the horizon. A magnet for alpinists, aesthetic emblem, mountain with ideal proportions. Rugged rock with magical light.There are a wide variety of different attractions to be discovered around the Matterhorn. A top excursion is Gornergrat. On this three-thousand metre mountain ridge there is a viewing platform with a truly unforgettable view of the Matterhorn and the surrounding mountain world. Our if you prefer, the Matterhorn can also be admired from the Rothorn. The Matterhorn glacier paradise is the highest summer ski region in Europe and is open 365 days a year. And there is still plenty to do when the sun isn’t shining! The Matterhorn Museum explains the historic development of Zermatt from a mountain village to an Alpine holiday resort and also has many photographs and facts about the first ascent of the Matterhorn., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Montreux, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central / Southern Switzerland To Montreux By Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Montreux with Swiss Pass. Upon your arrival at Montreux train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Montreux, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Montreux: Glacier 3000 Glacier 3000: Today escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer – including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks – Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland. Bollywood Tour (Optional Tour): You can opt to partake in a “Bollywood Tour” - Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Montreux, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Montreux Transfers: Make you way to the Montreux train station to go to the Airport for your journey back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 194909.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nIbis Zurich City West | Swiss Night By Fassbind | Ibis Styles Zurich City Center | Design Hotel Plattenhof | Montana | Welcome Inn| | Hotel Sternen Oerlikon Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nVilla Toscane | Hotel De Chailly | J5 Hotels Helvetie Montreux | Bon Port or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nZuri By Fassbind | 25hours Hotel Zurich West | Krone Unterstrass | Hotel Allegra | Holiday Inn Zurich Messe or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nEden Palace Au Lac | Rene Capt Golf or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental breakfast at the hotel (except on the day of arrival)\xa0\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 1 Night accommodation in Zurich based on the hotel category selected or similar 4 Nights’ accommodation in Central / Southern Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Montreux based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] Swiss Pass 8 Days Consecutive Saver Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Zurich: Zurich City Tour - Seat in Coach Basis Mt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Mt Jungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Montreux: Glacier 3000 (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of CHF 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Swiss Special' package is an 8-day tour covering St Moritz, Central and Southern Switzerland, Montreux, and Zurich. The itinerary includes visits to the glamorous resort town of St Moritz, the scenic shores of Lake Geneva in Montreux, and the bustling streets of Zurich. Participants will enjoy breathtaking alpine train journeys, guided city sightseeing, cable car rides to stunning mountain peaks, and opportunities to explore historic castles and local Swiss chocolate shops.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Zurich\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Zurich airport, you will walk across to the Flughafen station (located adjacent to the airport) for your train to Central Switzerland. From train station transfer on your own to the hotel.\n\xa0\nLocal Sightseeing (Optional): Explore Lucerne with a Swiss Pass. Discover Lucerne’s highlights within walking distance, including the iconic Chapel Bridge and Water Tower – Switzerland’s most photographed landmark.\xa0\n\xa0\nZurich Airport Observation Deck (Optional): Stop by before your shuttle for close-up views of aircraft. Deck B: Public area with insights into airport operations. Deck E: Free for passengers with boarding pass.\n\xa0\nLindt Home of Chocolate (Optional): Enjoy an interactive chocolate tour, the world’s largest Lindt shop (500 m²), and a spectacular chocolate fountain.\n\xa0\nStoos Funicular Adventure (Optional): Ride the world’s steepest funicular (110% gradient) to Stoos village. Free with Swiss Half Fare Card.\n\xa0\nSwiss National Museum, Zurich (Optional): Explore Swiss history in a modern extension behind century-old walls. Discounted with Swiss Half Fare Card.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis City West\xa0(Standard) /\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Zurich'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nZurich To Central Switzerland By Train\nZurich City Tour: This panoramic tour takes you across the famous Bahnhofstrasse and the banking center of the lake with a view of the snow-capped mountains, part of the old town with its magnificent guild houses and the churches St. Peter, Grossmünster and Fraumünster. You’ll see the university quarter and the residential area Zürichberg, the National Museum and the Kunsthaus.\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the Zurich train station for your onward journey to Central Switzerland.\nUpon arrival at train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus\xa0Hertenstein\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nMt. Titlis Excursion\nMt. Titlis Excursion: Don\'t miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier\'s deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10\'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe\'s highest suspension bridge. (In conjunction with Swiss Pass)\n\xa0\nSwiss Museum of Transport (Optional): Today Sweet Chocolate Adventure awaits you at the famous Swiss Museum of Transport - Use the entrance ticket to head inside the Swiss Chocolate Adventure, a new attraction located at the Swiss Museum of Transport. Take your seat on a traveling cart to embark on a multimedia journey about Swiss chocolate. Listen to commentary on your audio guide as you pull up to 10 different displays to learn about the history of Swiss chocolate and how it has produced, transported and sold. [50% Discount with Swiss Pass]\n\xa0\nConvertible style cable car ‘CabriO’ (Optional): Later “Feel the wind in your hair in a convertible style cable car (CabriO)". Ride the unique double-decker cable car with an open upper deck to Mount Stanserhorn (1,900 m). Enjoy fresh air and stunning 360° views as you ascend. [Free with Swiss Pass]', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus\xa0Hertenstein\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nJungfraujoch Excursion\nJungfraujoch Excursion: Don't miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world-famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus\xa0Hertenstein\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nCentral Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity)\nMt. Matterhorn Excursion:\xa0 The Matterhorn – mystical, majestic, the mountain of mountains. No one can escape its fascination. Neither locals nor guests. Triangular. A cragged rock “tooth” ranging into the heavens. Standing alone on the horizon. A magnet for alpinists, aesthetic emblem, mountain with ideal proportions. Rugged rock with magical light.There are a wide variety of different attractions to be discovered around the Matterhorn. A top excursion is Gornergrat. On this three-thousand metre mountain ridge there is a viewing platform with a truly unforgettable view of the Matterhorn and the surrounding mountain world. Our if you prefer, the Matterhorn can also be admired from the Rothorn. The Matterhorn glacier paradise is the highest summer ski region in Europe and is open 365 days a year. And there is still plenty to do when the sun isn’t shining! The Matterhorn Museum explains the historic development of Zermatt from a mountain village to an Alpine holiday resort and also has many photographs and facts about the first ascent of the Matterhorn.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus\xa0Hertenstein\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nCentral / Southern Switzerland To Montreux By Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Montreux with Swiss Pass.\xa0\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Montreux train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Villa Toscane (Standard) /\xa0Eden Palace Au Lac\xa0(Value) or similar in Montreux'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nMontreux: Glacier 3000\nGlacier 3000: Today escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer – including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks – Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland.\n\xa0\nBollywood Tour (Optional Tour): You can opt to partake in a “Bollywood Tour” - Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Villa Toscane (Standard) /\xa0Eden Palace Au Lac\xa0(Value) or similar in Montreux'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Montreux\n\xa0\nTransfers: Make you way to the Montreux train station to go to the Airport for your journey back home.\n\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nIbis Zurich City West | Swiss Night By Fassbind | Ibis Styles Zurich City Center | Design Hotel Plattenhof | Montana | Welcome Inn| | Hotel Sternen Oerlikon Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nVilla Toscane | Hotel De Chailly | J5 Hotels Helvetie Montreux | Bon Port or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nZuri By Fassbind | 25hours Hotel Zurich West | Krone Unterstrass | Hotel Allegra | Holiday Inn Zurich Messe or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nEden Palace Au Lac | Rene Capt Golf or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nZuri By Fassbind | 25hours Hotel Zurich West | Krone Unterstrass | Hotel Allegra | Holiday Inn Zurich Messe or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nEden Palace Au Lac | Rene Capt Golf or similar\n\n\n\n', '0': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nIbis Zurich City West | Swiss Night By Fassbind | Ibis Styles Zurich City Center | Design Hotel Plattenhof | Montana | Welcome Inn| | Hotel Sternen Oerlikon Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nVilla Toscane | Hotel De Chailly | J5 Hotels Helvetie Montreux | Bon Port or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 194900.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nIbis Zurich City West | Swiss Night By Fassbind | Ibis Styles Zurich City Center | Design Hotel Plattenhof | Montana | Welcome Inn| | Hotel Sternen Oerlikon Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nVilla Toscane | Hotel De Chailly | J5 Hotels Helvetie Montreux | Bon Port or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 250300.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZurich\n\n\nZuri By Fassbind | 25hours Hotel Zurich West | Krone Unterstrass | Hotel Allegra | Holiday Inn Zurich Messe or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nMontreux\n\n\nEden Palace Au Lac | Rene Capt Golf or similar\n\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental breakfast at the hotel (except on the day of arrival)\xa0\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0\n\nTrain Tickets:\xa0[Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\nSwiss Pass 8 Days Consecutive Saver\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nZurich: Zurich City Tour - Seat in Coach Basis\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nMt Jungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nMontreux: Glacier 3000 (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n1 Night accommodation in Zurich based on the hotel category selected or similar\n4 Nights’ accommodation in Central / Southern Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Montreux based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation:\xa0\n\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\nSwiss Pass 8 Days Consecutive Saver\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nZurich: Zurich City Tour - Seat in Coach Basis\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nMt Jungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nMontreux: Glacier 3000 (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\xa0\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of CHF 10 per person per day is not included\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/Glacier.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/Zurich_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/9063_Lucerne_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/77233_Matterhorn_slopes_Zermatt_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/62869_Lake_Geneva_Montreux_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/Glacier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014552/itinerary/Montreux.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012965', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012965', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Fascinating Georgia', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kazbegi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012965_0_20260817120521.pdf', 'price': 62428, 'packageSummary': "The 'Fascinating Georgia' package is a 6-day tour covering the historic capital of Tbilisi and the breathtaking mountain region of Kazbegi. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, the iconic Gergeti Trinity Church set against the Caucasus Mountains, the famous sulfur baths, and the Chronicles of Georgia monument. Participants will enjoy guided city tours of Tbilisi's charming Old Town, scenic cable car rides, traditional Georgian wine tastings, and immersive cultural and culinary experiences.", 'images': ['georgia_753.png', 'Kakheti-tour_C.jpg', '2.jpg', 'Kazbegi_C.jpg', 'Mtskheta-D2.png', 'Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 62428, 'thumbnailImage': 'Georgia1.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG012965 is named \'Fascinating Georgia\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival - Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Welcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.). Start the city tour by visiting Old Tbilisi. We will first visit Metekhi, which overlooks Meidan Square. After that, we will walk on the Bridge of Peace that links the old part of the city to the Rike Park. After that, we will visit The Clock Tower, where you can see an angel comes out every hour to ring the bell with a small hammer. Shortly, we will walk towards Shardeni Street, which is so well known that any guest that travels to Georgia never leaves this country without visiting it. Later, we will take a cable car to Narikala Fortress and continue walking to the statue of Mother of Georgia. Soon then, we will visit Abanotubani with sulfur baths. Then, we will pass by Juma Mosque, which is unique for the fact that Sunnis and Shias can pray together and continue to Mtatsminda Park via Funicular Train ride. It is the best place for fun and relaxation in the city. The Tbilisi TV tower is also located in the park. Breathtaking views from the park can be seen all over Tbilisi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Sighnaghi & Kakheti Tour - Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel. Kakheti, with its centuries-old culture, is very rich in monuments of different periods. Here you will find ancient settlements, interesting and distinctive medieval temples, which were also important cultural and educational centers, impressive castles, Tush towers and slate houses, etc. This region is also unique and diverse in terms of nature. There is also Alazani area which is the biggest straight place in East of Georgia. In this region, you will meet a completely different landscape from other regions of Georgia. Sighnaghi (The City of Love), KTW Wine Factory with wine tasting, Bodbe Monastery, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Ananuri Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Ananuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round tower, is mostly in ruins. Later, check-in to hotel in Gudauri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kazbegi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Gudauri & Kazbegi Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Gudauri Ski Resort - is a small touristic settlement and ski mountain resort located at the altitude of 3,000m on the southern slopes of the Lesser Caucasus range of Georgia. Gudauri is situated 120 km from Tbilisi. You can reach it by the Georgian Military Road for about 2 hours by car. It has served as an important link between Europe and Asia since ancient times, though it was only after Russia’s annexation of east Georgia in the 19th century and the subsequent improvement of the track for troop movements that it became known as the “Military Highway”. Today it serves as the best route via which we can enjoy the dramatic scenery, crystal-clear air and indescribable grandeur of the mighty Caucasus Mountains. Vicinity of Stepantsminda is picturesque. There is a river Thergi running below the town, with snowed peaks of Caucasus rising among which the Mount Kazbek standing out, with its 5033m height. There are quite a few valley glaciers and forests, both deciduous and coniferous. Fresh mountain air and mineral springs of Stepantsminda are considered to be the main therapy for breathing or eating disorders., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mtskheta - Gori & Uplistsikhe Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Our road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord, is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people. Gori is one of the important cities on the Silk Road, during the tour you will see museum of the Joseph Stalin. Georgia dedicated to the life of Joseph Stalin, the leader of the Soviet Union, who was born in Gori. The Museum retains its Soviet-era characteristics. The museum has three sections, all located in the town\'s central square. It was officially dedicated to Stalin in 1957. With the downfall of the Soviet Union and independence movement of Georgia, the museum was closed in 1989, but has since been reopened, and is a popular tourist attraction., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India Tour Ends: The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice Validity: 01 Oct 2026 to 26 Mar 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-10 PAX STANDARD 483 545 610 VALUE 547 609 674 PREMIUM 722 783 849, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 62428.0. Hotels envisaged include: Hotel Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Tbilisi\xa0\nHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Value) or similar in Kazbegi, Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Premium) or similar in Kazbegi, Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) or similar in TblisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Standard) or similar in Kazbegi. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n. Inclusions: 04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi 01 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kazbegi Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Sighnaghi & Kakheti Tour - Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Ananuri Tour – Gudauri (PVT Basis) Gudauri & Kazbegi Tour (PVT Basis) Mtskheta - Gori & Uplistsikhe Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Entrance fee for, Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, Stalin museum, Uplistsikhe Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa charges Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights services Meals not mentioned in the itinerary Any tips (Around SGD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc ) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. BLACKOUT DATES – 15 DEC’26 – 06 JAN’27 (CHRISTMAS & NEW YEAR). Product Terms and Conditions: The package price is valid until 25 MAR 2025 The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Fascinating Georgia' package is a 6-day tour covering the historic capital of Tbilisi and the breathtaking mountain region of Kazbegi. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, the iconic Gergeti Trinity Church set against the Caucasus Mountains, the famous sulfur baths, and the Chronicles of Georgia monument. Participants will enjoy guided city tours of Tbilisi's charming Old Town, scenic cable car rides, traditional Georgian wine tastings, and immersive cultural and culinary experiences.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival - Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nWelcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.).\n\xa0\nStart the city tour by visiting Old Tbilisi. We will first visit Metekhi, which overlooks Meidan Square. After that, we will walk on the Bridge of Peace that links the old part of the city to the Rike Park. After that, we will visit The Clock Tower, where you can see an angel comes out every hour to ring the bell with a small hammer. Shortly, we will walk towards Shardeni Street, which is so well known that any guest that travels to Georgia never leaves this country without visiting it. Later, we will take a cable car to Narikala Fortress and continue walking to the statue of Mother of Georgia. Soon then, we will visit Abanotubani with sulfur baths. Then, we will pass by Juma Mosque, which is unique for the fact that Sunnis and Shias can pray together and continue to Mtatsminda Park via Funicular Train ride. It is the best place for fun and relaxation in the city. The Tbilisi TV tower is also located in the park. Breathtaking views from the park can be seen all over Tbilisi.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi\xa0(Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi\xa0(Value) /\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Sighnaghi & Kakheti Tour - Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.\n\xa0\nKakheti, with its centuries-old culture, is very rich in monuments of different periods. Here you will find ancient settlements, interesting and distinctive medieval temples, which were also important cultural and educational centers, impressive castles, Tush towers and slate houses, etc. This region is also unique and diverse in terms of nature. There is also Alazani area which is the biggest straight place in East of Georgia. In this region, you will meet a completely different landscape from other regions of Georgia. Sighnaghi (The City of Love), KTW Wine Factory with wine tasting, Bodbe Monastery', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi\xa0(Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi\xa0(Value) /\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nTbilisi - Ananuri Tour (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nAnanuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round tower, is mostly in ruins. Later, check-in to hotel in Gudauri.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi\xa0(Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi\xa0(Value) /\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nGudauri & Kazbegi Tour (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nGudauri Ski Resort - is a small touristic settlement and ski mountain resort located at the altitude of 3,000m on the southern slopes of the Lesser Caucasus range of Georgia. Gudauri is situated 120 km from Tbilisi. You can reach it by the Georgian Military Road for about 2 hours by car. It has served as an important link between Europe and Asia since ancient times, though it was only after Russia’s annexation of east Georgia in the 19th century and the subsequent improvement of the track for troop movements that it became known as the “Military Highway”. Today it serves as the best route via which we can enjoy the dramatic scenery, crystal-clear air and indescribable grandeur of the mighty Caucasus Mountains. Vicinity of Stepantsminda is picturesque. There is a river\xa0 \xa0Thergi running below the town, with snowed peaks of Caucasus rising among which the Mount Kazbek standing out, with its 5033m height. There are quite a few valley glaciers and forests, both deciduous and coniferous. Fresh mountain air and mineral springs of Stepantsminda are considered to be the main therapy for breathing or eating disorders.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Memoir Kazbegi (Standard) / (Value) / (Premium) or similar in Kazbegi'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nMtskheta - Gori & Uplistsikhe Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nOur road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord, is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people.\nGori is one of the important cities on the Silk Road, during the tour you will see museum of the Joseph Stalin. Georgia dedicated to the life of Joseph Stalin, the leader of the Soviet Union, who was born in Gori. The Museum retains its Soviet-era characteristics. The museum has three sections, all located in the town\'s central square. It was officially dedicated to Stalin in 1957. With the downfall of the Soviet Union and independence movement of Georgia, the museum was closed in 1989, but has since been reopened, and is a popular tourist attraction.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture\xa0\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India\xa0\n\xa0\nTour Ends: The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice\nValidity: 01 Oct 2026 to 26 Mar 2027\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n4-5 PAX\n6-7 PAX\n8-10 PAX\n\n\nSTANDARD\n483\n545\n610\n\n\nVALUE\n547\n609\n674\n\n\nPREMIUM\n722\n783\n849\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Hotel Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Tbilisi\xa0\nHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Value) or similar in Kazbegi', 'Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Premium) or similar in Kazbegi', 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) or similar in TblisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Standard) or similar in Kazbegi'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Hotel Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Tbilisi\xa0\nHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Value) or similar in Kazbegi', '2': 'Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Premium) or similar in Kazbegi', '0': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) or similar in TblisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Standard) or similar in Kazbegi'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GE', 'countryName': 'Georgia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 62400.0, 'hotels': ['Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) or similar in TblisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Standard) or similar in Kazbegi']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 68800.0, 'hotels': ['Hotel Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Tbilisi\xa0\nHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Value) or similar in Kazbegi']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 86000.0, 'hotels': ['Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Memoir Kazbegi (Premium) or similar in Kazbegi']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nAirport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Ananuri Tour – Gudauri (PVT Basis)\nGudauri & Kazbegi Tour (PVT Basis)\nMtskheta - Gori & Uplistsikhe Tour – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nEntrance fee for, Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, Stalin museum, Uplistsikhe\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi\n01 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kazbegi\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\nAirport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Sighnaghi & Kakheti Tour - Tbilisi (PVT Bas