ator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & etc.)\nAll drink and beverages\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\nMidnight surcharge\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling together at all times.\n\nProduct Validity : 20th December 2026 - 5th January 2027\n\nSINGLE SUPPLEMENT - USD 357.00\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'The prices will not be valid for any blackout date/ Stop sale period which is informed during confirmation of the booking; if any change in the price, the same will be applicable for all bookings and to be borne by the customer.\n\xa0\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until 05th January 2027.\nThe hotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe hotel upgrade prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nFor the upgrade hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels.\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL\xa0is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client.\xa0TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015295/AlmatyCity.jpeg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014526', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014526', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Italian Charm With Southern Coast', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amalfi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amalfi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014526_0_20260916122539.pdf', 'price': 238787, 'packageSummary': "The 'Italian Charm With Southern Coast' package is a 9-day tour covering the spectacular destinations of Venice, Florence, Amalfi, and Rome. The itinerary includes iconic experiences such as a romantic gondola ride along the canals of Venice, a visit to the historic Duomo in Florence, a scenic drive along the breathtaking Amalfi Coast, and a tour of the ancient Colosseum and Vatican City in Rome. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, historical sightseeing, and opportunities to savor authentic Italian cuisine and local wines throughout this unforgettable journey.", 'images': ['Rome753.jpg', 'Colosseum_753.jpg', 'Naples_753.jpg', '033755_Amalfi_Coast_Sorrento_Italy_753.jpg', '2987_Florence_753.jpg', 'LeaningTower.jpg', '62615_Venice_753.jpg', '71702_Venice_753.jpg', 'StMarkVenice.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 238787, 'thumbnailImage': 'Florence.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cultural', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014526 is named \'Italian Charm With Southern Coast\' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Rome, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Italy Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Fiumicino Leonardo Da Vinci (FCO) airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hop On Hop Off Tour Hop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome\'s iconic sights and landmarks on a hop-on hop-off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Amalfi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Rome To Naples Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Naples. (Duration approx. 1.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Naples train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Amalfi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Southern Coast - Day At Leisure Cattedrale di Sant’Andrea Tour (Optional): The Cattedrale di Sant’Andrea, perched above Amalfi’s main square, is a stunning 9th-century cathedral dedicated to Saint Andrew. The tour begins with the dramatic climb up its grand staircase, leading to a striking façade adorned with colorful mosaics and neo-Moorish details. Inside, you’ll explore a rich blend of Romanesque, Gothic, Baroque, and Arab-Norman architecture. Highlights include the Cloister of Paradise with its elegant columns, the Basilica of the Crucifix housing sacred art, and the crypt where Saint Andrew’s relics rest. This experience offers history, art, and breathtaking views, making it a must-see on the Amalfi Coast., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Naples To Florence Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Florence. (Duration approx. 3 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Florence with Uffizi Gallery (Optional): Depending on the train timing, you can opt for 14:15 hrs Visit of Florence with Uffizi Gallery - Afternoon slot. "You depart by coach for a brief excursion to Fiesole, a delightful town of Etruscan origin, positioned on the hill that dominates Florence and the Arno Valley. The tour continues to the historic centre for a visit to the Church of Santa Croce (outside view). A short walk through the historical streets in the heart of Florence brings you to the famous Piazza della Signoria, where you can admire the imposing Palazzo Vecchio (exterior) and the beautiful Loggia dei Lanzi. The tour will then take you to the famous Uffizi Gallery where it is possible to admire the superb paintings of the Botticelli, Michelangelo, Leonardo da Vinci, Raffaello, Giotto, Cimabue and Masaccio., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Pisa And The Leaning Tower Tour Transfers: You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence. Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half-day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Florence To Venice Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Gondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice\'s main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano — three islands in the Venetian Lagoon — on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water. Highlights: Visit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat Watch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano See Byzantine churches on Torcello— the Church of Santa Fosca Browse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses McArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional): Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfy your thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable. Planning to Visit? Click the link below to conveniently book your shuttle bus tickets and enjoy exciting deals at the nearest outlet: https://mgbooking.tripodeck.com/home?orderCustId=6977233, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Venice Transfers: From Venice hotel to airport, you will have a private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 238787.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nAmalfi / Sorrento\n\n\nHotel Fontana / Amalfi / Floridiana / Hotel La Pergola / Admiral Sorrento / Hotel La Meridiana or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\n\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D\'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nAmalfi / Sorrento\n\n\nLa Bussola / Grand Hotel Excelsior / Art Hotel Gran Paradiso / Michelangelo or Similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Amalfi / Sorrento based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Rome Airport to Rome Hotel Arrival Transfer from Naples Station to Hotel in Amalfi / Sorrento Departure Transfer from Amalfi Hotel to Naples Train Station Departure Airport Transfer from Venice City Center to Marco Polo VCE Airport (Water Taxi + Car) Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Rome to Naples 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Naples to Florence 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Florence to Venice Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Hop On Hop Off Bus tour in Rome Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour Milan City Sightseeing Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the ho