n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Madrid based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Seville based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Barcelona based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Madrid Airport to Madrid Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Barcelona Hotel to Barcelona Airport\n\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Madrid to Seville (Subject to availability until ticketed)\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Seville to Barcelona (Subject to availability until ticketed)\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nMadrid Panoramic City Tour\nSeville Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket\nBarcelona Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/Seville.bmp', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/Madrid2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/MadridRoyalPalace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/seville1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/Seville.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/Barcelona.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/BarcelonaSpain.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014542/itinerary/AdobeStock_200457802_barcelona.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015035', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015035', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026'], 'packageName': 'UK Delights (Winter)', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Manchester', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Aberdeen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Birmingham', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG003199_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 335451, 'packageSummary': "The 'UK Delights (Winter)' package is a 10-day tour covering Strathclyde, Aberdeen, London, Birmingham, and Manchester. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks, historic castles, and vibrant city centers across Scotland and England. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic drives through the picturesque British countryside, shopping at festive winter markets, and exploring the rich cultural and industrial heritage of these major UK destinations.", 'images': ['TownHall_Manchester.jpg', '332374_Old_Trafford_Manchester_United_Kingdom_753.jpg', '753_EdinburghCastle.jpg', 'Kelpies_Aberdeen_Scotland_753.jpg', 'Loch_Ness_Glasgow_753.jpg', 'Lake_Windermere.jpg', 'Shakespeares_Birthplace.jpg', 'LondonEye.jpg', 'Stonehenge-753.jpg', 'London_Bridge_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 335451, 'thumbnailImage': 'Oxford_newSRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015035 is named 'UK Delights (Winter)' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Manchester, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Manchester! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Manchester City Football Stadium – Visit Gretna Green Today, we proceed to visit the famous Manchester City Football Stadium. Visit the home changing room, sit in the dugout & run down the tunnel which leads to the football field. Next, we proceed to the town of Gretna Green and have some free time in the city. Note: On days when Manchester City Stadium is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Edinburgh - Visit the Edinburgh Castle - Johny Walker Experience Today, we drive to Edinburgh. On arrival, enjoy a Guided city tour of Edinburgh, visit the Edinburgh castle, and see the Scottish Parliament and many more interesting sights. Next, we visit the Johny Walker Experience in Scotland’s capital city. In the evening, you have some free time at Princess Street., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Aberdeen, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Photo stop at Kelpies – Guided City Tour of Aberdeen Today we check out and proceed to Falkirk, for a photo stop at The Kelpies - a 30 meter high horse head sculpture which is a monument to honor Scotland’s horse powered industrial heritage. Next, we drive to Aberdeen, known for its beach front, where we spend some time on the esplanade. On Arrival, enjoy a Guided Tour of Aberdeen Admire Aberdeen's incredible silver granite architecture as you wander through its beautiful, cobbled streets., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fort Augustus – Loch Ness Cruise Today, we drive to Fort Augustus, famous for spectacular views down Loch Ness and it is a paradise for keen walkers. Next, we proceed for a cruise on the mighty Loch Ness one of the largest lochs in Scotland and famous for the tale of the Loch Ness monster. Later, we take a photo stop at Three Sister View Point., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Birmingham, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Lake Windermere Cruise Today, we proceed to Windermere & we take a cruise on Lake Windermere: England’s largest lake. Next, we proceed to Birmingham., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - London, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Shakespeare Birthplace at Stratford Upon Avon – Visit Windsor Castle Today, we drive to Stratford upon Avon and Visit Shakespeare's Birthplace to walk in Shakespeare's footsteps and explore the house he was born in. Next, we drive to Windsor for a visit of the famous Windsor Castle - Queen Elizabeth II’s favorite weekend home., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Ride on London Eye – Tower of London – Guided City Tour of London – Lords Cricket Ground Today, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye. Next, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond and we proceed for a Guided city tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. Later, enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground where you relive the historic moments. Note: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Stonehenge – Visit a Roman Bath – Guided Tour of Oxford Today, we proceed to visit the famous Stonehenge: an ancient and mysterious monument with a sophisticated architectural design, its astronomical alignments, and its mystery of purpose. Next, we drive to Bath and we visit a Roman Bath: well preserved thermae in the city of Bath. Later, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 335451.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton or similar in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n, \n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Strathclyde + 01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Tea and Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches., Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements UK visa This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of GBP 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 10 Days, the total Tips amount is GBP 30 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed off by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: AIRLINE AND AIRFARE The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. JOINING DIRECT CLIENTS Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. HOTELS All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. COACHES Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. MEALS Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. SIGHTSEEING On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. No refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures. GENERAL On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE768', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'UK Delights (Winter)' package is a 10-day tour covering Strathclyde, Aberdeen, London, Birmingham, and Manchester. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks, historic castles, and vibrant city centers across Scotland and England. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic drives through the picturesque British countryside, shopping at festive winter markets, and exploring the rich cultural and industrial heritage of these major UK destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Manchester!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Hilton Manchester\xa0similar in Manchester, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Manchester City Football Stadium – Visit Gretna Green \n Today, we proceed to visit the famous Manchester City Football Stadium. Visit the home changing room, sit in the dugout & run down the tunnel which leads to the football field. Next, we proceed to the town of Gretna Green and have some free time in the city.\nNote: On days when Manchester City Stadium is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Edinburgh - Visit the Edinburgh Castle - Johny Walker Experience\nToday, we drive to Edinburgh. On arrival, enjoy a Guided city tour of Edinburgh, visit the Edinburgh castle, and see the Scottish Parliament and many more interesting sights. Next, we visit the Johny Walker Experience in Scotland’s capital city. In the evening, you have some free time at Princess Street.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell,\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nPhoto stop at Kelpies – Guided City Tour of Aberdeen\nToday we check out and proceed to Falkirk, for a photo stop at The Kelpies - a 30 meter high horse head sculpture which is a monument to honor Scotland’s horse powered industrial heritage. Next, we drive to Aberdeen, known for its beach front, where we spend some time on the esplanade. On Arrival, enjoy a Guided Tour of Aberdeen Admire Aberdeen's incredible\xa0silver granite architecture\xa0as you wander through its beautiful, cobbled streets.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nFort Augustus – Loch Ness Cruise\nToday, we drive to Fort Augustus, famous for spectacular views down Loch Ness and it is a paradise for keen walkers. Next, we proceed for a cruise on the mighty Loch Ness one of the largest lochs in Scotland and famous for the tale of the Loch Ness monster. Later, we take a photo stop at Three Sister View Point.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell,\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nLake Windermere Cruise\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Windermere & we take a cruise on Lake Windermere: England’s largest lake. Next, we proceed to Birmingham.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Birmingham, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 7, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Shakespeare Birthplace at Stratford Upon Avon – Visit Windsor Castle\nToday, we drive to Stratford upon Avon and Visit Shakespeare's Birthplace to walk in Shakespeare's footsteps and explore the house he was born in. Next, we drive to Windsor for a visit of the famous Windsor Castle - Queen Elizabeth II’s favorite weekend home.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nRide on London Eye – Tower of London – Guided City Tour of London – Lords Cricket Ground\nToday, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye. Next, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond and we proceed for a Guided city tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. Later, enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground where you relive the historic moments.\nNote: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Stonehenge – Visit a Roman Bath – Guided Tour of Oxford\nToday, we proceed to visit the famous Stonehenge: an ancient and mysterious monument with a sophisticated architectural design, its astronomical alignments, and its mystery of purpose. Next, we drive to Bath and we visit a Roman Bath: well preserved thermae in the city of Bath. Later, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and\xa0Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton or similar in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n', '\n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Strathclyde + 01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Strathclyde + 01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n', '1': '\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton or similar in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GB', 'countryName': 'United Kingdom', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': '44', 'countryName': 'Scotland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 335500.0, 'hotels': ['\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton or similar in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Tea and Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\n09 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', 'England\n\nVisit Manchester City Football Stadium\nVisit Shakespeare birthplace\nVisit a Roman Bath\nVisit Stonehenge\nGuided City Tour of London\nVisit the Tower of London - see the famous Koh i Noor Diamond\nEnjoy a Ride on the London Eye\nVisit the Lords Cricket Ground in London\nVisit Windsor Castle\nGuided Tour of Oxford\nEnjoy a scenic cruise on Lake Windermere\xa0 \xa0\n\nScotland\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 \n\nVisit Gretna Green\nGuided City Tour of Edinburgh\nVisit Edinburgh Castle\nEnjoy the Johnnie Walker Experience in Edinburgh\nPhoto stop at Kelpies in Falkirk\nGuided Tour of Aberdeen\nEnjoy Loch Ness Cruise\nVisit Fort Augustus\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\xa0\n\nUK visa\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of GBP 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 10 Days, the total Tips amount is GBP 30 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed off by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\n\xa0\nAIRLINE AND AIRFARE\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJOINING DIRECT CLIENTS\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHOTELS\xa0\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCOACHES\xa0\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nMEALS\xa0\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSIGHTSEEING\xa0\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGENERAL\xa0\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/Oxford_newSRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/TownHall_Manchester.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/332374_Old_Trafford_Manchester_United_Kingdom_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/753_EdinburghCastle.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/Kelpies_Aberdeen_Scotland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/Loch_Ness_Glasgow_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/Lake_Windermere.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/Shakespeares_Birthplace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/LondonEye.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/Stonehenge-753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015035/itinerary/London_Bridge_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014532', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014532', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'London Paris Delights', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014532_0_20260916124451.pdf', 'price': 196470, 'packageSummary': "The 'London Paris Delights' package is a 7-day tour covering the spectacular cities of London and Paris. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre Museum, Buckingham Palace, and the Tower of London. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic cruise along the River Seine, a ride on the London Eye, and a memorable journey connecting these two historic European capitals.", 'images': ['London_Bridge_754.jpg', 'London_new.jpg', 'LondonEye.jpg', 'Paris_753.jpg', 'EiffelTower_753.jpg', 'Paris_City_new753.jpeg', '29117_Paris_View_France_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 196470, 'thumbnailImage': 'TowerBridgeinLondon_160128833.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014532 is named 'London Paris Delights' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - London, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive London Transfers: Upon your arrival at the airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 14:00 - 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hop On Hop Off Tour - Madame Tussauds - London Eye - Tower Of London Hop on Hop Off Tour: The London Hop-On Hop-Off Bus Tour is a flexible sightseeing experience that lets you explore the city’s most iconic landmarks at your own pace with multiple routes and stops near attractions. Madame Tussauds With Marvel 4d Cinema and Star Wars Experience: Step into the world of fame and fantasy at Madame Tussauds London. Get up close with lifelike wax figures of celebrities, historical icons, and world leaders. Enjoy the thrilling Marvel 4D Cinema, where superheroes come alive in an immersive experience, and explore the Star Wars Experience, featuring iconic characters and scenes from the legendary saga. It’s an unforgettable mix of glamour, action, and adventure for all ages. London Eye – Ticket: The London Eye is one of the city’s most iconic attractions, offering breathtaking 360° views of London’s skyline from a giant observation wheel on the South Bank of the River Thames. Standing at 135 meters tall, it provides a unique perspective of landmarks like Big Ben, Buckingham Palace, and St. Paul’s Cathedral. A must-visit for stunning photo opportunities and an unforgettable experience. Tower of London: The Tower of London is a historic fortress on the north bank of the River Thames, famous for its rich history as a royal palace, prison, and treasury. Home to the dazzling Crown Jewels and centuries of intrigue, it offers visitors a glimpse into Britain’s royal past, iconic Yeoman Warders, and legendary tales like that of the ravens. A must-see UNESCO World Heritage Site for history lovers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Description: London Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Warner Bros. Studio Tour London (Optional): Visiting fabled Harry Potter filming locations from London typically involves juggling a lot of logistics—especially for families with children. Take the stress out of planning during this full-day tour to Warner Bros. Studios. Travel by climate-controlled coach from central London. Visit original sets and uncover behind-the-scenes secrets, with air-conditioned transportation from central London. This Harry Potter studio London tour includes round-trip coach transport and entrance tickets. Read more about - Harry Potter Warner Bros. Studio Tour with Transport from London., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: London To Paris Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Paris. Upon your arrival at Paris train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Moulin Rouge Show (Optional): Experience the world-famous Moulin Rouge in Paris, an iconic cabaret known for its dazzling performances, vibrant costumes, and spectacular dance routines, including the legendary French Cancan. Located in the heart of Montmartre, this unforgettable show combines music, glamour, and artistry, offering a true taste of Parisian nightlife., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour Paris City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour-long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time. Special Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Disneyland® Paris: 1 Day 2 Parks (Optional): Experience the magic of Disneyland Paris, Europe’s most enchanting theme park destination. Located just outside Paris, the resort features two incredible parks: Disneyland Park, where fairy tales come to life with iconic attractions like Sleeping Beauty’s Castle, and Walt Disney Studios Park, offering behind-the-scenes movie magic. Enjoy thrilling rides, spectacular parades, and meet your favourite Disney characters. Disneyland Paris is perfect for families, friends, and Disney fans of all ages. OR The Palace of Versailles – A Royal Journey (Optional): Experience the grandeur of Versailles in true royal fashion. Accompanied by a knowledgeable guide, explore a curated selection of the palace’s 700 opulent rooms, and uncover fascinating stories of Louis XIV – the Sun King, his successors, queens, mistresses, and courtiers including Marie Antoinette. Once a humble hunting lodge, Versailles became the dazzling seat of the French court in the 17th and 18th centuries. Even today, its splendour and historical richness remain unmatched., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Paris Transfers: From Paris hotel to the Airport in Private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 196470.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nIbis London Earls Court Hotel /\xa0Point A Hotel, London Paddington / Best Western Buckingham Palace Rd\xa0\xa0/The W14 Hotel Kensington / London House Hotel / Mentone Hotel / BW Swiss Cottage or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hôtel Champerret-Elysées / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nPark Plaza London / Park International / Copthorne Tara London Kensington / Holiday Inn® London Kensington / Mercure London Paddington or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: