s\nSanta Village Tour on shared basis\nCrossing the Arctic Circle on shared basis\nMeeting Santa at his home on shared basis\nAurora Snowshoeing and Wilderness Hut with bonfire experience on shared basis\nHusky sleigh ride experience on shared basis\nReindeer Farm Visit and Authentic Sami experience on shared basis\nAurora Snowmobile driving experience (2 Pax share 1 Snowmobile. Driver of Snowmobile must be in physical possession of a valid driving License from any county).\nCultural visit to Pentik on shared basis\nVisit to Kuusamo / Village center for local shopping on shared basis\n\nInsurance:\xa0\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\xa0\n\nOPTIONAL TOUR\xa0\n\nArctic Ice breaker cruise 2.5 hrs. : EUR 495\nGuided Authentic Smoke Sauna and Ice dip experience : EUR 200\n\nSPECIAL NOTE:\xa0\n\nLuggage Capacity 1 check inn and 1 Cabin Luggage Per person.\nTriple Room at Pikku Syote Resort will be an Upgraded Larger room: Deluxe/ Jr Suite Category. No Quad sharing Possible. For Quad bookings, 2 Dbl room Prices must be calculated.\xa0\nTriple Sharing booking: During Overnight Train, 2 cabins will be allocated for 3 Pax booking. 1 Cabin for 2 Pax and 1 cabin sharing with another passenger.\nAge limit to participate in FD: 06 Years and above.\nOvernight Santa Express Train Solo and 3 Pax booking clarification:\xa0\n\nSolo Pax during Overnight Train will be required to share the cabin with another passenger (Shared basis: 2 Pax in 1 Cabin).\xa0\xa0\nTriple Sharing booking: During Overnight Train, 2 cabins will be allocated for 3 Pax booking. 1 Cabin for 2 Pax and 1 cabin sharing with another passenger.\n\n\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'IMPORTANT NOTES:\xa0\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\xa0\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\xa0\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\xa0\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\xa0\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\xa0\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\xa0\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\xa0\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\xa0\n\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS:\xa0\n\nTravel Validity: 1 November 2026 – 31 March 2027\xa0\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\xa0\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\xa0\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\xa0\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\xa0\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\xa0\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseein