due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015666/Finland-Rovaniemi.jpg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015089', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015089', 'availableMonths': ['march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Russian Dhamaka (Winter)', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015089_0_20260910210239', 'price': 188230, 'packageSummary': "The 'Russian Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering the majestic cities of Moscow and St. Petersburg. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Kremlin, Red Square, St. Basil's Cathedral, and the world-famous Hermitage Museum. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic high-speed Sapsan train ride between the two historic cities, and the unique opportunity to experience Russia's breathtaking winter landscapes and rich cultural heritage.", 'images': ['89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', '861367_Church_of_the_Saviour_on_Blood_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', '56599_Kazan_Cathedral_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', '12117_Hermitage_Museum_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'Petersburg7534.jpg', '89882_Arbat_street_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'MoscowRussia7534.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 188230, 'thumbnailImage': '50718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015089 is named 'Russian Dhamaka (Winter)' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Moscow, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Moscow! Welcome to Moscow - the capital and the largest city of Russia. On arrival, you will be met by your Tour Manager / Local Representative outside the custom area who will welcome you and take you to your hotel for check -in. The evening is free at leisure. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Moscow – Sparrow hill Cable car - Metro Tour Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Moscow: Visit the Red Square, see the St. Basil’s Cathedral, the White House and Christ the Saviour Cathedral. What’s more! Enjoy unique views of the iconic buildings in Moscow from the cable car which connects the two banks of the Moskva-river and has shortly become a new hallmark of the city. Next, we visit the Metro station of Moscow often called 'The People's Palaces', for their elegant designs, lavish and profuse use of marble, mosaics, sculptures and chandeliers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - St Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Onto St Petersburg – Guided City Tour of St Petersburg – Visit Kazan Cathedral Today we check out and proceed to the railway station to board a SAPSAN / AURORA / NEVSKY train onto St Petersburg: A major historical and cultural centre and Russia’s second largest city. On arrival procced for guided city tour of St. Petersburg city, see Issac's Cathedral, The Peter and Paul Fortress. Later visit Kazan cathedral., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - St Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Peterhof Gardens - Visit Hermitage Museum Today, we proceed to Peterhof to visit the gardens. Peterhof is like an encyclopaedia of park design through the age of empire. Marvel at the intricate fountains and stunning landscapes. These gardens are referred as “Russian Versailles Garden”. Next, we visit the iconic Hermitage Museum, famous for holding nearly three million items dating from the Stone Age to the present, including many masterpieces by Renaissance Italian and Baroque Dutch, Flemish, and French painters., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - St Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Grand Maket (Russia in Miniature) – Neva Cruise Today, we visit the Grand Maket; a private museum showcasing the largest miniature model of Russia. Next, we embark on a scenic canal cruise, gliding along the city’s waterways and admiring its elegant bridges, historic landmarks and picturesque architecture., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Train to Moscow Today, we check out and proceed to the railway station to board the train onto Moscow. On arrival check in to the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! After breakfast, we transfer you to the airport. Board your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: - In capital city like Moscow & St Petersburg, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 188230.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n, \n\n02 nights at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\xa0\n03 nights at Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 night at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n, \nDaily continental breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Russian visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of USD 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 7 Days, the total Tips amount is USD 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline And Airfare The Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July,2026 Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers. Passengers Missing Flights To Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves. Hotels All Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts. Most Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size. As A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room. Most Hotel Rooms In Europe May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions. Functioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority. The Average Room Size Of The Hotels In Europe Are Between 16 – 20 Sq. Mts. Most Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms. Any Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers. We Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary. Coaches Most Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean. Due To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives. Eating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach. One Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach. Coaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach. Meals Meals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible. On Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided. Sightseeing On Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same. Generally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And At The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible. In The Case Of Missing A Paid Entrance Due To Sudden Closure Or Non-Availability The Same Will Be Replaced By Another Visit Of Similar Value And / Or Type Or A Refund Will Be Provided. General A Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour. Security Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary. Please Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage. Tcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour. Normal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges. The Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services. The Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same. There Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour. All Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In The Currency As Mentioned In Your Tour Price Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted). Optional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy. Gst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India. In Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed. The Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only. Tours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In The Currency As Mentioned In Your Tour Price Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange. Please Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE158', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Russian Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering the majestic cities of Moscow and St. Petersburg. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Kremlin, Red Square, St. Basil's Cathedral, and the world-famous Hermitage Museum. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic high-speed Sapsan train ride between the two historic cities, and the unique opportunity to experience Russia's breathtaking winter landscapes and rich cultural heritage.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Moscow!\nWelcome to Moscow - the capital and the largest city of Russia. On arrival, you will be met by your Tour Manager / Local Representative outside the custom area who will welcome you and take you to your hotel for check -in. The evening is free at leisure.\n\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Edge Seligerskaya/ Aerostar or Similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided city tour of Moscow – Sparrow hill Cable car - Metro Tour\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Moscow: Visit the Red Square, see the St. Basil’s Cathedral, the White House and Christ the Saviour Cathedral. What’s more! Enjoy unique views of the iconic buildings in Moscow from the cable car which connects the two banks of the Moskva-river and has shortly become a new hallmark of the city. Next, we visit the Metro station of Moscow often called 'The People's Palaces', for their elegant designs, lavish and profuse use of marble, mosaics, sculptures and chandeliers.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Edge Seligerskaya/ Aerostar or Similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nOnto St Petersburg – Guided City Tour of St Petersburg – Visit Kazan Cathedral\nToday we check out and proceed to the railway station to board a SAPSAN / AURORA / NEVSKY train onto St Petersburg: A major historical and cultural centre and Russia’s second largest city. On arrival procced for guided city tour of St. Petersburg city, see Issac's Cathedral, The Peter and Paul Fortress. Later visit Kazan cathedral.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Peterhof Gardens - Visit Hermitage Museum \nToday, we proceed to Peterhof to visit the gardens. Peterhof is like an encyclopaedia of park design through the age of empire. Marvel at the intricate fountains and stunning landscapes. These gardens are referred as “Russian Versailles Garden”. Next, we visit the iconic Hermitage Museum, famous for holding nearly three million items dating from the Stone Age to the present, including many masterpieces by Renaissance Italian and Baroque Dutch, Flemish, and French painters.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGrand Maket (Russia in Miniature) – Neva Cruise\nToday, we visit the Grand Maket; a private museum showcasing the largest miniature model of Russia. Next, we embark on a scenic canal cruise, gliding along the city’s waterways and admiring its elegant bridges, historic landmarks and picturesque architecture.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTrain to Moscow\nToday, we check out and proceed to the railway station to board the train onto Moscow. On arrival check in to the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Edge Seligerskaya/ Aerostar or Similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nAfter breakfast, we transfer you to the airport. Board your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n\xa0\nNote: - In capital city like Moscow & St Petersburg, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n', '\n\n02 nights at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\xa0\n03 nights at Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 night at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n', '1': '\n\n02 nights at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\xa0\n03 nights at Cosmos Pribaltiskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 night at Edge Seligerskaya/ Hotel Aerostar or Similar in Moscow\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'RU', 'countryName': 'Russia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 188200.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n', '\nDaily continental breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners\n'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', 'Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Moscow\n\nGuided city tour of Moscow\nRadisson River cruise\xa0\nChance to visit Great Moscow Circus (OPTIONAL)\n\n\xa0\nSt Petersburg\n\nGuided City Tour of St Petersburg\nGrand Maket - Russia in Miniature\xa0\nVisit Museum of Russian Vodka\nChance to visit Peterhof Gardens & Hermitage Museum (OPTIONAL)\n', 'Moscow\n\nGuided city tour of Moscow\nRide on Metro Tour\xa0\nSparrow Hill cable car ride\xa0\nRussian Circus\n\n\xa0\nSt Petersburg\n\nGuided City Tour of St Petersburg\nVisit Kazan Cathedral\nHermitage Museum\xa0\nVisit Peterhof Gardens\nNeva Cruise\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\n\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\n\nRussian visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of USD 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 7 Days, the total Tips amount is USD 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\nAirline And Airfare\xa0\n\nThe Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 1st July,2026\xa0\nAny Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers.\xa0\nPassengers Missing Flights To Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nHotels\xa0\n\nAll Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or On The Outskirts.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size.\xa0\nAs A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room.\xa0\nMost Hotel Rooms In Europe May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority.\xa0\nThe Average Room Size Of The Hotels In Europe Are Between 16 – 20 Sq. Mts.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms.\xa0\nAny Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers.\xa0\nWe Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches\xa0\n\nMost Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean.\xa0\nDue To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives.\xa0\nEating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach.\xa0\nOne Check-In Bag And One Handbag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space On The Coach.\xa0\nCoaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach.\n\nMeals\xa0\n\nMeals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible.\xa0\nOn Certain Days, A Packed Lunch Will Be Provided.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nGenerally, You Will Have To Walk To Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And At The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However, The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry A Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible.\xa0\nIn The Case Of Missing A Paid Entrance Due To Sudden Closure Or Non-Availability The Same Will Be Replaced By Another Visit Of Similar Value And / Or Type Or A Refund Will Be Provided.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral\xa0\n\nA Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour.\xa0\nSecurity Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary.\xa0\nPlease Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage.\xa0\nTcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour.\xa0\nNormal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges.\xa0\nThe Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nThere Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour.\xa0\nAll Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In The Currency As Mentioned In Your Tour Price Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted).\xa0\nOptional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy.\xa0\nGst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India.\xa0\nIn Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed.\xa0\nThe Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only.\xa0\nTours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In The Currency As Mentioned In Your Tour Price Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange.\xa0\nPlease Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/50718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/861367_Church_of_the_Saviour_on_Blood_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/56599_Kazan_Cathedral_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/12117_Hermitage_Museum_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/Petersburg7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/89882_Arbat_street_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015089/itinerary/MoscowRussia7534.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015189', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015189', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Scandinavian Adventure', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 370627, 'packageSummary': "The 'Scandinavian Adventure' package is a 10-day tour covering the beautiful Nordic capitals of Oslo, Helsinki, Stockholm, and Copenhagen. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Royal Palace in Oslo, the unique Temppeliaukio Church in Helsinki, Stockholm's historic Gamla Stan, and the famous Little Mermaid statue in Copenhagen. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic canal and fjord cruises, overnight ferry crossings, and ample opportunities to explore the rich cultural heritage and vibrant local markets of these stunning destinations.", 'images': ['Helsinki2.jpg', 'Helsinki1.jpg', 'Helsinki3.jpg', 'Stockholm2.jpg', 'Stockholm1.jpg', 'Oslo1.jpg', 'Oslo2jpg.jpg', 'Copenhagen2.jpg', 'Copenhagen1.jpg', 'Copenhagen3.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 370627, 'thumbnailImage': 'Stockholm.avif', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015189 is named 'Scandinavian Adventure' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Helsinki, Meals: NA, Description: Arrive Helsinki Transfers: Upon your arrival at Helsinki Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour: Join a small group walking tour of Helsinki covering key landmarks Helsingin Tuomiokirkko Market Square Temppeliaukio Church Uspenski Cathedral and Sibelius Park plus historic quarters between Market and Senate Squares with cafes and restaurants., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki to Stockholm by Cruise Transfers: You will be transferred from Helsinki hotel to the port on private basis for the overnight cruise. Helsinki to Stockholm Overnight Cruise: In the evening take overnight cruise to Stockholm and enjoy live entertainment duty free shopping sightseeing. Special Notes: In Helsinki it will be day free at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Visit Icebar Transfers: Upon arrival in Stockholm you will be transferred from port to the hotel on private basis. Early check in is subject to hotel discretion. Visit Icebar: Visit Icebar Stockholm made entirely of ice even the glasses. Kept at minus five degrees entry includes a drink forty five minute visit and ice cape with gloves. A unique Arctic style experience in central Stockholm. Special Note: You will check in at the hotel post completing the sightseeing., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Walking City Tour Stockholm Small Group Walking Tour: Small group walking tour of Stockholm covering City Hall Sergel Square and Gamla Stan one of Europes best preserved medieval centers. Visit the Nobel Museum Royal Palace with changing of the guards and the Vasa Museum., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm to Oslo by Train Transfers: You will be transferred from the Stockholm hotel to the train station. Upon arrival at the Oslo train station you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour: Visit Oslos Royal Palace Vigeland Sculpture Park and Opera House. Explore the Kon Tiki FRAM and Maritime museums Akershus Fortress and its history museums then stroll Karl Johans Gate filled with shops cafes bars and nightlife., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo to Copenhagen by Cruise Transfers: You will be transferred from Oslo hotel to the port on private basis for overnight cruise to Copenhagen. Oslo to Copenhagen Overnight Cruise: In the evening take overnight cruise to Copenhagen and enjoy on board. Special Notes: In Oslo it will be day free at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Copenhagen City Walking Tour Transfers: Upon reaching Copenhagen you will be transferred from port to the hotel on private basis. Early check in is subject to hotel discretion. Copenhagen Small Group Walking City Tour: Enjoy small group walking tour of Copenhagen with views from Rundetaarn and visit to Trinitatis Church. Stroll Stroget see Nyhavn Amalienborg Palace Gefion Fountain and the Little Mermaid inspired by H C Andersen., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will be transferred from Copenhagen hotel to the airport on private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 370627.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHELSINKI\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScandic\xa0Hotel\xa0or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSTOCKHOLM\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClarion hotel or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOSLO\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClarion hotel\xa0or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOPENHAGEN\xa0\n\n\n\n\nScandic Hotel or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1). Inclusions: Accommodation 2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm 2 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Oslo to Copenhagen 1 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals Daily Breakfast (Except Day 1) Transportation [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis] Arrival Transfers from Helsinki Airport to the Hotel Private Transfer from Helsinki hotel to the Port Private Transfer from Stockholm Port to the hotel Private Transfer from Stockholm hotel to the train station Private Transfer from Oslo Train station to the hotel Private Transfer from Oslo hotel to the Port station Private Transfer from Copenhagen Port to the hotel Departure Transfer from Copenhagen hotel to the Airport Sightseeing (For SIC Package tours