-Elysées / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 509300.0, 'hotels': ["\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nPark Plaza London / Park International / Copthorne Tara London Kensington / Holiday Inn® London Kensington / Mercure London Paddington or similar\n\n\n\n\nParis\n\n\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n"]}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from London Airport to London Hotel\nDeparture Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Rome Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets:\xa0[Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket London – Paris (Eurostar): –\xa0Subject to availability until ticketed\xa0\n2nd Class Train Ticket Paris – Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver\nLucerne – Zurich Airport: –\xa0Subject to availability until ticketed.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nLondon Hop On Hop Off Bus tour.\nLondon Eye (Entrance Only).\nMadame Tussauds (Entrance Only).\nTower of London (Entrance Only)\nInteractive City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC)\xa0\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade.\xa0\nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\xa0\nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Paris based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in London based on the hotel category selected or similar\n4 Nights’ accommodation in Central Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation:[Includes Privates service s on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from London Airport to London Hotel\nDeparture Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Rome Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket London - Paris (Eurostar): - Subject to availability until ticketed\n2nd Class Train Ticket Paris - Zurich /Geneva / Basel (TGV).\n2nd Class Train Ticket Lucerne - Zurich - Subject to availability until ticketed.\n2nd Class Train Ticket Zurich - Venice: - Subject to availability until ticketed.\n2nd Class Train Ticket Venice to Florence: - Subject to availability until ticketed.\n2nd Class Train Ticket Florence - Rome: - Subject to availability until ticketed.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nLondon Hop On Hop Off Bus tour.\nLondon Eye (Entrance Only).\nMadame Tussauds (Entrance Only).\nTower of London (Entrance Only)\nInteractive City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC)\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade.\nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n\n\xa0\nIntercity travel by Train (Second Class):\n\nLondon – Paris (Eurostar).\nParis – Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver.\nLucerne – Venice.\nVenice – Florence.\nFlorence – Rome.\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/Rome_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/London7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/LondonTowerBridge7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Paris75390.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Interlaken2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Jungfraujoch75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Glacier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/VeniceRialtoBridgeItaly75312.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/71702_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Florence_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/rome.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Rome-Colosseum.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014896/itinerary/Rome789.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015164', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015164', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Spain Portugal And Morocco (Winter)', 'days': 16, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Casablanca', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Casablanca', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Fes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tangier', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Costa Del Sol', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Granada', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Huelva', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lisbon', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lisbon', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Porto', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Enjoy a traditional Moroccan Experience in Fes. Enjoy Flamenco show with a drink. Enjoy Belem Pastry in Lisbon. Wine tasting in Porto. Enjoy Hot Chocolate with Churros in Madrid. Authentic Paella dinner in Granada. Enjoy Horchata drink in Valencia.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG009837_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 421562, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Spain Portugal And Morocco (Winter)' package is a 16-day tour covering Casablanca, Barcelona, Valencia, Madrid, Costa Del Sol, Granada, Fes, Lisbon, Tangier, Huelva, and Porto. Throughout this journey, participants will enjoy a variety of unique cultural and culinary experiences, including a traditional Moroccan Experience in Fes and a lively Flamenco show accompanied by a drink. The itinerary also features delicious local treats such as tasting Belem Pastry in Lisbon, wine tasting in Porto, savoring hot chocolate with churros in Madrid, indulging in an authentic Paella dinner in Granada, and enjoying a refreshing Horchata drink in Valencia.", 'images': ['42053_Hassan_Mosque_city_of_Casablanca_Morocco_753.jpg', 'Casablanca753.jpg', 'fes.jpg', 'Chefchaouene_7531.jpg', 'tangier.jpg', 'Alhambra_Granada_Spain.jpg', 'Cordoba753.jpg', 'Lisbon2.jpg', 'Lisbon3.jpg', 'Porto753.jpg', 'Salamanca753.jpg', 'Madrid_753.jpg', 'Valencia753.jpg', 'SagradaFamiliaBARCELONASPAINshutterstock101054833.jpg', 'LasRamblasBarcelona753.jpg', 'Barcelona7531.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 421562, 'thumbnailImage': 'Cordoba267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015164 is named 'Highlights Of Spain Portugal And Morocco (Winter)' and spans 16 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Casablanca, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Casablanca! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Casablanca, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Marrakesh Today we proceed for a guided tour of Marakkesh: See the Bahia Palace, El Badi Palace, Koutoubia Mosque & gardens, Kasbah Area, Free time at Jemma El Fna Square, Visit Souk El Attarin & Smata., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Fes, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Casablanca with Entrance to Hassan II Mosque - Guided City Tour of Fes Today, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Casablanca: See Royal Palace, Hassan II Mosque with free time in Boulevard de la Corniche. Next, we drive to Fes for a Guided City Tour of Fes: Visit the Old Madinas, See the Chouara Tannary, the exotic ancient Medina, UNESCO World Heritage Site, walk through the narrow, bustling streets and alleys that are home to brilliantly, the Bab Boujlloud Gate, En-Nejjarine Square, Es-Seffarine Square, huedsouks., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tangier, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Chefchaouen Today, we drive to Chefchaouen for the Guided City Tour: See the Place Outa El Hammam, Grand Mosque. Later drive towards Tangiers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Costa Del Sol, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Tangier – Ferry to Algecires, Spain Today, we proceed for a Guided City Tour: See the Spartel Cape at the extreme northwest of Africa and the Hercules Caves, linked with Hercules, the man who separated Africa from Europe. From here, you will get an exceptional view of the Strait of Gibraltar and the Atlantic Ocean as well. Later we take a ferry to Algecires, Spain., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Granada, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Castillo de Colomres – Guided tour of Alhambra Complex - Generalife Gardens Today we visit Castillo de Colomres: a castle dedicated to the life and adventures of Christopher Columbus. Next, we proceed to the McArthur Glen shopping outlet (if time permitting) where you can enjoy great deals on designer labels. Later, we drive to Granada and on arrival enjoy guided tour of the Alhambra Complex and Generalife Gardens., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Huelva, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Cordoba – Visit Mezquita - Guided City Tour of Sevilla – Flamenco Show Today, we drive to Cordoba for a guided city tour of the city with entrance to Mezquita. The Mosque–Cathedral of Córdoba, officially known as the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption is a former Islamic Mosque and a UNESCO world heritage site. Next, we drive to Sevilla for a Guided City Tour: See the Sevilla Tower, Sevilla Cathedral, Giralda, Santacruz Quarter. Later this evening, we enjoy the traditional Flamenco show., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Lisbon, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Algarve boat tour – Proceed to Lisbon, Portugal Today, we drive to Lagos. Upon arrival, we proceed the boat tour at Algarve experiencing its walled old town, cliffs and Atlantic beaches. Next, we drive to Lisbon., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Lisbon, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Lisbon - Visit Cabo da Roca Today, we enjoy a Guided City Tour of Lisbon, Belem Tower, Jeronimos Monastery, Monument to the Discoveries, 25th April Bridge and more interesting sites. We also visit the town of Sintra and Cabo da Roca – Western most end of the European continent., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Porto, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Porto – Visit a wine cellar with wine tasting Today we drive to Porto and enjoy a Guided City Tour. World-famous for its port wine, Porto is Portugal’s second largest city. The historic centre of Porto was designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1996. Next, we visit a Wine Cellar with Wine Tasting., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Salamanca – Photo stop at the walls of Avila - Proceed to Madrid Today, we first visit the city of Avila, where you shall get see the ‘Walls of Avila’. Later proceed to Salamanca; known as the “Golden city” for the sandstone used in the construction of its buildings, it has the third oldest existing university in the world, one of the Top 10 cathedrals in Spain, and one of the most beautiful plazas in all of Spain. On arrival we proceed on a Guided Tour of Salamanca where see the: Ponte Roma, Salamanca University, Salamanca Cathedral and the Salamanca square. Next, we continue our journey to Madrid., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Madrid – Visit a Bullring – Guided city tour of Toledo – Visit a Sword factory Today, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Madrid: Visit the largest bullring of Madrid – Las Ventas Plaza De Torros, see the old town, the City Centre, Church of San Francisco El Grande, Royal Palace and many more historical and modern sites. Later, we drive to Toledo. On arrival, we enjoy a guided tour: see the cathedral of Toledo, Puente San Martin through narrow winding cobblestone streets. Next, we visit a Sword factory and then drive to Madrid., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfst, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Valencia Today, we drive to Valencia. On arrival, we enjoy a Guided City Tour: See the Plaza Reina, the stunning cathedral, the central market and much more., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 14 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Barcelona – Visit Sagrada Familia Today, we drive to Barcelona. On arrival, we enjoy a Guided City Tour: See the Olympic Village, Montjuic, Placa de Catalunya, and many more beautiful sights. Later, we visit the Sagrada Familia - the yet unfinished minor basilica, a UNESCO World Heritage site. Note: Entrance to Sagrada Familia depends upon the availability given by the Sagrada Familia officials and may not necessarily be done on this day. In such cases, the itinerary will be amended accordingly to cover all inclusions, or an alternate attraction will be provided., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 15 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Montserrat Today, we drive to Montserrat – a multi peaked rocky range which houses the virgin of Montserrat and Spain’s first national park. Next, we drive back to Barcelona and spend Later, spend some free time at Barcelona beach., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 16 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Spain and Portugal tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European Cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 421562.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n2 nights at Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca, Morocco.\xa0\n1 night at Ramada by Wyndham / Barcelo Fes or similar in Fes, Morocco.\n1 night at Hotel Kenzi Solazur or similar in Tangier, Morocco.\n1 night at\xa0TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa Del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain\n1 nights at Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 night at\xa0Alcora or similar in Huelva / Sevilla, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 nights at AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Exe Puerto Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n03 Local lunches.\n13 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n02 Local dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements: Multiple entry Schengen and Moroccan visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 16 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 48 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline And Airfare The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to/ from the hub city at their own expense. Joining Direct Clients Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. Hotels All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds, and the room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air-conditioned / air cooled, nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat waves in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. The Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms, to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. General On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary, to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer about the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non-cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at the prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Enjoy a traditional Moroccan Experience in Fes. Enjoy Flamenco show with a drink. Enjoy Belem Pastry in Lisbon. Wine tasting in Porto. Enjoy Hot Chocolate with Churros in Madrid. Authentic Paella dinner in Granada. Enjoy Horchata drink in Valencia..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE807', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Spain Portugal And Morocco (Winter)' package is a 16-day tour covering Casablanca, Barcelona, Valencia, Madrid, Costa Del Sol, Granada, Fes, Lisbon, Tangier, Huelva, and Porto. Throughout this journey, participants will enjoy a variety of unique cultural and culinary experiences, including a traditional Moroccan Experience in Fes and a lively Flamenco show accompanied by a drink. The itinerary also features delicious local treats such as tasting Belem Pastry in Lisbon, wine tasting in Porto, savoring hot chocolate with churros in Madrid, indulging in an authentic Paella dinner in Granada, and enjoying a refreshing Horchata drink in Valencia.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome to Casablanca!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca, Morocco'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Marrakesh\nToday we proceed for a guided tour of Marakkesh: See the Bahia Palace, El Badi Palace, Koutoubia Mosque & gardens, Kasbah Area, Free time at Jemma El Fna Square, Visit Souk El Attarin & Smata.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca,\xa0Morocco'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Casablanca with Entrance to Hassan II Mosque - Guided City Tour of Fes\nToday, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Casablanca: See Royal Palace, Hassan II Mosque with free time in Boulevard de la Corniche. Next, we drive to Fes for a Guided City Tour of Fes: Visit the Old Madinas, See the Chouara Tannary, the exotic ancient Medina, UNESCO World Heritage Site, walk through the narrow, bustling streets and alleys that are home to brilliantly, the Bab Boujlloud Gate, En-Nejjarine Square, Es-Seffarine Square, huedsouks.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ramada by Wyndham / Barcelo Fes or similar in Fes, Morocco'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided Tour of Chefchaouen\nToday, we drive to Chefchaouen for the Guided City Tour: See the Place Outa El Hammam, Grand Mosque. Later drive towards Tangiers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Kenzi Solazur or similar in Tangier, Morocco'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Tangier – Ferry to Algecires, Spain\nToday, we proceed for a Guided City Tour: See the Spartel Cape at the extreme northwest of Africa and the Hercules Caves, linked with Hercules, the man who separated Africa from Europe. From here, you will get an exceptional view of the Strait of Gibraltar and the Atlantic Ocean as well.\xa0 Later we take a ferry to Algecires, Spain.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Castillo de Colomres – Guided tour of Alhambra Complex - Generalife Gardens\nToday we visit Castillo de Colomres: a castle dedicated to the life and adventures of Christopher Columbus. Next, we proceed to the McArthur Glen shopping outlet (if time permitting) where you can enjoy great deals on designer labels. Later, we drive to Granada and on arrival enjoy guided tour of the Alhambra Complex and Generalife Gardens.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Cordoba – Visit Mezquita - Guided City Tour of Sevilla – Flamenco Show\nToday, we drive to Cordoba for a guided city tour of the city with entrance to Mezquita. The Mosque–Cathedral of Córdoba, officially known as the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption is a former Islamic Mosque and a UNESCO world heritage site. Next, we drive to Sevilla for a Guided City Tour: See the Sevilla Tower, Sevilla Cathedral, Giralda, Santacruz Quarter. Later this evening, we enjoy the traditional Flamenco show.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alcora or similar in Huelva/ Sevilla, Spain'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nAlgarve boat tour – Proceed to Lisbon, Portugal\nToday, we drive to Lagos. Upon arrival, we proceed the boat tour at Algarve experiencing its walled old town, cliffs and Atlantic beaches. Next, we drive to Lisbon.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon, Portugal'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Lisbon - Visit Cabo da Roca\nToday, we enjoy a Guided City Tour of Lisbon, Belem Tower, Jeronimos Monastery, Monument to the Discoveries, 25th April Bridge and more interesting sites. We also visit the town of Sintra and Cabo da Roca – Western most end of the European continent.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon,\xa0Portugal'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Porto – Visit a wine cellar with wine tasting\nToday we drive to Porto and enjoy a Guided City Tour. World-famous for its port wine, Porto is Portugal’s second largest city. The historic centre of Porto was designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1996. Next, we visit a Wine Cellar with Wine Tasting.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided city tour of Salamanca – Photo stop at the walls of Avila - Proceed to Madrid\nToday, we first visit the city of Avila, where you shall get see the ‘Walls of Avila’. Later proceed to Salamanca; known as the “Golden city” for the sandstone used in the construction of its buildings, it has the third oldest existing university in the world, one of the Top 10 cathedrals in Spain, and one of the most beautiful plazas in all of Spain. On arrival we proceed on a Guided Tour of Salamanca where see the: Ponte Roma, Salamanca University, Salamanca Cathedral and the Salamanca square. Next, we continue our journey to Madrid.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Madrid – Visit a Bullring – Guided city tour of Toledo – Visit a Sword factory\nToday, we proceed for a Guided City Tour of Madrid: Visit the largest bullring of Madrid – Las Ventas Plaza De Torros, see the old town, the City Centre, Church of San Francisco El Grande, Royal Palace and many more historical and modern sites. Later, we drive to Toledo. On arrival, we enjoy a guided tour: see the cathedral of Toledo, Puente San Martin through narrow winding cobblestone streets. Next, we visit a Sword factory and then drive to Madrid.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid,\xa0Spain'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Valencia\nToday, we drive to Valencia.\xa0 On arrival, we enjoy a Guided City Tour: See the Plaza Reina, the stunning cathedral, the central market and much more.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfst, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Exe Puerto Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain'}, {'day': 14, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Barcelona – Visit Sagrada Familia\nToday, we drive to Barcelona.\xa0 On arrival, we enjoy a Guided City Tour: See the Olympic Village, Montjuic, Placa de Catalunya, and many more beautiful sights. Later, we visit the Sagrada Familia - the yet unfinished minor basilica, a UNESCO World Heritage site.\n\xa0\nNote: Entrance to Sagrada Familia depends upon the availability given by the Sagrada Familia officials and may not necessarily be done on this day. In such cases, the itinerary will be amended accordingly to cover all inclusions, or an alternate attraction will be provided.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain'}, {'day': 15, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation tour of Montserrat\nToday, we drive to Montserrat – a multi peaked rocky range which houses the virgin of Montserrat and Spain’s first national park. Next, we drive back to Barcelona and spend Later, spend some free time at Barcelona beach.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona,\xa0Spain'}, {'day': 16, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Spain and Portugal tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n\xa0\nNote: In major European Cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n2 nights at Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca, Morocco.\xa0\n1 night at Ramada by Wyndham / Barcelo Fes or similar in Fes, Morocco.\n1 night at Hotel Kenzi Solazur or similar in Tangier, Morocco.\n1 night at\xa0TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa Del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain\n1 nights at Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 night at\xa0Alcora or similar in Huelva / Sevilla, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 nights at AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Exe Puerto Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n2 nights at Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca, Morocco.\xa0\n1 night at Ramada by Wyndham / Barcelo Fes or similar in Fes, Morocco.\n1 night at Hotel Kenzi Solazur or similar in Tangier, Morocco.\n1 night at\xa0TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa Del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain\n1 nights at Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 night at\xa0Alcora or similar in Huelva / Sevilla, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 nights at AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Exe Puerto Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'ES', 'countryName': 'Spain', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'MORC', 'countryName': 'Morocco', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'PT', 'countryName': 'Portugal', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 421600.0, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights at Kenzi Basma / Marriott or similar in Casablanca, Morocco.\xa0\n1 night at Ramada by Wyndham / Barcelo Fes or similar in Fes, Morocco.\n1 night at Hotel Kenzi Solazur or similar in Tangier, Morocco.\n1 night at\xa0TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa Del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain\n1 nights at Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 night at\xa0Alcora or similar in Huelva / Sevilla, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Lagoas Park / Mercure Almada or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 nights at AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Exe Puerto Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches.\n03 Local lunches.\n13 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n02 Local dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nMultiple entry Schengen and Moroccan visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', 'MOROCCO\nMarrakesh\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nCasablanca\n\nGuided City Tour with entrance to Hassan II Mosque\n\nFes\n\nGuided City Tour including the 02 oldest Medinas\n\nChefchaouen\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nTangier\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nSPAIN\nBenalmadena\nVisit Castillo de Colomres\n\xa0\nGranada\n\xa0\n\nGuided tour of Alhambra Palace complex and the Generalife Gardens\n\nCordoba\n\nGuided City Tour\nEntrance to Mezquita\n\nSeville\n\nGuided City Tour\nSee the Flamenco show\n\nSalamanca\n\nOrientation Tour\n\nAvila\n\nPhoto stop at the walls of Avila\\\n\nMadrid\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit the bullring - Las Ventas Plaza De Torros\n\nToledo\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Sword Factory\n\nValencia\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nBarcelona\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Sagrada Familia\n\nMontserrat\n\nVisit Montserrat Monastery\n\nPORTUGAL\nLisbon\n\nGuided city tour\xa0\nVisit Sintra and Cabo de Roca\n\nPorto\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit to a wine cellar with wine tasting\n\nLagos\n\nAlgarve boat tour\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nMultiple entry Schengen and Moroccan visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0 \xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 16 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 48 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\nAirline And Airfare\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. \nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. \nPassengers joining this tour must travel to/ from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nJoining Direct Clients\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. \nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\nHotels\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds, and the room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air-conditioned / air cooled, nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat waves in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0Coaches\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. \nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. \nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. \nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. \nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. The Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. \nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms, to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\n\nMeals \n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. \nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing \n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. \nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\n\nGeneral \n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. \nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. \nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary, to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer about the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. \nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. \nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. \nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. \nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. \nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. \nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. \nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. \nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non-cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0\xa0 \nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. \nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. \nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at the prevailing rate of exchange. \nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/Cordoba267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/42053_Hassan_Mosque_city_of_Casablanca_Morocco_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Casablanca753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/fes.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Chefchaouene_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/tangier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Alhambra_Granada_Spain.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Cordoba753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Lisbon2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Lisbon3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Porto753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Salamanca753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Madrid_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/Valencia753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015164/itinerary/SagradaFamiliaBARCELONASPAINshutte