rgh\n\xa0\nHop on Hop Off Sightseeing: Explore Edinburgh at your own pace with a hop-on hop-off bus ticket. Ascend the city's seven hills for spectacular views and marvel at iconic landmarks like Edinburgh Castle and the Royal Mile, connecting the castle to the Palace of Holyrood House. This flexible tour lets you discover the city's rich history, museums, galleries, and restaurants exactly as you wish.\n\xa0\nScotch Whisky Tasting - The True Spirit of Scotland (Optional Activity): Whisky Tasting In English 17:30 [Duration Approximately 90 mins]\xa0\nEnjoy a tasting of three single malts from regions across Scotland, plus a new make spirit (unaged whisky). The experience is enriched with the history, traditions, and anecdotes that Scotch carries with it. The experience begins at the entrance of John Knox House, from where we will head to a central whisky bar for the tasting. Experienced local guide. Origins and evolution of Scotch The Golden Age of Scotch whisky Edinburgh’s influence on Scotch’s fame Regions and styles Memorable anecdotes Includes: 3 tastings of exclusive single malts + 1 new make (unaged whisky) [Supplement Cost - € 45 Per Adult, child entrance will be upon request basis only]", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Centre Royal Mile - Hunter Square (Standard) /\xa0Leonardo Royal Haymarket (Value) or similar in\xa0Edinburgh'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nEdinburgh To Inverness\n\xa0\nTransfer:\n\nYou will travel from Edinburgh to Inverness on a 2nd Class Train Ticket with changes (4 hrs)\nUpon your arrival at Inverness train station, make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Royal Highland (Standard) /\xa0Leonardo (Value) or similar in Inverness'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nInverness\n\xa0\nCity Sightseeing Inverness Hop-On Hop-Off Tour: Explore the very best of Inverness on this unlimited hop-on hop-off bus tour. With unlimited access for 24 hours, you'll see all of the key landmarks of this pretty Scottish destination. The bus tour includes an informative audio tour commentary in English, ensuring there is an educational element to the experience. Enjoy stunning panoramic from the open-top deck, seeing Castle Street, Ness Bank, Bank Street, Bishops Road, Dochgarroch Lock and Tomnahurich Bridge on your way round.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Royal Highland (Standard) /\xa0Leonardo (Value) or similar in Inverness'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nInverness To Glasgow\n\xa0\nTransfer:\n\nYou will travel from Inverness to Glasgow on a 2nd Class Train Ticket with changes (4 hrs)\nUpon your arrival at Glasgow train station, make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Mercure (Standard) /\xa0Jurys Inn (Value) or similar in Glasgow'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGlasgow\n\xa0\nGuided Walking Tour: Discover Glasgow’s heritage on a short walking tour featuring iconic landmarks like City Chambers, George Square, Merchant City, and Glasgow Cathedral. Enjoy fascinating stories, stunning Victorian architecture, and quirky statues—all in just about an hour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Mercure (Standard) /\xa0Jurys Inn (Value) or similar in Glasgow'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Glasgow\n\xa0\nTransfer: 3- 4 hrs prior to your departure flight, you will have a private transfer from the hotel to Glasgow (GLA) airport.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a life