 on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\nBlack out Period: Royal Edinburgh Military Tattoo festival: August 7–29, 2026 (*Approx. Surcharge to be GBP 50 – 80 Per Person)\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 01st April to 30th September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/EdinburghCity7534.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/Edinburgh7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/EdinburghCastle7536.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/Inverness2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/inverness-ness.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/Glasgow_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/Glasgow_Cathedral_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014545/itinerary/Glasgow_1500.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015515', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015515', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Georgia Van Tour - Tbilisi with Kazbegi', 'days': 5, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Travel across Georgia on an exclusive & personalized itinerary designed for individuals, families and small groups. On VAN TOURS, your journeys are planned exclusively by private vans and hosted by English speaking drivers & guides. Travel from Tbilisi; covering the most scenic sights of Georgia. Visit Tbilisi; walk through the old town. Don’t miss the snowcapped Caucasian mountains and the Gaudari Ski Resort. Experience the charms of Georgia as you visit the oldest winery regions and visit Kazbegi. Visit old towns and drive past the high passes at Gaudari. Lastly, don’t miss the walk over the Dashbashi Canyon as you visit Diamond Bridge. Our specially designed VAN TOURS will ensure comfort and convenience throughout your travel. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS: Visit TBILISI, MSHKETA & CHRONOCILES OF GEORGIA; walk through the old town of Tbilsi and take a cable car to get a beautiful view of the city from the Narikala fortress. Visit Mtskheta, the ancient capital and enclaved city. Visit the Chronicles of Georgia. Visit SIGHNAGHI & KAKHETI, the old town of Sighnaghi & one of the oldest wines making regions of the world. Visit KAZBEGI & GAUDARI. Drive past the countryside and stop by the Annauari fortress, visit Gaudari Ski Resort, Friendship Monument and Holy Trinity Church in Kazbegi. Visit DASHBASHI CANYON & DIAMOND BRIDGE'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013001_0_20241007131222.pdf', 'price': 54425, 'packageSummary': "The 'Georgia Van Tour - Tbilisi with Kazbegi' package is a 5-day tour covering Tbilisi and its surrounding scenic regions. The itinerary includes visits to the historic old town of Tbilisi, the ancient capital of Mtskheta, the Chronicles of Georgia, and the beautiful winemaking region of Sighnaghi and Kakheti. Participants will enjoy a personalized private van experience with an English-speaking driver and guide, taking a cable car to Narikala fortress, exploring the Ananuri fortress, visiting the Gudauri Ski Resort and the Holy Trinity Church in Kazbegi, and walking across the spectacular Diamond Bridge at Dashbashi Canyon.", 'images': [], 'minimumPrice': 54425, 'thumbnailImage': 'AlmatyCity.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Van Tours', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015515 is named 'Georgia Van Tour - Tbilisi with Kazbegi' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tbilisi, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 54425.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n\n\nCity\n\xa0Hotel\n\n\nAlmaty (5N)\n\xa0Hotel Regardel or Kazakhstan or similar in Almaty\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nBreakfast\xa0:\xa0Buffet\xa0Breakfast\xa0will\xa0be\xa0offered\xa0at\xa0all\xa0the\xa0hotels.\xa0(\xa0Except\xa0Day\xa01).\xa0\nDinner : Indian Dinner\n. Inclusions: Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Services of an English-speaking driver cum guide. Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Entrance fees - Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine Tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, Diamond bridge 2 half a litre bottles of water per person per day. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism Tax Visa charges for NRI passengers (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage, or passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure as of 1st August 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leads to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink are not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips for guides, hotel waiters, drivers, etc. Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Test. Highlights of the package: Travel across Georgia on an exclusive & personalized itinerary designed for individuals, families and small groups. On VAN TOURS, your journeys are planned exclusively by private vans and hosted by English speaking drivers & guides. Travel from Tbilisi; covering the most scenic sights of Georgia. Visit Tbilisi; walk through the old town. Don’t miss the snowcapped Caucasian mountains and the Gaudari Ski Resort. Experience the charms of Georgia as you visit the oldest winery regions and visit Kazbegi. Visit old towns and drive past the high passes at Gaudari. Lastly, don’t miss the walk over the Dashbashi Canyon as you visit Diamond Bridge. Our specially designed VAN TOURS will ensure comfort and convenience throughout your travel. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS: Visit TBILISI, MSHKETA & CHRONOCILES OF GEORGIA; walk through the old town of Tbilsi and take a cable car to get a beautiful view of the city from the Narikala fortress. Visit Mtskheta, the ancient capital and enclaved city. Visit the Chronicles of Georgia. Visit SIGHNAGHI & KAKHETI, the old town of Sighnaghi & one of the oldest wines making regions of the world. Visit KAZBEGI & GAUDARI. Drive past the countryside and stop by the Annauari fortress, visit Gaudari Ski Resort, Friendship Monument and Holy Trinity Church in Kazbegi. Visit DASHBASHI CANYON & DIAMOND BRIDGE.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaisalmer', 'cityCode': 'JSA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': '