y/StGilles.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015332/itinerary/PITONDELAFOURNAISE.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014603', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014603', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Classical Greece', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Olympia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Delphi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kalambaka', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014603_0_20260903151210', 'price': 138626, 'packageSummary': "The 'Classical Greece' package is a 7-day tour covering Athens, Olympia, Delphi, and Kalambaka, before returning to Athens. Throughout this historic journey, participants will explore iconic archaeological sites, visit ancient ruins, and immerse themselves in the rich mythology and culture of Greece through guided sightseeing tours of legendary landmarks.", 'images': ['Athens.jpg', 'Olympia.jpg', 'Delphi.jpeg', 'Meteora_Monastry.avif', 'Athense.jpeg', 'AcropolisinAthens.avif', 'Athens_1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 138626, 'thumbnailImage': 'AcropolisinAthens.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014603 is named 'Classical Greece' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Athens, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Athens Transfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Olympia, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Start Of The 4 Days Classical Tour The Classical Tour: Explore the glory of ancient Greece and delve into its rich history with this four-day adventure tour from Athens. Visit five UNESCO'S world heritage sites including the impressive Meteora, the mythical site of Ancient Olympia and Delphi archaeological site also known as the 'The Navel of the world'. Leave by the coastal road to the Corinth Canal (short stop). Drive on and visit the Theatre of Epidauros, famous for its remarkable acoustics. Then proceed to the town of Nauplion (short photo stop), drive on to Mycenae and visit the Archaeological Site and the Tomb of Agamemnon. Then depart for Olympia through Central Peloponnese and the towns of Tripolis and Megalopolis. Overnight in Olympia, the cradle of the Olympic Games. Special Note: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick up for the same will be from selected central points., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Delphi, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Olympia To Delphi Transfers: The Classical tour is an escorted covering the most popular historical circuits of the country Olympia to Delphi will be a coach transfer as a part of the Classical Tour In the morning visit the Archaeological Site with the Sanctuary of Olympian Zeus, the Ancient Stadium and the Archaeological Museum. Then drive on through the plains of Eliad and Achaia until the magnificent bridge which is crossing the Corinthian Bay from Rion to Antirion. Pass by the picturesque towns of Nafpactos (Lepanto) and Itea, later arrive in Delphi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kalambaka, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Delphi To Kalambaka Transfers: The Classical tour is an escorted covering the most popular historical circuits of the country Delphi to Kalambaka will be a coach transfer as a part of the Classical Tour In the morning visit the Archaeological Site and the Museum. Depart for Kalambaka, a small town stated at the foot of the astonishing complex of Meteora, gigantic rocks., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Kalambaka To Meteora - Athens Transfers: The Classical tour is an escorted covering the most popular historical circuits of the country Kalambaka will be a coach transfer as a part of the Classical Tour Visit Meteora, among striking scenery, perched on top of huge rocks which seem to be suspended in mid-air, stand ageless Monasteries, where you can see exquisite specimens of Byzantine art. Return to Athens via Trikala, Lamia, Thermopylae (short stop to see across the road the Leonida's Monument). Arrive in Athens early in the evening., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half-Day Guided Tour Of Athens On Shared Basis (Sic) Athens Sightseeing The Acropolis and Acropolis Museum Step into history on a half-day guided tour of Athens. The morning begins at the Panathenaic Stadium, birthplace of the modern Olympic Games, then past the Temple of Olympian Zeus and the elegant Athens Trilogy University, Academy, and National Library. Ascend to the legendary Acropolis to explore the Parthenon, Erechtheion, and Temple of Athena Nike. End your morning at the Acropolis Museum, where ancient treasures are brought to life. [Entrance fees to Acropolis & Museum is included] Special Note: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick up for the same will be from selected central points., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Athens Transfers: From Athens hotel to the Airport in private transfer. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 138626.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nPremium\xa0Category (5* Hotels Or Similar)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nATHENS\n\n\nOlympia » Delphi » Kalambaka\n\n\n\n\nRoyal Olympic or similar\n\n\nOn Request - Hotels will be confirmed closer to the date of travel\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nStandard Category (3* Hotels Or Similar)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nAthens\n\n\nOlympia » Delphi » Kalambaka\n\n\n\n\nAcropolis Ami or similar\n\n\nOn Request - Hotels will be confirmed closer to the date of travel\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nValue Category (4* Hotels Or Similar)\xa0\n\n\n\n\nATHENS\n\n\nOlympia » Delphi » Kalambaka\n\n\n\n\nTitania or similar\n\n\nOn Request - Hotels will be confirmed closer to the date of travel\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\nHalf Board Meal arrangement as part of Classical Tour\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 1 Night accommodation in Athens based on the hotel category selected or similar 4 Days / 3 nights Classical tour in First class hotels on Half - Board basis (SIC) 2 Nights’ accommodation in Athens based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Half Board Meal arrangement as part of Classical Tour Transportation: Private Airport Transfer from Athens Airport to Hotel Escorted Tour from Day 2 to Day 5 Private Airport transfer from Santorini Hotel to Airport Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Half-day City tour of Athens with new Acropolis Museum on sharing basis tour coach. Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 May 2026 – 15 October 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'ci