y and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015379/44164_Radisson_Hotel_Cruise_Moscow_Russia_Optional_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015379/itinerary/89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015379/itinerary/007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015379/itinerary/650718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015379/itinerary/Murmansk-1.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014771', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014771', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Truly Turkiye - Private Tour', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kusadasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kusadasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Antalya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Antalya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Antalya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG004643_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 188488, 'packageSummary': "The 'Truly Turkiye - Private Tour' package is a 9-day tour covering Antalya, Kusadasi, Cappadocia, and Istanbul. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient ruins of Ephesus, the breathtaking fairy chimneys of Cappadocia, the historic old town of Kaleici in Antalya, and iconic landmarks in Istanbul such as the Hagia Sophia and the Blue Mosque. Participants will enjoy private guided city tours, a scenic Bosphorus cruise, and the unforgettable experience of a hot air balloon ride over the unique Cappadocian landscape.", 'images': ['Istanbul753.jpg', 'Istanbul.jpg', 'Cappadocia7532.jpg', 'Cappadocia7531.jpg', 'Kusadasi_1.jpg', 'Pamukkale.jpg', 'Antalya.jpg', 'Antalya-Beach.jpg', 'return-home.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 188488, 'thumbnailImage': '60842_Mevlana_Museum_in_Konya_Turkey_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cultural', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014771 is named 'Truly Turkiye - Private Tour' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Istanbul, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival into Istanbul Transfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion Optional Activity: Bosphorus Dinner Cruise Enjoy an enchanting evening on the Bosphorus Strait with a leisurely dinner cruise that showcases Istanbul’s beauty by night. Sail between Europe and Asia as you pass iconic landmarks such as the Bosphorus Bridge, Dolmabahçe Palace, and the illuminated waterfront mansions. The experience is complemented by a delicious Turkish dinner and live entertainment, often including traditional music and folk dance performances, making it a memorable blend of scenic views, culture, and cuisine. [The supplement cost for this activity will be approx. US$ 80/- per adult & US$ 55/- for children below 6 years], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full-Day Guided Tour Of Istanbul On Private Basis Istanbul City Tour : Between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel (pickup time subject to hotel location) for a full day guided city tour. The tour includes visits to the Hagia Sophia Mosque (entrance not included), the pride of Byzantine architecture; the Byzantine Hippodrome, once the venue for ancient chariot races; and the Blue Mosque, renowned for its exquisite blue Iznik tiles. You will also visit the Topkapi Palace (entrance not included), the former residence of the Ottoman Sultans, followed by time at the Grand Bazaar, Turkey’s largest covered market with over 4,000 shops. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant, after which you will be transferred back to your hotel. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a private basis, The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary. Entrance to the Hagia Sophia Mosque and Topkapi Palace is available at an additional supplement. Supplement costs: Hagia Sophia: US$ 35 - 40/- Per adult (*Under 8 years Free) Topkapi Palace US$ 65/- Per adult (*Under 6 years Free), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Istanbul To Cappadocia Transfers: Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight Upon arrival at Cappadocia, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the Hotel. Special Notes: Please note that the domestic flight from Istanbul to Cappadocia is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement. Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Explore Cappadocia Optional Activity: Hot Air Balloon If a hot air balloon ride is on your bucket list, Cappadocia offers one of the most iconic experiences in the world. Drift gently at sunrise above a surreal, lunar like landscape of volcanic rock formations, fairy chimneys, and honeycombed valleys, as dozens of vibrantly colored balloons rise alongside you. This unforgettable experience offers breathtaking panoramic views and spectacular photo opportunities. [The supplement cost for this activity will be upon “On Request Basis”] Please Note: Children below 6 years of age or under 120 cm in height are not permitted to participate in the hot air balloon ride. Cappadocia Sightseeing: After breakfast, between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel to begin a full day tour of Cappadocia. The first stop is Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley), known for its spectacular fairy chimneys and uniquely shaped rock formations set amidst beautiful landscape. You will then visit Pasabag (Monks Valley), famous for its remarkable double and triple headed rock formations, once used as hermit dwellings by monks. Lunch will be served in Avanos, a town renowned for its traditional pottery craftsmanship and located along the Red River (Kizilirmak). After lunch (on your own), continue to the Goreme Open Air Museum, the heart of Cappadocia, celebrated for its rock cut churches adorned with wall paintings dating back to the 10th century, depicting scenes from the life of Jesus and early Christian monastic life. The tour concludes with a photo stop at Uchisar Castle, a natural rock citadel and one of the largest fairy chimney formations in the region, offering panoramic views of Cappadocia. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a private basis, The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kusadasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Cappadocia To Izmir Transfers: 1. Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight 2. Upon arrival at Izmir, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the hotel in Kusadasi. Special Notes: 1. Please note that the domestic flight from Cappadocia to Izmir is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement. 2. Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kusadasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full Day Kusadasi Tour On Private Basis Transfers: The sightseeing will be on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary. Full Day Kusadasi Tour on PVT basis: Enjoy a full-day guided tour of Kusadasi, including a visit to the ancient city of Ephesus, one of the best-preserved archaeological sites in the Mediterranean followed by the Temple of Artemis and the charming Sirince Village The tour then takes you to the charming Sirince Village, known for its traditional architecture, local crafts, and scenic hillside atmosphere. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant. After the tour, you will be transferred back to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Antalya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full Day Pamukkale Tour On Private Basis Transfers: The sightseeing will be on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary. Full Day Pamukkale Tour on PVT basis: Enjoy a full-day guided tour of Pamukkale, including visits to the ancient city of Hierapolis , the famous Cotton Terraces, and key archaeological sites such as the Domitian Gate, Latrina, Oil Factory, Agora, Byzantine Gate, Triton Fountain, and the Temple of Apollo. After the tour, you will be transferred to Antalya., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Antalya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full Day Antalya Tour On Private Basis Transfers: The sightseeing will be on a private basis. The vehicle will be provided only for the scheduled sightseeing activities and will not be at disposal beyond the itinerary. Full Day Antalya Tour with Kursunlu Waterfall on PVT basis: Enjoy a full day sightseeing experience in Antalya, featuring visits to Kursunlu Waterfall, the historic Old Town of Kaleici, and key landmarks including Hadrian’s Gate, Hidirlik Hill, the Clock Tower, the Fluted Minaret, and Palm Street., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Antalya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Antalya Transfers: From Antalya hotel to Antalya Airport in a private transfer.Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 188488.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nFour Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy Hotel/ Konak Taksim\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nDedeli Cave / Sunak Cave Hote\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nEfe Boutique Hotel/ Karaaslan Inn hotel/ Ladies Beach or similar\n\n\n\n\nAntalya\n\n\nBest western Khan / Prime Hotel / Ring Downtown or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n5* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nThe Elysium Taksim/Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa Hotel\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nHanedan Cave Suites / Acer Cave Suites\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nSignature Blue Hotel / Le Bleu Hotel / Ramada Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nAntalya\n\n\nHoliday Inn Lara / Doubletree Hilton City Center or similar\n\n\n\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Istanbul based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Kusadasi based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Antalya based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: Private Airport Transfer from Istanbul Airport to Hotel Private transfer from Istanbul hotel to Istanbul Airprort Private Airport Transfer from Kayseri Airport to Cappadocia Hotel Private Airport transfer from Cappadocia Hotel to Kayseri Airport Private Airport Transfer from Izmir Airport to Kusadasi Hotel Private Airport transfer from Kusadasi Hotel to Izmir Airport Private Airport Transfer from Antalya Airport to Antalya Hotel Private Airport transfer from Antalya Hotel to Antalya Airport Sightseeing: (Sightseeing is provided on a private basis only. The vehicle is available strictly as per the sightseeing itinerary and is not available at disposal) Full Day Tour of Istanbul on private basis (PVT) Cappadocia Sightseeing Tour on private basis (PVT) Full Day Kusadasi Tour on private basis (PVT) Full Day Pamukkale Tour on private basis (PVT) Full Day Antalya Tour on private basis (PVT) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Blackout Dates: HOLIDAY DATE National Sovereignty and Children’s Day 23-04-2026 Labor and Solidarity Day 01-05-2026 Commemoration of Atatürk, Youth and Sports Day 19-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 1st day 27-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 2nd day 28-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 3rd day 29-04-2026 Eid al-Adha last day 30-05-2026 Democracy and National Unity Day 15-07-2026 Victory Day 30-08-2026 Republic Day 29-10-2026. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': '