Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL\xa0is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client.\xa0TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015523/AlmatyCity.jpeg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014871', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014871', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Paris, Swiss & Italy (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)', 'days': 12, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Free upgrade to 1st class TGV (Paris - Swiss Train sector)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014871_0_20260609181401.pdf', 'price': 359063, 'packageSummary': "The 'Paris, Swiss & Italy (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 12-day tour covering the scenic and historic destinations of Paris, Central and Southern Switzerland, Venice, Florence, and Rome. This specially curated itinerary offers travelers a seamless journey through Europe's most iconic cities, with key highlights including a complimentary upgrade to first-class travel on the high-speed TGV train sector connecting Paris to Switzerland. Participants will experience a rich blend of cultural sightseeing, breathtaking alpine landscapes, and historic landmarks across France, Switzerland, and Italy.", 'images': ['ParisViewFrance7533.jpg', 'EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'Lake_Lucerne.jpg', '89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'Glacier_3000_753.jpg', 'Zurich_753.jpg', 'VeniceGrandCanal.jpg', 'Florence09.jpg', 'RomeCity.jpg', 'TreviFountain11.jpg', 'colosseum11.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 359063, 'thumbnailImage': 'Interlaken2678.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Durga Puja Special', 'Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Trending Now', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014871 is named 'Paris, Swiss & Italy (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' and spans 12 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Paris Transfers: Upon your arrival at the airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 14:00 - 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Moulin Rouge Show (Optional): Experience the world famous Moulin Rouge in Paris, an iconic cabaret known for its dazzling performances, vibrant costumes, and spectacular dance routines, including the legendary French Cancan. Located in the heart of Montmartre, this unforgettable show combines music, glamour, and artistry, offering a true taste of Parisian nightlife., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour Paris City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time. Special Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris To Central Switzerland Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Central Switzerland. Upon your arrival in Central Switzerland, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Lucerne Tour with Swiss Pass on your own (Optional): Travel to Lucerne with Swiss pass on your own as there are many sights in a small area in Lucerne like Chapel Bridge with the Water Tower which is the landmark of Lucerne and the most photographed monument in Switzerland., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mt. Titlis Excursion Mt. Titlis Excursion: Don't miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier's deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe's highest suspension bridge. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Jungfraujoch Excursion Jungfraujoch Excursion: Don't miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world - famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Glacier 3000 (Optional): Escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Optional Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer - including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks - Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland. Bollywood Tour (Optional): Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central / Southern Swiss To Venice Via Train Transfers: 1. Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. 2. Upon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Gondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice's main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour Murano, Burano and Torcello Half - Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano - three islands in the Venetian Lagoon - on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water. Highlights: Visit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat Watch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano See Byzantine churches on Torcello - the Church of Santa Fosca Browse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses McArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional): Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfy your thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Venice To Florence Via Train Transfers: 1. Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Florence. 2. Upon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. 3. You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Florence To Rome Via Train Transfers: 1. Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Rome. 2. Upon your arrival at Rome train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Rome - Hop On Hop Off Tour Hop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome's iconic sights and landmarks on a hop on hop off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Rome Breakfast at the hotel and free time until check out (depending on the flight departure time). Gather your memories of tour and head on to airport in a private vehicle for your return Journey., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 359063.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nPARIS\n\n\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hotel Champerret Elysees / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nCENTRAL / SOUTHERN SWITZERLAND\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern - city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nROME\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFLORENCE\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\n\n\n\n\nVENICE\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\n\n\n\n, Hotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\nCITY NAME\nValue\n\n\nPARIS\nMercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel ParisCenter Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse /Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque H