\xa0\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket Paris – Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver\nLucerne - Venice.\nVenice - Florence.\nFlorence - Rome.\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nInteractive City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC)\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade.\nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n\nIntercity travel by Train (Second Class):\n\n\xa0London - Paris (Eurostar).\nParis - Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver.\nLucerne - Venice.\nVenice - Florence.\nFlorence - Rome.\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/Interlaken2678.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/ParisViewFrance7533.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/Lake_Lucerne.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/Glacier_3000_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/Zurich_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/VeniceGrandCanal.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/Florence09.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/RomeCity.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/TreviFountain11.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014871/itinerary/colosseum11.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015301', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015301', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan, Georgia And Armenia - Winter', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Sheki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yerevan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yerevan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yerevan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['What’s More Like - Azerbaijani Tea and Halwa tasting at Nizami street Hi-tea at Gabala Wine tasting and local bread at Kakheti Wine Region Brandy Tasting at Ararat Brandy Distellery'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 219656, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan, Georgia And Armenia - Winter' package is a 10-day tour covering the scenic cities of Tbilisi, Baku, Yerevan, and Sheki. The itinerary offers a rich blend of cultural and culinary experiences, featuring unique activities such as Azerbaijani tea and halwa tasting at Nizami Street, a delightful hi-tea at Gabala, and wine tasting paired with traditional local bread in the famous Kakheti Wine Region. Additionally, participants will enjoy a premium brandy tasting session at the historic Ararat Brandy Distillery, making this winter journey through the Caucasus truly unforgettable.", 'images': ['Baku_753.jpg', 'MaidenTower.jpg', 'Gabala_753.jpg', 'Sheki753.jpg', 'MtskhetaTiblisi753.jpg', 'GergetiTrinityChurch753.jpg', 'Signagi753.jpg', 'Yerevan7534.jpg', 'Yerevan7535.jpg', 'Yervan7536.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 219656, 'thumbnailImage': 'ArmeniayervanCity2679.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015301 is named 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan, Georgia And Armenia - Winter' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Baku, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome Azerbaijan - Arrival - Check in Welcome to Baku, Azerbaijan. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500 hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. NOTE All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Baku, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Baku - Walking tour of Old Town – Visit Hyder Aliyev Center - Free time at Nizami Street This morning after buffet breakfast, visit the Heydar Aliyev Center, a building complex in Baku, Azerbaijan designed by Iraqi-British architect Zaha Hadid. Later visit to Highland Park and Alley of Martyrs followed by photo-stop at the National Assembly and the Flame towers - the tallest skyscraper in Baku. Post lunch, we proceed on walking tour of Old City - the historical core of Baku. Photo stop at the Shirvanshahs Palace and Maiden Tower. Later enjoy some free time at Nizami Street.Walking tour of Old Town : 2 KMS (Approx.) Walking tour of Old Town : 2 KMS (Approx.), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Baku, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Ateshgah ( Fire Temple) - Visit Yanar Dag ( Fire Mountain) - Free time at Deniz Mall This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed towards Ateshgah (Fire Temple) - a temple used as a Hindu and Zoroastrian place of worship. The pentagonal complex, which has a courtyard surrounded by cells for monks and a tetra pillar-altar in the middle, was built during the 17th and 18th centuries. Later proceed to Yanar Dag (Fire Mountain)- a natural gas fire which blazes continuously on a hillside on the Absheron Peninsula. Free time at Deniz Mall., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Sheki, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion to Gabala - Visit Tufandag Ski Resort - Photo stop at Lake Nohur This morning after buffet breakfast, checkout and depart towards Gabala, the north-west of Azerbaijan. On arrival proceed on a Cable Car ride to Tufandaq Winter-Summer Tourism Complex located at 1920 meters above sea level. Enjoy free time at the top. Later we stop at Nohur Lake - one of the most beautiful lakes surrounded by mountains. Drive to Sheki and Check-in to hotel. DRIVING DISTANCE: Baku to Gabala: 220 KMS (Approx.) Gabala to Sheki: 90 KMS (Approx.), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive to Tbilisi, Georgia - Arrival - Guided City Tour of Tbilisi - Visit Chronicles of Georgia - Visit Mtskheta This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and drive to Tbilisi, Georgia. On arrival proceed for an orientation tour. Visit Metekhi Cathedral.Take a cable car ride to Narikala Fortress. Walk across the Bridge of Peace & continue to explore underground sulphur baths the district of naturally hot mineral waters. Walk pass the cafe street - Shardeni, Synagogue, Sioni Cathedral and the most ancient Anchiskhati Basilica.Visit Chronicles of Georgia. Drive to Mtskheta - Visit the Jvari Monastery and Svetitskoveli Cathedral Walk along the narrow streets of Mtskheta for some souvenir shopping. Sheki to Tbilisi: 275 KMS (Approx.) Note: There will be Border Crossing today with a walk involving approx. 800 metres with your luggage followed with immigration formalities Minimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion - Visit Ananuri Fortress – Visit Zhinvali Reservoir – Gudauri Ski Resort – Visit Georgia - Russia Friendship Monument - Visit Kazbegi & Gregeti Trinity Church This morning after buffet breakfast, we will drive on the Georgian Military Highway, to the border with Russia. Throughout the route you will be surrounded by dramatic mountain scenery. Visit Ananuri Fortress. Stop at the Zhinvali Water Reservoir and see an amazing view of the Gudauri Ski Resort. Later we visit Stepantsminda known as Kazbegi, small town in the north-east Georgia. Visit the Gergeti Trinity Church located 2200 meters above sea level. Return to Tbilisi. (Note: The route to Kazbegi passes through high altitude mountain passes; driving pass the route is subject to weather conditions that affected by heavy snowfall. In case of heavy snow fall the tour routing will be altered.) Tbilisi to Kazbegi: 160 KMS (Approx.), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion - Visit Kahheti Wine Region - Visit Old Town of Sighnaghi - Visit Bodbe Monastery This morning after buffet breakfast, we will visit the most picturesque hilltop town of Sighnaghi, situated in the very heart of Georgia’s wine growing region, with pastel houses and narrow cobblestone streets overlooking the vast Alazani Valley and Caucasus Mountains. After wine tasting & bread making at Kakheti Winery we will visit Bodbe Female Monastery (grave of Saint Nino - enlightener of Georgia). Return to Tbilisi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Yerevan, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive to Armenia - Photo-stop at Dilijan National Reserve - Photostop at Lake Sevan - Visit Sevanavank Monastery - Visit Vernissage Market This morning after buffet breakfast, we check-out and proceed to Armenia via Georgian border. Stop at Dilijan - famous for its amazing surroundings, situated in Dilijan National Park. This small city, lost in forests and mountains with alpine meadows around, is home to numerous Armenian artists, composers, and filmmakers. The next stop is Lake Sevan - a blue gem of the Armenian mountain cape. Visit Sevanavank monastery located on Lake Sevan. Later we visit Vernissage; a famous street market in Yervan., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Yerevan, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Yervan - Visit Genocide Museum - Visit Ararat Brandy Distillery - Museum & Brandy Tasting Tour - Visit Charents Arch - Visit Geghard Monastery - Visit Garni Pagan Temple This morning after buffet breakfast, we will proceed on a guided city tour of Yerevan - visit to Mother Armenia statue & Cascade, a giant stairway in the capital city which links downtown Kentron area of Yerevan with the Monument neighbourhood. Later visit Tsitsernakaberd - The Armenian Genocide Museum .See the Opera House and visit the Republic Square. Visit the Ararat Brandy Distillery; visit the brandy museum followed by tasting. After lunch we proceed to the valley of Azat river, stop first at Charent’s Arch – the breathtaking lookout point of the biblical Mount Ararat (known from the Bible as the landing place of Noah’s Ark). Drive to the Geghard Monastery carved out of a huge monolithic rock. Visit Geghard Monastery.Visit the Garni Pagan Temple. Drive back to Yerevan. Evening free to walk around the city center., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Yerevan, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 219656.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott /\xa0Hotel Hilton Garden Inn Riverview\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\n02 nights accommodation at Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yervan\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast (Except Day 1)\n03 Local / Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n05 Indian Jain/ Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian lunches\n08 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n01 Indian Packed Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B – Breakfast/ L- Lunch/ LC- Lunch coupon/PL – Packed Lunch/ D – Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodations at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same has to be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Thomas Cook Tour Manager/ local representative. (subjected to minimum 25 customers) Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st August 2026. Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Exclusions: Airfare not included for JD passenger Minimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia. Compulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 3/guest/day The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Visa charges for NRI passengers. Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st August, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Thomas Cook will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. Meals other than what is mentioned in itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passenger other than those included in your itinerary.. Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: What’s More Like - Azerbaijani Tea and Halwa tasting at Nizami street Hi-tea at Gabala Wine tasting and local bread at Kakheti Wine Region Brandy Tasting at Ararat Brandy Distellery.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Udaipur', 'cityCode': 'UDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'cityCode': 'SXR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAA650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan, Georgia And Armenia - Winter' package is a 10-day tour covering the scenic cities of Tbilisi, Baku, Yerevan, and Sheki. The itinerary offers a rich blend of cultural and culinary experiences, featuring unique activities such as Azerbaijani tea and halwa tasting at Nizami Street, a delightful hi-tea at Gabala, and wine tasting paired with traditional local bread in the famous Kakheti Wine Region. Additionally, participants will enjoy a premium brandy tasting session at the historic Ararat Brandy Distillery, making this winter journey through the Caucasus truly unforgettable.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome Azerbaijan - Arrival - Check in\nWelcome to Baku, Azerbaijan. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500 hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nNOTE\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided city tour of Baku - Walking tour of Old Town – Visit Hyder Aliyev Center - Free time at Nizami Street\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, visit the Heydar Aliyev Center, a building complex in Baku, Azerbaijan designed by Iraqi-British architect Zaha Hadid. Later visit to Highland Park and Alley of Martyrs followed by photo-stop at the National Assembly and the Flame towers - the tallest skyscraper in Baku. Post lunch, we proceed on walking tour of Old City - the historical core of Baku. Photo stop at the Shirvanshahs Palace \xa0and Maiden Tower. Later enjoy some free time at Nizami Street.Walking tour of Old Town : 2 KMS (Approx.)\nWalking tour of Old Town : 2 KMS (Approx.)\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Ateshgah ( Fire Temple) - Visit Yanar Dag ( Fire Mountain) - Free time at Deniz Mall\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed towards Ateshgah (Fire\xa0 Temple) - a temple used as a Hindu and Zoroastrian place of worship. The pentagonal complex, which has a courtyard surrounded by cells for monks and a tetra pillar-altar in the middle, was built during the 17th and 18th centuries. Later proceed to Yanar Dag (Fire Mountain)- a natural gas fire which blazes continuously on a hillside on the Absheron Peninsula. Free time at Deniz Mall.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion to Gabala - Visit Tufandag Ski Resort -\xa0 Photo stop at Lake Nohur\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, checkout and\xa0 depart towards Gabala, the north-west of Azerbaijan. On arrival proceed on a Cable Car ride to Tufandaq Winter-Summer Tourism Complex located at 1920 meters above sea level. Enjoy free time at the top. Later we stop at\xa0 Nohur Lake - one of the most beautiful lakes surrounded by mountains. Drive to Sheki and Check-in to hotel.\nDRIVING DISTANCE:\n\nBaku to Gabala: 220 KMS (Approx.)\nGabala to Sheki: 90 KMS (Approx.)\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Palace or similar in Sheki'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive to Tbilisi, Georgia - Arrival - Guided City Tour of Tbilisi - Visit Chronicles of Georgia -\xa0 Visit\xa0 Mtskheta\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out and drive to Tbilisi, Georgia. On arrival proceed for an orientation tour. Visit Metekhi Cathedral.Take a cable car ride to Narikala Fortress. Walk across the Bridge of Peace & continue to explore underground sulphur baths the district of naturally hot mineral waters. Walk pass the cafe street - \xa0Shardeni, Synagogue, Sioni Cathedral and the most ancient Anchiskhati Basilica.Visit Chronicles of Georgia. Drive to Mtskheta - Visit the Jvari Monastery and Svetitskoveli Cathedral Walk along the narrow streets of Mtskheta for some souvenir shopping.\nSheki to Tbilisi: 275 KMS (Approx.)\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\n\nThere will be Border Crossing today with a walk involving approx. 800 metres with your luggage followed with immigration formalities\nMinimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard By Marriott\xa0or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion -\xa0 Visit Ananuri\xa0 Fortress – Visit Zhinvali Reservoir –\xa0 Gudauri Ski Resort\xa0 – Visit Georgia - Russia Friendship Monument - Visit Kazbegi & Gregeti Trinity Church\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, we will drive on the Georgian Military Highway, to the border with Russia. Throughout the route you will be surrounded by dramatic mountain scenery. Visit Ananuri Fortress. Stop at the\xa0 Zhinvali Water Reservoir and see an amazing view of the Gudauri Ski Resort. Later we visit Stepantsminda known as Kazbegi, small town in the north-east Georgia. Visit the\xa0 Gergeti Trinity Church located 2200 meters above sea level. Return to Tbilisi.\n\xa0\n(Note: The route to Kazbegi passes through high altitude mountain passes; driving pass the route is subject to weather conditions that affected by heavy snowfall. In case of heavy snow fall the tour routing will be altered.)\n\xa0\nTbilisi to Kazbegi: 160 KMS (Approx.)', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard By Marriott\xa0or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion - Visit Kahheti Wine Region - Visit Old Town of\xa0 Sighnaghi - Visit Bodbe Monastery\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, we will visit the most picturesque hilltop town of Sighnaghi, situated in the very heart of Georgia’s wine growing region, with pastel houses and narrow cobblestone streets overlooking the vast Alazani Valley and Caucasus Mountains. After wine tasting & bread making at Kakheti Winery we will visit Bodbe Female Monastery (grave of Saint Nino - enlightener of Georgia). Return to Tbilisi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard By Marriott\xa0or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive to Armenia - Photo-stop at Dilijan National Reserve - Photostop at Lake Sevan - Visit Sevanavank Monastery - Visit Vernissage Market\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, we check-out and\xa0 proceed to Armenia via Georgian border. Stop at \xa0Dilijan - famous for its amazing surroundings, situated in Dilijan National Park. This small city, lost in forests and mountains with alpine meadows around, is home to numerous Armenian artists, composers, and filmmakers. The next stop is Lake Sevan - a blue gem of the Armenian mountain cape.\xa0Visit Sevanavank monastery located on Lake Sevan. Later we visit Vernissage; a famous street market in Yervan.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yerevan'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Yervan - Visit Genocide Museum - Visit Ararat Brandy Distillery -\xa0 Museum & Brandy Tasting Tour\xa0 - Visit Charents Arch - Visit Geghard Monastery - Visit Garni Pagan Temple\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, we will proceed on a guided city tour of\xa0 Yerevan - visit to \xa0Mother Armenia statue & Cascade, a giant stairway in the capital city which links downtown Kentron area of Yerevan with the Monument neighbourhood. Later visit Tsitsernakaberd - The Armenian Genocide Museum .See the Opera House and visit the Republic Square. Visit the Ararat Brandy Distillery; visit the brandy museum followed by tasting. After lunch we proceed to the valley of Azat river, stop first at\xa0Charent’s Arch\xa0– the breathtaking lookout point of the biblical Mount Ararat (known from the Bible as the landing place of Noah’s Ark). Drive to the\xa0Geghard Monastery\xa0carved out of a huge monolithic rock. Visit Geghard Monastery.Visit the\xa0Garni Pagan Temple. Drive back to Yerevan. Evening free to walk around the city center.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yerevan'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd of\xa0 Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott /\xa0Hotel Hilton Garden Inn Riverview\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\n02 nights accommodation at Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yervan\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott /\xa0Hotel Hilton Garden Inn Riverview\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\n02 nights accommodation at Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yervan\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GE', 'countryName': 'Georgia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AZ', 'countryName': 'Azerbaijan', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AM', 'countryName': 'Armenia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 219700.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott /\xa0Hotel Hilton Garden Inn Riverview\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\n02 nights accommodation at Hotel Ani Plaza or similar in Yervan\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast (Except Day 1)\n03 Local / Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n05 Indian Jain/ Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian lunches\n08 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n01 Indian Packed Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B – Breakfast/ L- Lunch/ LC- Lunch coupon/PL – Packed Lunch/ D – Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', 'VISA REQUIREMENTS \n\nSingle - Azerbaijan visa - It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nSingle - Georgia visa - It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nVisa On arrival Exemptions applicable in case of Valid Visa Holders to specified countries.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nTransfers as per itinerary.\n', '\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', '\nBaku\n\nGuided City Tour Of Baku\nWalking Tour Of Baku Old Town\xa0\nPhotostop At Maiden Tower\nPhotostop At Shirvanshahs Palace\xa0\xa0\nVisit To Heydar Aliyev Center\xa0\nVisit Ateshgah (Fire Temple) & Yanar Dag (Fire Mountain)\xa0\nFree Time At Nizami Street\xa0\nDay Excursion To Gabala Ski Resort & Photo Stop At Lake Nohur\nDrive To Tbilisi\n\n\xa0\nTbilisi\n\nGuided City Tour Of Tbilisi With Cable Car To Narikala Fortress\nVisit Chronicles Of Georgia\nGuided City Tour Of Mtskheta\nDay Excursion - Visit Ananuri Fortress , Zhinvali Reservoir, Gudauri Ski Resort, Visit Georgia\xa0\nRussia Frienship Monument & Kazbegi\xa0\nDay Excursion - Kakheti Wine Region , Old Town Of Sighnaghi & Bodbe Monsatery\nFree Time For Shopping\n\n\xa0\nSevan & Yervan\n\nVisit Dilijan National Park\nPhotostop At Lake Sevan\nVisit Sevanavank Monastery\nVisit Charents Arch\nVisit Geghard Monastery\nVisit Garni Pagan Temple\xa0\nGuided City Tour Of Yervan\nVisit Armenian Genocide Memorial\nVisit Ararat Brandy Distillery With Tasting Tour\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n<li><span style="color: #ff6600;"><strong>Airfare not included for JD passenger</strong></span></li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\nAccommodations at the hotels specified above or similar.\xa0\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same has to be borne by the guest).\xa0\nServices of a professional & multilingual Thomas Cook Tour Manager/ local representative. (subjected to minimum 25 customers)\xa0\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of\xa01st August 2026.\xa0\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nAirfare not included for JD passenger\nMinimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia.\nCompulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 3/guest/day\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\xa0\xa0\nVisa charges for NRI passengers.\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\xa0\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\xa0\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\xa0\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\xa0\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st August, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Thomas Cook will not be held responsible for the same.\xa0\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\xa0\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\xa0\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\xa0\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc.\xa0\nMeals other than what is mentioned in itinerary.\xa0\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passenger other than those included in your itinerary.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/ArmeniayervanCity2679.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Baku_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/MaidenTower.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Gabala_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Sheki753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/MtskhetaTiblisi753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/GergetiTrinityChurch753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Signagi753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Yerevan7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Yerevan7535.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015301/itinerary/Yervan7536.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014535', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014535', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Swiss and Italy', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014535_0_20260920223908', 'price': 297021, 'packageSummary': "The 'Swiss and Italy' package is a 10-day tour covering Central and Southern Switzerland, Venice, Rome, and Florence. The itinerary includes visits to the majestic Swiss Alps, the historic Colosseum, the Vatican City, the scenic canals of Venice, and the artistic treasures of Florence. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic mountain excursions, romantic gondola rides, and immersive cultural experiences across these iconic European destinations.", 'images': ['Lucerne_3.jpg', '89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'Glacier.jpg', '62615_Venice_753.jpg', 'MuranoGlassShowroomVenice.jpg', '51449_Field_of_Miracles_Pisa_Italy_753.jpg', 'Rome753.jpg', 'Colosseum_753.jpg', 'rome.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 297021, 'thumbnailImage': 'VENICE_6.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014535 is named 'Swiss and Italy' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zurich Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Zurich airport, you will walk across to the Flughafen station (located adjacent to the airport) for your train to Central Switzerland. From train station transfer on your own to the hotel. Free Time Optional Sightseeing: Travel to Lucerne with Swiss pass on your own as there are many sights in a small area in Lucerne like Chapel Bridge with the Water Tower which is the landmark of Lucerne and the most photographed monument in Switzerland., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mt. Titlis Excursion Mt. Titlis Excursion: Don't miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier's deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe's highest suspension bridge. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Jungfraujoch Excursion Jungfraujoch Excursion: Don't miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world-famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Glacier 3000 (Optional): Escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Optional Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer – including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks – Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland. Bollywood Tour (Optional): Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central / Southern Swiss To Venice Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. Upon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own (combination of car and water taxi). Gondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice's main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano — three islands in the Venetian Lagoon — on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water. Highlights: Visit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat Watch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano See Byzantine churches on Torcello— the Church of Santa Fosca Browse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses McArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional): Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfy your thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable. Planning to Visit? Click the link below to conveniently book your shuttle bus tickets and enjoy exciting deals at the nearest outlet: https://mgbooking.tripodeck.com/home?orderCustId=6977233, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Venice To Florence Via Train & Excursion To Pisa Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Florence. Upon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half-day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Florence To Rome Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Rome. Upon your arrival at Rome train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Rome - Hop On Hop Off Tour Hop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome's iconic sights and landmarks on a hop-on hop-off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Rome Breakfast at the hotel and free time until check out (depending on the flight departure time). Gather your memories of tour and head on to airport in a private vehicle for your return Journey. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 297021.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 4 Nights’ accommodation in Central Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Departure Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Airport Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] Swiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver Lucerne – Venice. (Subject to availability until ticketed) Venice – Florence. (Subject to availability until ticketed) Florence – Rome. (Subject to availability until ticketed) Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Mt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Jungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Venice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade. Venice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour Florence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence Rome: Hop on Hop off in Rome Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms And Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''