 ["\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0"]}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nDeparture Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets:\xa0[Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver\nLucerne\xa0– Venice.\xa0(Subject to availability until ticketed)\nVenice – Florence.\xa0(Subject to availability until ticketed)\nFlorence – Rome.\xa0(Subject to availability until ticketed)\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade. \nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence \nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n4 Nights’ accommodation in Central Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Night accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Meals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nDeparture Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver\nLucerne – Venice. (Subject to availability until ticketed)\nVenice – Florence. (Subject to availability until ticketed)\nFlorence – Rome. (Subject to availability until ticketed)\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade. \nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence \nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Insurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. \n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\n\xa0Terms And Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n\xa0\n\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/VENICE_6.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/Lucerne_3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/Glacier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/62615_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/MuranoGlassShowroomVenice.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/51449_Field_of_Miracles_Pisa_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/Rome753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/Colosseum_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014535/itinerary/rome.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015115', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015115', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Lapland of Norway', 'days': 5, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 278775, 'packageSummary': "The 'Lapland of Norway' package is a 5-day tour focusing on the Arctic city of Tromso. The itinerary includes visits to the iconic Arctic Cathedral, the Polaria aquarium, and the Tromso Cable Car for breathtaking panoramic views of the surrounding mountains. Participants will enjoy unforgettable activities such as chasing the magical Northern Lights, embarking on husky sledding adventures, and exploring the stunning Norwegian fjords.", 'images': ['Tromso3.jpg', 'Tromso1.jpg', 'Tromso2.jpg', 'Rovaniemi4.jpg', 'Norway1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 278775, 'thumbnailImage': '', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015115 is named 'Lapland of Norway' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tromso, Meals: NA, Description: Arrive Tromso Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Tromso Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Tromso Northern lights chase by minivan: Join an evening minivan tour in Tromso North Norway to chase the magical Northern Lights. With a local guide we take you to spots with the highest chance to witness this unique natural phenomenon. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Walking Tour and Gondola Ride Tromso Walking City Tour: Join a guided walking tour of Tromsos historic city centre founded in 1795. Explore Storgata, the Market Place, Catholic and Protestant Cathedrals, Roald Amundsen monument, and Mack Brewery the Gateway to the Arctic. Fjellheisen Gondola Ride: Take a short ride to the Fjellheisen cable car and ascend quickly to the top. Enjoy breathtaking views as you reach the summit where a spectacular panoramic view of Tromso awaits., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reindeer Sledding Tour Reindeer sledding Tour: Experience traditional Sami reindeer sledding near Tromso. Travel through nature on authentic sleds, learn about Arctic life, and meet your Sami guide who shares insights into reindeer herding and local culture above the Arctic Circle., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Husky Safari Tour Husky safari Tour: Enjoy a husky safari in Tromso guiding your own sled through snowy landscapes frozen lakes and forests. Visit a husky farm meet friendly dogs and learn about their training while exploring the Arctic wilderness. Special Note: Northern Lights Cruise optional at EUR 120., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will be transferred from Tromso hotel to the Airport on private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Day 01 Welcome to Berlin! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Overnight in Berlin, Germany (D) Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration. Day 02 Guided tour of Potsdam - Entrance to Sanssouci Gardens - Guided tour of Berlin – Visit Topography of Terror Museum Today, we proceed for a guided tour of Potsdam with entrance to Sanssouci Gardens. We also take a Photo stop at Glienicke - Bridge of Spies. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Berlin: Visit the Berlin tower, See the famous Berlin Wall, the Reichstag, visit the Alexander Platz, where you will see the World Time Clock. Later, we visit the Topography of Terror, an indoor and open-air museum where between 1933 and 1945 the principal instruments of Nazi persecution and terror were located. Overnight in Berlin, Germany (B, L, D) Day 03 Proceed to Krakow – Horse Carriage ride Today, we drive to Krakow. Upon arrival, we proceed for a Horse Carriage ride in the old town. Overnight in Krakow, Poland (B, L, D) Day 04 Auschwitz Concentration Camp - Wieliczka Salt mines Today we proceed for a guided tour of the Auschwitz Concentration Camp of WW II. A sombre experience that highlights the atrocities that occurred here between 1939 – 1945. Later we visit to Wieliczka Salt mines – one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site. Overnight in Krakow, Poland (B, L, D) Day 05 Visit Brewery with beer tasting – Onto Prague Today, we proceed to visit a local brewery to taste their famous beers. We also spend some free time in the city. Next, we drive to Prague. Overnight in Prague, Czech Republic (B, L, D) Day 06 Guided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane Today, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917. Overnight in Prague, Czech Republic (B, LL, D) Day 07 Guided Walking tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Vienna Today we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. We also see the Church of St Vitus & the clock bridge. Next, we proceed to Vienna. Overnight in Vienna, Austria (B, PL, D) Day 08 Guided city tour of Vienna – Visit the glorious Schonbrunn Palace – Orientation city tour of Bratislava Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, Parliament building, Hofburg Palace and many more interesting monuments. Next, we visit the famous Schonbrunn Palace - a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site and experience the grand tour. Later we proceed to Bratislava for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Later, we drive to Budapest. Overnight in Budapest, Hungary (B, L, D) Day 09 Guided city tour of Budapest – Hungarian Horsemanship show Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Budapest: Visit the Citadel, Fisherman’s Bastion Heroes Square, see the Chain Bridge that connects the cities of Buda and Pest. Next, we proceed to enjoy a show of Hungarian Horsemanship. Overnight in Budapest, Hungary (B, LL, D) Day 10 See the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre – Farewell dinner on Danube River Cruise Today, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes. In the evening, we enjoy a farewell dinner on board the Danube River Cruise. Overnight in Budapest, Hungary (B, LL, D) Day 11 Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. (B) Note: · In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. EX- HUBS: MUMBAI | DELHI| BANGALORE| HYDERABAD |CHENNAI |COCHIN | AHMEDABAD | KOLKATA | JD DEPARTURE DATES OCT 2026 18 NOV 2026 17 WHAT YOUR TOUR PRICE INCLUDES · Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. · All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. · Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. · Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. · All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. · Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). WHAT YOUR TOUR PRICE DOES NOT INCLUDE · If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. · Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. · Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 278775.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 4 Nights’ accommodation in Tromso based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis] Arrival Transfers from Tromso Airport to the Hotel Departure transfers from Tromso hotel to the Tromso Airport Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Tromso Northern lights chase by minivan Walking City Tour Fjellheisen Gondola Ride Reindeer sledding Tour Husky safari Tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Black out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 – 10 January’27. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 1 November 2026 – 31 March 2027 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Lapland of Norway' package is a 5-day tour focusing on the Arctic city of Tromso. The itinerary includes visits to the iconic Arctic Cathedral, the Polaria aquarium, and the Tromso Cable Car for breathtaking panoramic views of the surrounding mountains. Participants will enjoy unforgettable activities such as chasing the magical Northern Lights, embarking on husky sledding adventures, and exploring the stunning Norwegian fjords.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Tromso\xa0\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Tromso Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\xa0\xa0\nTromso Northern lights chase by minivan: Join an evening minivan tour in Tromso North Norway to chase the magical Northern Lights. With a local guide we take you to spots with the highest chance to witness this unique natural phenomenon.\xa0\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'NA', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Saga or similar\xa0'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nWalking Tour and Gondola Ride\xa0\xa0\nTromso Walking City Tour: Join a guided walking tour of Tromsos historic city centre founded in 1795. Explore Storgata, the Market Place, Catholic and Protestant Cathedrals, Roald Amundsen monument, and Mack Brewery the Gateway to the Arctic.\xa0\xa0\nFjellheisen Gondola Ride: Take a short ride to the Fjellheisen cable car and ascend quickly to the top. Enjoy breathtaking views as you reach the summit where a spectacular panoramic view of Tromso awaits.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Saga or similar\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nReindeer Sledding Tour\xa0\xa0\nReindeer sledding Tour: Experience traditional Sami reindeer sledding near Tromso. Travel through nature on authentic sleds, learn about Arctic life, and meet your Sami guide who shares insights into reindeer herding and local culture above the Arctic Circle.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Saga or similar\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nHusky Safari Tour\nHusky safari Tour: Enjoy a husky safari in Tromso guiding your own sled through snowy landscapes frozen lakes and forests. Visit a husky farm meet friendly dogs and learn about their training while exploring the Arctic wilderness.\nSpecial Note: Northern Lights Cruise optional at EUR\xa0120.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Saga or similar\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\xa0\xa0\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Tromso hotel to the Airport on private transfer.\xa0\xa0\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight.\xa0\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDay 01\nWelcome to Berlin!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Overnight in Berlin, Germany\n(D)\n\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.\n\xa0\nDay 02\nGuided tour of Potsdam - Entrance to Sanssouci Gardens - Guided tour of Berlin – Visit Topography of Terror Museum\nToday, we proceed for a guided tour of Potsdam with entrance to Sanssouci Gardens. We also take a Photo stop at Glienicke - Bridge of Spies. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Berlin: Visit the Berlin tower, See the famous Berlin Wall, the Reichstag, visit the Alexander Platz, where you will see the World Time Clock. Later, we visit the Topography of Terror, an indoor and open-air museum where between 1933 and 1945 the principal instruments of Nazi persecution and terror were located.\nOvernight in Berlin, Germany\n(B, L, D)\n\xa0\nDay 03\nProceed to Krakow – Horse Carriage ride\nToday, we drive to Krakow. Upon arrival, we proceed for a Horse Carriage ride in the old town.\nOvernight in Krakow, Poland\n(B, L, D)\n\xa0\nDay 04\nAuschwitz Concentration Camp - Wieliczka Salt mines\nToday we proceed for a guided tour of the Auschwitz Concentration Camp of WW II. A sombre experience that highlights the atrocities that occurred here between 1939 – 1945. Later we visit to Wieliczka Salt mines – one of the oldest in Europe and a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site.\nOvernight in Krakow, Poland\n(B, L, D)\n\xa0\nDay 05\nVisit Brewery with beer tasting – Onto Prague\nToday, we proceed to visit a local brewery to taste their famous beers. We also spend some free time in the city. Next, we drive to Prague.\nOvernight in Prague, Czech Republic\n(B, L, D)\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDay 06\nGuided city tour of Prague – Entrance to the Prague Castle – Visit St. Vitus Cathedral – Golden Lane\nToday, we proceed for a walking guided city tour of Prague: Visit the Prague Castle, its courtyards and St. Vitus Cathedral from inside and walk through the Golden Lane and see the house where Franz Kafka, the famous Czech writer stayed between 1916 and 1917.\nOvernight in Prague, Czech Republic\n(B, LL, D)\n\xa0\nDay 07\nGuided Walking tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Vienna\nToday we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. We also see the Church of St Vitus & the clock bridge. Next, we proceed to Vienna.\nOvernight in Vienna, Austria\n(B, PL, D)\n\xa0\nDay 08\nGuided city tour of Vienna – Visit the glorious Schonbrunn Palace – Orientation city tour of Bratislava\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, Parliament building, Hofburg Palace and many more interesting monuments. Next, we visit the famous Schonbrunn Palace - a UNESCO World Cultural Heritage site and experience the grand tour. Later we proceed to Bratislava for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town. Later, we drive to Budapest.\nOvernight in Budapest, Hungary\n(B, L, D)\n\xa0\nDay 09\nGuided city tour of Budapest – Hungarian Horsemanship show\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Budapest: Visit the Citadel, Fisherman’s Bastion Heroes Square, see the Chain Bridge that connects the cities of Buda and Pest. Next, we proceed to enjoy a show of Hungarian Horsemanship.\nOvernight in Budapest, Hungary\n(B, LL, D)\n\xa0\nDay 10\nSee the Basilica Esztergom - Visit Visegrad Castle – See the Knight Tournament – Visit Szentendre – Farewell dinner on Danube River Cruise\nToday, we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Next we proceed for the Danube bend tour: Visit the Visegrad Castle located on the banks of river Danube with breath taking views of the river. Experience the Knight tournament and learn about the ways of the medieval age. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes. In the evening, we enjoy a farewell dinner on board the Danube River Cruise.\nOvernight in Budapest, Hungary\n(B, LL, D)\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDay 11\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n(B)\n\xa0\nNote:\n\xa0\n· In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n\xa0\nEX- HUBS: MUMBAI | DELHI| BANGALORE| HYDERABAD |CHENNAI |COCHIN | AHMEDABAD | KOLKATA | JD\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDEPARTURE DATES\nOCT 2026 18\nNOV 2026 17\nWHAT YOUR TOUR PRICE INCLUDES\n· Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\n· All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\n· Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\n· Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\n· All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n· Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\xa0\nWHAT YOUR TOUR PRICE DOES NOT INCLUDE\n· If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\n· Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 11 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 33 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\n· Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality Saga or similar\xa0'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 278800.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nArrival Transfers from Tromso Airport to the Hotel\nDeparture transfers from Tromso hotel to the Tromso Airport\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\xa0\n\nTromso Northern lights chase by minivan\xa0\xa0\nWalking City Tour\xa0\xa0\nFjellheisen Gondola Ride\xa0\nReindeer sledding Tour\xa0\xa0\nHusky safari Tour\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n4 Nights’ accommodation in Tromso based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\nTransportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis]\n\nArrival Transfers from Tromso Airport to the Hotel\nDeparture transfers from Tromso hotel to the Tromso Airport\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\n\nTromso Northern lights chase by minivan\xa0\nWalking City Tour\xa0\nFjellheisen Gondola Ride\nReindeer sledding Tour\xa0\xa0\nHusky safari Tour\xa0\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\nBlack out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 – 10 January’27\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'IMPORTANT NOTES:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700