ling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/Interlaken2678.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/ParisViewFrance7533.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/Lake_Lucerne.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/Glacier_3000_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014520/itinerary/Zurich_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014757', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014757', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026'], 'packageName': 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Nov - Dec 2026)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stokmarknes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Narvik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kiruna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG009291_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 465892, 'packageSummary': "The 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Nov - Dec 2026)' package is a 9-day tour covering Rovaniemi, Narvik, Stokmarknes, Kiruna, Helsinki, and Tromso. The itinerary includes spectacular opportunities to witness the magical Aurora Borealis, visit the world-famous Santa Claus Village, and explore the stunning winter landscapes of the Arctic. Participants will enjoy thrilling husky and reindeer sledding safaris, scenic fjord excursions, and guided city sightseeing tours that showcase the unique culture and beauty of these northern destinations.", 'images': ['Tromso_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Northern_Lights_Tromso_753_Adobe.jpg', 'ArcticDay3.jpg', 'ArcticDay4.jpg', 'ArcticDay5.jpg', 'Rovaniemi2.jpg', 'Romaniemi_7534.jpg', 'Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'Helsinki1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 465892, 'thumbnailImage': 'Arctic_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014757 is named 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Nov - Dec 2026)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tromso, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Tromso! The Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local representative will meet you outside the airport. Proceed to the hotel and check–in. Spend some free time on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Whale Watching Cruise (OPTIONAL) - Fjellheisn Cable Car – Northern Lights Hunting Tour Today, the morning is at leisure OR you have a chance to see the orcas and humpback whales feed on herring in the nearby fjords. Next, we take a cable car to Fjellheisen and enjoy a spectacular view of Tromsø and its beautiful surroundings from above. Later in the evening, we proceed on a Northern Lights Hunting Tour. Tromsø is famous for being one of the best places in the world to see the Northern Lights., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Stokmarknes, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Tromso - Visit Polaria - Express Ferry to Harstad Today, proceed for an orientation tour of Tromsø known for its role as a gateway to the Arctic. Next, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Narvik, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Sea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum Today, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today. Next, we proceed to Narvik., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kiruna, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda Today, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Arktikum Musuem – Northern Lights Hunting tour Today, we proceed to Rovaniemi: Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus. Upon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Santa Claus Village - Visit Husky Farm with Husky Ride Today, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later, we arrive at a husky dog farm. On arrival at the husky kennel you will be welcomed by eager, but friendly barking, as these dogs are keen to get going! This adventurous safari through the Lappish wilderness takes you on a fun journey with friendly husky dogs who truly love running. Here we enjoy husky ride., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Fly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church Today, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Return back home with pleasant memories! Today, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give us your suggestions. Till we meet again! Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 465892.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna,\xa0Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi,\xa0Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland.\n, \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n05 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n02 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n03 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 01st Feb 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g. Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of Euro 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour which is 9 Days, the total Tips amount is Euros 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 01st Feb, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that what is mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: Airline And Airfare The Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 01st Feb, 2026. Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers. Passengers Missing Flights To Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves For Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents. Passengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To / From The Hub City At Their Own Expense. Hotels All Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or In The Outskirts. Most Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size. As A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room. For Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room. A Person 12 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And Above 12 Years, An Adult. Hotel Rooms May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions. Functioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority. During Heat Wave In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures. Most Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms. Due To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City. Any Damages Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay, Shall Be Payable By The Passengers. We Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary. In Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast. Coaches Most Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean. Due To Hygienic Reasons It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets In The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives. Eating & Drinking Is Not Permitted In The Coach. One Check In Bag And One Hand Bag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space In The Coach. In Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop. Coaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach. Due To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities; As Per Eu Norms To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And By Foot. Meals Meals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible. On Certain Days Packed Lunch Will Be Provided. Sightseeing On Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same. Generally, You Will Have To Walk At Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And At The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible. General In Case Any Member Of The Group Tests Positive For Covid-19, Customers Will Need To Unconditionally Abide, Adhere And Comply Solely At Your Costs And Expenses To All Laws, Rules, Notifications, Travel Advisories, Guidelines, Directives And Communications Issued From Time To Time By All Or Any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies In India Or Abroad, Related To Your Tour To The Foreign Destination And/Or On Your Return From The Tour To Your Home Destination In India Or Abroad Including But Not Limited To Covid-19 Protocols On Quarantine, Vaccinations Etc. Or In Connection With Any Other Pandemic, Epidemic, Disease, Condition Etc., Which May Be Communicated By All Or Any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies In India Or Abroad With Or Without Notice At Any Point Of Time Whether At The Commencement Of The Tour, During The Tour And/Or On The Completion Of The Tour, As The Case May Be”. On Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members. A Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour. Security Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary. Please Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage. Disabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client. Tcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour. Normal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges. The Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delay Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services. The Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same. There Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E. Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour All Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted). Optional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy. Gst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India. In Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed. The Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purpose Only. Tours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange. Please Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE210', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Nov - Dec 2026)' package is a 9-day tour covering Rovaniemi, Narvik, Stokmarknes, Kiruna, Helsinki, and Tromso. The itinerary includes spectacular opportunities to witness the magical Aurora Borealis, visit the world-famous Santa Claus Village, and explore the stunning winter landscapes of the Arctic. Participants will enjoy thrilling husky and reindeer sledding safaris, scenic fjord excursions, and guided city sightseeing tours that showcase the unique culture and beauty of these northern destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome to Tromso!\nThe Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local representative will meet you outside the airport. Proceed to the hotel and check–in. Spend some free time on your own.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWhale Watching Cruise (OPTIONAL) - Fjellheisn Cable Car – Northern Lights Hunting Tour \nToday, the morning is at leisure OR you have a chance to see the orcas and humpback whales feed on herring in the nearby fjords.\xa0Next, we take a cable car to Fjellheisen and enjoy a spectacular view of Tromsø and its beautiful surroundings from above. Later in the evening, we proceed on a Northern Lights Hunting Tour. Tromsø is famous for being one of the best places in the world to see the Northern Lights.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation tour of Tromso - Visit Polaria - Express Ferry to Harstad\nToday, proceed for an orientation tour of Tromsø known for its role as a gateway to the Arctic. Next, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum\nToday, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today.\xa0 Next, we proceed to Narvik.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda\nToday, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Arktikum Musuem – Northern Lights Hunting tour \nToday, we proceed to Rovaniemi: Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus.\nUpon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Visit Santa Claus Village - Visit Husky Farm with Husky Ride\nToday, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later, we arrive at a husky dog farm. On arrival at the husky kennel you will be welcomed by eager, but friendly barking, as these dogs are keen to get going! This adventurous safari through the Lappish wilderness takes you on a fun journey with friendly husky dogs who truly love running. Here we enjoy husky ride.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\nToday, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nReturn back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give\xa0us your suggestions. Till we meet again!\xa0\n\xa0\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna,\xa0Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi,\xa0Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland.\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna,\xa0Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi,\xa0Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland.\n', '1': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 465900.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik,\xa0Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna,\xa0Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi,\xa0Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki,\xa0Finland.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n05 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n02 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.', '\nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n03 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\n', 'As per itinerary', '\nMultiple entry Schengen visa. \nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['NORWAY\nTromso\n\nOrientation Tour\xa0\nFjellheisen Cable Car\xa0\nNorthern Lights Hunting Tour\xa0\nVisit Polaria\xa0\nExpress Ferry To Harstad\n\nStokmarknes\n\nSea Eagle Safari To Trollfjord By Rib Boat\nVisit Hurtigruten Museum\n\nSWEDEN\nJukkasjarvi\xa0\n\nVisit Narvik War Museum\nVisit The Ice Hotel With Lunch\n\nKiruna\n\nVisit Nuti Sami Silda\n\nFINLAND\nRovaniemi\xa0\n\nVisit The Santa Claus Village\xa0\nNorthern Lights Hunting Tour\n\nSaariselka\xa0\n\nVisit Husky Farm With Husky Ride\n\nHelsinki:\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Helsinki\xa0\nVisit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\xa0\n', 'NORWAY:\nTromso:\n\nOrientation Tour\xa0\nWhale Watching Cruise\nFjellheisen Cable Car\xa0\nVisit Polaria\xa0\nGuided Northern Lights Tour\xa0\nExpress Ferry to Harstad\n\nNarvik:\n\nVsist the Narvik War Museum\n\nStokmarknes:\n\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat\nVisit Hurtigruten Museum\n\nSWEDEN:\nJukkasjarvi:\n\nVisit the Ice Hotel with lunch\n\nKiruna:\n\nOrientation tour\nVisit Nuti Sami Silda with Reindeer Feeding\n\nFINLAND:\nRovaniemi:\n\nVisit the Santa Claus Village\xa0\nArctic Crossing with Certificate\xa0\n\nSaariselka:\n\nVisit Husky Farm and Enjoy a Forest Walk (NOV)\nOR\nVisit Husky Farm and Enjoy a Husky Ride (DEC)\xa0\n\nHelsinki:\n\nGuided City Tour of Helsinki\xa0\nVisIt Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\xa0\nVisit Sibelius Park and Sibelius Monument\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<div>Rest assured, Thomas Cook\'s experienced &amp; knowledgeable&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it\'s a question or a challenge, our&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Manager</span>&nbsp;is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</div>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 01st Feb 2026.\xa0\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g. Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of Euro 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour which is 9 Days, the total Tips amount is Euros 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 01st Feb, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that what is mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'IMPORTANT NOTES:\nAirline And Airfare\n\nThe Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 01st Feb, 2026. Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers.\nPassengers Missing Flights To Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves\xa0\nFor Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents.\xa0\nPassengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To / From The Hub City At Their Own Expense.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\n\nAll Hotels Will Be Either Around The Airport Area Or In The Outskirts.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Have Only Twin Beds. Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size.\xa0\nAs A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room.\xa0\nFor Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room.\xa0\nA Person 12 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And Above 12 Years, An Adult.\xa0\nHotel Rooms May Not Be Air Conditioned / Air Cooled Nor Will Fans Be Provided. Air Conditioning / Cooling In Hotels Are Set As Per European Weather Conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority.\xa0\nDuring Heat Wave In Europe Air Conditioning Of The Hotels And Coaches May Cease To Function As They Are Not Built For Such High Temperatures.\xa0\nMost Hotels In Europe Do Not Provide Tea Kettles In The Rooms.\xa0\nDue To International Events And Trade Fairs All Throughout Europe Such As Air Show, Music Festivals, Ice Skating Championships Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City.\xa0\nAny Damages Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Coach During Your Stay, Shall Be Payable By The Passengers.\xa0\nWe Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary.\xa0\nIn Certain Cities Hotels Have Not Started The Buffet Breakfasts Yet And If The Same Does Not Change By The Time The Tours Begin, We Will Either Provide Breakfast Or The Groups Will Be Taken To An Indian / Local Restaurant For Breakfast.\n\nCoaches\xa0\n\nMost Of Your Journey In Europe Is By Coach And Hence You Are Requested To Keep The Coach Clean.\xa0\nDue To Hygienic Reasons It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets In The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives.\xa0\nEating & Drinking Is Not Permitted In The Coach.\xa0\nOne Check In Bag And One Hand Bag Per Person Only, Due To Limited Boot Space In The Coach.\xa0\nIn Major European Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop.\nCoaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach.\xa0\nDue To Private Coaches Being Forbidden Inside Most Of The European Cities; As Per Eu Norms To Preserve Them And To Avoid Getting Them Polluted And Overcrowded, Most Of Your Sightseeing Will Be Done By Local Buses And By Foot.\n\nMeals\xa0\n\nMeals Are Pre–Set And A–La Carte Is Not Possible.\xa0\nOn Certain Days Packed Lunch Will Be Provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nGenerally, You Will Have To Walk At Sightseeing Places, Amusement Parks And At The Airports Sometimes For A Long Distance; However The Same Will Be Timely Instructed By The Tour Manager. It Is Advisable To Carry Good Pair Of Comfortable Sports Shoes. The Tour Manager And The Driver Will Do Their Best To Get You As Close To The Monuments As Possible.\n\nGeneral\xa0\n\nIn Case Any Member Of The Group Tests Positive For Covid-19, Customers Will Need To Unconditionally Abide, Adhere And Comply Solely At Your Costs And Expenses\xa0 To All Laws, Rules, Notifications, Travel Advisories, Guidelines, Directives And Communications Issued From Time To Time By All Or Any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies In India Or Abroad, Related To Your Tour To The Foreign Destination And/Or On Your Return From The Tour To Your Home Destination In India Or Abroad Including But Not Limited To Covid-19 Protocols On Quarantine, Vaccinations Etc. Or In Connection With Any Other Pandemic, Epidemic, Disease, Condition Etc., Which May Be Communicated By All Or Any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies In India Or Abroad With Or Without Notice At Any Point Of Time Whether At The Commencement Of The Tour, During The Tour And/Or On The Completion Of The Tour, As The Case May Be”.\nOn Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members.\xa0\nA Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour.\xa0\nSecurity Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary.\xa0\nPlease Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Tcil Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage.\xa0\nDisabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client.\xa0\nTcil Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour.\xa0\nNormal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges.\xa0\nThe Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delay Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nThere Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E. Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour\xa0\nAll Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Euro Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted).\nOptional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non Cancellation Policy.\nGst Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed.\xa0\nThe Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purpose Only.\xa0\nTours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Euro Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange.\xa0\nPlease Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/Arctic_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Tromso_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Northern_Lights_Tromso_753_Adobe.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/ArcticDay3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/ArcticDay4.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/ArcticDay5.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Rovaniemi2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Romaniemi_7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014757/itinerary/Helsinki1.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015182', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015182', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Scandinavia Grand Route', 'days': 14, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Flam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Copenhagen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 512992, 'packageSummary': "The 'Scandinavia Grand Route' package is a spectacular 14-day journey covering the iconic cities of Stockholm, Copenhagen, Bergen, Helsinki, Flam, and Oslo. This extensive itinerary offers travelers a deep dive into Nordic culture and nature, featuring guided city tours of historic capitals, breathtaking fjord cruises, and a scenic ride on the world-famous Flåm Railway. Participants will enjoy exploring key highlights such as Stockholm's Gamla Stan, Copenhagen's vibrant Nyhavn, Bergen's colorful Bryggen wharf, and the unique Temppeliaukio Church in Helsinki, making for an unforgettable Scandinavian adventure.", 'images': ['Helsinki1.jpg', 'Helsinki2.jpg', 'Helsinki3.jpg', 'Stockholm2.jpg', 'Stockholm1.jpg', 'Stockholm3.jpg', 'Oslo1.jpg', 'Oslo2jpg.jpg', 'Flam1jpg.jpg', 'Bergen1.jpg', 'Bergen2jpg.jpg', 'Copenhagen2.jpg', 'Copenhagen1.jpg', 'Copenhagen5.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 512992, 'thumbnailImage': 'Norway1.avif', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015182 is named 'Scandinavia Grand Route' and spans 14 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Helsinki, Meals: NA, Description: Arrive Helsinki Transfers: Upon your arrival at Helsinki Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour: Join a small group walking tour of Helsinki covering key landmarks Helsingin Tuomiokirkko Market Square Temppeliaukio Church Uspenski Cathedral and Sibelius Park plus historic quarters between Market and Senate Squares with cafes and restaurants., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki to Stockholm by Cruise Transfers: You will be transferred from Helsinki hotel to the port on private basis for the overnight cruise. Helsinki to Stockholm Overnight Cruise: In the evening take overnight cruise to Stockholm and enjoy live entertainment duty free shopping sightseeing. Special Notes: In Helsinki it will be day free at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Visit Icebar Transfers: Upon reaching Stockholm you will be transferred from Stockholm port to the hotel on private basis. Early check in is subject to hotel discretion. Visit Icebar: Visit Icebar Stockholm made entirely of ice even the glasses. Kept at minus five degrees entry includes a drink forty five minute visit and ice cape with gloves. A unique Arctic style experience in central Stockholm. Special Note: You will check in at the hotel post completing the sightseeing., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Walking City Tour Stockholm Small Group Walking Tour: Small group walking tour of Stockholm covering City Hall Sergel Square and Gamla Stan one of Europes best preserved medieval centers. Visit the Nobel Museum Royal Palace with changing of the guards and the Vasa Museum., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Boat Tour Stockholm Boat Tour: Enjoy a relaxed morning then take a boat tour of the Swedish archipelago. Listen to onboard stories about its history culture and nature as you pass scenic sights. Relax and soak in the stunning views and fascinating tales along the way., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm to Oslo by Train Transfers: You will be transferred from the Stockholm hotel to the train station. Upon arrival at the Oslo train station you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour: Visit Oslos Royal Palace Vigeland Sculpture Park and Opera House. Explore the Kon Tiki FRAM and Maritime museums Akershus Fortress and its history museums then stroll Karl Johans Gate filled with shops cafes bars and nightlife., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Flam, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo to Flam by Train Transfers: You will be transferred from Oslo hotel to the train station on private basis. Upon arrival in Flam you will make your way to the hotel. Norway in a Nutshell Oslo to Flam: Start your day with the Norway in a Nutshell tour a dream for nature lovers. Marvel at waterfalls cascading down mountains and ride the Flam Railway one of the worlds steepest train journeys for a truly spectacular experience. Special Notes: Your luggage will be transferred from Oslo hotel to Bergen hotel. Take a small bag for overnight stay in Flam. Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Flam to BergenTransfers: You will make your way from Flam hotel to the port for your onward journey to Bergen. Upon arrival at Bergen you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Norway in a Nutshell Flam to Bergen: Cruise along one of Norways most beautiful fjords a UNESCO World Heritage Site with deep blue waters towering cliffs and waterfalls. Pass scenic villages and farms then journey through stunning landscapes to Bergen the city of seven fjords. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bergen City Walking Tour Bergen City Walking Tour: Enjoy a small group walking tour in Bergen. The Floibanen funicular can be found in the city center near the fish market and Bryggen. Explore the charming Hanseatic town with historic warehouses cathedral and colorful wooden houses., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bergen to Copenhagen Transfers: You will be transferred from Bergen hotel to the airport on a private basis. Upon arrival at Copenhagen you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Copenhagen Walking Tour Copenhagen Small Group Walking Tour: Enjoy city views from Rundetaarn and visit Trinitatis Kirke. Walk to Stroget in the Old Town pass colorful Nyhavn to Amalienborg Palace then see the Gefion Fountain and The Little Mermaid inspired by H C Andersen., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 14 - Copenhagen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will be transferred from Copenhagen hotel to the airport on private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 512992.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm\xa0\n3 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation in Flam based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Bergen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n. Meals include: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1). Inclusions: Accommodation 2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm 3 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Flam based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Bergen based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals Daily Breakfast (Except Day 1) Transportation [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis] Arrival Transfers from Helsinki Airport to the Hotel Private Transfer from Helsinki hotel to the Port Private Transfer from Stockholm Port to the hotel Private Transfer from Stockolm hotel to the train station Return Private Transfer from Oslo Train station to the hotel Private transfer from Bergen train station to the Hotel Private transfer from Bergen hotel to the Airport Private Transfer from Copenhagen Airport to the hotel Departure Transfer from Copenhagen hotel to the Airport Sightseeing (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Entry tickets – Vasa Museum, Ice bar Stockholm Small Group Walking City Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Stockholm Boat Tour Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Norway in a Nutshell Oslo to Flam Norway in a Nutshell Flam to Bergen Bergen City Walking Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Copenhagen Small Group Walking City Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Entry tickets – Vasa Museum, Stockholm archipelago tour, Floibanen funicular ride Bergen, Ice bar Insurance Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only) SPECIAL NOTE: Please Note that in fjord small towns, it could be 3-star hotel or similar. Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES • The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together • The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events • Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room • Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. • WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed • (Supplement charges may apply for such services) • Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. • Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned • At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability • TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost TERMS AND CONDITIONS • Travel Validity: 1 July 2026 – 15 December 2026 • Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ • The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times • Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room • The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses • Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking • To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour • Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly • The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates • We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package • International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed • Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only • No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service • All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking • Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice • Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends • Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time • As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients • The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Scandinavia Grand Route' package is a spectacular 14-day journey covering the iconic cities of Stockholm, Copenhagen, Bergen, Helsinki, Flam, and Oslo. This extensive itinerary offers travelers a deep dive into Nordic culture and nature, featuring guided city tours of historic capitals, breathtaking fjord cruises, and a scenic ride on the world-famous Flåm Railway. Participants will enjoy exploring key highlights such as Stockholm's Gamla Stan, Copenhagen's vibrant Nyhavn, Bergen's colorful Bryggen wharf, and the unique Temppeliaukio Church in Helsinki, making for an unforgettable Scandinavian adventure.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Helsinki\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at Helsinki Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.', 'mealDescription': 'NA', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic or similar in Helsinki'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nHelsinki Small Group Walking Tour\n\xa0\nHelsinki Small Group Walking Tour: Join a small group walking tour of Helsinki covering key landmarks Helsingin Tuomiokirkko Market Square Temppeliaukio Church Uspenski Cathedral and Sibelius Park plus historic quarters between Market and Senate Squares with cafes and restaurants.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic or similar in Helsinki'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nHelsinki to Stockholm by Cruise\n\xa0\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Helsinki hotel to the port on private basis for the overnight cruise.\n\xa0\nHelsinki to Stockholm Overnight Cruise: In the evening take overnight cruise to Stockholm and enjoy live entertainment duty free shopping sightseeing.\n\xa0\nSpecial Notes: In Helsinki it will be day free at leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Overnight on Cruise'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nStockholm Visit Icebar\nTransfers: Upon reaching Stockholm you will be transferred from Stockholm port to the hotel on private basis. Early check in is subject to hotel discretion.\nVisit Icebar: Visit Icebar Stockholm made entirely of ice even the glasses. Kept at minus five degrees entry includes a drink forty five minute visit and ice cape with gloves. A unique Arctic style experience in central Stockholm.\nSpecial Note: You will check in at the hotel post completing the sightseeing.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion or similar in Stockholm'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nStockholm Walking City Tour\nStockholm Small Group Walking Tour: Small group walking tour of Stockholm covering City Hall Sergel Square and Gamla Stan one of Europes best preserved medieval centers. Visit the Nobel Museum Royal Palace with changing of the guards and the Vasa Museum.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion or similar in Stockholm'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nStockholm Boat Tour\nStockholm Boat Tour: Enjoy a relaxed morning then take a boat tour of the Swedish archipelago. Listen to onboard stories about its history culture and nature as you pass scenic sights. Relax and soak in the stunning views and fascinating tales along the way.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion or similar in Stockholm'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nStockholm to Oslo by Train\nTransfers: You will be transferred from the Stockholm hotel to the train station. Upon arrival at the Oslo train station you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis.\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion or similar in\xa0Oslo'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nOslo Small Group Walking City Tour\nOslo Small Group Walking City Tour: Visit Oslos Royal Palace Vigeland Sculpture Park and Opera House. Explore the Kon Tiki FRAM and Maritime museums Akershus Fortress and its history museums then stroll Karl Johans Gate filled with shops cafes bars and nightlife.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Clarion or similar in\xa0Oslo'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nOslo to Flam by Train\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Oslo hotel to the train station on private basis. Upon arrival in Flam you will make your way to the hotel.\nNorway in a Nutshell Oslo to Flam: Start your day with the Norway in a Nutshell tour a dream for nature lovers. Marvel at waterfalls cascading down mountains and ride the Flam Railway one of the worlds steepest train journeys for a truly spectacular experience.\nSpecial Notes: Your luggage will be transferred from Oslo hotel to Bergen hotel. Take a small bag for overnight stay in Flam. Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Flamsbrygga\xa0Hotel\xa0or similar\xa0in Flam'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nFlam to BergenTransfers: You will make your way from Flam hotel to the port for your onward journey to Bergen. Upon arrival at Bergen you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis.\nNorway in a Nutshell Flam to Bergen: Cruise along one of Norways most beautiful fjords a UNESCO World Heritage Site with deep blue waters towering cliffs and waterfalls. Pass scenic villages and farms then journey through stunning landscapes to Bergen the city of seven fjords.\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Thon or similar in Bergen'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nBergen City Walking Tour\nBergen City Walking Tour: Enjoy a small group walking tour in Bergen. The Floibanen funicular can be found in the city center near the fish market and Bryggen. Explore the charming Hanseatic town with historic warehouses cathedral and colorful wooden houses.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Thon or similar in Bergen'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nBergen to Copenhagen\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Bergen hotel to the airport on a private basis. Upon arrival at Copenhagen you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis.\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic or similar in Copenhagen'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nCopenhagen Walking Tour\nCopenhagen Small Group Walking Tour: Enjoy city views from Rundetaarn and visit Trinitatis Kirke. Walk to Stroget in the Old Town pass colorful Nyhavn to Amalienborg Palace then see the Gefion Fountain and The Little Mermaid inspired by H C Andersen.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic or similar in Copenhagen'}, {'day': 14, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\nTransfers: You will be transferred from Copenhagen hotel to the airport on private transfer.\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'NA'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm\xa0\n3 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation in Flam based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Bergen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm\xa0\n3 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation in Flam based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Bergen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SE', 'countryName': 'Sweden', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FI', 'countryName': 'Finland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NO', 'countryName': 'Norway', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DK', 'countryName': 'Denmark', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 513000.0, 'hotels': ['\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm\xa0\n3 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n1 Night accommodation in Flam based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Bergen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Copenhagen based on the hotel category selected or similar\xa0\n']}], 'meals': ['Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis]\xa0\n\nArrival Transfers from Helsinki Airport to the Hotel\xa0\nPrivate Transfer from Helsinki hotel to the Port\xa0\nPrivate Transfer from Stockholm Port to the hotel\xa0\nPrivate Transfer from Stockolm hotel to the train station\xa0\nReturn Private Transfer from Oslo Train station to the hotel\xa0\nPrivate transfer from Bergen train station to the Hotel\xa0\nPrivate transfer from Bergen hotel to the Airport\xa0\nPrivate Transfer from Copenhagen Airport to the hotel\xa0\nDeparture Transfer from Copenhagen hotel to the Airport\xa0\xa0\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package t