er of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/Italy_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/40866_Colosseum_Rome_Italy_753.jpg', "https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/447998_Saint_Peter's_Square_Rome_Italy_753.jpg", 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/2987_Florence_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/51449_Field_of_Miracles_Pisa_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/62615_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/59724_Venice_Mark_Square753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014514/itinerary/0886_Venice753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014538', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014538', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Best Of London And Scotland', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Windermere Lake', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Windermere Lake', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Edinburgh', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Edinburgh', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Edinburgh', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014538_0_20260917092716', 'price': 214681, 'packageSummary': "The 'Best Of London And Scotland' package is an 8-day tour covering London, Edinburgh, and Windermere Lake. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Tower of London, Buckingham Palace, and the historic Edinburgh Castle. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a scenic boat cruise on Windermere Lake, and leisurely walks along the Royal Mile, offering a perfect blend of vibrant city life and breathtaking natural beauty.", 'images': ['London7531.jpg', 'LondonTowerBridge7531.jpg', 'AdobeStock_222232218_BuckinghamPalaceLondon.jpeg', 'Windermere7532.jpg', 'Windermere7533.jpg', 'Edinburgh7534.jpg', 'EdinburghCastle7536.jpg', 'EdinburghCity7534.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 214681, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_211359758_BuckinghamPalaceLondon.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014538 is named 'Best Of London And Scotland' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - London, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive London Transfer: Arrival in London Airport (LHR), you will be met by the representative and have a private transfer to the hotel. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Description: London London Sightseeing: This sightseeing package offers a comprehensive London experience by combining a hop-on hop-off bus pass for flexible sightseeing. The package also includes a 30-minute ride on the London Eye, giving you panoramic views of the city from a unique perspective. A skip-the-line entry to Madame Tussauds, and entry to the historic Tower of London., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Description: London - Free Day Changing of the Guard Guided Tour at Buckingham Palace (Optional Activity) Walking Tour - English 09:00 [Duration approx. 90 mins]Begin this regal tour at the Duke of York Column in St. James's. Greet the guide and don a personal headset for a historical overview of the iconic Changing of the Guard ceremony. Unlike typical tours that gather outside Buckingham Palace, this experience utilizes handpicked vantage points to guarantee the best views of the royal tradition. Listen to expert commentary explaining each part of the performance as you admire the shimmering Household Cavalry and capture photographs of the King's foot soldiers in their iconic red and black attire. The tour concludes outside of Buckingham Palace (Spur Road, London, United Kingdom). [Supplement Cost - GBP 20 Per Adult and GBP 16 Per Child] Please Note: The Changing of the Guard ceremony is subject to schedule changes or cancellation by British authorities, often without prior notice before 11 am. If cancelled due to weather, a 'wet change' march without music still takes place. Jack the Ripper Small Group Guided Tour (Optional Activity) Walking Tour - English 18:00 [Duration Approximately 2 hours (6 stops, 20 minutes each] This is a walking tour of the Jack the Ripper murders in Whitechapel, London, with each 20-minute stop focusing on a different victim: Martha Tabram, Mary Ann Nichols, Annie Chapman, Elizabeth Stride, Catherine Eddowes, and Mary Jane Kelly. The tour is in the evening and is led by an expert guide who discusses the murders and the origin of the killer's name. [Supplement Cost - GBP 20 Per Adult and GBP 16 Per Child], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Windermere Lake, Meals: Breakfast, Description: London To Windermere Transfer: You will travel from London to Windermere on a 2nd Class Train Ticket with changes (3.5 hrs) Upon your arrival at Windermere train station, make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Windermere Lake, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day At Leisure Windermere Lake Cruises (Optional Activity) Windermere Lake Cruises offers scenic boat trips on England's largest lake, with daily sailings from piers in Ambleside, Bowness, and Lakeside. A day out on Windermere with a visit to the Lakeland Motor MuseumWith this great-value combined ticket, you can explore the full length of Lake Windermere with unlimited hop-on, hop-off travel for 24 hours. Cruise between Lakeside, Bowness, Ambleside and more, taking in stunning views and stopping at lakeside attractions along the way. You’ll also receive entry to the Lakeland Motor Museum in Backbarrow, which you can visit at any point up to five days after your cruise. [Supplement Cost - GBP 33 Per Adult and GBP 18 Per Child], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Edinburgh, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Windermere To Edinburgh Transfer: You will travel from Windermere to Edinburgh on a 2nd Class Train Ticket with changes Upon your arrival at Edinburgh train station, make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 15:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion. Scotch Whisky Tasting - The True Spirit of Scotland (Optional Activity) Whisky Tasting In English 17:30 [Duration Approximately 90 mins] Enjoy a tasting of three single malts from regions across Scotland, plus a new make spirit (unaged whisky). The experience is enriched with the history, traditions, and anecdotes that Scotch carries with it. The experience begins at the entrance of John Knox House, from where we will head to a central whisky bar for the tasting. Experienced local guide. Origins and evolution of Scotch The Golden Age of Scotch whisky Edinburgh’s influence on Scotch’s fame Regions and styles Memorable anecdotes Includes: 3 tastings of exclusive single malts + 1 new make (unaged whisky) [Supplement Cost - GBP 50 Per Adult, child entrance will be upon request basis only], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Edinburgh, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Edinburgh Hop on Hop Off Sightseeing: Explore Edinburgh at your own pace with a hop-on hop-off bus ticket. Ascend the city's seven hills for spectacular views and marvel at iconic landmarks like Edinburgh Castle and the Royal Mile, connecting the castle to the Palace of Holyrood House. This flexible tour lets you discover the city's rich history, museums, galleries, and restaurants exactly as you wish., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Edinburgh, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Edinburgh Transfer: 3- 4 hrs prior to your departure flight, you will have a private transfer from the hotel to Edinburgh (EDI) airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which you are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 214681.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n   \n\xa0HOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCity\n\n\nStandard \n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nIbis London Earls Court Hotel /\xa0Point A Hotel, London Paddington / Best Western Buckingham Palace Rd\xa0\xa0/The W14 Hotel Kensington / London House Hotel / Mentone Hotel / BW Swiss Cottage or similar\n\n\n\n\nWindermere\n\n\nWindermere Manor Hotel (3*) / Beech Hill Hotel / The Ro Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nEdinburgh\n\n\nIbis Edinburgh Centre Royal Mile - Hunter Square / Leonardo Hotel Edinburgh City / Holiday Inn Express Edinburgh City - West / Ibis Edinburgh Centre South Bridge - Royal Mile or similar\n\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\n   \n\xa0HOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCity\n\n\nValue\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nPark Plaza London / Park International / Copthorne Tara London Kensington / Holiday Inn® London Kensington / Mercure London Paddington or similar\n\n\n\n\nWindermere\n\n\nMacdonald Old England Hotel & Spa / Lindeth Howe or similar\n\n\n\n\nEdinburgh\n\n\nLeonardo Royal Hotel Edinburgh Haymarket / Leonardo Royal Hotel Edinburgh / Novotel Edinburgh Centre Hotel / Mercure Edinburgh Haymarket or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 