nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\xa0\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\xa0\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\n\xa0Special Note:\n\nThe itinerary and sightseeing may vary based on availability and seasonality\nPlease note that should the Covid-19 pandemic necessitate further protocols as mandated by the Government and/or the individual properties in the future which results in an increase in our standard tour operator rates, then Thomas Cook India reserves the right to adjust the above quoted rates accordingly. This may lead to an increase in prices quoted. Certain Activities are subject to weather conditions and protocols.\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015161/Kiruna.avif', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015161/itinerary/Kiruna.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014763', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014763', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Pure Croatia', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zadar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014763_0_20260518115709.pdf', 'price': 169543, 'packageSummary': "The 'Pure Croatia' package is an 8-day tour covering the historic and scenic cities of Dubrovnik, Zadar, Zagreb, and Split. Throughout this captivating journey, participants will immerse themselves in Croatia's rich heritage and stunning coastal beauty through guided city tours of ancient Roman ruins, walks along medieval city walls, and visits to vibrant local markets. Travelers will also enjoy scenic coastal drives along the Adriatic Sea, explore historic cathedrals, and experience the unique blend of cultural charm and modern life that defines these iconic Croatian destinations.", 'images': ['Zagerb.jpg', 'ZAGRAB-CROATIA (1).jpg', 'Plitvice-Lakes-National-Park-1 (1).jpg', 'split.jpg', 'croatia-Split_2.jpg', 'dubrovnik_2.jpg', 'Elaphiti_Islands.jpg', 'Dubrovnik.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 169543, 'thumbnailImage': 'Split_SRP.png', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014763 is named 'Pure Croatia' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Zagreb, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zagreb Transfers: Upon your arrival at Zagreb airport, you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Walking Tour of Zagreb: Explore Zagreb’s highlights on a guided walking tour with a scenic funicular ride. Discover the charm of both Lower and Upper Town, uncover hidden gems, and hear the stories that shaped Croatia’s vibrant capital. Special Note: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Zagreb, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Free At Leisure Optional Day Trip To Slovenia on SIC Basis: Enjoy a free day or take an optional trip to Slovenia. Visit the charming capital Ljubljana, then escape into nature at Lake Bled, famous for its scenic lake and hilltop castle—an unforgettable getaway from Zagreb. Special Note: You need to be in possession of a multiple entry Schengen visa to visit Slovenia. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Zadar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zagreb - Zadar | Enroute Plitvice National Park | Transfers: This morning travel to Zadar, enroute visit Plitvice National Park. Later continue your journey to Zadar Plitvice National Park: Plitvice National Park dazzles with waterfalls, lakes, and forested cliffs. Your ticket includes full access to trails and boardwalks, a panoramic train ride, shuttle buses between lakes, and an electric boat cruise on Kozjak Lake., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Walking Tour of Zadar | Zadar - Split Transfers: Today you will travel from Zadar to Split by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Zadar: Enjoy a guided walking tour of Zadar’s Old City, including St. Donat, St. Anastasia, city gates, walls, and the Square of Five Wells. Sample Maraschino liqueur and Pag cheese, then relax by the Sea Organ and admire the sunset. Special Note: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour | Walking Tour of Split Blue Lagoon – 3 Island Tour: Enjoy a relaxing Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour, visiting UNESCO listed Trogir, the Blue Lagoon, and Šolta’s Stomorska village for swimming and exploring. You can also take a Blue Cave 5 Island Tour to Biševo, Vis, Pakleni, Hvar and Brac for stunning views and swims. Walking Tour of Split: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Split and explore the 1700 year old Diocletian’s Palace. See St. Domnius Cathedral, the Peristil, Golden Gate, and Gregory of Nin. End with the 24 hour sun clock at City Square and the Riva promenade. Special Note: You have an opportunity to upgrade your Blue Lagoon and Guided walking tour of Split to a full-day Blue Cave Tour at an additional cost. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Split – Dubrovnik | Walking Tour of Dubrovnik | Transfers: Today you will travel from Split to Dubrovnik by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Dubrovnik: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Dubrovnik and a Cable Car ride. Explore the Old Town’s history, architecture, and culture, then ride to the top of Srd Hill for stunning views of the Adriatic Sea and the city below. Special Note: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only. You can opt for a Sunset Dinner Cruise (Dalmatian Cuisine) at a supplement cost, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Trip To Bosnia & Herzegovina Trip to Bosnia & Herzegovina: Explore Bosnia and Herzegovina on a day trip and visit UNESCO listed Mostar. Wander cobbled streets, see Ottoman era mosques and bathhouses, and admire the iconic Stari Most—one of the modern world’s most remarkable bridges. Special Note: Guest should be carrying their passport with valid Schengen Visa. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Dubrovnik hotel to Dubrovnik Airport Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 169543.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nCity\n\nHotels\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel Sheraton, Hotel Esplanade Zagreb, Hotel Westin or Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare Hotel, Teatro Verdi Boutique Hotel, Hotel Bastion or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nCornaro Hotel, Radisson Blu Resort & Spa, Hotel Ambasador or Similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel President, Hotel Sun Gardens, Hotel Hilton Imperial or Similar\n\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\n\nCity\xa0\n\n\n