r Similar\n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 235500.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nCity\n\nHotels\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel Sheraton, Hotel Esplanade Zagreb, Hotel Westin or Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare Hotel, Teatro Verdi Boutique Hotel, Hotel Bastion or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nCornaro Hotel, Radisson Blu Resort & Spa, Hotel Ambasador or Similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel President, Hotel Sun Gardens, Hotel Hilton Imperial or Similar\n\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', 'Transfers:\n\nPrivate Airport transfers (Arrival and Departure City)\nPrivate transfers (Pick Up and Drop Off) to Inter-city Bus Terminal\nInter-city travel by SCHEDULED Air-Conditioned shared coach service.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['(For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nWalking tour of Zagreb with Funicular Ride in a group\nWalking tour of Zadar old town in a group from a central meeting point\nBlue Lagoon and 3 island group tour from Split\nWalking tour of Split in group\nWalking tour of Dubrovnik in group\nDubrovnik Cable Car Roundtrip ticket\nTrip to Bosnia & Herzegovina\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': '<p>Return Economy Class Airfare</p>', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Zagreb based on the hotel category selected or similar\n1 Nights’ accommodation in Zadar based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Split based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Dubrovnik based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nPrivate Transfer from Zagreb Airport to Zagreb Hotel\nPrivate transfer from Zagreb Hotel to Zadar Hotel enroute visit Plitvice National Park\nPrivate Transfer from Dubrovnik Hotel to Dubrovnik Airport\n\nBus Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\nBus ticket from Zadar to Split (Subject to availability until ticketed)\nBus Ticket from Split to Dubrovnik (Subject to availability until ticketed)\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nWalking tour of Zagreb with Funicular Ride in a group\nWalking tour of Zadar old town in a group from a central meeting point\nBlue Lagoon and 3 island group tour from Split\nWalking tour of Split in group\nWalking tour of Dubrovnik in group\nDubrovnik Cable Car Roundtrip ticket\nTrip to Bosnia & Herzegovina\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 November 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/Split_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Zagerb.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/ZAGRAB-CROATIA_(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Plitvice-Lakes-National-Park-1_(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/split.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/croatia-Split_2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/dubrovnik_2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Elaphiti_Islands.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Dubrovnik.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG011334', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG011334', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Discover Georgia', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG011334_0_20260814123115.pdf', 'price': 86634, 'packageSummary': "The 'Discover Georgia' package is a 7-day tour dedicated to exploring the historic and vibrant city of Tbilisi. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, the iconic Holy Trinity Cathedral, and the charming, cobblestone streets of the Old Town. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, relaxing in the famous sulfur baths, riding the aerial cable car for panoramic views of the city, and experiencing traditional Georgian wine tastings and authentic culinary delights.", 'images': ['georgia_753.png', 'Mtskheta.png', 'Kakheti_Georgia_753.jpg', 'Gudauri_C.jpg', 'Uplistsikhe.png', 'Mtskheta.jpg', 'tbilisi_city.png'], 'minimumPrice': 86634, 'thumbnailImage': 'Georgia_srp.png', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG011334 is named \'Discover Georgia\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival Tbilisi Welcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) Overnight in Tbilisi, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.Start the city tour by visiting Old Tbilisi. We will first visit Metekhi, which overlooks Meidan Square. After that, we will walk on the Bridge of Peace that links the old part of the city to the Rike Park. After that, we will visit The Clock Tower, where you can see an angel comes out every hour to ring the bell with a small hammer. Shortly, we will walk towards Shardeni Street, which is so well known that any guest that travels to Georgia never leaves this country without visiting it. Later, we will take a cable car to Narikala Fortress and continue walking to the statue of Mother of Georgia. Soon then, we will visit Abanotubani with sulfur baths. Then, we will pass by Juma Mosque, which is unique for the fact that Sunnis and Shias can pray together and continue to Mtatsminda Park via Funicular Train ride. It is the best place for fun and relaxation in the city. The Tbilisi TV tower is also located in the park. Breathtaking views from the park can be seen all over Tbilisi. Overnight stay at Tbilisi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Bodbe - Sighnaghi - Chronicles of Georgia – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Start the tour by driving to Kakheti, the main wine producing region in the country. First, we will visit Bodbe, immersed in green with colorful flower beds and in the east, there is an observation deck with a beautiful view of the Alazani Valley. After enjoying the panoramic views, we will continue to Sighnaghi which is called the City of Love. Home to Georgia’s famous painter Pirosmani, the city is full of 18th- and 19th-century architecture and with a Tuscan feel. Here you will have a chance to climb the old Sighnaghi Wall which is five kilometers long and incorporate 23 towers. After that, we will return to Tbilisi and visit Chronicles of Georgia or History Memorial of Georgia. The monument consists of huge pillars that showcase the history of Georgia and life of Jesus. Overnight stay at Tbilisi, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Ananuri - Gudauri -Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel. Start the tour by driving to Gudauri in northeastern Georgia. Our first stop will be at Ananuri Complex, a former residence of the Aragvi Dukes dating back to the 16th and 17th centuries. The fortress beautifully overlooks the Zhinvali Dam, one of the main reservoirs of Georgia. Shortly, we will head to Gudauri Panorama, built in the late 19th century, is a circular balcony hanging off a 600-meter cliff with breathtaking views of the Caucasus Mountains. After enjoying your time, we will head back to Tbilisi. Overnight stay at Tbilisi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Gori - Uplistsikhe Cave – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel start our tour by driving to Gori, where we will visit Josef Stalin Museum and then visit Gori Fortress, situated above the city of Gori on a rocky hill and was originally built in the 13th century. After that, you will continue to Uplistsikhe Cave, a rock-hewn town, one of the oldest settlements in the Caucasus. Its literal translation is “Lord’s Fortress" and continued to be inhabited until the 13th century AD. Nowadays, it is considered to be an open-air museum. After enjoying your time there, we will return to Tbilisi. Overnight stay at Tbilisi, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Mtskheta - Borjomi – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Start the tour by driving to Mtskheta, the first capital of Georgia. Here we will visit Jvari, a 6th century monument standing on the top of the mountain overlooking the confluence of the Mtkvari and Aragvi rivers. We will then head to Svetitskhoveli Cathedral, a burial site of Christ’s robe, was originally built in the 11th century and along with Jvari is inscribed on UNESCO World Heritage Site. After that, we will head to Borjomi, the southern part of Georgia. It’s a hydrothermal health spa resort with well-known mineral water. Here we will visit Borjomi Park. The park has an ecological theme with a statue of Prometheus which stands at the base of a small waterfall. After enjoying your time in the park, we will return to Tbilisi. Overnight stay at Tbilisi, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 86634.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nPark Plaza London / Park International / Copthorne Tara London Kensington / Holiday Inn® London Kensington / Mercure London Paddington or similar\n\n\n\n, Holiday Inn Express Avlabari or similar, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 06 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi. Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Bodbe - Sighnaghi - Chronicles of Georgia – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Ananuri - Gudauri -Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Gori - Uplistsikhe Cave – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Mtskheta - Borjomi – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Entrance Fees: Tbilisi Cable Car (two ways), Funicular Ride (TW), Stalin Museum, Uplistsikhe Cave, Borjomi Park Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa charges Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights services Meals not mentioned in the itinerary Any tips (Around USD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Black out dates: Christmas and New Year - 15 Dec 2026 - 06 Jan 2027. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions : The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Discover Georgia' package is a 7-day tour dedicated to exploring the historic and vibrant city of Tbilisi. The itinerary includes visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, the iconic Holy Trinity Cathedral, and the charming, cobblestone streets of the Old Town. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, relaxing in the famous sulfur baths, riding the aerial cable car for panoramic views of the city, and experiencing traditional Georgian wine tastings and authentic culinary delights.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival Tbilisi\n\xa0\nWelcome to Georgia, Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.)\n\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight in Tbilisi', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.Start the city tour by visiting Old Tbilisi. We will first visit Metekhi, which overlooks Meidan Square. After that, we will walk on the Bridge of Peace that links the old part of the city to the Rike Park. After that, we will visit The Clock Tower, where you can see an angel comes out every hour to ring the bell with a small hammer. Shortly, we will walk towards Shardeni Street, which is so well known that any guest that travels to Georgia never leaves this country without visiting it. Later, we will take a cable car to Narikala Fortress and continue walking to the statue of Mother of Georgia. Soon then, we will visit Abanotubani with sulfur baths. Then, we will pass by Juma Mosque, which is unique for the fact that Sunnis and Shias can pray together and continue to Mtatsminda Park via Funicular Train ride. It is the best place for fun and relaxation in the city. The Tbilisi TV tower is also located in the park. Breathtaking views from the park can be seen all over Tbilisi.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Tbilisi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham\xa0Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nTbilisi - Bodbe - Sighnaghi - Chronicles of Georgia – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nStart the tour by driving to Kakheti, the main wine producing region in the country. First, we will visit Bodbe, immersed in green with colorful flower beds and in the east, there is an observation deck with a beautiful view of the Alazani Valley. After enjoying the panoramic views, we will continue to Sighnaghi which is called the City of Love. Home to Georgia’s famous painter Pirosmani, the city is full of 18th- and 19th-century architecture and with a Tuscan feel. Here you will have a chance to climb the old Sighnaghi Wall which is five kilometers long and incorporate 23 towers. After that, we will return to Tbilisi and visit Chronicles of Georgia or History Memorial of Georgia. The monument consists of huge pillars that showcase the history of Georgia and life of Jesus.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Tbilisi', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham\xa0Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Ananuri - Gudauri -Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel.\n\xa0\nStart the tour by driving to Gudauri in northeastern Georgia. Our first stop will be at Ananuri Complex, a former residence of the Aragvi Dukes dating back to the 16th and 17th centuries. The fortress beautifully overlooks the Zhinvali Dam, one of the main reservoirs of Georgia. Shortly, we will head to Gudauri Panorama, built in the late 19th century, is a circular balcony hanging off a 600-meter cliff with breathtaking views of the Caucasus Mountains. After enjoying your time, we will head back to Tbilisi.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Tbilisi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham\xa0Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Gori - Uplistsikhe Cave – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nstart our tour by driving to Gori, where we will visit Josef Stalin Museum and then visit Gori Fortress, situated above the city of Gori on a rocky hill and was originally built in the 13th century. After that, you will continue to Uplistsikhe Cave, a rock-hewn town, one of the oldest settlements in the Caucasus. Its literal translation is “Lord’s Fortress" and continued to be inhabited until the 13th century AD. Nowadays, it is considered to be an open-air museum. After enjoying your time there, we will return to Tbilisi.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Tbilisi', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham\xa0Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Mtskheta - Borjomi – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nStart the tour by driving to Mtskheta, the first capital of Georgia. Here we will visit Jvari, a 6th century monument standing on the top of the mountain overlooking the confluence of the Mtkvari and Aragvi rivers. We will then head to Svetitskhoveli Cathedral, a burial site of Christ’s robe, was originally built in the 11th century and along with Jvari is inscribed on UNESCO World Heritage Site. After that, we will head to Borjomi, the southern part of Georgia. It’s a hydrothermal health spa resort with well-known mineral water. Here we will visit Borjomi Park. The park has an ecological theme with a statue of Prometheus which stands at the base of a small waterfall. After enjoying your time in the park, we will return to Tbilisi.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Tbilisi', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel New Tiflis (Standard) / Holiday Inn Express (Value) / Wyndham\xa0Grand (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India.\nNote : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nLondon\n\n\nPark Plaza London / Park International / Copthorne Tara London Kensingt