 – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Ananuri - Gudauri -Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Gori - Uplistsikhe Cave – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Mtskheta - Borjomi – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\xa0\nEntrance Fees: Tbilisi Cable Car (two ways), Funicular Ride (TW), Stalin Museum, Uplistsikhe Cave, Borjomi Park\xa0\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.)\n', 'exclusions': '\nTCS & GST\nVisa charges\xa0\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable\xa0\nAll flights services\xa0\nMeals not mentioned in the itinerary\nAny tips (Around USD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver\xa0\nAnything not mentioned in the inclusions\nPre & Post tour services & cost\xa0\nExpenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc)\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\xa0\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\nMidnight surcharge\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nBlack out dates: Christmas and New Year - 15 Dec 2026 - 06 Jan 2027\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nTerms and Conditions :\n\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/Georgia_srp.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/georgia_753.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/Mtskheta.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/Kakheti_Georgia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/Gudauri_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/Uplistsikhe.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/Mtskheta.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011334/itinerary/tbilisi_city.png']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015626', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015626', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Norway In A Nutshell With Tromso', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bergen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015626_0_20260921145223.pdf', 'price': 221060, 'packageSummary': "The 'Norway In A Nutshell With Tromso' package is a 9-day tour covering the beautiful cities of Tromso, Bergen, and Oslo. This captivating itinerary offers travelers the chance to experience the legendary Norway in a Nutshell journey, featuring a scenic fjord cruise through the UNESCO-listed Nærøyfjord and a ride on the famous Flåm Railway. Participants will also enjoy chasing the mesmerizing Northern Lights in Tromso, exploring the historic Hanseatic wharf of Bryggen in Bergen, and discovering the rich cultural sights and modern architecture of Oslo.", 'images': ['59065_Oslo_Norway_753.jpg', 'Oslo-Norway.jpg', 'Oslo1.png', 'Bergen_norway1.jpg', 'Norway-Bergen.jpg', 'Tromso_753.png', 'Norway_tromso.png', 'Tromso.png', 'SRP_blue-lagoon.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 221060, 'thumbnailImage': 'Tromso_SRP.png', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015626 is named 'Norway In A Nutshell With Tromso' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Oslo, Meals: N/A, Description: Welcome to Oslo! Surrounded by mountains and sea, this compact, cultured and fun city has a palpable sense of reinvention. Oslo is famous for modern design and architecture, and its Oslo Opera House definitely stands out from the crowd. Specially designed so that visitors can walk on its rooftop, the iconic building boasts an impressive facade. On arrival at Oslo Airport, the driver / representative who will transfer you to your centrally located hotel. Rest of the day is free to recuperate from the journey. Depending upon the arrival time of the flight, in the afternoon recuperate with a visit to some of the famous attractions in Oslo. You can opt for “Oslo Grünerløkka Food & Culture Walking Tour” The experience starts in Vulkan. Here, old meets new in a colorful blend of street art, eco-friendly architecture, and industrial-chic style. Vulkan is home to Mathallen, a buzzing food hall filled with global flavors and local delicacies, where Oslo’s foodies come to play. This vibrant area is a haven for hip cafes, artisanal shops, and riverside hangouts that are perfect for chilling out or people-watching. Whether you’re exploring its green spaces or sampling the diverse eats, Vulkan is all about savoring the city’s coolest side, where innovation and flavor collide. The next stop is Grünerløkka --> the go-to spot in Oslo for anyone craving a taste of the city’s diverse food scene. This hip neighborhood is a foodie’s playground, with an eclectic mix of street food stalls, cozy cafes, and innovative restaurants tucked into every corner., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo Like a Local - Customized Private Tour Breakfast at hotel. Today you will have a sightseeing Tour of Oslo like a Local. Getting to know a new city is not just about seeing its sights but meeting its people. With this private custom Oslo tour, connect with a local for a real feel of the city they love. Share your interests with your friend-in-the-making before meeting for a walking tour that delivers a personalized and authentic take on the city: from pointers on restaurants to finding little-known sights and ways to get around (Duration – 2 hours) OR opt for a “Christmas Tour & Christmas Market with a Local Guide” (Starting from 15 November) Enjoy a complex Norwegian Christmas experience by combining Oslo's top highlights with traditional food and drink sampling while learning more about Norwegian Christmas history and traditions., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo - Free Day Today after breakfast, you will have the day to explore Oslo on your own. You can also opt for the below activities if needed. Make a visit at Kon-Tiki Museum Entrance Ticket. Thor Heyerdahl (1914-2002) gained worldwide fame when he crossed the Pacific Ocean on the balsawood raft Kon-Tiki in 1947. He followed this up with spectacular expeditions on the reed boats Ra and Tigris. At the Kon-Tiki Museum guests can experience original vessels and up-to-date exhibits on Heyerdahl’s expeditions, including Kon-Tiki, Ra, Tigris, Easter Island, Fatu-Hiva, Tùcume, Galapagos, a 30-metre cave tour, an underwater exhibit with a 10-metre model of a whale shark, Thor Heyerdahl’s library, Thor Heyerdahl in person, and Tiki pop culture. The original, Oscar-winning Kon-Tiki documentary film is screened every day at 12 noon in the cinema, and the museum has a well-stocked souvenir shop. OR You can opt for “Oslo Fjord 3 Course Dinner Sightseeing Cruise” Welcome on the silent dinner cruise on the Oslo fjord. Take in the unique ambience of hybrid-electric boat with panoramic windows and outside deck. The perfect setting to enjoy a 3-course dinner and drink in the evening sun. Step on board for the evening trip through the Oslo fjord. During the cruise you will leave the hustle and bustle of the city behind find the calm waters of the Oslo fjord and its green islands with picturesque lighthouses such as Dyna Fir. On the way back you can enjoy the Oslo skyline and will cruise past some of its most popular sights such as the Opera House and Aker fortress. Enjoy a delicious locally sourced dinner buffet inspired by Nordic traditions and contemporary trends. Pair the dinner with one of the wines that have been carefully selected to complement the food available for purchase., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo to Bergen (Norway in a Nutshell) Today after breakfast, you will have to make your way to Oslo Train Station by 0800 am for your onward journey on Norway in a Nutshell - This legendary tour takes you through Norway’s most breathtaking UNESCO-protected fjord and mountain scenery, as well as a trip on Europe’s top scenic rail journey. Go on a winter adventure in Norway and experience the scenic Bergen Railway, the breathtaking Flam Railway, the narrow and dramatic Naeroyfjord, and a bus trip through the beautiful winter scenery of Western Norway. This tour is meant to give you the best fjord- and mountain scenery Western Norway has to offer, in a comfortable and sustainable way. The tour has several highlights, such as the Flam Railway- one of the world’s most beautiful train journeys, a winter fjord cruise on the Nærøyfjord and Aurlandsfjord, and the Nærøydalen valley, also a UNESCO World Heritage Site. [Duration of the tour approx 12 – 13 hours] – expected arrival time in Bergen: 21: 11 hrsOvernight in Bergen. Note : Lunch on your own in Flam OR on Cruise, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bergen, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bergen Like A Local: Customized Private Tour After breakfast at the hotel Today you will have a sightseeing Tour of Bergen like a Local. With no set itinerary, you can customize the tour or leave it up to the local for an insightful introduction to the city. Make travel about the people you meet not just the places you see. With the walking tours, you will skip the mundane historical tours and discover the city through a local’s eyes. Experience a tour that will transform the way you travel to make it as much about the people you meet, as it is the places you see. The local guides (Lokafyers) are passionate about their city and eager to share their knowledge and perspective. Since Lokafyers are not professional guides and tour occasionally, they provide an experience that is authentic and personal, like a friend showing you around their city. By the end of the tour, you will feel comfortable navigating the city and confident that you have all the information you need to make the most of your stay. (Duration – 2 hours), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bergen To Tromso Today after breakfast, you will have a private airport transfer for the flight to Tromso (Internal Flights not included). Welcome to Tromsø, which is located in the heart of the Arctic wilderness, surrounded by steep mountains and beautiful fjords. The stunning nature is so close that you can admire the landscape from the city centre or from the Cable Car. It is also possible to see sea eagles and seals from Tromsø. Upon arrival at Tromsø Airport, Langnes (TOS), you will have a private transfer to your hotel for check in process. Rest of the day will be free at leisure for relax. Or you can opt for “Night Reindeer Sledding with Camp Dinner and Chance of Northern Lights” Travel out into the wilderness and walk among 300 reindeer (with the opportunity to feed them too) before enjoying a 15 to 20-minute sleigh ride. Afterwards, enter a candlelit Gamme to enjoy a relaxed three-course meal followed by the sounds of joiking (songs), Sami history and stories. On a clear night, you might be lucky enough to catch the majestic northern lights., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tromso - Free Day After breakfast at the hotel, rest of the day is free to witness the amazing location or opt for some sightseeing. Reindeer Sledding Excursion at Wilderness Camp (Available from 15 November onwards) (Optional) Get close to the majestic and festive creatures and learn about the people that have been herding them for centuries. Come on this reindeer sledding experience, meet the indigenous Sami people as you learn about their culture, interact with, and feed their reindeers. OR Snowmobile Safari in the Scenic Lyngen Alps (Optional) Explore the majestic Lyngen Alps on our Lyngen Snowmobile Safari. Behold nature at its very best in the Lyngen Alps, which offers some of the most beautiful scenery in Northern Norway. This is a big wilderness playground where we follow some approved and well-established trails. Later in the evening, we have included the Small Northern Lights Tour Max8 Guests PRO Photographer included (Start Time 18:30 / Duration 6 - 8hrs) Join a special journey through the beautiful Arctic landscapes of Tromsø to chase the magical Northern Lights. Best location is chosen based on the aurora forecast and the experience, ensuring the best chances to see the lights. You'll explore peaceful, snowy areas, perfect for capturing the beauty of the Northern Lights. Tour extends between 6 to 8 Hours regarding some weather conditions as it takes time to travel away and find the treasure lights of Aurora., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Tromso, Meals: N/A, Description: Tromso - Free Day Breakfast at the hotel followed by a day free to explore this amazing destination on your own. You can also opt for the below Optional activities. Whale watching in Magic Skjervoy - RIB Boat [Duration 11 hrs with 530 am start time] We pick you up at 5:30 am outside Scandic Ishavshotel, drive you to Skjervoy, give you warm flotation suits, and take you on a once in a life time whale watching experience by Rib-boat! Then we give you sandwiches, tea and coffee, and start the panoramic drive (back in Tromso at 6:00 pm). What’s Included: Round trip Tromso-Skjervoy-Tromso RIB-Boat whale watching excursion English speaking skipper/guide Warm flotation suits Boots Mittens Sandwiches Tea & coffee. Snacks Coffee and/or Tea OR Dog Sledding Afternoon in the Lyngen Alps (Available from 18 November onwards) Proceed for an afternoon of Dog Sledding at Breivikeidet with views of the majestic Lyngen Alps. Enjoy mushing through stunning scenery and whizzing across open terrain with the friendly and eager huskies., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart from Tromso Breakfast at the hotel, complete check out formalities and have some free time depending on the flight back home. 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight – you will have a private transfer to Tromsø Airport (TOS), for your flight back to home, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 221060.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nHotels Envigised OR Similar\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\