Basis\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrivate Oslo Tour with a Local, Highlights & Hidden Gems, 100% Personalised\xa0\nBergen Walking Tour: Explore Top Sights & Hidden Gems\xa0\nNorway in a Nutshell (Journey from Oslo to Bergen)\nTromsø: Aurora Magic Northern Lights Tour with Photos\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\nBlack out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 – 10 January’27\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms & Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 October 2026 – 31 March 2027\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/Tromso_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/59065_Oslo_Norway_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Oslo-Norway.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Oslo1.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Bergen_norway1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Norway-Bergen.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Tromso_753.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Norway_tromso.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/Tromso.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015626/itinerary/SRP_blue-lagoon.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015057', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015057', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Spain & Portugal (Winter)', 'days': 12, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Porto', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lisbon', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lisbon', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seville', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Benalmadena', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Granada', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Enjoy Hot Chocolate with Churros in Madrid. Wine tasting at an old wine seller in Porto. Enjoy Belem pastry in Lisbon. Enjoy boat ride in Algarve. Enjoy Flamenco show with a drink. Authentic Paella dinner in Granada. Enjoy Horchata drink in Valencia.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG009837_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 321176, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Spain & Portugal (Winter)' package is a 12-day tour covering Benalmadena, Porto, Barcelona, Granada, Valencia, Madrid, Lisbon, and Seville. Throughout this journey, participants will indulge in unique local culinary and cultural experiences, including enjoying hot chocolate with churros in Madrid, wine tasting at an old wine cellar in Porto, and savoring a traditional Belem pastry in Lisbon. The itinerary also features a scenic boat ride in the Algarve, a passionate Flamenco show accompanied by a drink, an authentic Paella dinner in Granada, and a refreshing Horchata drink in Valencia.", 'images': ['Madrid_753.jpg', 'PlazadeTorosdelasVentas_Madrid_753.jpg', 'Salamanca.jpg', 'Porto_WineCeller.jpg', 'BELEM_TOWER_LISBON.jpg', 'FlamencoShow_753.jpg', 'Mezquita_Cordoba.jpg', 'Granada_Alhambra.jpg', 'PlazaReina_Valencia.jpg', 'SagradaFamiliaBARCELONASPAINshutterstock101054833.jpg', 'MonasteryofMontserratBarcelona.jpg', 'Barcelona.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 321176, 'thumbnailImage': 'Seville.bmp', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015057 is named 'Highlights Of Spain & Portugal (Winter)' and spans 12 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Madrid, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Madrid On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Madrid – Visit a Bullring – Guided city tour of Toledo – Visit a Sword factory Today, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Madrid: Visit the largest bullring of Madrid – Las Ventas Plaza De Torros, see the old town, the city centre, church of San Francisco El Grande, the fountains of Paseo del Prado, Atocha station, and many more historical and modern sites. Next, we drive to Toledo. On arrival, we enjoy a guided tour: see the cathedral of Toledo, Puente San Martin, important squares and narrow winding cobblestone streets. Next, we visit a Sword factory., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Porto, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Salamanca via Avila – Onto Porto, Portugal Today, we first visit the city of Avila, where you shall get see the ‘Walls of Avila’. Later proceed to Salamanca; known as the “Golden city” for the sandstone used in the construction of its buildings, it has the third oldest existing university in the world, one of the Top 10 cathedrals in Spain, and one of the most beautiful plazas in all of Spain. On arrival we proceed on a Guided Tour of Salamanca where see the: Ponte Roma, Salamanca University, Salamanca Cathedral and the Salamanca square. Next, we continue our journey to Porto., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Lisbon, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Porto – Onto Lisbon Today, we enjoy a guided city tour Porto. World famous for its port wine, Porto is Portugal's second largest city. The historic centre of Porto was designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1996. Here, we also visit an old Wine cellar with wine tasting. Later, we drive to Lisbon., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Lisbon, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Lisbon - Visit Cabo da Roca Today, we proceed for a guided city tour Lisbon, Belem Tower, Jeronimos Monastery, Monument to the Discoveries, 25th April Bridge and more interesting sites. We also visit the town of Sintra and Cabo da Roca – Western most end of the European continent., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Seville, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Algarve boat tour – Flamenco show Today, we drive to Lagos. Upon arrival, we proceed the boat tour at Algarve experiencing its walled old town, cliffs and Atlantic beaches. Next, we drive to Sevilla situated on the banks of the River Guadalquivir. On arrival, we enjoy the traditional Flamenco show., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Benalmadena, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Sevilla - Guided city tour of Cordoba – Visit Mezquita Today, we enjoy a Guided city tour of Sevilla: See the Sevilla cathedral and Plaza Espana, followed by a horse carriage ride. Next, we drive to Cordoba for a guided city tour of the city along with entrance to Mezquita. The Mosque–Cathedral of Córdoba, officially known as the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption is a former Islamic Mosque and a UNESCO world heritage site., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Granada, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Castillo de Colomres – Guided tour of Alhambra Complex - Generalife Gardens Today we visit Castillo de Colomres: a castle dedicated to the life and adventures of Christopher Columbus. Next, we proceed to the McArthur Glen shopping outlet (if time permitting) where you can enjoy great deals on designer labels. Later, we drive to Granada and on arrival enjoy guided tour of the Alhambra Complex and Generalife Gardens., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Valencia Today, we drive to Valencia. On arrival, we enjoy a guided city tour: See the Plaza Reina, the stunning Cathedral, the central market and more. Also, see the City of Arts & Sciences, one of the more recent architectural landmarks of Valencia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Barcelona – Visit Sagrada Familia Today, we drive to Barcelona. On arrival, we enjoy a guided city tour: See the Olympic Village, Montjuic, Placa de Catalunya, and many more beautiful sights. Later, we visit the Sagrada Familia - the yet unfinished minor basilica, a UNESCO World Heritage site. Later, if time permitting enjoy some free time at La Rambla - the famous tree-lined central avenue of Barcelona with cafes and souvenir shops. Note: Entrance to Sagrada Familia depends upon the availability given by the Sagrada Familia officials and may not necessarily be done on this day. In such cases, the itinerary will be amended accordingly to cover all inclusions, or an alternate attraction will be provided., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Montserrat Today, we drive to Montserrat – a multi peaked rocky range which houses the virgin of Montserrat and Spain’s first national park. Next, we drive back to Barcelona and spend Later, spend some free time at Barcelona beach., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories Today, we proceed to Barcelona airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Spain and Portugal tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 321176.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n2 nights at Hotel Senator Barajas / NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 night at Hotel Alcora or similar in Seville, Spain.\n1 Night at Hotel Ilunion Hacienda del Sol / TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel Alixares / Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Port Azafata Valencia / Exe Puerto de Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July,2026 Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 12 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 36 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. The cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeings: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue. There are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided. General: In case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Enjoy Hot Chocolate with Churros in Madrid. Wine tasting at an old wine seller in Porto. Enjoy Belem pastry in Lisbon. Enjoy boat ride in Algarve. Enjoy Flamenco show with a drink. Authentic Paella dinner in Granada. Enjoy Horchata drink in Valencia..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE766', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Spain & Portugal (Winter)' package is a 12-day tour covering Benalmadena, Porto, Barcelona, Granada, Valencia, Madrid, Lisbon, and Seville. Throughout this journey, participants will indulge in unique local culinary and cultural experiences, including enjoying hot chocolate with churros in Madrid, wine tasting at an old wine cellar in Porto, and savoring a traditional Belem pastry in Lisbon. The itinerary also features a scenic boat ride in the Algarve, a passionate Flamenco show accompanied by a drink, an authentic Paella dinner in Granada, and a refreshing Horchata drink in Valencia.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Madrid\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Senator Barajas /NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Madrid – Visit a Bullring – Guided city tour of Toledo – Visit a Sword factory\nToday, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Madrid: Visit the largest bullring of Madrid – Las Ventas Plaza De Torros, see the old town, the city centre, church of San Francisco El Grande, the fountains of Paseo del Prado, Atocha station, and many more historical and modern sites. Next, we drive to Toledo. On arrival, we enjoy a guided tour: see the cathedral of Toledo, Puente San Martin, important squares and narrow winding cobblestone streets. Next, we visit a Sword factory.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Senator Barajas /NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Salamanca via Avila – Onto Porto, Portugal\nToday, we first visit the city of Avila, where you shall get see the ‘Walls of Avila’. Later proceed to Salamanca; known as the “Golden city” for the sandstone used in the construction of its buildings, it has the third oldest existing university in the world, one of the Top 10 cathedrals in Spain, and one of the most beautiful plazas in all of Spain. On arrival we proceed on a Guided Tour of Salamanca where see the: Ponte Roma, Salamanca University, Salamanca Cathedral and the Salamanca square. Next, we continue our journey to Porto.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nGuided tour of Porto – Onto Lisbon\nToday, we enjoy a guided city tour Porto. World famous for its port wine, Porto is Portugal's second largest city. The historic centre of Porto was designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1996. Here, we also visit an old Wine cellar with wine tasting. Later, we drive to Lisbon.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Lisbon - Visit Cabo da Roca \nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour Lisbon, Belem Tower, Jeronimos Monastery,\xa0Monument to the Discoveries, 25th April Bridge and more interesting sites.\xa0We also visit the town of Sintra and Cabo da Roca – Western most end of the European continent.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nAlgarve boat tour – Flamenco show\nToday, we drive to Lagos. Upon arrival, we proceed the boat tour at Algarve experiencing its walled old town, cliffs and Atlantic beaches. Next, we drive to Sevilla situated on the banks of the River Guadalquivir. On arrival, we enjoy the traditional Flamenco show.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alcora or similar in Seville, Spain'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Sevilla - Guided city tour of Cordoba – Visit Mezquita\nToday, we enjoy a Guided city tour of Sevilla: See the Sevilla cathedral and Plaza Espana, followed by a horse carriage ride. Next, we drive to Cordoba for a guided city tour of the city along with entrance to Mezquita. The Mosque–Cathedral of Córdoba, officially known as the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption is a former Islamic Mosque and a UNESCO world heritage site.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ilunion Hacienda del Sol / TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain.'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Castillo de Colomres – Guided tour of Alhambra Complex - Generalife Gardens\nToday we visit Castillo de Colomres: a castle dedicated to the life and adventures of Christopher Columbus. Next, we proceed to the McArthur Glen shopping outlet (if time permitting) where you can enjoy great deals on designer labels. Later, we drive to Granada and on arrival enjoy guided tour of the Alhambra Complex and Generalife Gardens.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alixares / Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Valencia\nToday, we drive to Valencia. On arrival, we enjoy a guided city tour: See the Plaza Reina, the stunning Cathedral, the central market and more. Also, see the City of Arts & Sciences, one of the more recent architectural landmarks of Valencia.\xa0\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Port Azafata Valencia / Exe Puerto de Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Barcelona – Visit Sagrada Familia\nToday, we drive to Barcelona.\xa0 On arrival, we enjoy a guided city tour: See the Olympic Village, Montjuic, Placa de Catalunya, and many more beautiful sights. Later, we visit the Sagrada Familia - the yet unfinished minor basilica, a UNESCO World Heritage site. Later, if time permitting enjoy some free time at La Rambla - the famous tree-lined central avenue of Barcelona with cafes and souvenir shops.\nNote: Entrance to Sagrada Familia depends upon the availability given by the Sagrada Familia officials and may not necessarily be done on this day. In such cases, the itinerary will be amended accordingly to cover all inclusions, or an alternate attraction will be provided.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Montserrat\nToday, we drive to Montserrat – a multi peaked rocky range which houses the virgin of Montserrat and Spain’s first national park. Next, we drive back to Barcelona and spend Later, spend some free time at Barcelona beach.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories\nToday, we proceed to Barcelona airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Spain and Portugal tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n2 nights at Hotel Senator Barajas / NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 night at Hotel Alcora or similar in Seville, Spain.\n1 Night at Hotel Ilunion Hacienda del Sol / TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel Alixares / Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Port Azafata Valencia / Exe Puerto de Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n2 nights at Hotel Senator Barajas / NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 night at Hotel Alcora or similar in Seville, Spain.\n1 Night at Hotel Ilunion Hacienda del Sol / TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel Alixares / Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Port Azafata Valencia / Exe Puerto de Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'ES', 'countryName': 'Spain', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'PT', 'countryName': 'Portugal', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 321200.0, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights at Hotel Senator Barajas / NH / Holiday Inn / Secrotel or similar in Madrid, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel AC / Premium Maia or similar in Porto, Portugal.\n2 nights at Hotel Tryp Lisboa / Mercure Almada / Lagoas Park or similar in Lisbon, Portugal.\n1 night at Hotel Alcora or similar in Seville, Spain.\n1 Night at Hotel Ilunion Hacienda del Sol / TRH Paraiso or similar in Costa del Sol / Benalmadena, Spain.\n1 night at Hotel Alixares / Abades Nevada or similar in Granada, Spain.\n1 nights at Hotel Port Azafata Valencia / Exe Puerto de Sagunto or similar in Valencia, Spain.\n2 nights at Hotel Front Air Congress / Fira Congress or similar in Barcelona, Spain.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian lunches.\n01 Local Lunch\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local dinner.\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.\n'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', 'SPAIN\nMadrid \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit the bullring - Las Ventas Plaza De Torros\n\n\xa0\nToledo \n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit a sword factory\n\n\xa0\nAvila\n\nPhoto stop at Walls of Avila\n\n\xa0\nSalamanca\n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nSeville \n\nGuided City Tour\nSee the Flamenco show\n\n\xa0\nCordoba\n\nGuided City Tour\nEntrance to Mesquita\n\n\xa0\nBenalmadena\n\nVisit Castillo de Colomres\n\n\xa0\xa0\nGranada\n\nGuided tour of Alhambra Complex\xa0\nVisit the Generalife Gardens\n\n\xa0\nValencia\n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nBarcelona\n\nGuided City Tour\nVisit Sagrada Familia\n\n\xa0\nMontserrat\xa0\n\nOrientation Tour\n\n\xa0\nPORTUGAL\nPorto\n\nGuided city tour\xa0\nVisit to an old wine cellar with wine tasting\n\nLisbon \xa0\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\nVisit Sintra and Cabo de Roca\n\nLagos\n\nAlgarve boat tour.\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July,2026\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 12 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 36 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nThe cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on15th November 2021.\xa0 Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\xa0\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot.\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain Days packed lunch will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeings:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eifel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 3-4 hours in the queue.\nThere are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nIn case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses\xa0 to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”.\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO / CHF only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/Seville.bmp', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Madrid_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/PlazadeTorosdelasVentas_Madrid_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Salamanca.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Porto_WineCeller.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/BELEM_TOWER_LISBON.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/FlamencoShow_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Mezquita_Cordoba.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Granada_Alhambra.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/PlazaReina_Valencia.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/SagradaFamiliaBARCELONASPAINshutterstock101054833.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/MonasteryofMontserratBarcelona.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015057/itinerary/Barcelona.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014859', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014859', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Ideal Iceland (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Free Sightseeing (Whale Watching)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014859_0_20260609181957.pdf', 'price': 107051, 'packageSummary': "The 'Ideal Iceland (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 6-day tour based in Reykjavik, offering travelers a focused and immersive experience in Iceland's vibrant capital city. Throughout the duration of the trip, participants will stay in Reykjavik and enjoy the unique opportunity to explore the surrounding natural wonders, with the main highlight of the itinerary being an exciting free sightseeing whale watching excursion to spot these majestic marine creatures in their natural habitat.", 'images': ['03286_reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', 'Reykjavik.jpg', 'Gullfoss_waterfall.jpg', 'Skogafoss_1.jpg', '8894627_Reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', 'Reykjavik-1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 107051, 'thumbnailImage': 'ICELAND_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014859 is named 'Ideal Iceland (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Reykjavik, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive In Reykjavik Transfer: Arrival in Keflavik Airport (KEF), you will be met by the representative and have a private transfer to the hotel. Special Note: Hotel check-in will be as per the property’s standard check-in timings or at the sole discretion of the hotel. Early check-in requests are subject to availability and may incur additional charges. Rest of the day is free. Dinner on your own. Optional Activity: “FlyOver Iceland Admission Ticket” Soar over Iceland’s stunning landscapes on FlyOver Iceland, a 30 minute immersive flying ride experience with real aerial footage, a pre show, and local Icelandic refreshments. [Supplement cost for Per Adult would be approx. € 45/- & or € 25/- Per Child ], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reykjavik Walking Tour - With a Viking Or Small Group Reykjavik Highlights Walking Tour: Meet the guide at Ingolfur Square and explore Reykjavik’s historic heart. Visit landmarks like Hallgrimskirkja, Harpa Concert Hall, and the Old Harbour, along with hidden gems such as Iceland’s oldest house and Elf stones. Enjoy stories of Vikings, local culture, and insider tips for the best spots to eat and explore. Optional Activity: “Classic Puffin Watching Cruise” [Subject to favorable weather] Depart from Reykjavík’s Old Harbour for a one hour cruise to the puffin islands, where you can observe Iceland’s summer puffins up close from the boat. The journey also showcases Reykjavík’s landmarks, including Harpa and Hallgrímskirkja. [1000 AM / 12 Noon Activity for approx. 60 - 90 mins at a supplement cost of € 55/- Per Adult & € 28/- Per Child] OR Optional Activity: “Lava Show Reykjavik Admission Ticket” Experience the only live LAVA SHOW in the world! We recreate a volcano eruption by superheating real lava and pouring it into a showroom full of people. A one-of-a-kind experience! Admission Ticket Included [Tour Activity for approx. 50 - 70 mins at a supplement cost of € 55/- Per Adult. This activity is not recommended for Children below 13 years] Special Note for above activity: Please make sure you answer all the mandatory questions during the booking process, otherwise we cannot guarantee the correct provision of the service., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reykjavik Free Day Optional Activity: “Small-group Golden Circle Classic Tour” Discover Iceland’s iconic Golden Circle on a small group tour featuring the powerful Gullfoss Waterfall, erupting Strokkur geyser, and historic Þingvellir National Park. Enjoy scenic stops, including Kerið volcanic crater, with time to explore each landmark comfortably. [Full Day Activity for approx. 8 hrs at a supplement cost of EUR 115 Per Adult & EUR 55 Per Child] Special Note for above activity: Due to weather and road conditions we cannot guarantee visits to Nesjavellir in the winter season. Please make sure you answer all the mandatory questions during the booking process. Kindly note that excursions may be subject to change or not available during adverse weather conditions. OR Optional Activity: “Reykjavík - Blue Lagoon - Comfort (*Entrance only - No Transfers included)” Relax in the warm, mineral - rich waters of Iceland’s iconic Blue Lagoon, surrounded by stunning lava fields. Enjoy silica mud masks, state-of-the-art facilities, and a drink of your choice before returning to Reykjavik. [Multiple Slot Options for approx. 4 hrs at a supplement cost of EUR 210 Per Adult & Per Child will be “On Request Basis”], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: South Coast Full Day Small - Group Tour Journey along Iceland’s stunning South Coast to visit Skogafoss and Seljalandsfoss waterfalls, the Solheimajokull glacier, and the dramatic black sands of Reynisfjara Beach. Enjoy breathtaking views, rich history, and a photo stop in the charming village of Vik before returning to Reykjavik., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reykjavik Free Day Special Note: No activity or sightseeing planned for this day. You would be on your own. Optional activities to choose from Optional Activity: “Red Lava Horse Riding Tour” Enjoy a 2.5 hour horseback riding adventure through the scenic Heiðmörk Nature Reserve, exploring lava hills, volcanic landscapes, and forested trails. Suitable for both beginners and experienced riders, the tour includes gear, small group guidance, and friendly Icelandic horses. [Supplement cost of EUR 145 Per Adult & EUR 65 Per Child - Note: Max weight 110 kgs] OR Optional Activity: “Whale Watching & Dolphin Yacht Cruise” [Subject to weather permitting] Set sail from Reykjavík’s Old Harbour on a scenic 3 hour cruise across Faxaflói Bay, watching for whales, dolphins, and summer puffins. Enjoy panoramic views of the coastline and city landmarks, with expert wildlife commentary and cozy blankets onboard. [Supplement cost of EUR 105 Per Adult & EUR 55 Per Child], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Reykjavik Transfer: 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight you will have a private transfer to Keflavik Airport (KEF) Airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 107051.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nHotel Reykjavik Saga /\xa0 Fosshotel Baron / Reykjavik Lights / Fosshotel Lind or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nGrand Hotel Reykjavik / Fosshotel Reykjavik / Hotel Odinsve / Hotel Reykjavik Centrum / Icelandair Hotel Reykjavik Marina or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 5 Nights’ accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Service will be on Point to Point Basis Only] Return Airport transfers in Reykjavik on private basis Sightseeing: [Tour will commence from a designated point, no transfers, unless specified] Reykjavik Walking Tour - Walk with a Viking or Small Group on shared basis Iceland South Coast Full Day Small-Group Tour from Reykjavik (SIC basis) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and conditions: Travel Validity: As per dates specified (*01 December 2025 - 31 March 2026) Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. TCS & GST would be levied as applicable The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: Free Sightseeing (Whale Watching).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Ideal Iceland (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 6-day tour based in Reykjavik, offering travelers a focused and immersive experience in Iceland's vibrant capital city. Throughout the duration of the trip, participants will stay in Reykjavik and enjoy the unique opportunity to explore the surrounding natural wonders, with the main highlight of the itinerary being an exciting free sightseeing whale watching excursion to spot these majestic marine creatures in their natural habitat.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive In Reykjavik\n\xa0\nTransfer: Arrival in Keflavik Airport (KEF), you will be met by the representative and have a private transfer to the hotel.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotel check-in will be as per the property’s standard check-in timings or at the sole discretion of the hotel. Early check-in requests are subject to availability and may incur additional charges. Rest of the day is free. Dinner on your own.\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: “FlyOver Iceland Admission Ticket”\nSoar over Iceland’s stunning landscapes on FlyOver Iceland, a 30 minute immersive flying ride experience with real aerial footage, a pre show, and local Icelandic refreshments. [Supplement cost for Per Adult would be approx. € 45/- & or € 25/- Per Child ]', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Saga (Standard) / Grand Hotel Reykjavik (Value) or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nReykjavik Walking Tour - With a Viking Or Small Group\n\xa0\nReykjavik Highlights Walking Tour: Meet the guide at Ingolfur Square and explore Reykjavik’s historic heart. Visit landmarks like Hallgrimskirkja, Harpa Concert Hall, and the Old Harbour, along with hidden gems such as Iceland’s oldest house and Elf stones. Enjoy stories of Vikings, local culture, and insider tips for the best spots to eat and explore.\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: “Classic Puffin Watching Cruise” [Subject to favorable weather]\nDepart from Reykjavík’s Old Harbour for a one hour cruise to the puffin islands, where you can observe Iceland’s summer puffins up close from the boat. The journey also showcases Reykjavík’s landmarks, including Harpa and Hallgrímskirkja. [1000 AM / 12 Noon Activity for approx. 60 - 90 mins at a supplement cost of € 55/-\xa0 Per Adult & € 28/-\xa0 Per Child]\n\xa0\nOR\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: “Lava Show Reykjavik Admission Ticket”\nExperience the only live LAVA SHOW in the world! We recreate a volcano eruption by superheating real lava and pouring it into a showroom full of people. A one-of-a-kind experience! Admission Ticket Included [Tour Activity for approx. 50 - 70 mins at a supplement cost of € 55/- Per Adult. This activity is not recommended for Children below 13 years]\n\xa0\nSpecial Note for above activity:\n\nPlease make sure you answer all the mandatory questions during the booking process, otherwise we cannot guarantee the correct provision of the service.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Saga (Standard) / Grand Hotel Reykjavik\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nReykjavik Free Day\nOptional Activity: “Small-group Golden Circle Classic Tour”\nDiscover Iceland’s iconic Golden Circle on a small group tour featuring the powerful Gullfoss Waterfall, erupting Strokkur geyser, and historic Þingvellir National Park. Enjoy scenic stops, including Kerið volcanic crater, with time to explore each landmark comfortably.\xa0 [Full Day Activity for approx. 8 hrs at a supplement cost of EUR 115 Per Adult & EUR 55 Per Child]\nSpecial Note for above activity: Due to weather and road conditions we cannot guarantee visits to Nesjavellir in the winter season. Please make sure you answer all the mandatory questions during the booking process. Kindly note that excursions may be subject to change or not available during adverse weather conditions.\nOR Optional Activity: “Reykjavík - Blue Lagoon - Comfort (*Entrance only - No Transfers included)”\nRelax in the warm, mineral - rich waters of Iceland’s iconic Blue Lagoon, surrounded by stunning lava fields. Enjoy silica mud masks, state-of-the-art facilities, and a drink of your choice before returning to Reykjavik. [Multiple Slot Options for approx. 4 hrs at a supplement cost of EUR 210 Per Adult & Per Child will be “On Request Basis”]', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Saga (Standard) / Grand Hotel Reykjavik\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSouth Coast Full Day Small - Group Tour\n\xa0\nJourney along Iceland’s stunning South Coast to visit Skogafoss and Seljalandsfoss waterfalls, the Solheimajokull glacier, and the dramatic black sands of Reynisfjara Beach. Enjoy breathtaking views, rich history, and a photo stop in the charming village of Vik before returning to Reykjavik.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Saga (Standard) / Grand Hotel Reykjavik\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nReykjavik Free Day\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: No activity or sightseeing planned for this day. You would be on your own.\nOptional activities to choose from\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: “Red Lava Horse Riding Tour”\nEnjoy a 2.5 hour horseback riding adventure through the scenic Heiðmörk Nature Reserve, exploring lava hills, volcanic landscapes, and forested trails. Suitable for both beginners and experienced riders, the tour includes gear, small group guidance, and friendly Icelandic horses. [Supplement cost of EUR 145 Per Adult & EUR 65 Per Child - Note: Max weight 110 kgs]\n\xa0\nOR Optional Activity: “Whale Watching & Dolphin Yacht Cruise” [Subject to weather permitting]\nSet sail from Reykjavík’s Old Harbour on a scenic 3 hour cruise across Faxaflói Bay, watching for whales, dolphins, and summer puffins. Enjoy panoramic views of the coastline and city landmarks, with expert wildlife commentary and cozy blankets onboard. [Supplement cost of EUR 105 Per Adult & EUR 55 Per Child]', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Saga (Standard) / Grand Hotel Reykjavik\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Reykjavik\n\xa0\nTransfer: 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight you will have a private transfer to Keflavik Airport (KEF) Airport.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nHotel Reykjavik Saga /\xa0 Fosshotel Baron / Reykjavik Lights / Fosshotel Lind or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nGrand Hotel Reykjavik / Fosshotel Reykjavik / Hotel Odinsve / Hotel Reykjavik Centrum / Icelandair Hotel Reykjavik Marina or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nHotel Reykjavik Saga /\xa0 Fosshotel Baron / Reykjavik Lights / Fosshotel Lind or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n', '1': '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nGrand Hotel Reykjavik / Fosshotel Reykjavik / Hotel Odinsve / Hotel Reykjavik Centrum / Icelandair Hotel Reykjavik Marina or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IS', 'countryName': 'Iceland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 107100.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nHotel Reykjavik Saga /\xa0 Fosshotel Baron / Reykjavik Lights / Fosshotel Lind or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 122000.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik (5N)\n\n\nGrand Hotel Reykjavik / Fosshotel Reykjavik / Hotel Odinsve / Hotel Reykjavik Centrum / Icelandair Hotel Reykjavik Marina or similar in Reykjavik\n\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0[Service will be on Point to Point Basis Only]\n\nReturn Airport transfers in Reykjavik on private basis\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: [Tour will commence from a designated point, no transfers, unless specified]\n\nReykjavik Walking Tour - Walk with a Viking or Small Group on shared basis\nIceland South Coast Full Day Small-Group Tour from Reykjavik (SIC basis)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n5 Nights’ accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Service will be on Point to Point Basis Only]\n\nReturn Airport transfers in Reykjavik on private basis\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: [Tour will commence from a designated point, no transfers, unless specified]\n\nReykjavik Walking Tour - Walk with a Viking or Small Group on shared basis\nIceland South Coast Full Day Small-Group Tour from Reykjavik (SIC basis)\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR10 per person per day is not included\xa0\nCity taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\n\xa0\nTerms and conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: As per dates specified (*01 December 2025 - 31 March 2026)\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/ICELAND_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/03286_reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/Reykjavik.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/Gullfoss_waterfall.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/Skogafoss_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/8894627_Reykjavik_Iceland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014859/itinerary/Reykjavik-1.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014550', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014550', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Spanish Delights With Ibiza', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ibiza', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ibiza', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014550_0_20260919183600', 'price': 156352, 'packageSummary': "The 'Spanish Delights With Ibiza' package is a 7-day tour covering Madrid, Barcelona, and Ibiza. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Royal Palace in Madrid, the breathtaking Sagrada Família in Barcelona, and the stunning beaches of Ibiza. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, cultural sightseeing, and experiencing the vibrant nightlife and coastal beauty of these world-famous Spanish destinations.", 'images': ['Madrid2.jpg', 'MadridRoyalPalace.jpg', 'Ibiza.jpeg', 'Ibiza-Castle.jpg', 'Barcelona.jpg', 'cityview_barca.jpg', 'BarcelonaCIty.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 156352, 'thumbnailImage': 'Ibiza_Castle.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014550 is named 'Spanish Delights With Ibiza' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Madrid, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Madrid Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Madrid airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid: Panoramic City Bus Tour Madrid Panoramic City Bus Tour: Route 1 (Blue) will take you to discover Historical Madrid. This circular route takes you through a complete historical, artistic, and monumental circuit featuring the city’s key landmarks. Travel along the beautiful tree-lined Paseo del Prado and admire the magnificent architectural treasures of the Habsburg royal legacy. Discover parts of Madrid’s Art Triangle and enjoy stunning views from the Royal Palace to the Temple of Debod. Route 2 (Green) will take you to discover Modern Madrid. Explore the city beyond its historical landmarks and royal monuments. From Atocha Station to Nuevos Ministerios, and from the iconic Puerta de Alcalá to Puerta del Sol. Admire the most contemporary architectural works in the capital, including the imposing KIO Towers, the modern sculptures of the Public Art Museum, and Real Madrid's Santiago Bernabéu Stadium. Discover Madrid’s vibrant life, art, and modern customs on this itinerary., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Ibiza, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid To Ibiza Transfer: You will be transferred to Madrid Airport for the flight to Ibiza. Upon your arrival at the Ibiza airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Please note Domestic Flight ticket is not included. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Ibiza, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Free At Leisure Local Sightseeing (Optional): Day is free at leisure to Explore the Beaches / Water Sports activities on your own. Ibiza Cathedral: Originally built in Gothic style in the 14th century on the site of the former Yebisah mosque, the cathedral was later restored in the 18th century with Baroque elements. Its exterior is austere with strong buttresses. Dedicated to Santa María la Mayor (Nuestra Señora de las Nieves), it reflects the promise made by Catalonian troops after conquering Ibiza in 1235. Ibiza Castle & Almudaina: The Almudaina, once the Muslim Wali’s military and administrative center, is now part of the castle complex. It features nine square towers and an elongated layout. Excavations reveal 12th–13th-century ruins, while current structures date from the 16th century (Ses Voltes building) and 18th century (infantry barracks)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ibiza To Barcelona Transfers: You will be transferred to Ibiza Airport for the flight to Barcelona. Upon your arrival at the Barcelona airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Please note Domestic Flight ticket is not included. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Barcelona: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Hop aboard the Barcelona Bus Turístic, and discover the best of the city aboard a panoramic double-decker bus. Not only can you hop on and off as you wish, but you have the freedom to explore the beautiful city of Barcelona at your own leisure. Highlights - See the most iconic landmarks of the city - Hop on and off as you wish at conveniently located route stops - Learn about the city with a fascinating audioguide available in 16 languages The Barcelona Bus Turístic is the city’s official sightseeing hop-on, hop-off tour. The red route and the blue route take approximately two hours to complete. Others Both routes depart between 9 am and 9:30 am from any stop. The last departures leave at 7pm during the winter months and 8pm in summer. Depending on the season, the bus frequency varies, between 5 and 25 minutes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Barcelona Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Barcelona hotel to the airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 156352.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nEurostars Casa De La Lirica / Hotel Madrid Plaza De Espana Affiliated By Melia /Petit Palace Plaza Espana / Catalonia Gran Via or similar \n\n\n\n\nIbiza\n\n\nRoyal Plaza / Simbad / El Hotel Pacha or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nExe Cristal Palace / Catalonia Diagonal Centro / Zenit Borell / Catalonia Eixample 1864 / Catalonia Gran Via Bcn or similar\n\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / Hotel Madrid Centro, Affiliated by Melia or similar\n\n\n\n\nIbiza\n\n\nVibra Maritimo / Aparthotel Vibra Lux Mar / Ryans Ibiza Apartments/ Apartamentos Vibra Panoramic or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nHotel Viladomat By Silken / Catalonia Roma / Leonardo Hotel Barcelona Gran Via / Continental Palacete or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Madrid based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Ibiza based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Barcelona based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transfers: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Return Airport Transfers from Madrid Airport to Hotel & back Return Airport Transfers from Ibiza Airport to Hotel & back Return Airport Transfers from Barcelona Airport to Hotel & back Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Madrid Panoramic City Tour Barcelona Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephne, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Spanish Delights With Ibiza' package is a 7-day tour covering Madrid, Barcelona, and Ibiza. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Royal Palace in Madrid, the breathtaking Sagrada Família in Barcelona, and the stunning beaches of Ibiza. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, cultural sightseeing, and experiencing the vibrant nightlife and coastal beauty of these world-famous Spanish destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'Arrive Madrid\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Madrid airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Petit Palace Cliper Gran Via\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Eurostars Casa De La Lirica\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Madrid'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nMadrid: Panoramic City Bus Tour\n\xa0\nMadrid Panoramic City Bus Tour: Route 1 (Blue) will take you to discover Historical Madrid. This circular route takes you through a complete historical, artistic, and monumental circuit featuring the city’s key landmarks. Travel along the beautiful tree-lined Paseo del Prado and admire the magnificent architectural treasures of the Habsburg royal legacy. Discover parts of Madrid’s Art Triangle and enjoy stunning views from the Royal Palace to the Temple of Debod.\n\xa0\nRoute 2 (Green) will take you to discover Modern Madrid. Explore the city beyond its historical landmarks and royal monuments. From Atocha Station to Nuevos Ministerios, and from the iconic Puerta de Alcalá to Puerta del Sol. Admire the most contemporary architectural works in the capital, including the imposing KIO Towers, the modern sculptures of the Public Art Museum, and Real Madrid's Santiago Bernabéu Stadium. Discover Madrid’s vibrant life, art, and modern customs on this itinerary.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Petit Palace Cliper Gran Via\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Eurostars Casa De La Lirica\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Madrid'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nMadrid To Ibiza\n\xa0\nTransfer:\xa0\n\nYou will be transferred to Madrid Airport for the flight to Ibiza.\nUpon your arrival at the Ibiza airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note Domestic Flight ticket is not included.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Vibra Maritimo (Standard) /\xa0Royal Plaza (Value) or similar in Ibiza'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay Free At Leisure\xa0\nLocal Sightseeing (Optional): Day is free at leisure to Explore the Beaches / Water Sports activities on your own.\xa0\n\xa0\nIbiza Cathedral: Originally built in Gothic style in the 14th century on the site of the former Yebisah mosque, the cathedral was later restored in the 18th century with Baroque elements. Its exterior is austere with strong buttresses. Dedicated to Santa María la Mayor (Nuestra Señora de las Nieves), it reflects the promise made by Catalonian troops after conquering Ibiza in 1235.\n\xa0\nIbiza Castle & Almudaina: The Almudaina, once the Muslim Wali’s military and administrative center, is now part of the castle complex. It features nine square towers and an elongated layout. Excavations reveal 12th–13th-century ruins, while current structures date from the 16th century (Ses Voltes building) and 18th century (infantry barracks).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Vibra Maritimo (Standard) /\xa0Royal Plaza (Value) or similar in Ibiza'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nIbiza To Barcelona\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nYou will be transferred to Ibiza Airport for the flight to Barcelona.\nUpon your arrival at the Barcelona airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note Domestic Flight ticket is not included.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Viladomat By Silken (Standard) / Exe Cristal Palace (Value) or similar in Barcelona'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nBarcelona: Hop On Hop Off\nHop on Hop off Tour: Hop aboard the Barcelona Bus Turístic, and discover the best of the city aboard a panoramic double-decker bus. Not only can you hop on and off as you wish, but you have the freedom to explore the beautiful city of Barcelona at your own leisure. Highlights - See the most iconic landmarks of the city - Hop on and off as you wish at conveniently located route stops - Learn about the city with a fascinating audioguide available in 16 languages The Barcelona Bus Turístic is the city’s official sightseeing hop-on, hop-off tour. The red route and the blue route take approximately two hours to complete. Others Both routes depart between 9 am and 9:30 am from any stop. The last departures leave at 7pm during the winter months and 8pm in summer. Depending on the season, the bus frequency varies, between 5 and 25 minutes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Viladomat By Silken (Standard) / Exe Cristal Palace (Value) or similar in Barcelona'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Barcelona\nTransfers: You will have a private transfer from Barcelona hotel to the airport.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nEurostars Casa De La Lirica / Hotel Madrid Plaza De Espana Affiliated By Melia /Petit Palace Plaza Espana / Catalonia Gran Via or similar \n\n\n\n\nIbiza\n\n\nRoyal Plaza / Simbad / El Hotel Pacha or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nExe Cristal Palace / Catalonia Diagonal Centro / Zenit Borell / Catalonia Eixample 1864 / Catalonia Gran Via Bcn or similar\n\n\n\n', '\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / Hot