d on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Galway based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Belfast based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Dublin Airport to Dublin Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Belfast Hotel to Belfast Airport\nSecond Class Train: Dublin - Killarney // Galway – Dublin // Dublin - Belfast\nBus Ticket: Killarney – Galway\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nDublin Hop On Hop Off (24 hours)\nRing of Kerry - Seat in Coach Basis\nCliffs of Moher & Burren Tour - Seat in Coach Basis\nGiant’s Causeway, Glens of Antrim and Dark Hedges Tour - Seat in Coach Basis\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n\n\xa0', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms And Conditions: \n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/belfast_castle.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Dublin_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Dublin_2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Killarney.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Ring_of_Kerry.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Galway.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/CLIFFS_4.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Dublin_7.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/belfast_castle.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/Causeway_code_poet.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014512/itinerary/BELFAST_2.jpeg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014674', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014674', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Akorshoniyo France O Swiss - Durga Puja Special', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lausanne', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Lausanne', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zurich', 'geoLocation': {'lat': 0.0, 'lon': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Indian dinners in the comforts of your hotel in some cities. Champagne lunch on top of Jungfraujoch. Fondue lunch at Glacier 3000. Chocolate tasting at the Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Illumination tour of Paris.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG009686_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 291003, 'packageSummary': "The 'Akorshoniyo France O Swiss - Durga Puja Special' package is an 8-day tour covering the beautiful cities of Paris, Lausanne, and Zurich. The itinerary offers a delightful mix of sightseeing and unique culinary experiences, featuring highlights such as Indian dinners served in the comfort of your hotel in select cities, a scenic Champagne lunch on top of Jungfraujoch, and a traditional fondue lunch at Glacier 3000. Additionally, participants will enjoy a sweet chocolate tasting experience at the Lindt: Home of Chocolate and a magical illumination tour of Paris.", 'images': ['Paris753.jpg', 'EiffelTower753.jpg', 'Disneyland75345.jpg', 'Switzerland7537.jpg', 'Gstaad753.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'LionMonument.jpg', 'Zurich753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 291003, 'thumbnailImage': 'Paris_Seine_River_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Durga Puja Special'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Durga Puja Special', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014674 is named 'Akorshoniyo France O Swiss - Durga Puja Special' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Paris! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside London Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Eiffel Tower (3rd Level) – Visit Louvre Museum – Guided city tour of Paris – Seine River Cruise - Illumination Tour of Paris Today, we visit the Eiffel Tower (3rd level). Next, we visit the world-famous Louvre Museum and get a glimpse of Mona Lisa. Later, we proceed on a Guided Tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House and Les Invalides. In the evening, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River along with ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up. Note: Visiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park) Today, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventure Land., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Lausanne, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Onto Swiss Today, check out and proceed for a scenic drive towards Switzerland., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Lausanne, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Glacier 3000 - Orientation tour of Saanen & Gstaad – Golden Pass Train Today, we proceed on an excursion to Glacier 3000. Enjoy breath- taking views of the iconic mountains such as Mont-Blanc, the Matterhorn, Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau from the Tissot Peak Walk. Next, we enjoy an orientation tour of Saanen & Gstaad - a shooting location for Indian films. Later, we board the scenic Golden Pass train and enjoy panoramic views as we journey through alpine forest and picturesque villages., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Excursion to Jungfraujoch with Lunch & Interlaken Today, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We take the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Enjoy lunch on Top. Later, descend and visit Interlaken., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Zurich – Cruise on Lake Zurich - Visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate - Orientation Tour of Lucerne Today, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Zurich where we explore the historic Old Town with its winding streets and iconic churches. Next, we enjoy a cruise on Lake Zurich. Later we proceed to Lindt: Home of Chocolate; where we get to discover Switzerland’s oldest chocolate brands and get to learn the art of chocolate making. In the evening, we proceed to Lucerne. On arrival we enjoy an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument, and Kapel Brucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Note: If Lindt is not available, we shall take the group to an alternate Chocolate experience., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Zurich, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to Zurich airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 291003.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\xa0\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 nights at Hotel Zenitude CDG / Suite Novotel CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\n02 Nights at Hotel Alpine Classic / Moxy or similar in Leysin / Sion / Lausanne, Switzerland\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe or similar in Zurich, Switzerland\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n06 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches.\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches., \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 01st February 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Tips for the entire duration of the stay is included in the tour cost. 1 x 500ml water bottle will be distributed in the coach everyday. Tour Manager travelling with the group from Kolkata. Visa Requirements Multiple Entry Schengen Visa. This Cost Includes Documentation, Processing And Consulate Fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 01st February 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers. Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st January, 2024. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Indian dinners in the comforts of your hotel in some cities. Champagne lunch on top of Jungfraujoch. Fondue lunch at Glacier 3000. Chocolate tasting at the Lindt: Home of Chocolate. Illumination tour of Paris..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE204', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE204', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE204', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Akorshoniyo France O Swiss - Durga Puja Special' package is an 8-day tour covering the beautiful cities of Paris, Lausanne, and Zurich. The itinerary offers a delightful mix of sightseeing and unique culinary experiences, featuring highlights such as Indian dinners served in the comfort of your hotel in select cities, a scenic Champagne lunch on top of Jungfraujoch, and a traditional fondue lunch at Glacier 3000. Additionally, participants will enjoy a sweet chocolate tasting experience at the Lindt: Home of Chocolate and a magical illumination tour of Paris.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome to Paris!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside London Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in.\n\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEiffel Tower (3rd Level) – Visit Louvre Museum – Guided city tour of Paris – Seine River Cruise - Illumination Tour of Paris\nToday, we visit the Eiffel Tower (3rd level). Next, we visit the world-famous Louvre Museum and get a glimpse of Mona Lisa. Later, we proceed on a Guided Tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House and Les Invalides. In the evening, we enjoy a cruise on the Seine River along with ‘Illumination Tour of Paris’ and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up.\nNote:\xa0\n\nVisiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level.\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 – 5 hours in the queue.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris,\xa0France'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDisneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\nToday, we proceed to Disneyland® Paris where you can visit Disneyland® Park OR Walt Disney Studios® Park. Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting rollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and others in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of the globe in Adventure Land.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris,\xa0France'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOnto Swiss\nToday, check out and proceed for a scenic drive towards Switzerland.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGlacier 3000 - Orientation tour of Saanen & Gstaad – Golden Pass Train\nToday, we proceed on an excursion to Glacier 3000. Enjoy breath- taking views of the iconic mountains such as Mont-Blanc, the Matterhorn, Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau from the Tissot Peak Walk. Next, we enjoy an orientation tour of Saanen & Gstaad - a shooting location for Indian films. Later, we board the scenic Golden Pass train and enjoy panoramic views as we journey through alpine forest and picturesque villages.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with Lunch & Interlaken\nToday, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We take the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Enjoy lunch on Top. Later, descend and visit Interlaken.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard\xa0by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation tour of Zurich – Cruise on Lake Zurich - Visit Lindt: Home of Chocolate - Orientation Tour of Lucerne\nToday, we proceed for an Orientation tour of Zurich where we explore the historic Old Town with its winding streets and iconic churches. Next, we enjoy a cruise on Lake Zurich. Later we proceed to Lindt: Home of Chocolate; where we get to discover Switzerland’s oldest chocolate brands and get to learn the art of chocolate making. In the evening, we proceed to Lucerne. On arrival we enjoy an orientation tour: See the Lion Monument, and Kapel Brucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates.\nNote: If Lindt is not available, we shall take the group to an alternate Chocolate experience.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Novotel Zurich Messe\xa0/ Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard\xa0by Mariott\xa0Biel or similar in Zurich,\xa0Switzerland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to Zurich airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote:\n\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\xa0\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n03 nights at Hotel Zenitude CDG / Suite Novotel CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\n02 Nights at Hotel Alpine Classic / Moxy or similar in Leysin / Sion / Lausanne, Switzerland\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe or similar in Zurich, Switzerland\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\xa0\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n03 nights at Hotel Zenitude CDG / Suite Novotel CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\n02 Nights at Hotel Alpine Classic / Moxy or similar in Leysin / Sion / Lausanne, Switzerland\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe or similar in Zurich, Switzerland\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'continentName': 'Europe', 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France'}, {'continentId': 5, 'continentName': 'Europe', 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 291000.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights at nights at Hotel Novotel Collegian / Golden Tulip / Mercure CDG / Clarion CDG / Millenium CDG or similar in Paris, France.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Agora by Fassbind / Alpine Classic / Eurotel or similar in Lausanne / Leysin / Villars, Switzerland.\xa0\n02 Nights at Hotel Novotel Zurich Messe / Intercity Zurich Airport / Courtyard by Mariott Biel or similar in Zurich, Switzerland.\xa0\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread with Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee).\n06 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches.\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.', '\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nMultiple Entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis Cost Includes Documentation, Processing And Consulate Fees.\n', '\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['France:\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\nVisit 2nd level of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Fragonard - French Perfume Museum\nIllumination Tour of Paris\xa0\nSeine river cruise\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\nSwitzerland:\n\nVisit Glacier 3000\xa0\nRide on the Scenic Golden Pass Train\nOrientation tour of Geneva\nOrientation Tour of Gstaad\nOrientation Tour of Montreux\nOrientation Tour of Lucerne\nCruise on Lake Lucerne\nVisit Lindt Home of Chocolate\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'France\n\nGuided City Tour Of Paris\nVisit 3rd Level Of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Louvre Museum\nIllumination Tour Of Paris\xa0\nSeine River Cruise\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\n\nSwitzerland\n\nVisit Glacier 3000\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Saanen & Gstaad\nRide On The Scenic Golden Pass Train\nExcursion To Jungfraujoch With Lunch And Interlaken\xa0\nVisit Lindt: Home Of Chocolate\nCruise On Lake Zurich\nOrientation Tour Of Lucerne\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 01st February 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\xa0\nTips for the entire duration of the stay is included in the tour cost.\n1 x 500ml water bottle will be distributed in the coach everyday.\nTour Manager travelling with the group from Kolkata.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple Entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis Cost Includes Documentation, Processing And Consulate Fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 01st February 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers.\nImportant Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st January, 2024.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\xa0\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches:\n\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\n\nMeals:\n\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\nOn certain days, packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing:\n\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and\xa0 the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\n\nGeneral:\n\n\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/Paris_Seine_River_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/Paris753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/EiffelTower753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/Disneyland75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/Switzerland7537.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/Gstaad753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/LionMonument.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014674/itinerary/Zurich753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014540', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014540', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Best Of Spain', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Madrid', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seville', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Seville', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Valencia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Barcelona', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014540_0_20260916161631', 'price': 169543, 'packageSummary': "The 'Best Of Spain' package is a 9-day tour covering Madrid, Barcelona, Valencia, and Seville. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the breathtaking Sagrada Familia, the historic Royal Palace, the futuristic City of Arts and Sciences, and the magnificent Plaza de España. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, authentic flamenco shows, and local culinary experiences like tapas tastings as they explore the rich culture and history of these vibrant cities.", 'images': ['Madrid2.jpg', 'MadridRoyalPalace.jpg', 'seville1.jpg', 'Seville.jpg', 'Valencia2.jpg', 'Valencia.jpg', 'Barcelona.jpg', 'BarcelonaSpain.jpg', 'BarcelonaCIty.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 169543, 'thumbnailImage': 'BArcelona_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014540 is named 'Best Of Spain' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Madrid, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Madrid Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Madrid airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Madrid, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid: Panoramic City Bus Tour Madrid Panoramic City Bus Tour: Route 1 (Blue) will take you to discover Historical Madrid. This circular route takes you through a complete historical, artistic, and monumental circuit featuring the city’s key landmarks. Travel along the beautiful tree-lined Paseo del Prado and admire the magnificent architectural treasures of the Habsburg royal legacy. Discover parts of Madrid’s Art Triangle and enjoy stunning views from the Royal Palace to the Temple of Debod. Route 2 (Green) will take you to discover Modern Madrid. Explore the city beyond its historical landmarks and royal monuments. From Atocha Station to Nuevos Ministerios, and from the iconic Puerta de Alcalá to Puerta del Sol. Admire the most contemporary architectural works in the capital, including the imposing KIO Towers, the modern sculptures of the Public Art Museum, and Real Madrid's Santiago Bernabéu Stadium. Discover Madrid’s vibrant life, art, and modern customs on this itinerary., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Seville, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Madrid To Seville By Train Transfer: Make your way to the Madrid train station for your onward journey to Seville. Upon arrival at Seville train station make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Seville, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Seville: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Later enjoy Seville Hop on Hop off sightseeing. This tour is operated by double decker buses you can make a route through more emblematic places of the city of Seville, with commentaries in 16 different languages, which make possible to know the history, culture and heritage of the city, which origin goes back to Old Age, that way this city is a cultures mixing . This service is valid for 24 (basic) or 48 hours (Experience) with a hop on / hop off system , so during this period you can get on and get off of the bus such times as you want in any bus stop. The ticket can be purchase as in the bus as in any of two main bus stop, furthermore in any official sales point. Multilingual Audio System: 16 languages. Panoramic route on double decker buses with 14 stops at the most important locations of the city: Paseo Colon, Plaza de Espana, 1929 Exhibition, Triana-San Jacinto, Triana-Castilla, 1992 Universal Exhibition, Isla Magica, Macarena, Torre de los Perdigones, Alameda de Hercules, Plaza del Duque, Plaza de Armas, plaza de Cuba y Acuario de Sevilla. Hop on , hop off. Individual headsets. Free Entrance: El Salvador Church, Museo de Carruajes, Pabellon de la Navegacion, Casa de la Ciencia, Torre de los Perdigones, Iglesia de Santa Ana and Hospital de la Caridad., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Seville To Valencia Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the Seville train station for your onward journey to Valencia. Upon your arrival at Valencia train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Valencia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Valencia: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Today enjoy Valencia Tourist Bus sightseeing. Get to know Valencia in a comfortable, rigorous and enjoyable way. You will be able to hop on and off the bus all day along the route of your choice or change to another, admiring the architectural and cultural magnificence of Valencia, with the commentaries offered through a headphones audio system in seven different languages (Spanish, English, French, German, Italian, Portuguese and Japanese). The tour offers you 2 Hop-on Hop-off routes (90 minutes duration each) to customise your own tour of Valencia. Route A (red colour) you will meet the city from a historical and monumental viewpoint and the route B (blue colour) you will know the Mediterranean Sea influence on the city of Valencia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Valencia To Barcelona Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Barcelona. Upon your arrival at Barcelona train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed. Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Barcelona: Hop On Hop Off Hop on Hop off Tour: Hop aboard the Barcelona Bus Turístic, and discover the best of the city aboard a panoramic double-decker bus. Not only can you hop on and off as you wish, but you have the freedom to explore the beautiful city of Barcelona at your own leisure. Highlights - See the most iconic landmarks of the city - Hop on and off as you wish at conveniently located route stops - Learn about the city with a fascinating audioguide available in 16 languages The Barcelona Bus Turístic is the city’s official sightseeing hop-on, hop-off tour. The red route and the blue route take approximately two hours to complete. Others Both routes depart between 9 am and 9:30 am from any stop. The last departures leave at 7pm during the winter months and 8pm in summer. Depending on the season, the bus frequency varies, between 5 and 25 minutes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Barcelona, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Barcelona Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Barcelona hotel to the airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 169543.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / Hotel Madrid Centro, Affiliated by Melia or similar\n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nHotel Derby Sevilla / Las Casas De Los Mercaderes By Silken / Eurostars Regina / H10 Corregidor Boutique Hotel or similar \n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nMediterraneo / Hotel Kramer / Hotel Sorolla Centro or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nHotel Viladomat By Silken / Catalonia Roma / Leonardo Hotel Barcelona Gran Via / Continental Palacete or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nEurostars Casa De La Lirica / Hotel Madrid Plaza De Espana Affiliated By Melia /Petit Palace Plaza Espana / Catalonia Gran Via or similar \n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nNH Sevilla Plaza de Armas / Catalonia Giralda / Hotel Las Casas de la Judería or similar\n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nSenator Parque Central / Nh Valencia Center / Silken Puerta Valencia or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nExe Cristal Palace / Catalonia Diagonal Centro / Zenit Borell / Catalonia Eixample 1864 / Catalonia Gran Via Bcn or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Madrid based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Seville based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Valencia based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Barcelona based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transfers: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Madrid Airport to Madrid Hotel Departure Airport transfer from Barcelona Hotel to Barcelona Airport Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Madrid to Seville (Subject to availability until ticketed) 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Seville to Valencia (Subject to availability until ticketed) 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Valencia to Barcelona (Subject to availability until ticketed) Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Madrid Panoramic City Tour Seville Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket Valencia Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket Barcelona Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Ticket Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not mentioned in inclusions. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Best Of Spain' package is a 9-day tour covering Madrid, Barcelona, Valencia, and Seville. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the breathtaking Sagrada Familia, the historic Royal Palace, the futuristic City of Arts and Sciences, and the magnificent Plaza de España. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, authentic flamenco shows, and local culinary experiences like tapas tastings as they explore the rich culture and history of these vibrant cities.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Madrid\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Madrid airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Petit Palace Cliper Gran Via\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Eurostars Casa De La Lirica\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Madrid'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nMadrid: Panoramic City Bus Tour\n\xa0\nMadrid Panoramic City Bus Tour: Route 1 (Blue) will take you to discover Historical Madrid. This circular route takes you through a complete historical, artistic, and monumental circuit featuring the city’s key landmarks. Travel along the beautiful tree-lined Paseo del Prado and admire the magnificent architectural treasures of the Habsburg royal legacy. Discover parts of Madrid’s Art Triangle and enjoy stunning views from the Royal Palace to the Temple of Debod.\n\xa0\nRoute 2 (Green) will take you to discover Modern Madrid. Explore the city beyond its historical landmarks and royal monuments. From Atocha Station to Nuevos Ministerios, and from the iconic Puerta de Alcalá to Puerta del Sol. Admire the most contemporary architectural works in the capital, including the imposing KIO Towers, the modern sculptures of the Public Art Museum, and Real Madrid's Santiago Bernabéu Stadium. Discover Madrid’s vibrant life, art, and modern customs on this itinerary.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Petit Palace Cliper Gran Via\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Eurostars Casa De La Lirica\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Madrid'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nMadrid To Seville By Train\n\xa0\nTransfer:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the Madrid train station for your onward journey to Seville.\nUpon arrival at Seville train station make your way to the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Derby (Standard) /\xa0NH Plaza de Armas (Value) or similar in\xa0Seville'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSeville: Hop On Hop Off\xa0\n\xa0\nHop on Hop off Tour: Later enjoy Seville Hop on Hop off sightseeing. This tour is operated by double decker buses you can make a route through more emblematic places of the city of Seville, with commentaries in 16 different languages, which make possible to know the history, culture and heritage of the city, which origin goes back to Old Age, that way this city is a cultures mixing . This service is valid for 24 (basic) or 48 hours (Experience) with a hop on / hop off system , so during this period you can get on and get off of the bus such times as you want in any bus stop. The ticket can be purchase as in the bus as in any of two main bus stop, furthermore in any official sales point. Multilingual Audio System: 16 languages. Panoramic route on double decker buses with 14 stops at the most important locations of the city: Paseo Colon, Plaza de Espana, 1929 Exhibition, Triana-San Jacinto, Triana-Castilla, 1992 Universal Exhibition, Isla Magica, Macarena, Torre de los Perdigones, Alameda de Hercules, Plaza del Duque, Plaza de Armas, plaza de Cuba y Acuario de Sevilla. Hop on , hop off. Individual headsets. Free Entrance: El Salvador Church, Museo de Carruajes, Pabellon de la Navegacion, Casa de la Ciencia, Torre de los Perdigones, Iglesia de Santa Ana and Hospital de la Caridad.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Derby (Standard) /\xa0NH Plaza de Armas (Value) or similar in\xa0Seville'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nSeville To Valencia Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the Seville train station for your onward journey to Valencia.\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Valencia train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Mediterraneo (Standard) /\xa0Senator Parque Central (Value) or similar in\xa0Valencia'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nValencia: Hop On Hop Off\n\xa0\nHop on Hop off Tour: Today enjoy Valencia Tourist Bus sightseeing. Get to know Valencia in a comfortable, rigorous and enjoyable way. You will be able to hop on and off the bus all day along the route of your choice or change to another, admiring the architectural and cultural magnificence of Valencia, with the commentaries offered through a headphones audio system in seven different languages (Spanish, English, French, German, Italian, Portuguese and Japanese). The tour offers you 2 Hop-on Hop-off routes (90 minutes duration each) to customise your own tour of Valencia. Route A (red colour) you will meet the city from a historical and monumental viewpoint and the route B (blue colour) you will know the Mediterranean Sea influence on the city of Valencia.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Mediterraneo (Standard) /\xa0Senator Parque Central (Value) or similar in\xa0Valencia'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nValencia To Barcelona Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Barcelona.\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Barcelona train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed.\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Viladomat By Silken (Standard) / Exe Cristal Palace (Value) or similar in Barcelona'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nBarcelona: Hop On Hop Off\n\xa0\nHop on Hop off Tour: Hop aboard the Barcelona Bus Turístic, and discover the best of the city aboard a panoramic double-decker bus. Not only can you hop on and off as you wish, but you have the freedom to explore the beautiful city of Barcelona at your own leisure. Highlights - See the most iconic landmarks of the city - Hop on and off as you wish at conveniently located route stops - Learn about the city with a fascinating audioguide available in 16 languages The Barcelona Bus Turístic is the city’s official sightseeing hop-on, hop-off tour. The red route and the blue route take approximately two hours to complete. Others Both routes depart between 9 am and 9:30 am from any stop. The last departures leave at 7pm during the winter months and 8pm in summer. Depending on the season, the bus frequency varies, between 5 and 25 minutes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Viladomat By Silken (Standard) / Exe Cristal Palace (Value) or similar in Barcelona'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Barcelona\n\xa0\n\xa0Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Barcelona hotel to the airport.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / Hotel Madrid Centro, Affiliated by Melia or similar\n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nHotel Derby Sevilla / Las Casas De Los Mercaderes By Silken / Eurostars Regina / H10 Corregidor Boutique Hotel or similar \n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nMediterraneo / Hotel Kramer / Hotel Sorolla Centro or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nHotel Viladomat By Silken / Catalonia Roma / Leonardo Hotel Barcelona Gran Via / Continental Palacete or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nEurostars Casa De La Lirica / Hotel Madrid Plaza De Espana Affiliated By Melia /Petit Palace Plaza Espana / Catalonia Gran Via or similar \n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nNH Sevilla Plaza de Armas / Catalonia Giralda / Hotel Las Casas de la Judería or similar\n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nSenator Parque Central / Nh Valencia Center / Silken Puerta Valencia or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nExe Cristal Palace / Catalonia Diagonal Centro / Zenit Borell / Catalonia Eixample 1864 / Catalonia Gran Via Bcn or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / Hotel Madrid Centro, Affiliated by Melia or similar\n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nHotel Derby Sevilla / Las Casas De Los Mercaderes By Silken / Eurostars Regina / H10 Corregidor Boutique Hotel or similar \n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nMediterraneo / Hotel Kramer / Hotel Sorolla Centro or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nHotel Viladomat By Silken / Catalonia Roma / Leonardo Hotel Barcelona Gran Via / Continental Palacete or similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n', '1': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nEurostars Casa De La Lirica / Hotel Madrid Plaza De Espana Affiliated By Melia /Petit Palace Plaza Espana / Catalonia Gran Via or similar \n\n\n\n\nSeville\n\n\nNH Sevilla Plaza de Armas / Catalonia Giralda / Hotel Las Casas de la Judería or similar\n\n\n\n\nValencia\n\n\nSenator Parque Central / Nh Valencia Center / Silken Puerta Valencia or similar\n\n\n\n\nBarcelona\n\n\nExe Cristal Palace / Catalonia Diagonal Centro / Zenit Borell / Catalonia Eixample 1864 / Catalonia Gran Via Bcn or similar\n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'ES', 'countryName': 'Spain', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 169500.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nMadrid\n\n\nPetit Palace Cliper Gran Via / Petit Palace Tres Cruces / Hotel Los Condes / Petit Palace Chueca / H