dical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nEntrance fees - Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine Tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, Diamond bridge\n2 half a litre bottles of water per person per day.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage, or passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure as of 1st August 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leads to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink are not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips for guides, hotel waiters, drivers, etc.\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Test', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015517/AlmatyCity.jpeg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015160', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015160', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Uk Delights With Ireland (Winter)', 'days': 15, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'London', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Birmingham', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Manchester', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Aberdeen', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Strathclyde', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Belfast', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Belfast', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Galway', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dublin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dublin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dublin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['ENGLAND Guided City Tour of London Visit the Tower of London – see the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond Enjoy a Ride on the London Eye Visit the Lords Cricket Ground in London Visit Windsor Castle Guided Tour of Oxford Visit Stonehenge Orientation tour of Bath with a visit to Roman Bath Visit Shakespeare birthplace Visit Manchester City Football Stadium Enjoy a scenic cruise on Lake Windermere SCOTLAND Visit Gretna Green Guided City Tour of Edinburgh Visit the Edinburgh Castle Enjoy a Johnnie Walker Experience in Edinburgh Photo stop at Kelpies in Falkirk Guided Tour of Aberdeen Enjoy Loch Ness Cruise Visit Fort Augustus NORTHERN IRELAND Visit to Titanic Exhibition Visit the Botanical Gardens Guided city tour of Belfast Tour the sights of the World-Famous Television Series - Game of Thrones Visit Giant’s Causeway REPUBLIC OF IRELAND Guided City tour of Galway See the Cliffs of Moher Guided city tour of Dublin with Entrance to Trinity College Entrance to Guinness Storehouse'], 'pdfName': 'PKG010438_0_20230727144907.pdf', 'price': 458048, 'packageSummary': "The 'Uk Delights With Ireland (Winter)' package is a 15-day tour covering London, Birmingham, Manchester, Strathclyde, Aberdeen, Belfast, Dublin, and Galway. This extensive itinerary features guided city tours of London, Edinburgh, Aberdeen, Belfast, Dublin, and Galway, alongside visits to iconic landmarks like the Tower of London, Windsor Castle, Stonehenge, the Roman Baths, Shakespeare's birthplace, and the Manchester City Football Stadium. Travelers will also enjoy scenic cruises on Lake Windermere and Loch Ness, explore Edinburgh Castle, experience the Johnnie Walker Experience, and see the Kelpies in Falkirk. The journey continues with a visit to the Titanic Exhibition, a tour of Game of Thrones filming locations, and a trip to the Giant’s Causeway in Northern Ireland, before concluding in the Republic of Ireland with visits to the breathtaking Cliffs of Moher, Trinity College, and the famous Guinness Storehouse.", 'images': ['25422_London_Tower_Bridge_753.jpg', '78202_Westminster_Parliament_London_753.jpg', 'Oxford_new_753.jpg', 'Stonehenge-753.jpg', 'Shakespeares_Birthplace.jpg', 'Lake_Windermere.jpg', '753_EdinburghCastle.jpg', 'kelpies_753.jpg', 'Loch_Ness_753.jpg', 'BelfastCity7531.jpg', 'Kingsroad_Belfast.jpg', 'Galway_753.jpg', 'Galway.png', 'TrinityCollege_Dublin.jpg', 'Dublin_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 458048, 'thumbnailImage': 'Stonehenge_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015160 is named 'Uk Delights With Ireland (Winter)' and spans 15 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - London, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to London! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Tower of London – Guided City Tour of London – Ride on London Eye – Lords Cricket Ground Today, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond. Next, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye. Later, we proceed for a Guided city tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. Also, enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground and relive the historic moments. Note: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit alternate stadium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - London, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Windsor Castle – Guided Tour of Oxford Today, we drive to Windsor for a visit of the famous Windsor Castle – Queen Elizabeth II’s favorite weekend home. Next, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”. Later in the evening, you have some free time for shopping at Bicester Village., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Birmingham, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Stonehenge – Orientation tour of Bath with a visit to a Roman Bath Today, we proceed to visit the famous Stonehenge: an ancient and mysterious monument with a sophisticated architectural design, its astronomical alignments, and its mystery of purpose. Next, we drive to Bath for an Orientation tour and we visit a Roman Bath: well-preserved thermae in the city of Bath., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Manchester, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Shakespeare Birthplace at Stratford Upon Avon - Visit Manchester City Football Stadium Today, we drive to Stratford upon Avon for an Orientation tour and we Visit Shakespeare's Birthplace to walk in Shakespeare's footsteps and explore the house he was born in. Later we proceed to visit the famous Manchester City Football Stadium. Visit the home changing room, sit in the dugout & run down the tunnel which leads to the football field. Note: On days when Manchester City Stadium is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Lake Windermere Cruise – Visit Gretna Green Today, we enjoy a stunning journey through the heart of The Lake District on board a historic 'steamer' and heritage railway. Later, we proceed to Windermere & we take a cruise on Lake Windermere: England’s largest lake. Next, we proceed to the town of Gretna Green and have some free time in the city., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Edinburgh – Visit the Edinburgh Castle – Johny Walker Experience Today, we drive to Edinburgh. On arrival, enjoy a Guided city tour of Edinburgh, visit the Edinburgh castle, and see the Scottish Parliament and many more interesting sights. Next, we visit the Johny Walker Experience in Scotland’s capital city. In the evening, you have some free time at Princess Street., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Aberdeen, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Photo stop at Kelpies – Guided City Tour of Aberdeen Today we check out and proceed to Falkirk, for a photo stop at The Kelpies – a 30-meter-high horse head sculpture which is a monument to honor Scotland’s horse-powered industrial heritage. Next, we drive to Aberdeen, known for its beach front, where we spend some time on the esplanade. On Arrival, enjoy a Guided Tour of Aberdeen Admire Aberdeen's incredible silver granite architecture as you wander through its beautiful, cobbled streets., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Strathclyde, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fort Augustus – Loch Ness Cruise Today, we drive to Fort Augustus, famous for spectacular views down Loch Ness and it is a paradise for keen walkers. Next, we proceed for a cruise on the mighty Loch Ness one of the largest lochs in Scotland and famous for the tale of the Loch Ness monster. Later, we take a photo stop at Three Sister View Point., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Belfast, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Ferry to Belfast – Visit to Titanic Exhibition - Visit the Botanic Gardens – Guided city Tour of Belfast Today, we proceed to the Cairnryan Ferry port to take a ferry to Belfast. On arrival, we visit the Titanic Exhibition. Later, we visit the Botanical Gardens. In the evening, we enjoy a guided city tour of Belfast., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Belfast, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Tour the sights of one of the world-famous Television series - Game of Thrones Today, we enjoy a full day tour of the sites and locations of the world famous Television Series - Game of Thrones. Visit the Dark Hedges, these trees are in an amazing formation and are well worth a photograph. This avenue of trees is known to series fans as the Kings Road. Also, we visit the Downhill beach. Next, we visit the Giant’s Causeway which is a UNESCO world heritage site. These Hexagonal rocks were formed by volcanic eruptions over 50 million years ago. Later, we drive back to Belfast and enjoy some free time in the city centre., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Galway, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City tour of Galway Today, we drive to Galway and proceed for a Guided City tour: a harbour city on Ireland’s west coast, sits where the River Corrib meets the Atlantic Ocean. The city’s hub is 18th-century Eyre Square, a popular meeting spot surrounded by shops and traditional pubs that often offer live Irish folk music., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Dublin, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: See the famous Cliffs of Moher Today, we proceed to see the famous Cliffs of Moher: renowned for their rugged beauty, dramatic cliffsides, and diverse birdlife, including puffins, gannets, and guillemots. They have been featured in numerous films., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 14 - Dublin, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided Tour of Dublin – Entrance to Trinity College – Visit Guinness Storehouse Today, enjoy a guided city tour of Dublin including entrance to Trinity College. Later, we do the Guinness Storehouse Brewery tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 15 - Dublin, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 458048.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n02 nights in Holiday inn express Belfast Queens Quarter or similar in Belfast\n02 nights at Roganstown Hotel / Rochestown Lodge Hotel or similar in Dublin\n, \n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton / Holiday inn Express in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast, Northern Ireland.\n01 night at Hotel Lough Rea Hotel & Spa or similar in Galway, Republic of Ireland.\n02 nights at Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin, Republic of Ireland.\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Tea and Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches.\n14 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches if applicable will be Jain / Vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements: UK + Ireland visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of GBP 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 15 Days, the total Tips amount is GBP 45 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as 15th November,2022 .Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeings: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. There are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided. General: In case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in GBP only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in GBP out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: ENGLAND Guided City Tour of London Visit the Tower of London – see the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond Enjoy a Ride on the London Eye Visit the Lords Cricket Ground in London Visit Windsor Castle Guided Tour of Oxford Visit Stonehenge Orientation tour of Bath with a visit to Roman Bath Visit Shakespeare birthplace Visit Manchester City Football Stadium Enjoy a scenic cruise on Lake Windermere SCOTLAND Visit Gretna Green Guided City Tour of Edinburgh Visit the Edinburgh Castle Enjoy a Johnnie Walker Experience in Edinburgh Photo stop at Kelpies in Falkirk Guided Tour of Aberdeen Enjoy Loch Ness Cruise Visit Fort Augustus NORTHERN IRELAND Visit to Titanic Exhibition Visit the Botanical Gardens Guided city tour of Belfast Tour the sights of the World-Famous Television Series - Game of Thrones Visit Giant’s Causeway REPUBLIC OF IRELAND Guided City tour of Galway See the Cliffs of Moher Guided city tour of Dublin with Entrance to Trinity College Entrance to Guinness Storehouse.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE808', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Uk Delights With Ireland (Winter)' package is a 15-day tour covering London, Birmingham, Manchester, Strathclyde, Aberdeen, Belfast, Dublin, and Galway. This extensive itinerary features guided city tours of London, Edinburgh, Aberdeen, Belfast, Dublin, and Galway, alongside visits to iconic landmarks like the Tower of London, Windsor Castle, Stonehenge, the Roman Baths, Shakespeare's birthplace, and the Manchester City Football Stadium. Travelers will also enjoy scenic cruises on Lake Windermere and Loch Ness, explore Edinburgh Castle, experience the Johnnie Walker Experience, and see the Kelpies in Falkirk. The journey continues with a visit to the Titanic Exhibition, a tour of Game of Thrones filming locations, and a trip to the Giant’s Causeway in Northern Ireland, before concluding in the Republic of Ireland with visits to the breathtaking Cliffs of Moher, Trinity College, and the famous Guinness Storehouse.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to London!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check–in. \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nTower of London – Guided City Tour of London – Ride on London Eye – Lords Cricket Ground\nToday, we proceed to the Tower of London to see the crown jewels of the British Royal family including the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond. Next, we enjoy a ride on the London Eye. Later, we proceed for a Guided city tour of London: See the Buckingham Palace, Hyde Park, Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, Houses of Parliament, Trafalgar Square, Tower Bridge and Thames River. Also, enjoy a guided tour of Lord’s Cricket Ground and relive the historic moments.\n\xa0\nNote: On days when Lord’s Cricket Ground is not available, the group will visit alternate stadium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or\xa0similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Windsor Castle – Guided Tour of Oxford\nToday, we drive to Windsor for a visit of the famous Windsor Castle – Queen Elizabeth II’s favorite weekend home. Next, we proceed to Oxford and enjoy a guided walking tour of Oxford, famous for its ancient university, beautiful buildings and iconic “Dreaming Spires”. Later in the evening, you have some free time for shopping at Bicester Village.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or\xa0similar in London (LHR Area),\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Stonehenge – Orientation tour of Bath with a visit to a Roman Bath\nToday, we proceed to visit the famous Stonehenge: an ancient and mysterious monument with a sophisticated architectural design, its astronomical alignments, and its mystery of purpose. Next, we drive to Bath for an Orientation tour and we visit a Roman Bath: well-preserved thermae in the city of Bath.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Hampton by Hilton / Holiday inn Express in Birmingham, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Shakespeare Birthplace at Stratford Upon Avon - Visit Manchester City Football Stadium\nToday, we drive to Stratford upon Avon for an Orientation tour and we Visit Shakespeare's Birthplace to walk in Shakespeare's footsteps and explore the house he was born in. Later we proceed to visit the famous Manchester City Football Stadium. Visit the home changing room, sit in the dugout & run down the tunnel which leads to the football field.\nNote: On days when Manchester City Stadium is not available, the group will visit any alternate stadium.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nLake Windermere Cruise – Visit Gretna Green\nToday, we enjoy a stunning\xa0journey\xa0through the heart of The Lake District on board a historic 'steamer' and heritage\xa0railway. Later, we proceed to Windermere & we take a cruise on Lake Windermere: England’s largest lake. Next, we proceed to the town of Gretna Green and have some free time in the city.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Edinburgh – Visit the Edinburgh Castle – Johny Walker Experience\nToday, we drive to Edinburgh. On arrival, enjoy a Guided city tour of Edinburgh, visit the Edinburgh castle, and see the Scottish Parliament and many more interesting sights. Next, we visit the Johny Walker Experience in Scotland’s capital city. In the evening, you have some free time at Princess Street.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell,\xa0United Kingdom'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0\nPhoto stop at Kelpies – Guided City Tour of Aberdeen\nToday we check out and proceed to Falkirk, for a photo stop at The Kelpies – a 30-meter-high horse head sculpture which is a monument to honor Scotland’s horse-powered industrial heritage. Next, we drive to Aberdeen, known for its beach front, where we spend some time on the esplanade. On Arrival, enjoy a Guided Tour of Aberdeen Admire Aberdeen's incredible\xa0silver granite architecture\xa0as you wander through its beautiful, cobbled streets.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nFort Augustus – Loch Ness Cruise\nToday, we drive to Fort Augustus, famous for spectacular views down Loch Ness and it is a paradise for keen walkers. Next, we proceed for a cruise on the mighty Loch Ness one of the largest lochs in Scotland and famous for the tale of the Loch Ness monster. Later, we take a photo stop at Three Sister View Point.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Strathclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nFerry to Belfast – Visit to Titanic Exhibition - Visit the Botanic Gardens – Guided city Tour of Belfast\nToday, we proceed to the Cairnryan Ferry port to take a ferry to Belfast. On arrival, we visit the Titanic Exhibition. Later, we visit the Botanical Gardens. In the evening, we enjoy a guided city tour of Belfast.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast, Northern Ireland'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nTour the sights of one of the world-famous Television series - Game of Thrones \nToday, we enjoy a full day tour of the sites and locations of the world famous Television Series - Game of Thrones. Visit the Dark Hedges, these trees are in an amazing formation and are well worth a photograph. This avenue of trees is known to series fans as the Kings Road. Also, we visit the Downhill beach. Next, we visit the Giant’s Causeway which is a UNESCO world heritage site. These Hexagonal rocks were formed by volcanic eruptions over 50 million years ago. Later, we drive back to Belfast and enjoy some free time in the city centre.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast,\xa0Northern Ireland'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City tour of Galway\nToday, we drive to Galway and proceed for a Guided City tour: a harbour city on Ireland’s west coast, sits where the River Corrib meets the Atlantic Ocean. The city’s hub is 18th-century Eyre Square, a popular meeting spot surrounded by shops and traditional pubs that often offer live Irish folk music.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Lough Rea Hotel & Spa or similar in Galway, Republic of Ireland'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nSee the famous Cliffs of Moher\nToday, we proceed to see the famous Cliffs of Moher: renowned for their rugged beauty, dramatic cliffsides, and diverse birdlife, including puffins, gannets, and guillemots. They have been featured in numerous films.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin, Republic of Ireland'}, {'day': 14, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided Tour of Dublin – Entrance to Trinity College – Visit Guinness Storehouse\nToday, enjoy a guided city tour of Dublin including entrance to Trinity College. Later, we do the Guinness Storehouse Brewery tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin,\xa0Republic of Ireland'}, {'day': 15, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n02 nights in Holiday inn express Belfast Queens Quarter or similar in Belfast\n02 nights at Roganstown Hotel / Rochestown Lodge Hotel or similar in Dublin\n', '\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton / Holiday inn Express in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast, Northern Ireland.\n01 night at Hotel Lough Rea Hotel & Spa or similar in Galway, Republic of Ireland.\n02 nights at Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin, Republic of Ireland.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n03 nights at Hotel Radisson LHR / Courtyard LHR or similar in London (Heathrow area)\xa0\n01 night at Hotel AC / Leonardo or similar in Manchester\xa0\n01 night at Hotel at Hotel Gretna hall or similar in Gretna / Carlisle\n02 nights at Hotel at Hotel Alona /\xa0 Holiday inn express or similar in Glasgow / Strathclyde\nOR\n02 nights in Holiday inn express Belfast Queens Quarter or similar in Belfast\n02 nights at Roganstown Hotel / Rochestown Lodge Hotel or similar in Dublin\n', '1': '\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton / Holiday inn Express in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast, Northern Ireland.\n01 night at Hotel Lough Rea Hotel & Spa or similar in Galway, Republic of Ireland.\n02 nights at Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin, Republic of Ireland.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': '44', 'countryName': 'Scotland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GB', 'countryName': 'United Kingdom', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IE', 'countryName': 'Ireland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 458000.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights at Hotel Courtyard by Marriott / Radisson Red or similar in London (LHR Area), United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Hampton by Hilton / Holiday inn Express in Birmingham, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hampton by Hilton Manchester or similar in Manchester, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Aloft / Hilton Aberdeen TECA or similar in Aberdeen, United Kingdom.\n01 night at Hotel Alona / Hotel Hampton by Hilton or similar in Starthclyde / Motherwell, United Kingdom.\n02 nights at Hotel Holiday Inn Express or similar in Belfast, Northern Ireland.\n01 night at Hotel Lough Rea Hotel & Spa or similar in Galway, Republic of Ireland.\n02 nights at Hotel Rogens Town / Roches Town or similar in Dublin, Republic of Ireland.\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Tea and Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches.\n14 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners.\n\nNote: Packed lunches if applicable will be Jain / Vegetarian. In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', "England:\n\nGuided City Tour of London\nVisit the Tower of London – see the famous Koh-i-Noor Diamond\nEnjoy a Ride on the London Eye\xa0\nVisit the Lords Cricket Ground in London\nVisit Windsor Castle\nGuided Tour of Oxford\nVisit Stonehenge\xa0\nOrientation tour of Bath with a visit to a Roman Bath\xa0\nVisit Shakespeare birthplace\nVisit Manchester City Football Stadium\nEnjoy a scenic cruise on Lake Windermere\xa0\n\nScotland:\n\nVisit Gretna Green\nGuided City Tour of Edinburgh\xa0\nVisit the Edinburgh Castle\xa0\nEnjoy a Johnnie Walker Experience in Edinburgh\nPhoto stop at Kelpies in Falkirk\nGuided Tour of Aberdeen\nEnjoy Loch Ness Cruise\nVisit Fort Augustus\n\nNorthern Ireland:\n\nVisit to Titanic Exhibition\nVisit the Botanical Gardens \xa0\nGuided city tour of Belfast\nTour the sights of the World-Famous Television Series - Game of Thrones\nVisit Giant's Causeway\n\nRepublic Of Ireland:\n\nGuided City tour of Galway\nSee the Cliffs of Moher\nGuided city tour of Dublin with Entrance to Trinity College\nVisit The Irish National Stud and Gardens in Kildare\nEntrance to Guinness Storehouse\n"], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0 \nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0 \nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nUK + Ireland visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of GBP 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 15 Days, the total Tips amount is GBP 45 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as 15th November,2022 .Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\xa0\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot.\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain Days packed lunch will be provided.\xa0\n\nSightseeings:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThere are a few attractions and entrances that are currently closed due to COVID and in case the same remain closed at the time of the groups visiting, a refund will be provided.\xa0\n\nGeneral:\n\nIn case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses\xa0 to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”.\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in GBP only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in GBP out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/Stonehenge_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/25422_London_Tower_Bridge_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/78202_Westminster_Parliament_London_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Oxford_new_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Stonehenge-753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Shakespeares_Birthplace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Lake_Windermere.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/753_EdinburghCastle.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/kelpies_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Loch_Ness_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/BelfastCity7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Kingsroad_Belfast.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Galway_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Galway.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/TrinityCollege_Dublin.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015160/itinerary/Dublin_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014760', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014760', 'availableMonths': ['march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Mar 2027)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tromso', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stokmarknes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Narvik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kiruna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rovaniemi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG009291_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 475986, 'packageSummary': "The 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Mar 2027)' package is a spectacular 9-day tour that takes travelers through the magical winter landscapes of Stokmarknes, Tromso, Helsinki, Kiruna, Narvik, and Rovaniemi. This unforgettable Arctic journey is packed with bucket-list experiences, including chasing the mesmerizing Northern Lights, exploring vibrant Nordic cities, and crossing the Arctic Circle. Participants will enjoy a diverse range of key highlights such as scenic train journeys, traditional husky and reindeer sledding adventures, visits to Santa Claus Village, and immersive cultural tours that showcase the unique heritage and breathtaking natural beauty of Lapland and Scandinavia.", 'images': ['Tromso_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Northern_Lights_Tromso_753_Adobe.jpg', 'ArcticDay3.jpg', 'ArcticDay4.jpg', 'ArcticDay5.jpg', 'Rovaniemi2.jpg', 'Romaniemi_7534.jpg', 'Helsinki_View_753.jpg', 'Helsinki1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 475986, 'thumbnailImage': 'Arctic2673.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014760 is named 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Mar 2027)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tromso, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Tromso! The Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local representative will meet you outside the airport. Proceed to the hotel and check–in. Spend some free time on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tromso, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Tromso - Fjellheisn Cable Car – Northern Lights Hunting Tour Today, we proceed for an orientation tour of Tromsø known for its role as a gateway to the Arctic. Next, we take a cable car to Fjellheisen and enjoy a spectacular view of Tromsø and its beautiful surroundings from above. Later in the evening, we proceed on a Northern Lights Hunting Tour. Tromsø is famous for being one of the best places in the world to see the Northern Lights., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Stokmarknes, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Polaria - Express Ferry to Harstad Today, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Narvik, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Sea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum Today, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today. Next, we proceed to Narvik., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kiruna, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda Today, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Arktikum Musuem – Northern Lights Hunting tour Today, we proceed to Rovaniemi: Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus. Upon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Rovaniemi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Santa Claus Village - Visit Husky Farm Today, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later, we arrive at a husky dog farm. On arrival at the husky kennel you will be welcomed by eager, but friendly barking, as these dogs are keen to get going! This adventurous safari through the Lappish wilderness takes you on a fun journey with friendly husky dogs who truly love running., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Fly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church Today, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Return back home with pleasant memories! Today, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give us your suggestions. Till we meet again! Note: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 475986.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n, \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n03 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., Breakfast Included, \nDaily Continental buffet breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n05 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n02 Local Lunches\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / Non-vegetarian Dinners\n03 Local Dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 01st Feb 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g. Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of Euro 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour which is 9 Days, the total Tips amount is Euros 27 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 01st Feb, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that what is mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: AIRLINE AND AIRFARE The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 01st June, 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. HOTELS All hotels will be either around the airport area or in the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. Double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. COACHES Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. MEALS Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed lunch will be provided. SIGHTSEEING On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. GENERAL In case any member of the group tests positive for COVID-19, customers will need to unconditionally abide, adhere and comply solely at your costs and expenses to all laws, rules, notifications, Travel advisories, guidelines, directives and communications issued from time to time by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad, related to your tour to the foreign destination and/or on your return from the tour to your home destination in India or Abroad including but not limited to Covid-19 Protocols on quarantine, vaccinations etc. or in connection with any other Pandemic, epidemic, disease, condition etc., which may be communicated by all or any Governments, Authorities, Ministries, Departments, Local Bodies in India or Abroad with or without notice at any point of time whether at the commencement of the tour, during the tour and/or on the completion of the tour, as the case may be”. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPE211', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Arctic Delights - Northern Lights Special (Mar 2027)' package is a spectacular 9-day tour that takes travelers through the magical winter landscapes of Stokmarknes, Tromso, Helsinki, Kiruna, Narvik, and Rovaniemi. This unforgettable Arctic journey is packed with bucket-list experiences, including chasing the mesmerizing Northern Lights, exploring vibrant Nordic cities, and crossing the Arctic Circle. Participants will enjoy a diverse range of key highlights such as scenic train journeys, traditional husky and reindeer sledding adventures, visits to Santa Claus Village, and immersive cultural tours that showcase the unique heritage and breathtaking natural beauty of Lapland and Scandinavia.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome to Tromso!\nThe Tour Manager / Station Manager / Local representative will meet you outside the airport. Proceed to the hotel and check–in. Spend some free time on your own.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation tour of Tromso - Fjellheisn Cable Car – Northern Lights Hunting Tour \nToday, we proceed for an orientation tour of Tromsø known for its role as a gateway to the Arctic. Next, we take a cable car to Fjellheisen and enjoy a spectacular view of Tromsø and its beautiful surroundings from above. Later in the evening, we proceed on a Northern Lights Hunting Tour. Tromsø is famous for being one of the best places in the world to see the Northern Lights.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Polaria - Express Ferry to Harstad\nToday, we visit Polaria – an Arctic Experience and the perfect place to meet and understand life in the Arctic. Later, we board an Express Ferry to Harstad. On arrival we board the coach and proceed to Stokmarknes. Located in the traditional region of Vesterålen at the northern end of the incredible Raftsundet strait, this is the place where, in 1893, Richard With founded the company that would develop into Hurtigruten.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSea Eagle Safari to Trollfjord by Rib Boat - Visit Hutigruten Museum\nToday, we proceed on an exciting rib-boat safari to Trollfjord. Located in an area with high peaks up to 1100 meters, with glaciers on the tops and beautiful waterfalls that end you can only get to this magnificent fjord by boat. Trollfjord has been photographed, filmed, and painted countless times over the years. When you experience it, you understand why. You have the chance to spot the magnificent white tailed sea eagles here. Next we return to Stokmarknes and visit the Hurtigruten museum. Walking along the waterfront of Stokmarknes, you can’t miss the big, bold, box-shaped building of glass, gleaming in the sunlight. As you draw closer, you’ll see that encased within is a full-sized ship - the MS Finnmarken from 1956. This is Hurtigrutemuseet, a modern museum that honours The Coastal Express and takes the form of a massive ship in a bottle. Enjoy a local meal on board the MS Finnmarken. Protected and preserved, MS Finnmarken houses paraphernalia, archives, photographs, and exhibitions that chronicle the stories of the many people who have made The Coastal Express the icon it is today.\xa0 Next, we proceed to Narvik.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Narvik War Museum - Visit the Ice Hotel with lunch – Visit Nuti Sami Silda\nToday, we visit the Narvik War Meseum: Narvik and the surrounding area were the scene of some of the most dramatic events of World War II. The Narvik War Museum tells many of the stories about the war and occupation and the human consequences. Later, we proceed to Jukkasjarvi and visit the Ice Hotel Jukkasjärvi and experience a local meal inside the ice hotel. Next, we visit Nuti Sami Silda, to experience a close, genuine and thorough insight into the Sami culture and its traditions. The Sami guides describe and demonstrate the everyday life in reindeer herder, the nomadic lifestyle, and how the old traditions are being preserved. Later, proceed to Kiruna.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Arktikum Musuem – Northern Lights Hunting tour \nToday, we proceed to Rovaniemi: Located in the Finnish Lapland – this magical place is also the home of Santa Claus.\nUpon arrival we visit the Arktikum Museum where they bring arctic nature, cultures, and history close to you. Later in the evening we proceed for Northern Lights Hunting tour for peak viewing opportunities.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Visit Santa Claus Village - Visit Husky Farm\nToday, we visit the most awaited place - Santa Claus Village. Santa Claus spends his time at the Santa Claus Village every day of the year to take care of his mission in life of spreading joy and happiness. Later, we arrive at a husky dog farm. On arrival at the husky kennel you will be welcomed by eager, but friendly barking, as these dogs are keen to get going! This adventurous safari through the Lappish wilderness takes you on a fun journey with friendly husky dogs who truly love running.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Helsinki – Guided tour of Helsinki – Visit Temppeliaukio – Rock Church\nToday, drive to the airport to take the flight back to Helsinki. In Helsinki - proceed on a guided city tour of Helsinki. See the important parts of Helsinki – the Presidential Palace, the Lutheran Church, Senate Square, Opera House and the Sibelius Park. Next, we visit the Temppeliaukio – Rock Church', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nReturn back home with pleasant memories!\nToday, we check out and drive to the airport for your flight back home. It’s time to say goodbye to all the new friends you have made. We hope you take back many happy memories of your holiday. If you could spare a few minutes, please write and tell us how you enjoyed your holiday and give\xa0us your suggestions. Till we meet again!\xa0\n\xa0\nNote: In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 night at Scandic / Arctic / Original Sokos or similar in Rovaniemi, Finland.\n01 night at Scandic Grand Marina / Scandic Park or similar in Helsinki, Finland.\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy / Scandic / Clarion or similar in Tromso, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic or similar in Stokmarknes / Sortland, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Quality / Scandic / Thon or similar in Narvik, Norway.\n01 night at Hotel Scandic Kiruna / Best Western Eden or similar in Kiruna, Sweden.\n02 nights at Scandi