f USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nImportant Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/Disneyland_4.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/Paris_CITY_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/Eiffeltowerwithseinecruise_753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/VersaillesPalace_new_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/DisneylandParis.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/Disneylandparis2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014521/itinerary/29117_Paris_View_France_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014546', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014546', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Serene Swiss', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central / Southern Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zermatt', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zermatt', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zermatt', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014546_0_20260916155417.pdf', 'price': 184062, 'packageSummary': "The 'Serene Swiss' package is a 7-day tour covering Central / Southern Switzerland and Zermatt. The itinerary includes breathtaking views of the iconic Matterhorn, scenic train journeys through the Swiss Alps, and leisurely walks through charming alpine villages. Participants will enjoy guided sightseeing tours, cable car rides to stunning mountain peaks, and opportunities to experience the tranquil beauty of pristine lakes and valleys.", 'images': ['Zurich_1.jpg', '89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'Glacier_3000_753.jpg', 'Zermatt.jpg', 'ZermattSwitzerland.jpg', 'Montreux.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 184062, 'thumbnailImage': 'Zurich_2.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014546 is named 'Serene Swiss' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zurich Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Zurich airport, you will walk across to the Flughafen station (located adjacent to the airport) for your train to Central Switzerland. From train station transfer on your own to the hotel. Local Sightseeing (Optional): Explore Lucerne with a Swiss Pass. Discover Lucerne’s highlights within walking distance, including the iconic Chapel Bridge and Water Tower – Switzerland’s most photographed landmark. Zurich Airport Observation Deck (Optional): Stop by before your shuttle for close-up views of aircraft. Deck B: Public area with insights into airport operations. Deck E: Free for passengers with boarding pass. Lindt Home of Chocolate (Optional): Enjoy an interactive chocolate tour, the world’s largest Lindt shop (500 m²), and a spectacular chocolate fountain. Stoos Funicular Adventure (Optional): Ride the world’s steepest funicular (110% gradient) to Stoos village. Free with Swiss Half Fare Card. Swiss National Museum, Zurich (Optional): Explore Swiss history in a modern extension behind century-old walls. Discounted with Swiss Half Fare Card. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Mt. Titlis Excursion Mt. Titlis Excursion: Don't miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier's deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe's highest suspension bridge. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Jungfraujoch Excursion Jungfraujoch Excursion: Don't miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world-famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Central / Southern Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity) Glacier 3000 (Optional): Escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Optional Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer – including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks – Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland. Bollywood Tour (Optional): Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Zermatt, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Central / Southern Swiss To Zermatt Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Zermatt with Swiss Pass. Upon arrival at Zermatt train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Zermatt, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zermatt - Matterhorn Mt. Matterhorn Excursion: The Matterhorn – mystical, majestic, the mountain of mountains. No one can escape its fascination. Neither locals nor guests. Triangular. A cragged rock “tooth” ranging into the heavens. Standing alone on the horizon. A magnet for alpinists, aesthetic emblem, mountain with ideal proportions. Rugged rock with magical light.There are a wide variety of different attractions to be discovered around the Matterhorn. A top excursion is Gornergrat. On this three-thousand metre mountain ridge there is a viewing platform with a truly unforgettable view of the Matterhorn and the surrounding mountain world. Our if you prefer, the Matterhorn can also be admired from the Rothorn. The Matterhorn glacier paradise is the highest summer ski region in Europe and is open 365 days a year. And there is still plenty to do when the sun isn’t shining! The Matterhorn Museum explains the historic development of Zermatt from a mountain village to an Alpine holiday resort and also has many photographs and facts about the first ascent of the Matterhorn., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Zermatt, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Montreux Transfers: Make you way to the Montreux train station to go to the Airport for your journey back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 184062.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nZermatt\n\n\nSchlosshotel Zermatt | Tradition Julen Hotel | Hotel Daniela | Best Western Plus Alpen | Hotel Ambassador or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nZermatt\n\n\nHotel Continental | Excelsior | Jagerhof - Hotel & Apartements | Testa Grigia / Walliserhof Zermatt | Hotel Butterfly, Bw Signature Collection or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 4 Nights’ accommodation in Central / Southern Switzerland based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Zermatt based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] Swiss Pass 8 Days Consecutive Saver Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Mt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Jungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass Zermatt: Mt Matterhorn Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms And Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Serene Swiss' package is a 7-day tour covering Central / Southern Switzerland and Zermatt. The itinerary includes breathtaking views of the iconic Matterhorn, scenic train journeys through the Swiss Alps, and leisurely walks through charming alpine villages. Participants will enjoy guided sightseeing tours, cable car rides to stunning mountain peaks, and opportunities to experience the tranquil beauty of pristine lakes and valleys.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Zurich\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Zurich airport, you will walk across to the Flughafen station (located adjacent to the airport) for your train to Central Switzerland. From train station transfer on your own to the hotel.\n\xa0\nLocal Sightseeing (Optional): Explore Lucerne with a Swiss Pass. Discover Lucerne’s highlights within walking distance, including the iconic Chapel Bridge and Water Tower – Switzerland’s most photographed landmark.\xa0\n\xa0\nZurich Airport Observation Deck (Optional): Stop by before your shuttle for close-up views of aircraft. Deck B: Public area with insights into airport operations. Deck E: Free for passengers with boarding pass.\n\xa0\nLindt Home of Chocolate (Optional): Enjoy an interactive chocolate tour, the world’s largest Lindt shop (500 m²), and a spectacular chocolate fountain.\n\xa0\nStoos Funicular Adventure (Optional): Ride the world’s steepest funicular (110% gradient) to Stoos village. Free with Swiss Half Fare Card.\n\xa0\nSwiss National Museum, Zurich (Optional): Explore Swiss history in a modern extension behind century-old walls. Discounted with Swiss Half Fare Card.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus Hertenstein (Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nMt. Titlis Excursion\n\xa0\nMt. Titlis Excursion: Don't miss the spectacular beauty of Mt Titlis! Discover eternal glaciers and other attractions from more than 3020m / 10000 ft high. Enjoy the spectacular sight of the glacier's deep crevasses and gigantic ice boulders from the revolving cable car ROTAIR. At the top of Mt. Titlis (10'000 ft. above sea level), a high alpine panorama awaits you. Visit the Ice Grotto or take a ride with the chairlift IceFlyer, which brings you close to the crevasses. Enjoy also the FunLift in the snow and the Cliff Walk, Europe's highest suspension bridge. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus Hertenstein (Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nJungfraujoch Excursion\n\xa0\nJungfraujoch Excursion: Don't miss the highlight of any Swiss holiday and go for this thrilling and unforgettable excursion to Jungfraujoch, Top of Europe! From Interlaken, the heart of the Jungfrau region mountain world and uniquely situated between two lakes, you make your way to famous mountain resort Grindelwald where you board the cogwheel train for a spectacular ride via Kleine Scheidegg to Jungfraujoch. Enjoy stunning views of the world-famous triple peaks of Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau accompany you all the way to the top. (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus Hertenstein (Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nCentral Switzerland Day At Leisure (Optional Activity)\n\xa0\nGlacier 3000 (Optional): Escape to the high Alps to breath a fresh air and spectacular mountain vistas on the Glacier 3000 (Optional Mountain Excursion). Glacier 3000, located at the highest point of the Vaudois Alps, is open all year round for winter activities for all! With its stunning views and wide range of activities on offer – including the Peak Walk, a unique suspension bridge linking two mountain peaks – Glacier 3000 is a must for your holidays in Switzerland.\n\xa0\nBollywood Tour (Optional): Gstaad region is known as one of the most scenic natural film sets in the world. Many Bollywood blockbusters have been filmed here, such as DDLJ “Bachana Ae Haseenno” and many more. Lunch can be included on this tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel La Pergola (Standard) /\xa0Campus Hertenstein (Value) or similar in\xa0Central / Southern Switzerland'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nCentral / Southern Swiss To Zermatt Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Zermatt with Swiss Pass.\xa0\nUpon arrival at Zermatt train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Continental\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Schlosshotel\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Zermatt'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nZermatt - Matterhorn\n\xa0\nMt. Matterhorn Excursion:\xa0 The Matterhorn – mystical, majestic, the mountain of mountains. No one can escape its fascination. Neither locals nor guests. Triangular. A cragged rock “tooth” ranging into the heavens. Standing alone on the horizon. A magnet for alpinists, aesthetic emblem, mountain with ideal proportions. Rugged rock with magical light.There are a wide variety of different attractions to be discovered around the Matterhorn. A top excursion is Gornergrat. On this three-thousand metre mountain ridge there is a viewing platform with a truly unforgettable view of the Matterhorn and the surrounding mountain world. Our if you prefer, the Matterhorn can also be admired from the Rothorn. The Matterhorn glacier paradise is the highest summer ski region in Europe and is open 365 days a year. And there is still plenty to do when the sun isn’t shining! The Matterhorn Museum explains the historic development of Zermatt from a mountain village to an Alpine holiday resort and also has many photographs and facts about the first ascent of the Matterhorn.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Continental\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Schlosshotel\xa0(Value) or similar in\xa0Zermatt'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Montreux\n\xa0\nTransfers: Make you way to the Montreux train station to go to the Airport for your journey back home.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nZermatt\n\n\nSchlosshotel Zermatt | Tradition Julen Hotel | Hotel Daniela | Best Western Plus Alpen | Hotel Ambassador or similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nLa Pergola | Ibis Styles Bern City | Prizeotel Bern-city | Jardin | Sorell Hotel Ador or similar\n\n\n\n\nZermatt\n\n\nHotel Continental | Excelsior | Jagerhof - Hotel & Apartements | Testa Grigia / Walliserhof Zermatt | Hotel Butterfly, Bw Signature Collection or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n\nCampus Hotel Hertenstein | Romantik Hotel Beau Rivage - Weggis | Hotel Baren Sigriswil | Hotel Eden Spiez | Seegarten Marina or similar\n\n\n\n\nZermatt\n\n\nSchlosshotel Zermatt | Tradition Julen Hotel | Hotel Daniela | Best Western Plus Alpen | Hotel Ambassador or similar\n\n\n\n', '0': '\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\n\n\nSTANDARD CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nCentral / Southern Switzerland\n\n