April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/Zurich_2.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/Zurich_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/JUNGFRAUJOCH_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/Glacier_3000_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/Zermatt.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/ZermattSwitzerland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014546/itinerary/Montreux.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014783', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014783', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Russia - Northern Lights Special', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Murmansk', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Murmansk', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012573_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 270396, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Russia - Northern Lights Special' package is an 8-day tour covering Moscow, St. Petersburg, and Murmansk. The itinerary includes exploring iconic landmarks such as Moscow's Red Square and the Kremlin, admiring the grand architecture and canals of St. Petersburg, and embarking on an unforgettable quest to witness the breathtaking Aurora Borealis in Murmansk. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, cultural excursions, and unique Arctic experiences in the Russian wilderness.", 'images': ['89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'Moscow-Red-square.jpg', 'Murmansk-1.jpg', 'Murmansk-Lapland.jpg', 'Saint-Petersburg.jpg', 'Saint-Petersburg-Kazan-Cathedral.jpg', '007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'MoscowRussia7534.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 270396, 'thumbnailImage': 'Petersburg_SRP.png', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014783 is named 'Highlights Of Russia - Northern Lights Special' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Moscow, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Moscow! Welcome to Moscow - the capital and the largest city of Russia. On arrival, you will be met by your Tour Manager / Local Representative outside the custom area who will welcome you and take you to your hotel for check-in. The evening is free at leisure. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Moscow – Sparrow hill Cable car - Metro Tour – Russian Circus Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Moscow: Visit the Red Square, see the St. Basil’s Cathedral, the White House and Christ the Saviour Cathedral. What’s more! Enjoy unique views of the iconic buildings in Moscow from the cable car which connects the two banks of the Moskva-river and has shortly become a new hallmark of the city. Next, we visit the Metro station of Moscow often called 'The People's Palaces', for their elegant designs, lavish and profuse use of marble, mosaics, sculptures and chandeliers. Later this evening be captivated by the performances at the traditional Russian circus., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Murmansk, Meals: Breakfast and Local Dinner, Description: Fly to Murmansk – Northern Lights Tour Today, take flight to Murmansk, known as the Russian Lapland. On arrival check in to the hotel. Tonight, we experience the Northern Lights phenomenon. Ride around the surroundings of Murmansk to observe the auroras. We will take you to several different spots to give you the best chance to see to chase the northern lights. (Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Northern Lights, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Northern Lights tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the lights)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Murmansk, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Visit Saami Village – Orientation Tour of Murmansk Today, visit the Saami village and experience the popular Saami show. Here you get the opportunity to interact feed the Reindeers and Siberian Huskies. Later, proceed to enjoy Husky Dog Sleigh and Snowmobile Ride in the snow. Then we drive back to Murmansk for an orientation tour with a photo stop at Lenin Ice Breaker Museum. Note: Activities may vary depending on Snow Conditions., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - St Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly to St Petersburg – Guided City Tour of St Petersburg Today we fly to St Petersburg. On arrival procced for guided city tour of St. Petersburg city, see Issac's Cathedral, The Peter and Paul Fortress. Later visit Kazan cathedral., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - St Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Hermitage Museum – Grand Maket (Russia in Miniature) Today, visit the iconic Hermitage Museum, famous for holding nearly three million items dating from the Stone Age to the present, including many masterpieces by Renaissance Italian and Baroque Dutch, Flemish, and French painters. Later, visit the Grand Maket; a private museum showcasing the largest miniature model of Russia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Train to Moscow Today, we check out and proceed to the railway station to board the train onto Moscow. On arrival check in to the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! After continental breakfast, we transfer you to the airport. Board your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: - In capital city like Moscow & St Petersburg, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. 'As Northern lights is a natural phenomenon, spotting the same is subject to weather conditions and luck.', GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 270396.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n, \n02 Nights in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow \n02 Nights in Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk \n02 Nights in Park Inn Pulkovskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 Night in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n01 Local Lunch.\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n02 Local Dinners.\xa0\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., \nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st Mar 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Russian visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 8 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 24 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st Mar 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers. Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st May 2024. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 14 – 16 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, the hotel in Paris may be in the outskirts of the city and may attract an extra surcharge. (1st July, 2024 – 31st September, 2024). Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain Days packed meals will be provided. Sightseeings: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4 - 5 hours in the queue. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Russia - Northern Lights Special' package is an 8-day tour covering Moscow, St. Petersburg, and Murmansk. The itinerary includes exploring iconic landmarks such as Moscow's Red Square and the Kremlin, admiring the grand architecture and canals of St. Petersburg, and embarking on an unforgettable quest to witness the breathtaking Aurora Borealis in Murmansk. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, cultural excursions, and unique Arctic experiences in the Russian wilderness.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Moscow!\nWelcome to Moscow - the capital and the largest city of Russia. On arrival, you will be met by your Tour Manager / Local Representative outside the custom area who will welcome you and take you to your hotel for check-in. The evening is free at leisure.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided city tour of Moscow – Sparrow hill Cable car - Metro Tour – Russian Circus\nToday, we proceed for a guided city tour of Moscow: Visit the Red Square, see the St. Basil’s Cathedral, the White House and Christ the Saviour Cathedral. What’s more! Enjoy unique views of the iconic buildings in Moscow from the cable car which connects the two banks of the Moskva-river and has shortly become a new hallmark of the city. Next, we visit the Metro station of Moscow often called 'The People's Palaces', for their elegant designs, lavish and profuse use of marble, mosaics, sculptures and chandeliers. Later this evening be captivated by the performances at the traditional Russian circus.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Murmansk – Northern Lights Tour\nToday, take flight to Murmansk, known as the Russian Lapland. On arrival check in to the hotel. Tonight, we experience the Northern Lights phenomenon. Ride around the surroundings of Murmansk to observe the auroras. We will take you to several different spots to give you the best chance to see to chase the northern lights.\xa0(Although we will do our best to ensure that you view the Northern Lights, it is a natural phenomenon and is not guaranteed. The days of the Northern Lights tour could also change based on the probability of viewing the lights).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Saami Village – Orientation Tour of Murmansk\nToday, visit the Saami village and experience the popular Saami show. Here you get the opportunity to interact feed the Reindeers and Siberian Huskies. Later, proceed to enjoy Husky Dog Sleigh and Snowmobile Ride in the snow. Then we drive back to Murmansk for an orientation tour with a photo stop at Lenin Ice Breaker Museum.\nNote: Activities may vary depending on Snow Conditions.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nFly to St Petersburg – Guided City Tour of St Petersburg\nToday we fly to St Petersburg. On arrival procced for guided city tour of St. Petersburg city, see Issac's Cathedral, The Peter and Paul Fortress. Later visit Kazan cathedral.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Park Inn Pulkovskaya\xa0or Similar in St. Petersburg'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Hermitage Museum – Grand Maket (Russia in Miniature)\nToday, visit the iconic Hermitage Museum, famous for holding nearly three million items dating from the Stone Age to the present, including many masterpieces by Renaissance Italian and Baroque Dutch, Flemish, and French painters. Later, visit the Grand Maket; a private museum showcasing the largest miniature model of Russia.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Park Inn Pulkovskaya\xa0or Similar in St. Petersburg'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTrain to Moscow\nToday, we check out and proceed to the railway station to board the train onto Moscow. On arrival check in to the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nAfter continental breakfast, we transfer you to the airport. Board your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\nNote: - In capital city like Moscow & St Petersburg, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it’s not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n'As Northern lights is a natural phenomenon, spotting the same is subject to weather conditions and luck.'\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n', '\n02 Nights in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow \n02 Nights in Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk \n02 Nights in Park Inn Pulkovskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 Night in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n02 nights at Hotel Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area),France\n01 night at Hotel Ramada Brussels Woulwe or similar in Belgium\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt West\xa0 or similar in Germany \n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n', '1': '\n02 Nights in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow \n02 Nights in Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk \n02 Nights in Park Inn Pulkovskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 Night in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'RU', 'countryName': 'Russia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 270400.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow \n02 Nights in Hotel Azimut or similar in Murmansk \n02 Nights in Park Inn Pulkovskaya or similar in St Petersburg\n01 Night in Holiday Inn Seligerskaya or Similar in Moscow\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental breakfast. (Breakfast includes bread with butter, jam, cereals, juice, milk, tea and coffee)\n01 Local Lunch.\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian dinners.\n02 Local Dinners.\xa0\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.', '\nDaily Continental Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Juice, Milk & Coffee)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non-vegetarian lunches\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners.\n'], 'visa': ['\nRussian visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0\n', 'Visa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen Visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n', '\nAs per itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Paris\n\nGuided City Tour Of Paris\nVisit 2nd Level Of Eiffel Tower\nVisit Disneyland® Paris (Up To 5 Hour Visit)\n\nBelgium:\n\nVisit Mini Europe\nOrientation Tour Of Brussels\n\nGermany:\n\nVisit The Cologne Cathedral\nEnjoy Rhine River Cruise\xa0\xa0\nVisit The Black Forest\xa0\nCuckoo Clock Demonstration\n\nSwitzerland\n\nVisit Mt. Titlis\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Lucerne\nVisit Lindt Home Of Chocolate\xa0\n', 'Moscow\n\nGuided city tour of Moscow\nRide on Metro Tour\xa0\nSparrow Hill cable car ride\xa0\nRussian Circus\n\nMurmansk\n\nNorthern Lights Tour\nVisit Saami Village\nEnjoy Husky Sleigh Ride, Reindeer feeding, Snowmobile ride.\nOrientation tour of Murmansk\n\nSt Petersburg\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\nVisit Kazan Cathedral\nHermitage Museum\xa0\nGrand Maket - Russia in Miniature\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st Mar 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nRussian visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 8 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 24 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st Mar 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers.\nImportant Note:\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st May 2024. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 14 – 16 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nDue to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, the hotel in Paris may be in the outskirts of the city and may attract an extra surcharge. (1st July, 2024 – 31st September, 2024).\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\xa0\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities; as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot.\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain Days packed meals will be provided.\xa0\n\nSightseeings:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4 - 5 hours in the queue.\n\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/Petersburg_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/Moscow-Red-square.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/Murmansk-1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/Murmansk-Lapland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/Saint-Petersburg.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/Saint-Petersburg-Kazan-Cathedral.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014783/itinerary/MoscowRussia7534.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014525', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014525', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Inspiring Italy', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Milan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Milan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Milan', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014525_0_20260916120811.pdf', 'price': 192809, 'packageSummary': "The 'Inspiring Italy' package is a 9-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Rome, Venice, Florence, and Milan. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Colosseum, the Vatican Museums, St. Mark's Square, the Florence Cathedral, and the magnificent Duomo di Milano. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a romantic gondola ride through the canals of Venice, wine tasting in the Tuscan countryside, and opportunities to explore Italy's world-renowned fashion, art, and culinary scenes.", 'images': ["447998_Saint_Peter's_Square_Rome_Italy_753.jpg", '40866_Colosseum_Rome_Italy_753.jpg', '2987_Florence_753.jpg', '51449_Field_of_Miracles_Pisa_Italy_753.jpg', '62615_Venice_753.jpg', '59724_Venice_Mark_Square753.jpg', 'Milan_Cityview_753.jpeg', '16950_Duomo_Square_Cathedral_Milan_Italy_753.jpg', '04993_Milan_Italy_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 192809, 'thumbnailImage': 'FLORENCE4.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014525 is named 'Inspiring Italy' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Rome, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Italy Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Fiumicino Leonardo Da Vinci (FCO) airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hop On Hop Off Tour Hop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome's iconic sights and landmarks on a hop-on hop-off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Rome To Florence Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Florence. (Duration approx. 1.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Pisa And The Leaning Tower Tour Transfers: You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence. Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half-day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Florence To Venice Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Gondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice's main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano — three islands in the Venetian Lagoon — on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water. Highlights: Visit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat Watch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano See Byzantine churches on Torcello— the Church of Santa Fosca Browse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses McArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional): Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfyyour thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable. Planning to Visit? Click the link below to conveniently book your shuttle bus tickets and enjoy exciting deals at the nearest outlet: https://mgbooking.tripodeck.com/home?orderCustId=6977233, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Milan, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Venice To Milan Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Milan. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Milan train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Visit to Scalo Milano Outlet (Optional): It is not just an outlet, but much more: a dynamic destination focused on excellence, to be experienced in every way. Scalo Milano outlet & more offers all visitors a unique shopping and entertainment experience: the very best of fashion, design and food, along with a rich calendar of events and a wide range of services. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Milan, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hop On Hop Off Bus Tour Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Belfast. (Duration approx 2 hrs 10 mins) Milan Hop on Hop off Tour: Today, make the most of your time during your stay in Milan with a City Sightseeing hop-on hop-off bus tour. Hop on and off as many times as you wish as you visit some of the most famous places in the fashion capital! Highlights Explore the city at your own pace onboard a panoramic Double Decker bus 4 routes with numerous stops Multilingual audio-guide on board, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Milan, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Milan Transfers: From Milan hotel to airport, you will have a private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 192809.0. Hotels envisaged include: Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nHotel Bristol / Nh Milano Machiavelli / Best Western Hotel Madison / Worldhotel Casati 18 or similar\n\n\n\n, Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nIbis Milano Centro / Terminal / Ibis Styles Milano Centro / Flora or similar or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast except day 1\nOne Beverage Voucher at the Show Cheese Factory in the Engelberg Monastery\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Milan based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Rome Airport to Rome Hotel Departure Airport transfer from Milan Hotel to Milan International Airport Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Rome to Florence 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Florence to Venice 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Venice to Milan Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Hop On Hop Off Bus tour in Rome Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour Milan City Sightseeing Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Inspiring Italy' package is a 9-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Rome, Venice, Florence, and Milan. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Colosseum, the Vatican Museums, St. Mark's Square, the Florence Cathedral, and the magnificent Duomo di Milano. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a romantic gondola ride through the canals of Venice, wine tasting in the Tuscan countryside, and opportunities to explore Italy's world-renowned fashion, art, and culinary scenes.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Italy\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at the Fiumicino Leonardo Da Vinci (FCO) airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Andreotti and Domus Australia (Standard) / Best Western Artdeco (Value) or similar in Rome'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nHop On Hop Off Tour\n\xa0\nHop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome's iconic sights and landmarks on a hop-on hop-off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Andreotti and Domus Australia (Standard) / Best Western Artdeco (Value) or similar in Rome'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nRome To Florence Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Florence. (Duration approx. 1.5 hrs.)\nUpon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Albergo Firenze (Standard) / Atlantic Palace (Value) or similar in Florence\n\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nPisa And The Leaning Tower Tour\n\xa0\nTransfers: You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence.\n\xa0\nPisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half-day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Albergo Firenze (Standard) / Atlantic Palace (Value) or similar in Florence'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nFlorence To Venice Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.)\nUpon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nGondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice's main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Diana (Standard) / Royal San Marco (Value) or similar in Venice'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nMurano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour\n\xa0\nMurano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano — three islands in the Venetian Lagoon — on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water.\n\xa0\nHighlights:\xa0\n\nVisit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat\xa0\nWatch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano\xa0\nSee Byzantine churches on Torcello— the Church of Santa Fosca\xa0\nBrowse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses\n\n\xa0\nMcArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional):\xa0 Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfyyour thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable.\n\xa0\nPlanning to Visit?\nClick the link below to conveniently book your shuttle bus tickets and enjoy exciting deals at the nearest outlet: https://mgbooking.tripodeck.com/home?orderCustId=6977233', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Diana (Standard) / Royal San Marco (Value) or similar in Venice'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nVenice To Milan Via Train\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station for your onward journey to Milan. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.)\nUpon your arrival at Milan train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own.\n\n\xa0\nVisit to Scalo Milano Outlet (Optional): It is not just an outlet, but much more: a dynamic destination focused on excellence, to be experienced in every way. Scalo Milano outlet & more offers all visitors a unique shopping and entertainment experience: the very best of fashion, design and food, along with a rich calendar of events and a wide range of services.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Milano Centro (Standard) / Hotel Bristol (Value) or similar in Milan'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nHop On Hop Off Bus Tour\n\xa0\nTransfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Belfast. (Duration approx 2 hrs 10 mins)\n\xa0\nMilan Hop on Hop off Tour: Today, make the most of your time during your stay in Milan with a City Sightseeing hop-on hop-off bus tour. Hop on and off as many times as you wish as you visit some of the most famous places in the fashion capital!\n\xa0\nHighlights\n\nExplore the city at your own pace onboard a panoramic Double Decker bus\n4 routes with numerous stops\nMultilingual audio-guide on board\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Milano Centro (Standard) / Hotel Bristol (Value) or similar in Milan'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Milan\n\xa0\nTransfers: From Milan hotel to airport, you will have a private transfer.\n\xa0\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ["Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nHotel Bristol / Nh Milano Machiavelli / Best Western Hotel Madison / Worldhotel Casati 18 or similar\n\n\n\n", 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nIbis Milano Centro / Terminal / Ibis Styles Milano Centro / Flora or similar or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': "Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nHotel Bristol / Nh Milano Machiavelli / Best Western Hotel Madison / Worldhotel Casati 18 or similar\n\n\n\n", '0': 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nIbis Milano Centro / Terminal / Ibis Styles Milano Centro / Flora or similar or similar\n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IT', 'countryName': 'Italy', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 192800.0, 'hotels': ['Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n3*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nAndreotti Hotel and Domus Australia / Hotel Villa San Lorenzo Maria / Hotel Des Artistes / Hotel Nord Nuova Roma / Hotel Windrose or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAlbergo Firenze / Hotel Boccaccio / Hotel Paris / Hotel Machiavelli Palace / Hotel Luxor Florence or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nHotel Diana / Albergo San Marco / San Zulian / Hotel Montecarlo or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nIbis Milano Centro / Terminal / Ibis Styles Milano Centro / Flora or similar or similar\n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 226600.0, 'hotels': ["Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\n\nCITY\n\n\n4*\n\n\n\n\nRome\n\n\nBest Western Hotel Artdeco / Atlantico / Hotel Massimo D'azeglio / Hotel Diana Roof Garden / Best Western President or similar\n\n\n\n\nFlorence\n\n\nAtlantic Palace / De La Ville / Embassy Hotel / Starhotels Michelangelo Florence / Hotel Principe di Firenze / C Hotel Club / C-hotels Ambassadors Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n\nVenice\n\n\nRoyal San Marco Hotel / San Marco Palace / Hotel Kette / Bonvecchiati or similar or similar\n\n\n\n\nMilan\n\n\nHotel Bristol / Nh Milano Machiavelli / Best Western Hotel Madison / Worldhotel Casati 18 or similar\n\n\n\n"]}], 'meals': ['\nDaily breakfast except day 1\nOne Beverage Voucher at the Show Cheese Factory in the Engelberg Monastery\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Rome Airport to Rome Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Milan Hotel to Milan International Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets:\xa0[Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Rome to Florence\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Florence to Venice\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Venice to Milan\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nHop On Hop Off Bus tour in Rome\nPisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\xa0\nVenice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade\xa0\nMurano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\xa0\xa0\nMilan City Sightseeing Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Rome based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Florence based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Venice based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Milan based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Rome Airport to Rome Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Milan Hotel to Milan International Airport\n\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Rome to Florence\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Florence to Venice\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Venice to Milan\n\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nHop On Hop Off Bus tour in Rome\nPisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\xa0\nVenice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade\xa0\nMurano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\xa0\xa0\nMilan City Sightseeing Hop on Hop Off (24 Hrs)\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/FLORENCE4.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ["https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/447998_Saint_Peter's_Square_Rome_Italy_753.jpg", 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/40866_Colosseum_Rome_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/2987_Florence_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/51449_Field_of_Miracles_Pisa_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/62615_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/59724_Venice_Mark_Square753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/Milan_Cityview_753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/16950_Duomo_Square_Cathedral_Milan_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014525/itinerary/04993_Milan_Italy_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014796', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014796', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Impressive Croatia', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Plitvice Lakes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zadar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014796_0_20260515160359.pdf', 'price': 156802, 'packageSummary': "The 'Impressive Croatia' package is a 9-day tour covering Zagreb, Dubrovnik, Plitvice Lakes, Zadar, and Split. The itinerary includes visits to the historic Old Towns, the breathtaking Plitvice Lakes National Park, the ancient Roman Diocletian's Palace, and the famous city walls of Dubrovnik. Participants will enjoy guided walking tours, scenic coastal drives, and opportunities to explore beautiful Adriatic beaches and local cultural landmarks.", 'images': ['Zagerb.jpg', 'ZAGRAB-CROATIA.jpg', 'Plitvice-Lakes-National-Park-1.jpg', 'ZADAR-c.jpg', 'croatia-Split.jpg', 'Diocletians.jpg', 'Dubrovnik (1).jpg', 'DUBROVNIK-para.jpg', 'Croatia-Dubrovnik.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 156802, 'thumbnailImage': 'Zagreb_SRP.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014796 is named 'Impressive Croatia' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Zagreb, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zagreb Transfers: Upon your arrival at Zagreb airport, you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Walking Tour of Zagreb: Explore Zagreb's highlights on a guided walking tour with a scenic funicular ride. Discover the charm of both Lower and Upper Town, uncover hidden gems, and hear the stories that shaped Croatia's vibrant capital. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Zagreb, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Free At Leisure Optional Day Trip to Slovenia on SIC Basis: Enjoy a free day or take an optional trip to Slovenia. Visit the charming capital Ljubljana, then escape into nature at Lake Bled, famous for its scenic lake and hilltop castle - an unforgettable getaway from Zagreb. Special Note: 1. You need to be in possession of a multiple entry Schengen visa to visit Slovenia. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Plitvice Lakes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zagreb - Plitvice | Visit Plitvice National Park Transfers: Today you will travel from Zagreb to Plitvice by bus on shared basis. Visit Plitvice National Park: Travel to Plitvice and check into your hotel. Explore Plitvice National Park, famous for its stunning waterfalls, lakes, and forested cliffs. Enjoy access to hiking trails, boardwalks, a panoramic train, shuttle buses, and a boat ride on Lake Kozjak. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Zadar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Plitvice - Zadar | Walking Tour Of Zadar Transfers: Today you will travel from Plitvice to Zadar by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Zadar: Enjoy a guided walking tour of Zadar's Old City, including St. Donat, St. Anastasia, city gates, walls, and the Square of Five Wells. Sample Maraschino liqueur and Pag cheese, then relax by the Sea Organ and admire the sunset. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only. 2. You can opt for a Romantic Sunset Cruise at a supplement cost, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zadar - Split | Walking Tour Of Split Transfers: Today you will travel from Zadar to Split by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Split: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Split and explore the 1700 year old Diocletian’s Palace. See St. Domnius Cathedral, the Peristil, Golden Gate, and Gregory of Nin. End with the 24 hour sun clock at City Square and the Riva promenade. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Blue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour Blue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour: Enjoy a relaxing Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour, visiting UNESCO listed Trogir, the Blue Lagoon, and Solta's Stomorska village for swimming and exploring. You can also take a Blue Cave 5 Island Tour to Biševo, Vis, Pakleni, Hvar and Brac for stunning views and swims. Special Note: 1. You have an opportunity to upgrade your Blue Lagoon tour to a full day Blue Cave Tour at an additional cost. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Split - Dubrovnik| Walking Tour Of Dubrovnik Transfers: Today you will travel from Split to Dubrovnik by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Dubrovnik: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Dubrovnik and a Cable Car ride. Explore the Old Town’s history, architecture, and culture, then ride to the top of Srd Hill for stunning views of the Adriatic Sea and the city below. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Trip To Bosnia & Herzegovina Trip to Bosnia & Herzegovina: Explore Bosnia and Herzegovina on a day trip and visit UNESCO listed Mostar. Wander cobbled streets, see Ottoman era mosques and bathhouses, and admire the iconic Stari Most - one of the modern world's most remarkable bridges. Special Note: 1. Guest should be carrying their passport with valid Schengen Visa. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Dubrovnik hotel to Dubrovnik Airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 156802.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nCity\xa0\n\n\nHotels\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0Sheraton,\xa0Hotel\xa0Esplanade\xa0Zagreb,\xa0Hotel\xa0Westin\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nFenomen\xa0Plitvice\xa0Resort\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare\xa0Hotel,\xa0Teatro\xa0Verdi\xa0Boutique\xa0Hotel\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nRadisson\xa0Blu\xa0Resort\xa0&\xa0Spa,\xa0Hotel\xa0Ambasador\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0President,\xa0hotel\xa0Sun\xa0Gardens,\xa0Hotel\xa0Hilton\xa0Imperial\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nCity\n\n\nVALUE\xa0\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0AS,\xa0Hotel\xa0Dubrovnik,\xa0Canopy\xa0by\xa0Hilton\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nEthno\xa0Houses\xa0Plitvice\xa0Lakes\xa0Hotel,\xa0Lyra\xa0Hotel\xa0Plitvice\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nFalkensteiner\xa0Club\xa0Funimation\xa0Borik,\xa0Hotel\xa0Kolovare\xa0or\xa0Similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nHotel\xa0Fanat,\xa0Hotel\xa0Globo,\xa0Hotel\xa0Cora\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0Lero,\xa0Hotel\xa0Valamar\xa0Lacroma,\xa0Hotel\xa0Lapad\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nCity\xa0Name\n\n\nSTANDARD\xa0CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0Laguna,\xa0Hotel\xa0Central\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nHotel\xa0Plitvice,\xa0Hotel\xa0Jezero\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nA'mare\xa0Hotel\xa0Zadar,\xa0Hotel\xa0Mediteran,\xa0Hotel\xa0Sky\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nHotel\xa0Jadrran,\xa0hotel\xa0AS\xa0Hotel\xa0Batuda\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0Vis,\xa0Hotel\xa0Komodor,\xa0Hotel\xa0Dubrovnik\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights accommodation in Zagreb based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Plitvice based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Zadar based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights accommodation in Split based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights accommodation in Dubrovnik based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: (Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis) Private Transfer from Zagreb Airport to Zagreb Hotel Private Transfer from Dubrovnik Hotel to Dubrovnik Airport Bus Tickets: (Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed) Bus ticket from Zagreb to Plitvice National park (Subject to availability until ticketed) Bus Ticket from Plitvice to Zadar (Subject to availability until ticketed) Bus ticket from Zadar to Split (Subject to availability until ticketed) Bus Ticket from Split to Dubrovnik (Subject to availability until ticketed) Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Walking tour of Zagreb with Funicular Ride in a group Walking tour of Zadar old town in a group from a central meeting point Entrance to Plitvice National Park Walking tour of Split in group Blue Lagoon and 3 island group tour from Split Walking tour of Dubrovnik in group (Dubrovnik Cable Car Roundtrip ticket) Trip to Bosnia & Herzegovina Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary 'INCLUSIONS' head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Prices are Starting from Rates (please recheck costs with exact dates) IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 01 April 2025 – 31 October 2025 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. TCS & GST would be levied as applicable The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Impressive Croatia' package is a 9-day tour covering Zagreb, Dubrovnik, Plitvice Lakes, Zadar, and Split. The itinerary includes visits to the historic Old Towns, the breathtaking Plitvice Lakes National Park, the ancient Roman Diocletian's Palace, and the famous city walls of Dubrovnik. Participants will enjoy guided walking tours, scenic coastal drives, and opportunities to explore beautiful Adriatic beaches and local cultural landmarks.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrive Zagreb\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at Zagreb airport, you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis.\nWalking Tour of Zagreb: Explore Zagreb's highlights on a guided walking tour with a scenic funicular ride. Discover the charm of both Lower and Upper Town, uncover hidden gems, and hear the stories that shaped Croatia's vibrant capital.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Laguna (Standard) // Canopy by Hilton (Value) // Hotel Sheraton (Premium)\xa0or similar in Zagreb'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0Day Free At Leisure\nOptional Day Trip to Slovenia on SIC Basis: Enjoy a free day or take an optional trip to Slovenia. Visit the charming capital Ljubljana, then escape into nature at Lake Bled, famous for its scenic lake and hilltop castle - an unforgettable getaway from Zagreb.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. You need to be in possession of a multiple entry Schengen visa to visit Slovenia.\n2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Laguna (Standard) // Canopy by Hilton (Value) // Hotel Sheraton (Premium)\xa0or similar in Zagreb'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0Zagreb - Plitvice | Visit Plitvice National Park\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Zagreb to Plitvice by bus on shared basis.\nVisit Plitvice National Park: Travel to Plitvice and check into your hotel. Explore Plitvice National Park, famous for its stunning waterfalls, lakes, and forested cliffs. Enjoy access to hiking trails, boardwalks, a panoramic train, shuttle buses, and a boat ride on Lake Kozjak.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Plitvice (Standard) // Ethno Houses Plitvice Lakes Hotel (Value) // Fenomen Plitvice Resort (Premium) or Similar in Plitvice'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0Plitvice - Zadar | Walking Tour Of Zadar\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Plitvice to Zadar by bus on shared basis.\nWalking Tour of Zadar:\xa0 Enjoy a guided walking tour of Zadar's Old City, including St. Donat, St. Anastasia, city gates, walls, and the Square of Five Wells. Sample Maraschino liqueur and Pag cheese, then relax by the Sea Organ and admire the sunset.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n2. You can opt for a Romantic Sunset Cruise at a supplement cost", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': "Hotel\xa0A'mare Zadar (Standard) //\xa0Falkensteiner Club Funimation Borik (Value) // Miramare Hotel (Premium)or similar in Zadar"}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0Zadar - Split | Walking Tour Of Split\xa0\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Zadar to Split by bus on shared basis.\nWalking Tour of Split: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Split and explore the 1700 year old Diocletian’s Palace. See St. Domnius Cathedral, the Peristil, Golden Gate, and Gregory of Nin. End with the 24 hour sun clock at City Square and the Riva promenade.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Jadrran (Standard) //\xa0Hotel Globo (Value) //\xa0Hotel Atrium (Premium)\xa0or similar in Split'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "Blue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour\xa0\xa0\nBlue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour:\xa0 Enjoy a relaxing Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour, visiting UNESCO listed Trogir, the Blue Lagoon, and Solta's Stomorska village for swimming and exploring. You can also take a Blue Cave 5 Island Tour to Biševo, Vis, Pakleni, Hvar and Brac\xa0for stunning views and swims.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. You have an opportunity to upgrade your Blue Lagoon tour to a full day Blue Cave Tour at an additional cost.\n2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Jadrran (Standard)//\xa0Hotel Globo (Value)//\xa0Hotel Atrium (Premium)\xa0or similar in Split'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nSplit - Dubrovnik| Walking Tour Of Dubrovnik\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Split to Dubrovnik by bus on shared basis.\nWalking Tour of Dubrovnik: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Dubrovnik and a Cable Car ride. Explore the Old Town’s history, architecture, and culture, then ride to the top of Srd Hill for stunning views of the Adriatic Sea and the city below.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Vis (Standard) //\xa0Hotel Lero (Value) //Hotel President (Premium) or\xa0similar in Dubrovnik'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0Trip To Bosnia & Herzegovina\xa0\xa0\nTrip to Bosnia & Herzegovina: Explore Bosnia and Herzegovina on a day trip and visit UNESCO listed Mostar. Wander cobbled streets, see Ottoman era mosques and bathhouses, and admire the iconic Stari Most - one of the modern world's most remarkable bridges.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n1. Guest should be carrying their passport with valid Schengen Visa.\n2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Vis (Standard) //\xa0Hotel Lero (Value) // Hotel President (Premium) or\xa0similar in Dubrovnik'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\nTransfers: You will have a private transfer from Dubrovnik hotel to Dubrovnik Airport.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nCity\xa0\n\n\nHotels\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0Sheraton,\xa0Hotel\xa0Esplanade\xa0Zagreb,\xa0Hotel\xa0Westin\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nFenomen\xa0Plitvice\xa0Resort\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare\xa0Hotel,\xa0Teatro\xa0Verdi\xa0Boutique\xa0Hotel\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nRadisson\xa0Blu\xa0Resort\xa0&\xa0Spa,\xa0Hotel\xa0Ambasador\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0President,\xa0hotel\xa0Sun\xa0Gardens,\xa0Hotel\xa0Hilton\xa0Imperial\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nCity\n\n\nVALUE\xa0\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0AS,\xa0Hotel\xa0Dubrovnik,\xa0Canopy\xa0by\xa0Hilton\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nEthno\xa0Houses\xa0Plitvice\xa0Lakes\xa0Hotel,\xa0Lyra\xa0Hotel\xa0Plitvice\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nFalkensteiner\xa0Club\xa0Funimation\xa0Borik,\xa0Hotel\xa0Kolovare\xa0or\xa0Similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nHotel\xa0Fanat,\xa0Hotel\xa0Globo,\xa0Hotel\