transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nRental of winter thermal clothing from day 2 to day 7 of the program\xa0\nDay 2: Visit to a husky dog farm & Santa Claus Village\nDay 3 - 3h30m cruise on the icebreaker ship Sampo & Visit to the Ice Castle in Kemi\nDay 5 - 2-hour snowmobile safari &\nVisit to a Sami farm including a short ride on a reindeer sleigh &\xa0\nNight Safari "Aurora Borealis" with grilled sausages and hot drinks\nDay 6 – 4-hour visit to Ranua Zoo\n', 'Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\n\nReykjavik Northern Lights Cruise Tour\xa0\nSouth Iceland Adventure Tour\xa0\nGolden Circle Tour\nReykjavik Northern Lights Evening Tour\xa0\nIce Cave Experience Tour (Subject to availability)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n4 Nights’ accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis]\n\nReturn Airport Transfer from Reykjavik airport to the Hotel\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point)\n\nReykjavik Northern Lights Cruise Tour\nSouth Iceland Adventure Tour\nGolden Circle Tour\nReykjavik Northern Lights Evening Tour\nIce Cave Experience Tour (Subject to availability)\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included\nCity taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\nBlack out Period: Surcharges could be applicable from 15 December’26 - 10 January’27\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\n\xa0Special Note:\n\nThe itinerary and sightseeing may vary based on availability and seasonality\nPlease note that should the Covid 19 pandemic necessitate further protocols as mandated by the Government and/or the individual properties in the future which results in an increase in our standard tour operator rates, then Thomas Cook India reserves the right to adjust the above quoted rates accordingly. This may lead to an increase in prices quoted. Certain Activities are subject to weather conditions and protocols.\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 November 2026 – 31 March 2027\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/Finland-Rovaniemi.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/itinerary/Reykjavik.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/itinerary/Reykjavik_11.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/itinerary/Gullfoss21.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/itinerary/Blulagoon21.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015072/itinerary/return_home.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015081', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015081', 'availableMonths': ['december_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Greece (Winter)', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Athens', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Santorini', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Santorini', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Santorini', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG011800_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 225668, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Greece (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic capital of Athens and the picturesque island of Santorini. The itinerary includes visits to iconic ancient landmarks such as the Acropolis, the Parthenon, and the historic Plaka neighborhood, as well as exploring the stunning volcanic caldera and charming whitewashed villages of Santorini. Participants will enjoy guided historical city tours, scenic walks, traditional Greek wine tastings, and the opportunity to experience the breathtaking, peaceful winter sunsets over the Aegean Sea.", 'images': ['Athens.jpg', 'Acropolis753.jpg', 'Mykons753.jpg', 'Santorini753.jpg', 'Santorini7532.jpg', 'Athens7534.jpg', 'Athens_Greece.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 225668, 'thumbnailImage': 'Santorini.bmp', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015081 is named 'Highlights Of Greece (Winter)' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Athens, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Athens! On arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour - Visit the Acropolis and the Museum Today, we go on a guided tour of Athens, we visit to the Acropolis, the crowning beauty and glory of Ancient Athens, the awesome Parthenon, the Propylea, the temple of Athena Nike and the Erechtheion, with its Porch of Maidens. Next, we drive to the Roman Temple of Olympic Zeus, the Panathinaikon Stadium (site of the first modern Olympic Games in 1896), and the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier in front of the Parliament House on Constitution Square. Then we drive along Panepistimiou Avenue and view the Catholic Cathedral, the Academy, University, and National Library. Later, you can enjoy free time at Plaka., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at Leisure or Change to Visit Delphi Archaeological Site and Museum (OPTIONAL) Today, the day is at leisure OR you have a chance to visit the Delphi Archaeological site and Museum: The pan Hellenic sanctuary of Delphi, where the oracle of Apollo spoke, was the site of the omphalos, the 'navel of the world' and one of the principal museums of Greece., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Athens, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at Leisure or Change to 3 Island Cruise with Mediterranean Lunch (OPTIONAL) Today, the day is at leisure OR you have a chance to experience a cruise and visit 3 famous Islands near Athens. Hydra: A completely car free, cobblestone island where transportation is done by donkeys and boats. Poros: Known for its pine forests, tranquil beaches, and quaint clock tower. Aegina: Famous for its world renowned pistachio groves and ancient ruins like the Temple of Aphaia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Santorini, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Flight / Ferry to Santorini – Visit the beautiful city of Fira Today, after breakfast, we take a flight/ferry to Santorini. On arrival, we proceed to Fira, the beautiful capital of the island and the biggest and most cosmopolitan settlement of Santorini. Enjoy some free time at Fira., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Santorini, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Santorini Island – Santo winery – Visit beautiful village of Megalochori - Prophet Elias Mountain Today, we proceed on a Guided tour of Santorini Island: world renowned for its whitewashed villages, sapphire waters, and dramatic cliffside caldera views. Next, we proceed to the Santo winery. Later, we will see the charming Megalochori village, a labyrinth of winding alleys, whitewashed houses, and blue domed churches with ornate bell towers. Enjoy panoramic view of the whole island village of Pyrgos from Prophet Elias Mountain. Next stop will be the traditional village of Oia which is on the northern tip of the island, high on the cliff top., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Santorini, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to the airport to take your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: In major cities like Athens, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop the coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 225668.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n04 nights at Gallery Central or similar in Athens.\n02 nights at SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.\n, \n02 nights at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n01 night at Hotel Paolas Town Boutique or similar in Mykonos.\n02 nights at Hotel Albatros or similar in Santorini.\n01 night at Hotel Grand Meteora or similar in Kalabaka.\n01 night at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental buffet breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n06 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non–vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local Dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian., \nDaily continental buffet breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n01 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non vegetarian lunch.\n06 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Single entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: AIRLINE AND AIRFARE The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. JOINING DIRECT CLIENTS Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. HOTELS All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled, nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. COACHES Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. MEALS Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. SIGHTSEEING On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. GENERAL On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE800', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Greece (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic capital of Athens and the picturesque island of Santorini. The itinerary includes visits to iconic ancient landmarks such as the Acropolis, the Parthenon, and the historic Plaka neighborhood, as well as exploring the stunning volcanic caldera and charming whitewashed villages of Santorini. Participants will enjoy guided historical city tours, scenic walks, traditional Greek wine tastings, and the opportunity to experience the breathtaking, peaceful winter sunsets over the Aegean Sea.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Athens!\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet and welcome you outside the airport. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in.\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Gallery Central or similar in Athens'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour - Visit the Acropolis and the Museum\nToday, we go on a guided tour of Athens, we visit to the Acropolis, the crowning beauty and glory of Ancient Athens, the awesome Parthenon, the Propylea, the temple of Athena Nike and the Erechtheion, with its Porch of Maidens. Next, we drive to the Roman Temple of Olympic Zeus, the Panathinaikon Stadium (site of the first modern Olympic Games in 1896), and the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier in front of the Parliament House on Constitution Square. Then we drive along Panepistimiou Avenue and view the Catholic Cathedral, the Academy, University, and National Library. Later, you can enjoy free time at Plaka.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Gallery Central or similar in Athens'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nDay at Leisure or Change to Visit Delphi Archaeological Site and Museum (OPTIONAL)\nToday, the day is at leisure OR you have a chance to visit the Delphi Archaeological site and Museum: The pan Hellenic sanctuary of Delphi, where the oracle of Apollo spoke, was the site of the omphalos, the 'navel of the world' and one of the principal museums of Greece.\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Gallery Central or similar in Athens'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay at Leisure or Change to 3 Island Cruise with Mediterranean Lunch (OPTIONAL)\nToday, the day is at leisure OR you have a chance to experience a cruise and visit 3 famous Islands near Athens. Hydra: A completely car free, cobblestone island where transportation is done by donkeys and boats. Poros: Known for its pine forests, tranquil beaches, and quaint clock tower. Aegina: Famous for its world renowned pistachio groves and ancient ruins like the Temple of Aphaia.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Gallery Central or similar in Athens'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nFlight / Ferry to Santorini – Visit the beautiful city of Fira\nToday, after breakfast, we take a flight/ferry to Santorini. On arrival, we proceed to Fira, the beautiful capital of the island and the biggest and most cosmopolitan settlement of Santorini. Enjoy some free time at Fira.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Santorini Island – Santo winery – Visit beautiful village of Megalochori - Prophet Elias Mountain\xa0\nToday, we proceed on a Guided tour of Santorini Island: world renowned for its whitewashed villages, sapphire waters, and dramatic cliffside caldera views. Next, we proceed to the Santo winery. Later, we will see the charming Megalochori village, a labyrinth of winding alleys, whitewashed houses, and blue domed churches with ornate bell towers. Enjoy panoramic view of the whole island village of Pyrgos from Prophet Elias Mountain. Next stop will be the traditional village of Oia which is on the northern tip of the island, high on the cliff top.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\xa0\nToday, we proceed to the airport to take your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote: In major cities like Athens, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop the coach wherever possible for a photo stop.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n04 nights at Gallery Central or similar in Athens.\n02 nights at SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n01 night at Hotel Paolas Town Boutique or similar in Mykonos.\n02 nights at Hotel Albatros or similar in Santorini.\n01 night at Hotel Grand Meteora or similar in Kalabaka.\n01 night at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n02 nights at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n01 night at Hotel Paolas Town Boutique or similar in Mykonos.\n02 nights at Hotel Albatros or similar in Santorini.\n01 night at Hotel Grand Meteora or similar in Kalabaka.\n01 night at Hotel Athens Stanley or similar in Athens.\n', '1': '\n04 nights at Gallery Central or similar in Athens.\n02 nights at SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GR', 'countryName': 'Greece', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 225700.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 nights at Gallery Central or similar in Athens.\n02 nights at SMY Mediterranean / Albatross or similar in Santorini.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental buffet breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n06 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non–vegetarian dinners.\n01 Local Dinner.\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.', '\nDaily continental buffet breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk, coffee, hot eggs and cut fruits)\n01 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non vegetarian lunch.\n06 Indian Jain /vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\n'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nSingle entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Athens\n\nGuided city tour\nVisit to Acropolis and the Museum\nVisit to Delphi Archaeological Site and Museum\n\nMykonos\n\nOrientation Tour\nParadise beach\n\nSantorini\n\nVisit the beautiful city of Fira\nHalf Day Santorini Island Tour\nStunning 360° views of Santorini from Prophet Elias Monastery\xa0\nVisit beautiful villages of Pyrgos and Megalochori\xa0\nVisit the most picturesque Oia village and watch the spectacular Sunset\n\nMeteora\n\nVisit two Monasteries\xa0\n', 'Athens\n\nGuided City Tour Of Athens\nVisit The Acropolis & The Museum\nChance To Visit The Delphi Archaeological Site (Optional)\n3 Island Cruise With Mediterranean Lunch (Optional)\n\nSantorini\n\nVisit The Beautiful City Of Fira\nGuided Tour Of Santorini\nStunning 360° Views Of Santorini From Prophet Elias Mountain\nVisit Beautiful Village Of Megalochori\nVisit The Most Picturesque Oia Village And Watch The Spectacular Sunset\nSanto Winery\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<div><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Rest assured, Thomas Cook\'s experienced &amp; knowledgeable&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it\'s a question or a challenge, our&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">manager</span>&nbsp;is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Tour</span>&nbsp;<span data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="">Manager</span>&nbsp;is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</span></div>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nSingle entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'AIRLINE AND AIRFARE\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJOINING DIRECT CLIENTS\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHOTELS \n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled, nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\nCOACHES \n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. \n\n\xa0\nMEALS \n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. \n\n\xa0\nSIGHTSEEING \n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. \n\n\xa0\nGENERAL \n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\n\n\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0\xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”. \n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/Santorini.bmp', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Athens.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Acropolis753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Mykons753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Santorini753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Santorini7532.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Athens7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015081/itinerary/Athens_Greece.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014519', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014519', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Passionate Paris', 'days': 4, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014519_0_20261012231001', 'price': 82123, 'packageSummary': "The 'Passionate Paris' package is a 4-day tour dedicated entirely to the beautiful city of Paris. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre Museum, the Arc de Triomphe, and the historic Notre-Dame Cathedral. Participants will enjoy a scenic cruise along the Seine River, guided walking tours through the artistic neighborhood of Montmartre, and ample time to experience the city's world-class dining and shopping along the Champs-Élysées.", 'images': ['Paris_new_753.jpeg', '53501_Eiffel_Tower_Paris_France_753.jpg', 'VersaillesPalace_new_753.jpg', 'Paris_City_new753.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 82123, 'thumbnailImage': 'EiffelTower_2.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure', 'Youth Special'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014519 is named 'Passionate Paris' and spans 4 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Paris Transfers: On arrival in Paris, you will have a private transfer from Airport to the hotel. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour Paris City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour-long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time. Special Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris Day At Leisure (Optional Activities) Disneyland Paris – 1-Day Tour Including Both Parks Option 1: Step into a world of enchantment with a full-day visit to Disneyland Park and Walt Disney Studios Park. More than just a theme park, Disneyland Paris brings the magic to life across its vibrant lands and attractions. Meet your favourite Disney characters, enjoy dazzling parades, and be captivated by spectacular shows. With Disney Village adding to the charm, this is the perfect family getaway filled with joy, wonder, and unforgettable memories. The Palace of Versailles – A Royal Journey Option 2: Experience the grandeur of Versailles in true royal fashion. Accompanied by a knowledgeable guide, explore a curated selection of the palace’s 700 opulent rooms, and uncover fascinating stories of Louis XIV – the Sun King, his successors, queens, mistresses, and courtiers including Marie Antoinette. Once a humble hunting lodge, Versailles became the dazzling seat of the French court in the 17th and 18th centuries. Even today, its splendour and historical richness remain unmatched., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Paris Transfers: From Paris hotel to the Airport in Private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which you are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 82123.0. Hotels envisaged include: Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name (Deluxe) - 4 Star\n\n\nParis\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\n, Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name (Standard) - 3 Star\n\n\nParis\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hôtel Champerret-Elysées / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n. Meals include: Daily breakfast except day 1. Inclusions: Accommodation: 3 Nights’ accommodation in Paris based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Return Airport Transfer in Paris on private basis Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Interactive City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC). Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Passionate Paris' package is a 4-day tour dedicated entirely to the beautiful city of Paris. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre Museum, the Arc de Triomphe, and the historic Notre-Dame Cathedral. Participants will enjoy a scenic cruise along the Seine River, guided walking tours through the artistic neighborhood of Montmartre, and ample time to experience the city's world-class dining and shopping along the Champs-Élysées.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Paris\n\xa0\nTransfers: On arrival in Paris, you will have a private transfer from Airport to the hotel.\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nParis City Tour + River Seine Cruise + Eiffel Tower Tour\n\xa0\nParis City Tour: Later discover Paris's most famous tourist sites and monuments on one unique tour. This tour features a visit to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower with breathtaking views of the capital, a panoramic city tour by coach, plus an hour-long boat trip along the River Seine. This comprehensive tour is the ideal way to discover Paris for the first time.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Thanks to your priority access, you can skip the line and speed up by elevator to the 2nd floor of the Eiffel Tower, Paris's most unmissable monument.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nParis Day At Leisure (Optional Activities)\n\xa0\nDisneyland Paris – 1-Day Tour Including Both Parks Option 1: Step into a world of enchantment with a full-day visit to Disneyland Park and Walt Disney Studios Park. More than just a theme park, Disneyland Paris brings the magic to life across its vibrant lands and attractions. Meet your favourite Disney characters, enjoy dazzling parades, and be captivated by spectacular shows. With Disney Village adding to the charm, this is the perfect family getaway filled with joy, wonder, and unforgettable memories.\n\xa0\nThe Palace of Versailles – A Royal Journey Option 2: Experience the grandeur of Versailles in true royal fashion. Accompanied by a knowledgeable guide, explore a curated selection of the palace’s 700 opulent rooms, and uncover fascinating stories of Louis XIV – the Sun King, his successors, queens, mistresses, and courtiers including Marie Antoinette. Once a humble hunting lodge, Versailles became the dazzling seat of the French court in the 17th and 18th centuries. Even today, its splendour and historical richness remain unmatched.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) / Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre (Value) or similar in Paris'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Paris\n\xa0\nTransfers: From Paris hotel to the Airport in Private transfer.\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which you are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name (Deluxe) - 4 Star\n\n\nParis\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\n', 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name (Standard) - 3 Star\n\n\nParis\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hôtel Champerret-Elysées / Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar :\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name (Standard) - 3 Star\n\n\nParis\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel / Hô