n (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nLake Lucerne Cruise with 3-course Gourmet Lunch (Pick up / drop off from designated points)\nCabriO convertible style cable car ride (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nEntrance to Chillon Castle (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\n\n\xa0\nTransport within Swiss:\n\n8 Days Consecutive Swiss Pass (2nd Class)\nGlacier 3000 Ticket (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\n\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Medical Insurance (Basic Coverage- Up to 60 years of age)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nMeals other than those specified (if any).\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 5 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n*** IMPORTANT NOTE: SURCHARGE OF EUR 50 – 80 PER PERSON COULD BE APPLICABLE DURING THE STAY PERIOD OF 15 JUNE – 15 JULY 2024 DUE TO INCREASED DEMAND ***\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions\n\nTravel Validity: 1st March 2026 till 31st October 2026.\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/Swiss267.bmp', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/zurich_shutterstock_329494742.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/LucerneKapellbrucke.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/Switzerland1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/Interlaken.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/Montreux753.bmp', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/Montreux7532.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014699/itinerary/Switzerland.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012843', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012843', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Radiant Russia With Murmansk', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Moscow', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St. Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St. Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'St. Petersburg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Murmansk', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Murmansk', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012843_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 258636, 'packageSummary': "The 'Radiant Russia With Murmansk' package is an 8-day tour covering St. Petersburg, Moscow, and Murmansk. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Red Square, the grand Kremlin, and the world-renowned Hermitage Museum. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a ride on the famous Moscow Metro, and thrilling Arctic adventures, including hunting for the spectacular Northern Lights and visiting a traditional husky farm.", 'images': ['89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', '007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', '650718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'Petersburg7534.jpg', '12117_Hermitage_Museum_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'Church_of_the_Saviour_on_Blood_St._Petersburg_Russia_753.jpgiti6.jpg', 'Murmansk-1.jpg', 'Teriberka.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 258636, 'thumbnailImage': '44164_Radisson_Hotel_Cruise_Moscow_Russia_Optional_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012843 is named 'Radiant Russia With Murmansk' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Moscow, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Moscow Transfer: Upon your arrival at Moscow International Airport (SVO), you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Hotel check-in will be as per the property’s standard check-in timings or at the sole discretion of the hotel. Early check-in requests are subject to availability and may incur additional charges. Rest of the day is free. Dinner on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Moscow City Tour & River Cruise Meet the English-speaking guide at the hotel lobby for a panoramic Moscow city tour covering iconic landmarks such as Sparrow Hills, Moscow State University, Stalin Buildings, White House, Victory Park, Christ the Savior Cathedral, and Bolshoi Theatre. Later, enjoy a scenic Radisson Cruise ride., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Moscow, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Explore Moscow by Metro & Private Vehicle Meet the English-speaking guide at the hotel lobby for a combined metro and vehicle tour. Explore Red Square with highlights including the Kremlin (inside territory), St. Basil’s Cathedral, Lenin Mausoleum (outside), and GUM Shopping Center. Conclude with a fascinating Moscow Metro tour, showcasing its historic stations adorned with marble, mosaics, and chandeliers, a true underground museum of Russian history., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - St. Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Moscow To Saint Petersburg By Train Transfer: Private transfer to the train station. Board the High Speed Sapsan Train from Moscow to St. Petersburg. Special Note: *2nd Economy Class Sapsan Train Ticket is included in the final price Transfer: Private transfer from the train station to the hotel. Special Note: Hotel check-in will be as per the property’s standard check-in timings or at the sole discretion of the hotel. Early check-in requests are subject to availability and may incur additional charges. Rest of the day is free. Dinner on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - St. Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Explore St. Petersburg Peterhof Palace & Paul Fortress Visit: Meet the English-speaking guide at the hotel lobby for a private tour by vehicle. Visit the magnificent Peterhof Palace and its stunning parklands (entrance included), followed by the historic Peter and Paul Fortress (with entrance), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - St. Petersburg, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Discover St. Petersburg St. Petersburg with entrance to Hermitage: Meet your English-speaking guide at the hotel lobby for a private tour by vehicle. Visit the world-renowned Hermitage Museum (entrance included), Kazan Cathedral, and Palace Square. Continue with a panoramic city tour featuring photo stops at Church of the Savior on Spilled Blood, St. Isaac’s Cathedral, the Bronze Horseman, and the historic Cruiser Aurora, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Murmansk, Meals: Breakfast, Description: St. Petersburg To Murmansk By Flight Transfer: Private Transfer to St. Petersburg Airport. Special Note: ** Domestic flight to Murmansk is not included and to be booked on your own ** Transfer: Private Transfer from Murmansk Airport to Hotel. Murmansk Tour with visit to Lenin Icebreaker Ship: Enjoy a city tour exploring World War II landmarks, including the Alyosha Monument honoring Subarctic defenders, followed by a photo stop at the historic Lenin Icebreaker Ship. Special Note: Hotel check-in will be as per the property’s standard check-in timings or at the sole discretion of the hotel. Early check-in requests are subject to availability and may incur additional charges. Rest of the day is free. Dinner on your own. Northern Lights Hunting Tour: At 21:00 hrs, embark on the ‘Hunting for Northern Lights’ night tour to experience the magical Aurora Borealis. Visibility is not guaranteed, but it’s an unforgettable adventure to try your luck under the Arctic sky., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Murmansk, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murmansk Full-Day Excursion To Teriberka: Depart at 09:00 hrs with your English-speaking chauffeur for a full-day excursion to Teriberka. Discover the Arctic Coast and Desert, with breathtaking views of the Barents Sea, tundra landscapes, lakes, and traditional village life. Highlights include the unique ‘Dragon Eggs’ rock formations and an optional motorbike-connected sledge ride (weather permitting). Return to the hotel by 18:00 hrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 258636.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\nStandard Category\n\n\n\n\nMoscow\n\n\nHotel Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSt. Petersburg\n\n\nCosmos Nevsky/Ambassador/Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nMurmansk\n\n\nAzimut/Meridian/Cosmos or Similar\n\n\n\n\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Buffet Breakfast except on Day 1.\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Moscow based on the hotel category selected or similar. 2 Nights’ accommodation in St. Petersburg based on the hotel category selected or similar. 3 Nights’ accommodation in Murmansk based on the hotel category selected or similar. Meals: Daily Breakfast (Except Day 1). Transportation: [Includes Private Transfers on Point-to-Point Basis] Private Transfer from Moscow Airport to the Hotel Private Transfer from Moscow Hotel to the Train station Private Transfer from St. Petersburg train station to the hotel Private Transfer from St. Petersburg Hotel to the Airport Return Private Transfer from Murmansk Hotel to the Airport Train Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed] Economy Class Train ticket from Moscow to St. Petersburg (Subject to availability until ticketed) Sightseeing: (The tours will operate on Private basis) Panoramic City tour of Moscow Red Square Walking Tour Visit Kremlin Inside Territory Area (Entrance tickets included) Moscow Metro tour The Hermitage Museum (With Entrance Ticket) Visit to Kazan Cathedral Only Photostop Visit to Palace Square. Murmansk Northern Lights Hunt Teriberka for the Arctic Coast and Arctic Desert Sledge Ride towards waterfall (Subject to weather conditions) Visit to Severnoe Siyanie park (Active Recreational Husky Park) Reindeer Sledge Ride (Subject to weather conditions) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs. age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Blackout Period: 15th December 26 – 15th January 27. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability Terms And Conditions: Travel Validity: 01 November 2026 – 31 March 2027 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The