dor / Holiday Inn\xa0or similar in\xa0St. Petersburg'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDiscover St. Petersburg\nSt. Petersburg with entrance to Hermitage:\nMeet your English-speaking guide at the hotel lobby for a private tour by vehicle. Visit the world-renowned Hermitage Museum (entrance included), Kazan Cathedral, and Palace Square. Continue with a panoramic city tour featuring photo stops at Church of the Savior on Spilled Blood, St. Isaac’s Cathedral, the Bronze Horseman, and the historic Cruiser Aurora', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Cosmos Nevsky / Ambassador / Holiday Inn\xa0or similar in\xa0St. Petersburg'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\nStandard Category\n\n\n\n\nMoscow\n\n\nHotel Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSt. Petersburg\n\n\nCosmos Nevsky/Ambassador/Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nMurmansk\n\n\nAzimut/Meridian/Cosmos or Similar\n\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': '\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\xa0 \n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\nStandard Category\n\n\n\n\nMoscow\n\n\nHotel Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSt. Petersburg\n\n\nCosmos Nevsky/Ambassador/Holiday Inn or Similar\n\n\n\n\nMurmansk\n\n\nAzimut/Meridian/Cosmos or Similar\n\n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'RU', 'countryName': 'Russia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 155400.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily Buffet Breakfast except on Day 1.\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nMetro tour to explore some beautiful metro stations of Moscow with English speaking guide. (With Entrance Tickets)\nPanoramic City tour of Moscow (Sparrow hills / Moscow State University / Stalin Buildings / White House /Victory Park View / Cathedral of Christ The Savior / Bolshoi Theatre) with English Speaking Guide.\n1 walking tour of Red square / Kremlin area & other surrounding area of famous places of City (To explore the Real heart of the city).\nVisit Kremlin Inside Territory Area with Cathedral (Entrance tickets included), English speaking guide.\nMoscow River 5* Radisson Cruise ride (Cruise ticket Included) (2.30 hrs. Ride)\nThe Hermitage Museum (With Entrance Ticket) with English speaking guide.\nPanoramic City tour of Saint Petersburg city with English speaking in A/c Vehicle on private basis.\nVisit to Kazan Cathedral (Free Entrance) with English speaking guide.\nVisit to Palace Square.\nPanoramic City Tour of Murmansk\nVisit to Peterhof Palace and Parkland (With Entrance)\nVisit the Lenin Icebreaker Museum (without Entrance) Only Photostop\xa0\nHunting for Northern Lights Tours” on shared basis\nTeriberka (Subject to weather conditions)\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n3 Nights’ accommodation in Moscow based on the hotel category selected or similar\n3 Nights’ accommodation in St. Petersburg based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast (Except Day 1).\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Private Transfers on Point-to-Point Basis]\n\nPrivate Transfer from Moscow Airport to the Hotel\nPrivate Transfer from Moscow Hotel to the Train station\nPrivate Transfer from St. Petersburg train station to the hotel\nPrivate Transfer from St. Petersburg Hotel to the Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Economy Class Train ticket from Moscow to St. Petersburg (Subject to availability until ticketed)\xa0\n\nSightseeing:\xa0(The tours will operate on Private basis)\n\nPanoramic City tour of Moscow\nMoscow River Cruise\xa0\nRed Square Walking Tour\nVisit Kremlin Inside Territory Area with Cathedral (Entrance tickets included)\nMoscow Metro tour\nThe Hermitage Museum (With Entrance Ticket)\nVisit to Kazan Cathedral Only Photostop\xa0\nVisit to Palace Square.\nVisit to Peterhof Parkland\nPeter and Paul Fortress\nPanoramic City tour of Saint Petersburg city with English speaking in Vehicle on private basis\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs. age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\nBlackout Period: 15th December 26 – 15th January 27\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 01 November 2026 – 31 March 2027\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/44164_Radisson_Hotel_Cruise_Moscow_Russia_Optional_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/89933_Moscow_Kremlin_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/007596_KREMLIN_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/650718_Christ_the_Savior_Cathedral_Moscow_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/Petersburg7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/12117_Hermitage_Museum_St_Petersburg_Russia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015329/itinerary/Church_of_the_Saviour_on_Blood_St._Petersburg_Russia_753.jpgiti6.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014758', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014758', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Trending Turkiye - SIC Tour', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kusadasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kusadasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kusadasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG004643_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 94178, 'packageSummary': "The 'Trending Turkiye - SIC Tour' package is a 7-day tour covering Istanbul, Kusadasi, and Cappadocia. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia, the Blue Mosque, the ancient ruins of Ephesus, and the breathtaking volcanic landscapes of Cappadocia. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, historical sightseeing, and opportunities to experience local Turkish culture and famous hot air balloon rides.", 'images': ['Istanbul753.jpg', 'Istanbul.jpg', 'Cappadocia7532.jpg', 'Cappadocia7531.jpg', 'Kusadasi_1.jpg', 'Pamukkale.jpg', 'Temple_of_apollo_pamukkale.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 94178, 'thumbnailImage': '60842_Mevlana_Museum_in_Konya_Turkey_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cultural', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014758 is named 'Trending Turkiye - SIC Tour' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Istanbul, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival into Istanbul Transfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion Optional Activity: Bosphorus Dinner Cruise Enjoy an enchanting evening on the Bosphorus Strait with a leisurely dinner cruise that showcases Istanbul’s beauty by night. Sail between Europe and Asia as you pass iconic landmarks such as the Bosphorus Bridge, Dolmabahçe Palace, and the illuminated waterfront mansions. The experience is complemented by a delicious Turkish dinner and live entertainment, often including traditional music and folk dance performances, making it a memorable blend of scenic views, culture, and cuisine. [The supplement cost for this activity will be approx. US$ 80/- per adult & US$ 55/- for children below 6 years], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast and Local Lunch, Description: Full-Day Guided Tour Of Istanbul On Shared Basis (SIC) Istanbul City Tour : Between 07:30 and 09:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel (pickup time subject to hotel location) for a full day guided city tour. The tour includes visits to the Hagia Sophia Mosque (entrance not included), the pride of Byzantine architecture; the Byzantine Hippodrome, once the venue for ancient chariot races; and the Blue Mosque, renowned for its exquisite blue Iznik tiles. You will also visit the Topkapi Palace (entrance not included), the former residence of the Ottoman Sultans, followed by time at the Grand Bazaar, Turkey’s largest covered market with over 4,000 shops. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant, after which you will be transferred back to your hotel. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only. Entrance to the Hagia Sophia Mosque and Topkapi Palace is available at an additional supplement. Supplement costs: Hagia Sophia: US$ 35 - 40/- Per adult (*Under 8 years Free) Topkapi Palace US$ 65/- Per adult (*Under 6 years Free), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Istanbul To Cappadocia Transfers: Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight Upon arrival at Cappadocia, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the Hotel. Special Notes: Please note that the domestic flight from Istanbul to Cappadocia is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement. Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast and Local Lunch, Description: Explore Cappadocia Optional Activity: Hot Air Balloon If a hot air balloon ride is on your bucket list, Cappadocia offers one of the most iconic experiences in the world. Drift gently at sunrise above a surreal, lunar like landscape of volcanic rock formations, fairy chimneys, and honeycombed valleys, as dozens of vibrantly colored balloons rise alongside you. This unforgettable experience offers breathtaking panoramic views and spectacular photo opportunities. [The supplement cost for this activity will be upon “On Request Basis”] Please Note: Children below 6 years of age or under 120 cm in height are not permitted to participate in the hot air balloon ride. Cappadocia Sightseeing: After breakfast, between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel to begin a full day tour of Cappadocia. The first stop is Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley), known for its spectacular fairy chimneys and uniquely shaped rock formations set amidst beautiful landscape. You will then visit Pasabag (Monks Valley), famous for its remarkable double and triple headed rock formations, once used as hermit dwellings by monks. Lunch will be served in Avanos, a town renowned for its traditional pottery craftsmanship and located along the Red River (Kizilirmak). After lunch, continue to the Goreme Open Air Museum, the heart of Cappadocia, celebrated for its rock cut churches adorned with wall paintings dating back to the 10th century, depicting scenes from the life of Jesus and early Christian monastic life. The tour concludes with a photo stop at Uchisar Castle, a natural rock citadel and one of the largest fairy chimney formations in the region, offering panoramic views of Cappadocia. Special Notes: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kusadasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Cappadocia To Izmir Transfers: 1. Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight 2. Upon arrival at Izmir, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the hotel in Kusadasi. Special Notes: 1. Please note that the domestic flight from Cappadocia to Izmir is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement. 2. Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kusadasi, Meals: Breakfast & Local Lunch as a part of the tour, Description: Full Day Pamukkale Tour On Shared Basis (Sic) Transfers: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick-up for the same will be from selected central points Full Day Pamukkale Tour on SIC basis: Enjoy a full-day guided tour of Pamukkale, including visits to the ancient city of Hierapolis and its remarkable landmarks. Explore the Domitian Gate, Latrina, Oil Factory, Agora, Byzantine Gate, Triton Fountain, and the Temple of Apollo, gaining insight into the region’s rich historical heritage. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant. The tour concludes with time to admire the spectacular Pamukkale travertines - the famous white terraces formed by mineral-rich thermal waters. Guests may enjoy a unique barefoot walk across these natural formations. At the end of the tour, return transfer to the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Kusadasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Izmir Transfers: From Kusadasi hotel to Izmir Airport in a private transfer., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 94178.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nFour Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy Hotel/ Konak Taksim\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nDedeli Cave / Sunak Cave Hote\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nEfe Boutique Hotel/ Karaaslan Inn hotel/ Ladies Beach or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n5* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nThe Elysium Taksim/Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa Hotel\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nHanedan Cave Suites / Acer Cave Suites\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nSignature Blue Hotel / Le Bleu Hotel / Ramada Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) // Half Board if you opt for 5* accommodation in Kusadasi\n3 Local Lunches as a part of the itinerary\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Istanbul based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Kusdasi based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) // Half Board if you opt for 5* accommodation in Kusadasi 3 Local Lunches as a part of the itinerary Transportation: Private Airport Transfer from Istanbul Airport to Hotel Private transfer from Istanbul hotel to Istanbul Airprort Private Airport Transfer from Kayseri Airport to Cappadocia Hotel Private Airport transfer from Cappadocia Hotel to Kayseri Airport Private Airport Transfer from Izmir Airport to Kusadasi Hotel Private Airport transfer from Kusadasi Hotel to Izmir Airport Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Full Day Guided Tour of Istanbul on sharing basis (SIC) Cappadocia Sightseeing Tour on sharing basis (SIC) Full Day Pamukkale Tour on sharing basis (SIC) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. Blackout Dates: HOLIDAY DATE National Sovereignty and Children’s Day 23-04-2026 Labor and Solidarity Day 01-05-2026 Commemoration of Atatürk, Youth and Sports Day 19-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 1st day 27-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 2nd day 28-05-2026 Eid al-Adha 3rd day 29-04-2026 Eid al-Adha last day 30-05-2026 Democracy and National Unity Day 15-07-2026 Victory Day 30-08-2026 Republic Day 29-10-2026. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TERMS AND CONDITIONS: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Trending Turkiye - SIC Tour' package is a 7-day tour covering Istanbul, Kusadasi, and Cappadocia. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia, the Blue Mosque, the ancient ruins of Ephesus, and the breathtaking volcanic landscapes of Cappadocia. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, historical sightseeing, and opportunities to experience local Turkish culture and famous hot air balloon rides.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'Arrival into Istanbul\nTransfers: Upon arrival you will be met the representative & transferred to the hotel on private basis.\nSpecial Note: Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion\nOptional Activity: Bosphorus Dinner Cruise\nEnjoy an enchanting evening on the Bosphorus Strait with a leisurely dinner cruise that showcases Istanbul’s beauty by night. Sail between Europe and Asia as you pass iconic landmarks such as the Bosphorus Bridge, Dolmabahçe Palace, and the illuminated waterfront mansions. The experience is complemented by a delicious Turkish dinner and live entertainment, often including traditional music and folk dance performances, making it a memorable blend of scenic views, culture, and cuisine. [The supplement cost for this activity will be approx. US$ 80/- per adult & US$ 55/- for children below 6 years]', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Four Side Lions Taksim\xa0(Value) /\xa0Hilton Double Tree Piyalepasa\xa0(Premium) or similar in\xa0Istanbul'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nFull-Day Guided Tour Of Istanbul On Shared Basis (SIC)\nIstanbul City Tour : Between 07:30 and 09:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel (pickup time subject to hotel location) for a full day guided city tour. The tour includes visits to the Hagia Sophia Mosque (entrance not included), the pride of Byzantine architecture; the Byzantine Hippodrome, once the venue for ancient chariot races; and the Blue Mosque, renowned for its exquisite blue Iznik tiles. You will also visit the Topkapi Palace (entrance not included), the former residence of the Ottoman Sultans, followed by time at the Grand Bazaar, Turkey’s largest covered market with over 4,000 shops.\nLunch will be served at a local restaurant, after which you will be transferred back to your hotel.\nSpecial Notes:\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\nEntrance to the Hagia Sophia Mosque and Topkapi Palace is available at an additional supplement.\nSupplement costs:\nHagia Sophia: US$ 35 - 40/- Per adult (*Under 8 years Free)\xa0 \xa0\nTopkapi Palace US$ 65/- Per adult (*Under 6 years Free)', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Local Lunch', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Four Side Lions Taksim\xa0(Value) /\xa0Hilton Double Tree Piyalepasa\xa0(Premium) or similar in\xa0Istanbul'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nIstanbul To Cappadocia\nTransfers:\n\nToday you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight\nUpon arrival at Cappadocia, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the Hotel.\n\nSpecial Notes:\n\nPlease note that the domestic flight from Istanbul to Cappadocia is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement.\nPlease note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Dedeli\xa0Cave\xa0\xa0(Value) /\xa0Hanedan\xa0Cave\xa0Suites\xa0(Premium)\xa0or similar in\xa0Cappadocia'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nExplore Cappadocia\xa0\nOptional Activity: Hot Air Balloon\nIf a hot air balloon ride is on your bucket list, Cappadocia offers one of the most iconic experiences in the world. Drift gently at sunrise above a surreal, lunar like landscape of volcanic rock formations, fairy chimneys, and honeycombed valleys, as dozens of vibrantly colored balloons rise alongside you. This unforgettable experience offers breathtaking panoramic views and spectacular photo opportunities. [The supplement cost for this activity will be upon “On Request Basis”]\nPlease Note:\xa0 Children below 6 years of age or under 120 cm in height are not permitted to participate in the hot air balloon ride.\nCappadocia Sightseeing: After breakfast, between 09:00 and 10:00 hrs, you will be picked up from your hotel to begin a full day tour of Cappadocia. The first stop is Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley), known for its spectacular fairy chimneys and uniquely shaped rock formations set amidst beautiful landscape.\nYou will then visit Pasabag (Monks Valley), famous for its remarkable double\xa0and triple headed rock formations, once used as hermit dwellings by monks. Lunch will be served in Avanos, a town renowned for its traditional pottery craftsmanship and located along the Red River (Kizilirmak).\nAfter lunch, continue to the Goreme Open Air Museum, the heart of Cappadocia, celebrated for its rock cut churches adorned with wall paintings dating back to the 10th century, depicting scenes from the life of Jesus and early Christian monastic life.\nThe tour concludes with a photo stop at Uchisar Castle, a natural rock citadel and one of the largest fairy chimney formations in the region, offering panoramic views of Cappadocia.\nSpecial Notes:\xa0\n\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Local Lunch', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Dedeli\xa0Cave\xa0\xa0(Value) /\xa0Hanedan\xa0Cave\xa0Suites\xa0(Premium)\xa0or similar in\xa0Cappadocia'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nCappadocia To Izmir\nTransfers:\xa0\n1. Today you will have a private transfer from the hotel to the Airport for onward flight\n2. Upon arrival at Izmir, there will be a private transfer from the airport to the hotel in Kusadasi.\nSpecial Notes:\xa0\n1. Please note that the domestic flight from Cappadocia to Izmir is not included in the tour cost and will be charged as an additional supplement.\xa0\n2. Please note the standard check in time would be at 14:00 hrs. or subject to hotel discretion', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Efe Boutique Hotel/ Karaaslan Inn hotel/ Ladies Beach or similar\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nFull Day Pamukkale Tour On Shared Basis (Sic)\nTransfers: The sightseeing will be on a shared basis and the pick-up for the same will be from selected central points\nFull Day Pamukkale Tour on SIC basis: Enjoy a full-day guided tour of Pamukkale, including visits to the ancient city of Hierapolis and its remarkable landmarks. Explore the Domitian Gate, Latrina, Oil Factory, Agora, Byzantine Gate, Triton Fountain, and the Temple of Apollo, gaining insight into the region’s rich historical heritage.\nLunch will be served at a local restaurant.\nThe tour concludes with time to admire the spectacular Pamukkale travertines - the famous white terraces formed by mineral-rich thermal waters. Guests may enjoy a unique barefoot walk across these natural formations.\nAt the end of the tour, return transfer to the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast & Local Lunch as a part of the tour', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Efe Boutique Hotel/ Karaaslan Inn hotel/ Ladies Beach or similar\n\xa0'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Izmir\nTransfers: From Kusadasi hotel to Izmir Airport in a private transfer.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'NA'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n4* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nFour Sides Lion Taksim / Erboy Hotel/ Konak Taksim\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nDedeli Cave / Sunak Cave Hote\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nEfe Boutique Hotel/ Karaaslan Inn hotel/ Ladies Beach or similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Name\n\n\n5* Category\n\n\n\n\nIstanbul\n\n\nThe Elysium Taksim/Doubletree Hilton Piyalepasa Hotel\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nCappadocia\n\n\nHanedan Cave Suites / Acer Cave Suites\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\nKusadasi\n\n\nSignature Blue Hotel / Le Bleu Hotel / Ramada Hotel or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCity Na