 City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC)\xa0\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'IMPORTANT NOTES:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/Titles753.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/LondonTowerBridge7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/London7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/Paris_new_753_2.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/Interlaken2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/Jungfraujoch75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/Glacier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014530/itinerary/9063_Lucerne_Switzerland_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015258', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015258', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Turkish Extravaganza - Winter', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cappadocia', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Antalya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Antalya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pamukkale', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Izmir ', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 252416, 'packageSummary': "The 'Turkish Extravaganza - Winter' package is an 11-day tour covering Istanbul, Cappadocia, Izmir, Antalya, and Pamukkale. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia and Blue Mosque in Istanbul, the ancient ruins of Ephesus near Izmir, and the stunning white thermal terraces of Pamukkale. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a breathtaking hot air balloon ride over the unique fairy chimneys of Cappadocia, and leisurely walks through the historic streets of Antalya's old town.", 'images': ['RepublicMonumentIstanbul1.jpg', 'BlueMosque2.jpg', 'BosphorusCruise753.jpg', 'Anitkabir753.jpg', 'Cappodocia753.jpg', 'Mevlana753.jpg', '0917_Kaleici_old_town753.jpg', '85319_Cotton_castle_travertine_pools_Pamukkale_Turkey_753.jpg', 'Amphitheaterephesus753.jpg', 'BursaGrandMosqueorUluCamilargestBursaTurkey_151019012.jpg', 'GrandBazar.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 252416, 'thumbnailImage': 'Turkey2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015258 is named 'Turkish Extravaganza - Winter' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Istanbul, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Turkey - ‘Istanbul is the New COOL’. Welcome to Istanbul, Turkey. Connecting two continents, Istanbul is the coolest city in the world because of its rich cultural heritage and distinctive beauty. On arrival at Istanbul Airport, you will be greeted and assisted by local representative/tour manager. Transfer to hotel & check in. The check-in time is 1500 Hrs. Please arrive max by 1200 hrs into Istanbul. (Check the voucher for the exact Exit gates upon arrival at IST airport) Check into your room and relax time permitting. Evening, get ready to explore Taksim Square and then have a nice walking tour of Istiklal Street. Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Overnight in Istanbul., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Explore Istanbul Post breakfast start your exploration of this amazing and unique city today. Visit the Blue Mosque (appropriate clothing will be required), Hippodrome. Next visit Dolmabahçe Palace (to be replaced with Topkapi Palace if closed). Indian Lunch at an Indian restaurant. Next, proceed for a photostop at Hagia Sophia mosque and end your day with free time for shopping at the super Grand Bazaar. Dinner at an Indian restaurant., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Bosphorus cruise – Drive to Ankara. Breakfast and check out from your hotel. Next, we take the amazing Bosphorus cruise tour in private boat. View the Bosphorus Strait which defines Istanbul. It is the divide between Europe and Asia, and the main connection between the Black Sea and the Sea of Marmara. Dotted with parks and elaborate Ottoman mansions, including Dolmabahçe Palace, and spanned by three intercontinental bridges. Next Lunch at an Indian restaurant. Drive towards Ankara the capital city of Turkey. Driving time is approx 6 hours. Dinner at a Local restaurant / at hotel. Overnight in Ankara., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Panoramic Tour of Ankara – Proceed to the magical fairytale land of Cappadocia After breakfast at the hotel check out and enjoy a quick panoramic city tour of Ankara. Photostop at the Mausoleum of Ataturk (Anitkabir). Next, we proceed towards Cappadocia. Arrive at Cappadocia and enjoy Indian Lunch at Indian restaurant. Driving time is approx 3 hours. Time permitting, check in at your hotel. Next enjoy Cardak Underground City, one of Cappadocia's many hidden wonders, offers a glimpse into the past. Carved into volcanic rock, this multi-level city served as a refuge for early Christians. You can explore its intricate tunnels, ventilation shafts, and ingenious design. Indian Dinner at an Indian restaurant., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Cappadocia, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Full day tour of Cappadocia OPTIONAL – HOT AIR BALLOON EXPERIENCE IN CAPPADOCIA - Soaring above Cappadocia in a hot air balloon is an unforgettable experience. As you drift over the unique fairy chimneys and valleys, you'll witness breathtaking sunrises and panoramic views of this otherworldly landscape. It's a truly magical way to explore this ancient region. NOTE – The rates for Hot Air Balloon fluctuate a lot due to demand and supply pressures locally. Kindly check all prices before you confirm the Hot Air Balloon ride with us. This activity is heavily weather dependent. Optional: Hot Air Balloon (01 April 2026 - 30 September 2026) USD ----- per person Post breakfast at the hotel we start the day by visiting Goreme open-air museum, a UNESCO heritage site. Next, we visit Devrent valley followed by Love valley. Enjoy Indian Lunch at an Indian restaurant. Enjoy Avanos village pottery workshop and panoramic photostop at Esentepe hill and photo stop at Uçhisar village. Finish the day with Onyx demonstration workshop at gem store. Indian Dinner at an Indian restaurant., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Antalya, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Konya – Antalya – The Turkish Rivera Breakfast and check out. Proceed by coach to Konya. Arrive in Konya. Driving time is approx. 3 hours between Cappadocia to Konya for local lunch. Enjoy a quick visit to Mevlana Museum which is free entrance. Next, we proceed to Antalya. Driving time is approx. 3 hours 30 mins between Konya to Antalya. Arrive and check into your hotel. Indian Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Evening is free to explore the vibrant nightlife of Antalya on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Antalya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Antalya Kaleici Old Town Tour. Breakfast. Today, enjoy a walking tour of Antalya Kaleici old town with photostops at Hadrian's Gate - An ancient Roman archway built to welcome Emperor Hadrian; The Clock Tower - A 9th-century medieval clock tower and Ancient City Walls amongst others. Indian Lunch Optional tours available on request. Indian Dinner at an Indian restaurant., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Pamukkale, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Onto Pamukkale. Visit the Ancient city of Hierapolis and the Cotton Castles of Pamukkale Breakfast and check out. Proceed to Pamukkale. Driving time is approx.3 hours between Antalya to Pamukkale. Arrive and enjoy a local lunch. Visit Hierapolis and Cotton Castles of Pamukkale. It’s an unreal landscape, made up of mineral forests, petrified waterfalls and a series of terraced basins given the name of Pamukkale (Cotton Palace). Check in. Free time to enjoy the Mud Pool Bath at your hotel which is in the hotel premises. Do bring your swimwear. Local Dinner at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Izmir , Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Ephesus Ruins and Sirince Village. Drive to Izmir hotel. After Breakfast, check out and proceed to Ephesus (Approx 2 hours’ drive), which is one of the best well-kept Greco- Roman ancient city in the world. This is a walking tour. Next, we visit the village of Sirince for a local lunch. Walk through the narrow, cobbled alleyways. The name, Sirince, suits this village perfectly. It means ‘pleasant,’ 'lovely,' 'sweet.' Drive towards Izmir. Driving time is approx. 2 hours. Check into your hotel. Local Dinner at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Proceed to Bursa and onto Istanbul Post breakfast, check-out and proceed to Bursa. It’s approx. 3 hours 30 mins journey. Next, have an Indian lunch and enjoy a panoramic city tour and time permitting Green Mosque. Later we drive towards Istanbul. Driving time is approx. 2 hours. (approx. as depends on traffic conditions). Upon arrival Indian Dinner at a local Indian restaurant., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart from Istanbul Breakfast and check out. Free time for last minute shopping at Spice Market. (This visit depends on your flight timings). No refunds if not visited. Local Lunch depending on flight timing. Transfer towards the Istanbul airport where your memorable tour of Turkey comes to an end. Distances: Istanbul to Ankara: 456km Ankara to Cappadocia: 300km Cappadocia to Konya: 234km Konya to Antalaya: 267km Antalya to Pammukale: 235km Pamukkale to Ephesus: 199km Izmir to Bursa: 346km Bursa to Istanbul: 154km Important Note: The routing of the itinerary may change as per flight & hotel availability Please DO NOT issue any tickets without confirming with the sales team JD cost does not include any main flights 04 passengers in one room are not allowed. Maximum capacity is 03 passengers Standard Hotel check-in time will be 1500 hours and check out at 1000 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 252416.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights’ accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n01 night accommodation in Ankara at Hotel New Park Ankara or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia at Hotel Barcello or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Antalya in Ring Downtown or similar\n01 night accommodation in Pamukkale in Hotel Pam Thermal or similar\n01 night accommodation in Izmir in Radisson Blu Aliaga or similar\n01 night accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily breakfast (Except Day 01)\n06 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian lunches\xa0\n04 local lunches*\xa0\n07 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian dinners)\n03 local dinners\xa0\nAll local meals will have local mix of authentic Turkish dishes and some international options to cater to a diverse clientele (depending on location to location).\n. Inclusions: Cost of Visa & Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour upto age of 58 years Return economy class Airfare ex India on Indigo / Royal Jordanian / Oman Air / Kuwait / Gulf Airways or similar airlines. Our main airline carrier is Indigo. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above mentioned itinerary All transfers & excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly & multilingual Thomas Cook Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 25 customers) or a local Representative. Visa Requirements: Turkish Visa. If you are holding an American valid visa, you might be eligible for an online Turkish Visa.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Applicable Government Taxes are additional. The tour cost does not include tips payable locally to the Tour Manager (USD 5 per person per day), POE charges & passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, food & drink that are not a part of the package. Additional Meals that are not mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees & local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note The group tour will operate with a Tour Manager subject to a minimum of 20 full-paying passengers travelling together There is a possibility that your TourManager could change in-between the tour On days when you are taking internal flights, there is a possibility that we might provide packed meal in case the flight timing does not suit the meal time As a third person in a Triple room, in some cities no extra bed or cot will be provided. Instead a room with two queen beds will be provided. OR in some cities a king bed with a roll away bed will be provided. Taxes as applicable extra. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members Land surcharges due to Local Events applicable on certain departures All local taxes and services (Presently calculated as prevailing on 01st July 2018). Some optional excursions are subject to minimum 20 paying passengers OR if less than 20 passengers then the optional will operates on Seat in Coach basis’s Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy A person below 12 years of age on date of return flight will be considered a child A baby below 24 months of age on date of return flight will be considered an infant Functioning of Air cooling/Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. All the internal flights will allow one piece of check in bag per person up to 20kg and carryon luggage will be upto 7kgs only For Turkey it is essential to carry your warm clothes & wollens. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEP200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Turkish Extravaganza - Winter' package is an 11-day tour covering Istanbul, Cappadocia, Izmir, Antalya, and Pamukkale. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hagia Sophia and Blue Mosque in Istanbul, the ancient ruins of Ephesus near Izmir, and the stunning white thermal terraces of Pamukkale. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a breathtaking hot air balloon ride over the unique fairy chimneys of Cappadocia, and leisurely walks t