ls and a series of terraced basins given the name of Pamukkale (Cotton Palace). Check in. Free time to enjoy the Mud Pool Bath at your hotel which is in the hotel premises. Do bring your swimwear.\nLocal Dinner at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Pam Thermal or similar in\xa0Pamukkale\xa0'}, {'day': 9, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nEphesus Ruins and Sirince\xa0Village. Drive to Izmir hotel.\nAfter Breakfast, check out and proceed to Ephesus (Approx 2 hours’ drive), which is one of the best well-kept Greco- Roman ancient city in the world. This is a walking tour.\nNext, we visit the village of Sirince for a local lunch. Walk through the narrow, cobbled alleyways. The name, Sirince, suits this village perfectly. It means ‘pleasant,’ 'lovely,' 'sweet.' Drive towards Izmir. Driving time is approx. 2 hours.\nCheck into your hotel. Local Dinner at the hotel.\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Radisson Blu Aliaga or similar in Izmir'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nProceed to Bursa and onto Istanbul\nPost breakfast, check-out and proceed to Bursa. It’s approx. 3 hours 30 mins journey.\nNext, have an Indian lunch and enjoy a panoramic city tour and time permitting Green Mosque. Later we drive towards Istanbul. Driving time is approx. 2 hours. (approx. as depends on traffic conditions). Upon arrival Indian Dinner at a local Indian restaurant.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar in\xa0Istanbul\xa0'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart from Istanbul\nBreakfast and check out. Free time for last minute shopping at Spice Market. (This visit depends on your flight timings). No refunds if not visited.\nLocal Lunch depending on flight timing. Transfer towards the Istanbul airport where your memorable tour of Turkey comes to an end.\n\xa0\nDistances:\n\nIstanbul to Ankara: 456km\nAnkara to Cappadocia: 300km\nCappadocia to Konya: 234km\nKonya to Antalaya: 267km\nAntalya to Pammukale: 235km\nPamukkale to Ephesus: 199km\nIzmir to Bursa: 346km\nBursa to Istanbul: 154km\n\nImportant Note:\n\nThe routing of the itinerary may change as per flight & hotel availability\nPlease DO NOT issue any tickets without confirming with the sales team\xa0\nJD cost does not include any main flights\n04 passengers in one room are not allowed. Maximum capacity is 03 passengers\xa0\nStandard Hotel check-in time will be 1500 hours and check out at 1000 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n01 night accommodation in Ankara at Hotel New Park Ankara or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia at Hotel Barcello or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Antalya in Ring Downtown or similar\n01 night accommodation in Pamukkale in Hotel Pam Thermal or similar\n01 night accommodation in Izmir in Radisson Blu Aliaga or similar\n01 night accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n01 night accommodation in Ankara at Hotel New Park Ankara or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia at Hotel Barcello or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Antalya in Ring Downtown or similar\n01 night accommodation in Pamukkale in Hotel Pam Thermal or similar\n01 night accommodation in Izmir in Radisson Blu Aliaga or similar\n01 night accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'TR', 'countryName': 'Turkey', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 252400.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n01 night accommodation in Ankara at Hotel New Park Ankara or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Cappadocia at Hotel Barcello or similar\n02 nights’ accommodation in Antalya in Ring Downtown or similar\n01 night accommodation in Pamukkale in Hotel Pam Thermal or similar\n01 night accommodation in Izmir in Radisson Blu Aliaga or similar\n01 night accommodation in Istanbul at Crowne Plaza Harbiye or similar\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily breakfast (Except Day 01)\n06 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian lunches\xa0\n04 local lunches*\xa0\n07 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian dinners)\n03 local dinners\xa0\nAll local meals will have local mix of authentic Turkish dishes and some international options to cater to a diverse clientele (depending on location to location).\n'], 'visa': ['\nTurkish Visa. If you are holding an American valid visa, you might be eligible for an online Turkish Visa.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAs per Itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'Istanbul:\xa0\n\nTaksim Square & Istiklal Street Walking Tour\nDolmabahce Palace\nIf Dolmabahçe Palace Is Not Open, We Will Take You To Topkapi Palace\nVisit Spice Market\nBlue Mosque\xa0\nHippodrome\nGrand Bazaar\nPhotostop At St Sophia Mosque (Hagia Sophia)\nBosphorus Cruise\n\nAnkara:\xa0\n\nPanoramic Tour Of The Capital City Of Turkey – Ankara\nPhotostop At The Mausoleum Of Ataturk (Anitkabir)\n\nCappadocia:\xa0\n\nGoreme Open Air Museum-Unesco\nDevrent Valley And Love Valley\nAvanos Village Pottery Workshop\nPanoramic Photostop At Esentepe Hill\nCardak Underground City\nPanoramic Photostop At Uchisar Village\nOnyx Demonstration Workshop At Gem Store\nOptional – Hot Air Balloon Experience\n\nKonya\n\nMevlana Museum\n\nAntalya:\n\nAntalya Kaleici Old Town Tour\n\nPamukkale:\n\nPamukkale Hierapolis – Unesco\nPamukkale Cotton Castle – Travertines Formations\xa0\nMud Pool Bath At The Hotel\n\nIzmir:\n\nUnesco Ephesus Ruins\nSirince Village\n\nBursa:\n\nPanoramic City Tour Of Bursa With Green Mosque Of Bursa\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class Airfare ex India on Indigo / Royal Jordanian / Oman Air / Kuwait / Gulf Airways or similar airlines. Our main airline carrier is Indigo.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nCost of Visa & Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour upto age of 58 years\nReturn economy class Airfare ex India on Indigo / Royal Jordanian / Oman Air / Kuwait / Gulf Airways or similar airlines. Our main airline carrier is Indigo.\nSightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above mentioned itinerary\nAll transfers & excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly & multilingual Thomas Cook Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 25 customers) or a local Representative.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements: \n\nTurkish Visa. If you are holding an American valid visa, you might be eligible for an online Turkish Visa.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\nApplicable Government Taxes are additional.\nThe tour cost does not include tips payable locally to the Tour Manager (USD 5 per person per day), POE charges & passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\xa0\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, food & drink that are not a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals that are not mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees & local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note\n\nThe group tour will operate with a Tour Manager subject to a minimum of 20 full-paying passengers travelling together\nThere is a possibility that your TourManager could change in-between the tour\nOn days when you are taking internal flights, there is a possibility that we might provide packed meal in case the flight timing does not suit the meal time\nAs a third person in a Triple room, in some cities no extra bed or cot will be provided. Instead a room with two queen beds will be provided. OR in some cities a king bed with a roll away bed will be provided. Taxes as applicable extra.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members\nLand surcharges due to Local Events applicable on certain departures\nAll local taxes and services (Presently calculated as prevailing on 01st July 2018).\nSome optional excursions are subject to minimum 20 paying passengers OR if less than 20 passengers then the optional will operates on Seat in Coach basis’s\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy\nA person below 12 years of age on date of return flight will be considered a child\nA baby below 24 months of age on date of return flight will be considered an infant\nFunctioning of Air cooling/Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\nAll the internal flights will allow one piece of check in bag per person up to 20kg and carryon luggage will be upto 7kgs only\nFor Turkey it is essential to carry your warm clothes & wollens\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/Turkey2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/RepublicMonumentIstanbul1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/BlueMosque2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/BosphorusCruise753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/Anitkabir753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/Cappodocia753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/Mevlana753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/0917_Kaleici_old_town753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/85319_Cotton_castle_travertine_pools_Pamukkale_Turkey_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/Amphitheaterephesus753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/BursaGrandMosqueorUluCamilargestBursaTurkey_151019012.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015258/itinerary/GrandBazar.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012966', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012966', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Trending  Georgia', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bakuriani', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bakuriani', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012966_0_20260817122038.pdf', 'price': 71913, 'packageSummary': "The 'Trending Georgia' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic capital of Tbilisi and the scenic mountain resort of Bakuriani. The itinerary includes guided city tours of Tbilisi's charming Old Town, visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, and a scenic cable car ride offering breathtaking views of the city. Participants will also travel to Bakuriani to enjoy its beautiful alpine landscapes, engage in exciting outdoor activities, and experience traditional Georgian hospitality, delicious local cuisine, and wine tastings.", 'images': ['georgia_753.png', 'Kakheti-tour_C.jpg', 'Bakuriani_C.jpg', 'Borjomi-Kharagauli National Park_C.jpg', 'Mtskheta_Church_Georgia_753.jpg', 'Gudauri_C.jpg', 'Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 71913, 'thumbnailImage': 'Tibilisi_SRP_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG012966 is named \'Trending  Georgia\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival - Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Upon arrival at Tbilisi, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) Go for Tbilisi City Tour. Start with the world largest orthodox Holy Trinity cathedral, Continue to Rike Park and then cross the Bridge of Peace. Proceed to the clock tower of famous Rezo Gabriadze Theatre, Anchiskhati basilica, visit Sioni Cathedral. Walk down to the district of Sulfur bath houses passing by the only mosque in Tbilisi. Stroll through the Sharden area full of narrow streets with cozy cafés, wine tasting bars, souvenir shops, and breathe in the living past. Continue to Metekhi church and monument to Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi. There we will take Cable car to Narikala Fortress. The best place to release adrenaline, dopamine, oxytocin, serotonin, endorphins and just feel happy. Charge with emotions and unforgettable memories., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Sighnaghi – Kakheti Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Kakheti, with its centuries-old culture, is very rich in monuments of different periods. Here you will find ancient settlements, interesting and distinctive medieval temples, which were also important cultural and educational centers, impressive castles, Tush towers and slate houses, etc. This region is also unique and diverse in terms of nature. There is also Alazani area which is the biggest straight place in East of Georgia. In this region, you will meet a completely different landscape from other regions of Georgia. Sighnaghi (The City of Love), KTW Wine Factory with wine tasting, Bodbe Monastery, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Borjomi – Bakuriani (PVT Basis) Breakfast at the Hotel Modern Borjomi is one of the popular resorts in Georgia, which is suitable for ecotourism and family holidays. Its convenient location in the beautiful mountains of the Lesser Caucasus attracts many tourists all year round with its landscapes, the opportunity to relax and improve your health. There are dozens of mineral springs in Borjomi. The main mineral spring is located in the Central Park of Borjomi. Visit to the city park Borjomi. Borjomi Central Park is a well-groomed place with a lot of vegetation, clean air, which is considered healing here, and a pleasant atmosphere where residents and guests of the city like to relax. Central Park gained its fame thanks to the city’s main hot spring of mineral water, which anyone can try for free. The source is located in the park in a beautiful blue pavilion with a dome with a glass roof. The main ally of the Central Park stretches along the Borjomula River passing here, over which bridges are installed, the length of the park itself is about a kilometer., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bakuriani City Tour & Martvili Canyon (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Assembly at hotel lobby. Proceed to Martvili Canyon (3.5 hrs approx.) Tours to Bakuriani ski resort is an excellent getaway to enjoy the mountainous nature of Georgia, where you can ski in winter; and take some treatment in the resort with healing springs in the off-season that is from March through November. Bakuriani has been a popular skiing destination for over 100 years, and once skier sportsmen from all around USSR used to gather there for training. If you fancy skiing and snowboarding, then go with Bakuriani tours. You will definitely fall in love with this resort., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bakuriani, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bakuriani - Mtskheta - Jvari – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Check out and start the tour by driving to Mtskheta, the first capital of Georgia. Our road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bakuriani, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ananuri – Gudauri Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at Hotel Ananuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round tower, is mostly in ruins. Gudauri Ski Resort - is a small touristic settlement and ski mountain resort located at the altitude of 3,000m on the southern slopes of the Lesser Caucasus range of Georgia. Gudauri is situated 120 km from Tbilisi. You can reach it by the Georgian Military Road for about 2 hours by car. It has served as an important link between Europe and Asia since ancient times, though it was only after Russia’s annexation of east Georgia in the 19th century and the subsequent improvement of the track for troop movements that it became known as the “Military Highway”. Today it serves as the best route via which we can enjoy the dramatic scenery, crystal-clear air and indescribable grandeur of the mighty Caucasus Mountains. Vicinity of Stepantsminda is picturesque. There is a river Thergi running below the town, with snowed peaks of Caucasus rising among which the Mount Kazbek standing out, with its 5033m height. There are quite a few valley glaciers and forests, both deciduous and coniferous. Fresh mountain air and mineral springs of Stepantsminda are considered to be the main therapy for breathing or eating disorders., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice Valitiy from 01 Oct 2026 - 25 Mar 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-10 PAX STANDARD 569 624 706 VALUE 633 688 771 PREMIUM 856 912 994, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 71913.0. Hotels envisaged include: \nHotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n, \nHotel\xa0Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n, Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Premium) or similar in Bakuriani. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n, \nDaily\xa0breakfast,\xa0except\xa0on\xa0Day\xa01\n. Inclusions: 04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi. 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Bakuriani Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Sighnaghi – Kakheti Tour (PVT Basis) Tbilisi - Borjomi – Bakuriani (PVT Basis) Bakuriani City Tour & Martvili Canyon (PVT Basis) Bakuriani - Mtskheta - Jvari – Tbilisi (PVT Basis) Ananuri – Gudauri Tour (PVT Basis) Entrance fee for, Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, National park Borjomi Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa charges Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights services Meals not mentioned in the itinerary Any tips (Around USD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc ) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling BLACKOUT DATES – 15 DEC’26 – 06 JAN’27 (CHRISTMAS & NEW YEAR). Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions : The package price is valid until 25 MAR 2026 The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Trending Georgia' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic capital of Tbilisi and the scenic mountain resort of Bakuriani. The itinerary includes guided city tours of Tbilisi's charming Old Town, visits to the ancient Narikala Fortress, and a scenic cable car ride offering breathtaking views of the city. Participants will also travel to Bakuriani to enjoy its beautiful alpine landscapes, engage in exciting outdoor activities, and experience traditional Georgian hospitality, delicious local cuisine, and wine tastings.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival - Tbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nUpon arrival at Tbilisi, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.)\n\xa0\nGo for Tbilisi City Tour. Start with the world largest orthodox Holy Trinity cathedral, Continue to Rike Park and then cross the Bridge of Peace. Proceed to the clock tower of famous Rezo Gabriadze Theatre, Anchiskhati basilica, visit Sioni Cathedral. Walk down to the district of Sulfur bath houses passing by the only mosque in Tbilisi. Stroll through the Sharden area full of narrow streets with cozy cafés, wine tasting bars, souvenir shops, and breathe in the living past.\xa0\n\xa0\nContinue to Metekhi church and monument to Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi.\xa0\n\xa0\nThere we will take Cable car to Narikala Fortress. The best place to release adrenaline, dopamine, oxytocin, serotonin, endorphins and just feel happy. Charge with emotions and unforgettable memories.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nTbilisi - Sighnaghi – Kakheti Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nKakheti, with its centuries-old culture, is very rich in monuments of different periods. Here you will find ancient settlements, interesting and distinctive medieval temples, which were also important cultural and educational centers, impressive castles, Tush towers and slate houses, etc. This region is also unique and diverse in terms of nature. There is also Alazani area which is the biggest straight place in East of Georgia. In this region, you will meet a completely different landscape from other regions of Georgia. Sighnaghi (The City of Love), KTW Wine Factory with wine tasting, Bodbe Monastery', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nTbilisi - Borjomi – Bakuriani (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nBreakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nModern Borjomi is one of the popular resorts in Georgia, which is suitable for ecotourism and family holidays. Its convenient location in the beautiful mountains of the Lesser Caucasus attracts many tourists all year round with its landscapes, the opportunity to relax and improve your health. There are dozens of mineral springs in Borjomi. The main mineral spring is located in the Central Park of Borjomi.\xa0\nVisit to the city park Borjomi. Borjomi Central Park is a well-groomed place with a lot of vegetation, clean air, which is considered healing here, and a pleasant atmosphere where residents and guests of the city like to relax. Central Park gained its fame thanks to the city’s main hot spring of mineral water, which anyone can try for free. The source is located in the park in a beautiful blue pavilion with a dome with a glass roof. The main ally of the Central Park stretches along the Borjomula River passing here, over which bridges are installed, the length of the park itself is about a kilometer.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nBakuriani City Tour & Martvili Canyon (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nAssembly at hotel lobby. Proceed to Martvili Canyon (3.5 hrs approx.)\n\xa0\nTours to Bakuriani ski resort is an excellent getaway to enjoy the mountainous nature of Georgia, where you can ski in winter; and take some treatment in the resort with healing springs in the off-season that is from March through November. Bakuriani has been a popular skiing destination for over 100 years, and once skier sportsmen from all around USSR used to gather there for training. If you fancy skiing and snowboarding, then go with Bakuriani tours. You will definitely fall in love with this resort.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard) / Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value) / Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nBakuriani - Mtskheta - Jvari – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nCheck out and start the tour by driving to Mtskheta, the first capital of Georgia. Our road goes to the ancient city of Mtskheta - a must-visit place in Georgia. This ancient city is called the "Second Jerusalem". One of the most revered saints in Georgia, who brought Christianity to the country St. Nino lived under the blackberry bush in Samtavro monastery in Mtskheta and put the first cross on Mount Jvari, made of vine and intertwined with her own hair. We will visit two greatest shrines of the Christian world - Jvary Monastery and Svetitskhoveli Cathedral. The Heaton of the Lord is kept here. The cathedral was the coronation site of the Georgian kings as well as their burial place for centuries and still remains one of the most venerated places of worship for Georgian people.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard) / (Value) / (Premium) or similar in Bakuriani'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nAnanuri – Gudauri Tour (PVT Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at Hotel\nAnanuri Fortress - situated on the foreland by the Aragvi River, not far from Zhinvali water reservoir and about 70 km from Tbilisi, Georgia. It was built by the Dukes of Aragvi and its earliest parts date from the 13th century. The fortress is on the UNESCO Tentative list. The fortress consists of two fortifications joined by a crenelated curtain wall. The upper fortification with a large square tower, known as Sheupovari, is well-preserved. The lower fortification, with a round tower, is mostly in ruins.\nGudauri Ski Resort - is a small touristic settlement and ski mountain resort located at the altitude of 3,000m on the southern slopes of the Lesser Caucasus range of Georgia. Gudauri is situated 120 km from Tbilisi. You can reach it by the Georgian Military Road for about 2 hours by car. It has served as an important link between Europe and Asia since ancient times, though it was only after Russia’s annexation of east Georgia in the 19th century and the subsequent improvement of the track for troop movements that it became known as the “Military Highway”. Today it serves as the best route via which we can enjoy the dramatic scenery, crystal-clear air and indescribable grandeur of the mighty Caucasus Mountains. Vicinity of Stepantsminda is picturesque. There is a river\xa0 \xa0Thergi running below the town, with snowed peaks of Caucasus rising among which the Mount Kazbek standing out, with its 5033m height. There are quite a few valley glaciers and forests, both deciduous and coniferous. Fresh mountain air and mineral springs of Stepantsminda are considered to be the main therapy for breathing or eating disorders.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard) / (Value) / (Premium) or similar in Bakuriani'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture\n\xa0\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India.\n\xa0\n* The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice\nValitiy from 01 Oct 2026 - 25 Mar 2027\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n4-5 PAX\n6-7 PAX\n8-10 PAX\n\n\nSTANDARD\n569\n624\n706\n\n\nVALUE\n633\n688\n771\n\n\nPREMIUM\n856\n912\n994\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\nHotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n', '\nHotel\xa0Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n', 'Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Premium) or similar in Bakuriani'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\nHotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n', '1': '\nHotel\xa0Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n', '2': 'Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Premium) or similar in Bakuriani'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'GE', 'countryName': 'Georgia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 71900.0, 'hotels': ['\nHotel Ibis Budget Tbilisi (Standard)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani (Standard)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 78300.0, 'hotels': ['\nHotel\xa0Ramada by Wyndham Tbilisi (Value)\xa0or similar in Tbilisi\nHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in Bakuriani\n']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 100400.0, 'hotels': ['Hotel\xa0Tbilisi Marriott (Premium) or similar in TbilisiHotel Raimond Palace Bakuriani\xa0(Premium) or similar in Bakuriani']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n', '\nDaily\xa0breakfast,\xa0except\xa0on\xa0Day\xa01\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAirport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis\n'], 'sightseeing': ['\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Sighnaghi – Kakheti Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Borjomi – Bakuriani (PVT Basis)\nBakuriani City Tour & Martvili Canyon (PVT Basis)\nBakuriani - Mtskheta - Jvari – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nAnanuri – Gudauri Tour (PVT Basis)\nEntrance fee for, Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, National park Borjomi\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Tbilisi.\n02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Bakuriani\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\nAirport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis\nTbilisi City Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Sighnaghi – Kakheti Tour (PVT Basis)\nTbilisi - Borjomi – Bakuriani (PVT Basis)\nBakuriani City Tour & Martvili Canyon (PVT Basis)\nBakuriani - Mtskheta - Jvari – Tbilisi (PVT Basis)\nAnanuri – Gudauri Tour (PVT Basis)\nEntrance fee for, Cable Car in Tbilisi, KTW Wine tasting, 4x4 jeep to Gergeti, National park Borjomi\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 yrs.)\n', 'exclusions': '\nTCS & GST\nVisa charges\xa0\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable\xa0\nAll flights services\xa0\nMeals not mentioned in the itinerary\nAny tips (Around USD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver\xa0\nAnything not mentioned in the inclusions\nPre & Post tour services & cost\xa0\nExpenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc )\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\xa0\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\nMidnight surcharge\nThe rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling\nBLACKOUT DATES – 15 DEC’26 – 06 JAN’27 (CHRISTMAS & NEW YEAR)\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Terms and Conditions :\n\nThe package price is valid until 25 MAR 2026\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/Tibilisi_SRP_267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/georgia_753.png', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Kakheti-tour_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Bakuriani_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Borjomi-Kharagauli_National_Park_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Mtskheta_Church_Georgia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Gudauri_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012966/itinerary/Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014880', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014880', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Italian Charm With Southern Coast (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)     ', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rome', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amalfi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amalfi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Florence', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Venice', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Free upgrade to 1st class Train sector tickets'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014880_0_20260609181614.pdf', 'price': 238787, 'packageSummary': "The 'Italian Charm With Southern Coast (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 9-day tour covering Florence, Venice, Amalfi, and Rome. The itinerary features a seamless journey through these iconic Italian destinations, with key highlights including a complimentary upgrade to first-class train sector tickets for travel between the cities.", 'images': ['Rome753.jpg', 'Colosseum_753.jpg', 'Naples_753.jpg', '033755_Amalfi_Coast_Sorrento_Italy_753.jpg', '2987_Florence_753.jpg', 'LeaningTower.jpg', '62615_Venice_753.jpg', '71702_Venice_753.jpg', 'StMarkVenice.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 238787, 'thumbnailImage': 'Florence.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cultural', 'Durga Puja Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014880 is named \'Italian Charm With Southern Coast (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)     \' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Rome, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Italy Transfers: Upon your arrival at the Fiumicino Leonardo Da Vinci (FCO) airport, you will meet the representative and transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Rome, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Hop On Hop Off Tour Hop on Hop Off Tour: Discover Rome\'s iconic sights and landmarks on a hop on hop off bus tour, offering a comprehensive overview of all the city’s highlights. Disembark at any of the multiple stops to see popular landmarks such as the Vatican City, Circus Maximus, the Pantheon, or the Colosseum. While on board the bus, listen to recorded commentary in multiple languages that details the history, architecture, culture, and traditions of the Eternal City., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Amalfi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Rome To Naples Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Naples. (Duration approx. 1.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Naples train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Amalfi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Southern Coast - Day At Leisure Cattedrale di Sant’Andrea Tour (Optional): The Cattedrale di SantAndrea, perched above Amalfis main square, is a stunning 9th century cathedral dedicated to Saint Andrew. The tour begins with the dramatic climb up its grand staircase, leading to a striking façade adorned with colorful mosaics and neo Moorish details. Inside, you’ll explore a rich blend of Romanesque, Gothic, Baroque, and Arab Norman architecture. Highlights include the Cloister of Paradise with its elegant columns, the Basilica of the Crucifix housing sacred art, and the crypt where Saint Andrew’s relics rest. This experience offers history, art, and breathtaking views, making it a must see on the Amalfi Coast., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Naples To Florence Via Train Transfers: Private transfer from Amalfi/Sorrento hotel to Naples train station for your onwards journey to Florence (Duration approx. 3 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Florence train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Special Note: Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion. Florence with Uffizi Gallery (Optional): Depending on the train timing, you can opt for 14:15 hrs Visit of Florence with Uffizi Gallery - Afternoon slot. "You depart by coach for a brief excursion to Fiesole, a delightful town of Etruscan origin, positioned on the hill that dominates Florence and the Arno Valley. The tour continues to the historic centre for a visit to the Church of Santa Croce (outside view). A short walk through the historical streets in the heart of Florence brings you to the famous Piazza della Signoria, where you can admire the imposing Palazzo Vecchio (exterior) and the beautiful Loggia dei Lanzi. The tour will then take you to the famous Uffizi Gallery where it is possible to admire the superb paintings of the Botticelli, Michelangelo, Leonardo da Vinci, Raffaello, Giotto, Cimabue and Masaccio., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Florence, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Pisa And The Leaning Tower Tour Transfers: You will have a transfer from Florence to Pisa and back to Florence. Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour: This popular half day trip takes you from Florence through the scenic Tuscan countryside to the historic city of Pisa. The tour focuses on Piazza dei Miracoli, a UNESCO World Heritage site, where you’ll see the Leaning Tower, the Cathedral, the Baptistery, and the Monumental Cemetery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Florence To Venice Via Train Transfers: Make your way to the train station for your onward journey to Venice. (Duration approx. 2.5 hrs.) Upon your arrival at Venice train station, you will make your way to the hotel on your own. Gondola Ride: Experience Venice in the most Venetian way possible: via a shared gondola ride while being serenaded. Choose between an afternoon or evening ride and then begin the ride, as part of a group of eight different gondolas, with a singer aboard one of the boats. In addition to the song being sun to you, enjoy the sites of Venice\'s main landmarks, including the grand Canal and Palazzo Barberino., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Murano, Burano And Torcello Half-Day Tour Murano, Burano and Torcello Half Day Sightseeing Tour: Today visit Torcello, Murano, and Burano - three islands in the Venetian Lagoon - on this tour from Venice by motorboat. With a guide, watch glass being blown at a Murano glass factory, see historical cathedrals on Torcello, and admire exquisite handmade lace on Burano. This is a great way to see more than just the central sights of Venice and enjoy a cruise on the water. Highlights: Visit the three most famous islands in the Venetian Lagoon by motorboat Watch master glass blowers at work at a factory on Murano See Byzantine churches on Torcello - the Church of Santa Fosca Browse for lace on Burano and admire the painted houses McArthurGlen Designer Outlet (Optional): Later you can opt to visit the McArthurGlen Designer Outlet in Noventa di Piave is the most prestigious shopping outlet in Veneto, where you can find the most prestigious fashion with discounts up to 70% all around the year. Located just 30 minutes by car from Venice. Over 100 shops, restaurants, bars, lounges, play areas for children, located in a beautiful setting with architectural mosaics and frescoes inspired by the palaces in Venice and Treviso, where you can satisfy your thirst for great fashion, taking advantage of the offers and services designed specifically to make time spent here unforgettable., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Venice, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Venice Transfers: From Venice hotel to airport, you will have a private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 238787.0. Hotels envisaged i