Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability.\n\n\xa0\nTerms & Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/Florence.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/Rome753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/Colosseum_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/Naples_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/033755_Amalfi_Coast_Sorrento_Italy_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/2987_Florence_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/LeaningTower.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/62615_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/71702_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014880/itinerary/StMarkVenice.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014698', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014698', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Paris - City Of Love - Honeymoon Special', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chantilly', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chantilly', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Enjoy a magical Paris evening with fine French dining on a romantic Seine cruise Discover Paris freely and romantically with a complimentary 24 hour Hop On Hop Off ticket Wander hand in hand through Chantilly, the elegant town of art, history, and romance Create timeless Paris memories together with a romantic photoshoot at the city’s iconic landmarks Craft your own fragrance in a romantic Paris perfume workshop that leaves a lasting impression Special Gift Hamper'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014698_0_20260917093317.pdf', 'price': 139180, 'packageSummary': "The 'Paris - City Of Love - Honeymoon Special' package is a romantic 6-day tour covering the elegant destinations of Chantilly and Paris. The itinerary offers couples a magical evening with fine French dining on a scenic Seine cruise, a complimentary 24-hour Hop On Hop Off ticket to explore the city at their own pace, and a professional photoshoot at iconic landmarks to capture timeless memories. Additionally, participants will wander hand-in-hand through the historic town of Chantilly, craft a custom fragrance in a romantic perfume workshop, and receive a special gift hamper to complete their unforgettable honeymoon experience.", 'images': ['753_SeineRiverCruise.jpg', '52478_Eiffel_tower_Seine_river_Paris_France_753.jpg', 'EurostarTrainParistoLondon834761.jpg', 'Chantilly_the_palace.jpg', 'Chantilly.png', 'Rivercruisesceine.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 139180, 'thumbnailImage': '9686_Paris_HoneyMoon.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Honeymoon'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Honeymoon Special', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014698 is named \'Paris - City Of Love - Honeymoon Special\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive In Paris | The City Of Love | Welcome to Paris, City of light is the capital city of France. It is also the center of French economy, politics, traffic and culture. On arrival in Paris, you will have a private transfer to Paris Hotel. Welcome to Paris, with its monument-lined boulevards, museums, classical bistros and boutiques are enhanced by a new wave of multimedia galleries, creative wine bars, design shops and tech start ups. Check in at the hotel and rest of the day is free Depending on the flight arrival, Savor French cuisine as Paris glows around you Paris Seine Dinner Cruise Enjoy a memorable 2 hour evening cruise along the Seine, departing from Solférino Port near the Musee d’Orsay. Settle into a cozy, intimate setting as you savor a seasonal 3 course French dinner with coffee or tea. Glide past Paris\' illuminated landmarks - including the Musee d\'Orsay, Notre Dame, the Conciergerie, the Louvre, and the sparkling Eiffel Tower - framed beautifully through panoramic windows. A perfect romantic night out combining fine dining, iconic views, and the magic of Paris by night., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris | Effiel Tower With An Entertaining Evening (Moulin Rouge)| Breakfast at the hotel. See Paris your way - hop on, hop off, and explore at your own pace. Discover Paris with complete freedom on a 24 hour Big Bus HopOn HopOff tour. Ride aboard an open top double decker bus and explore the city’s iconic landmarks - Eiffel Tower, Notre Dame, Champs Elysees and more - getting on and off as often as you like. Enjoy pre recorded commentary in multiple languages, free onboard WiFi, and a mobile app with live bus tracking. The perfect relaxed, flexible way to experience Paris at your own pace. Ascend skywards in the lift to the first floor of the Eiffel Tower and step into the contemporary yet cozy atmosphere of the Madame Brasserie restaurant. Indulge in a three course lunch, consisting of a starter, main course, and dessert, made from locally sourced and seasonal products. {*This restaurant is high on demand and strictly subject to availability} Later, Get acquainted with Paris\' famous Iron Lady - The Eiffel Tower! Avoid long lines as much as possible thanks to your priority access. With audio guided comments through an audiopen and a map or mobile application to download, brings about a unique touring experience. Enjoy one of the most beautiful views of the capital & visit the monument from all angles without time limit. Optional Activity: A sparkling Parisian night at the Moulin Rouge: Champagne, glamour, and pure magic. Enjoy an unforgettable evening in Paris with the world famous Moulin Rouge "Feerie" show. Travel in comfort with return transportation in an air conditioned vehicle and delight in ½ bottle of champagne per person as you immerse yourself in a dazzling spectacle featuring 100 artists, including the iconic Doris Girls, 1,000 glittering costumes, vibrant sets, and breathtaking performances. After the show, you’ll be conveniently dropped off in central Paris, near your hotel or a major landmark for easy onward travel. A glamorous, quintessential Paris night out. [Supplement cost of €180/- Per Person], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Chantilly, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Paris - Chantilly | Via Train Breakfast at the hotel. You will make your way to the train station or avail of a private transfer at the cost of EUR 60 per person to Paris Train station for your onward journey to Chantilly. [The journey time will be approx. 30 – 35 mins with few limited direct train options as well] Welcome to Chantilly! Chantilly is famous around the world for many things: its chateau, racecourse, and equine heritage, lace-making and, of course, its whipped cream! Located just to the north of Paris, Chantilly is the ideal place for an excursion outside of the city, or for a dedicated weekend break! Chantilly is listed as a \'town of art and history\'. The Castle will be the first port of call for many visitors here, and indeed many get no further. Have you seen the James Bond film A View to a Kill? The scenes at the villain’s fabulous country estate were filmed at the Chateau de Chantilly, and the chateau’s stables and racecourse also made an appearance. Check-in at the hotel and rest of the day is free for leisure activities and explore the town on your own. Insider Tip - Appreciate Chantilly’s Famous Lace Chantilly lace is world famous, and the art itself is utterly amazing. The intricate knotting and twisting of thin silk strands with dozens of wooden bobbins by hand is, sadly, a dying art. But in the 17th century, it was popular with the rich, who were the only ones who could afford the adornments that took hours and days to complete. Chantilly’s small museum dedicated to the art has some lovely examples of Chantilly lace, from shawls to lace collars to entire dresses., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Chantilly, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Explore Chantilly Breakfast at the hotel and get ready uncover the hidden gem of France - Chantilly! A beautiful stroll through the Forest The 15,675-acre Chantilly Forest is the reason why the chateau was built here in the first place. In the shade of the oak trees, limes, hornbeams, and pines, you’ll find plenty of hiking and walking trails, none of them strenuous. It is a perfect green oasis - so different from the manicured gardens of the chateau, and yet just across the road. If you love nature and cannot get enough of it - Saunter Through The Le Notre Gardens The gardens of the Chateau de Chantilly are actually three gardens stretching across more than 280 acres. The oldest is the French Garden, created by none other than master gardener Andre Le Notre of Versailles and Tuileries fame. Stylized, ornate, and organized, it is a garden where you can easily visualize royalty strolling about. Marvel At The Books In The Library The favorite part of the chateau, however, is the library; it’s simply perfect, with its floor to ceiling books, mezzanine level accessed by a wooden staircase, and reading nooks. Make sure to take time to examine the books in the vitrines in the center of the room; they are very old - many of them handwritten and illustrated - and just stunning Finally Fathom The Chateau And Its Art Henri d’Orleans was a serious collector. His chateau consists of an older part, built in 1358, and a newer part, dating to the 1800s, which has been turned into a museum. The museum holds his art collection, which is second only to the collection at the Louvre in size. Much of the artwork depicts scenes of war, since the duke was a military man, but there is much more to discover, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Chantilly - Paris | Photoshoot Tour With Professional Photographer | Breakfast at the hotel and head to the train station for the return back to Paris. Later get dressed for this privileged activity - Paris Photo shoot Tour with Professional Photographer! Create long lasting souvenirs of your holidays in Paris with a Photoshoot. After your booking for a 1, 2 or 3h photo shoot tour, the agency will contact you to decide in which places you would like to do be captured, depending on the duration you can choose between 1/2 places up to 3/4 places, such as the Eiffel tower, the Louvre, Notre-Dame, Montmartre etc... Later make “A Lasting Impression” – Perfume Workshop Activity” Discover the art of French perfumery with a guided visit to the Fragonard Perfume Museum, where you’ll explore the history, origins, and craftsmanship behind iconic fragrances. Then, enjoy a hands on olfactory workshop and create your own 12 ml Eau de Toilette, guided by a fragrance expert. A sensory, creative experience blending culture, tradition, and personal expression Later you can opt to Shop, unwind, and return to Paris in comfort Enjoy a smooth and relaxing return transfer from the McArthurGlen Paris Giverny Designer Outlet to central Paris. After a full day of shopping, board a spacious air conditioned coach where your bags are welcome onboard. Sit back and unwind as the direct shuttle takes you comfortably back to the city, dropping you off conveniently near the Eiffel Tower - an effortless and stress free end to your day. OR Taste France in one lunch, five wines, artisan cheeses, & a sommelier to guide the journey Enjoy a relaxed and delicious Wine & Cheese Lunch in Paris led by an expert sommelier. Taste five French wines, beginning with Champagne and exploring major wine regions, while sampling perfectly paired cheeses. Learn how to read French wine labels, understand Champagne production, and discover why certain cheeses complement specific wines. A fun, flavorful, and educational way to experience two of France\'s greatest culinary traditions all in one elegant lunchtime tasting. [Time: 12:15 hrs - Supplement cost of € 100/- Per Person], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Paris Post breakfast and check out, free time until you board your private transfer to the airport. Choose to add an extra day or even if you have a late evening flight to opt for the below tours. “A Magical Day in Disneyland® Paris” (Optional) Enjoy this wonderful offer: transportation by a shuttle bus from the center of Paris to Disneyland® Paris, and entrance to the Disney® Parks (Disneyland® Park and Walt Disney Studios® Park). OR Indulge in a Shopping Spree at “La Vallee Village” With return shuttle Transfers to an open-air village, discover more than 110 boutiques of prestigious French and international brands, at discounted prices* at “La Vallee Village” Or Later witness the “Power of Love” with a visit to Le Mur Des Je t’aime, The Wall of Love Tucked away in Montmartre’s petite Jehan Rictus garden square, Le Mur Des Je t’aime attracts its fair share of lovebirds each day. Artists Federic Baron and Claire Kito created the mural in 2000, adorning it with hundreds of variations of Je t’aime (I Love You) in 250 different languages and dialects. [on your own activity] Or Steal a kiss at Pont des Arts “Love Lock Bridge” Better known at Love Lock Bridge, Pont des Arts has been a popular spot for Parisian rendezvous since 2008—when committed couples first began affixing engraved locks on the bridge’s railings, dropping their keys into the Seine below. Though this practice is now banned, visitors are still encouraged to drop by and take photos as they enjoy the view and each other’s company. Or Experience 360 degrees View of Paris “Montparnasse Tower Top of the City” Witness one of the most iconic views in the world with this panoramic view of Paris. On the 56th floor of the Montparnasse Tower, you are offered a complete view of the city at every angle. Take the fast elevator which travels from the ground floor to the 56th floor in a mind-blowing 38 seconds, travelling at a speed of 6 metres per second. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 139180.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nCITY NAME\nHotel Name - 5*\n\n\nPARIS\nHotel du Collectionneur Arc De Triomphe / The Champs Elysees House / Maison Albar Hotel Paris Champs-Elysées / Square Hotel / Hotel Paris Bastille Boutet - Mgallery By Sofitel / Sofitel Paris Baltimore Eiffel Tower OR similar\n\n\nHotels near Disneyland® Paris\nRelais Spa Chessy / Radisson Blu Hotel Paris, Marne-la-Vallée / Dream Castle Paris / L\'Élysée Val D\'Europe OR Similar\n\n\n, Hotels Envisaged or Similar:\n\n\n\nCity Name\n4*\n\n\nParis\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\nChantilly\nBest Western Du Parc / Mercure Chantilly / Château de Montvillargenne or similar\n\n\n, Hotels Envisaged or Similar:\n\n\n\nCity Name\n3*\n\n\nParis\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel /\xa0 Hôtel Champerret-Elysées /\xa0 Londres Et New York Hotel or similar\n\n\nChantilly\nBest Western Du Parc / Mercure Chantilly / Kyriad Chantilly / Campanile Chantilly or similar\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast at the hotel (except on the day of arrival).\n, Daily breakfast except day 1. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Paris at the selected category from the above mentioned or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Chantilly at the selected category from the above mentioned or similar 1 Night accommodation in Paris at the selected category from the above mentioned or similar Meals: Daily breakfast at the hotel (except on the day of arrival). Sightseeing: (Tour starts from a city centre point, transportation to & from the hotel is not included) Eiffel Tower Ticket with Priority Access and Mobile App (Ticket Only) Paris Photoshoot Tour with Professional Photographer (1 hour Experience): Complimentary Gesture! 24Hr Hop on Hop Off Big Bus Ticket: Complimentary Gesture! Romantic Seine River Dinner Cruise @ 18:00 hrs / 21:00 hrs Perfume Workshop in Paris (90 Mins) Transport within France: Arrival Transfer from Airport to Paris hotel on Private basis Departure Transfer from Paris Hotel to Paris Airport Return Train Tickets to Chantilly Insurance: Overseas Medical Insurance (Basic Coverage- Up to 60 years of age). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Meals other than those specified (if any). Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 5 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head. BLACK OUT PERIOD: 21 June – 27 June 2026 (Paris Air Show) 30 April – 11 May 2026 (Foire de Paris (Paris Trade Fair) 01 - 07 June (Roland Garros) 17–23 June 2026 (Champs Élysées Film Festival) 28 September – 6 October 2026 (Paris Fashion Week – Women’s SS 2027) *** During the above period costing will be on “On Request” basis ***. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1st March 2026 till 31st October 2026. Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. TCS & GST would be levied as applicable The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.. Highlights of the package: Enjoy a magical Paris evening with fine French dining on a romantic Seine cruise Discover Paris freely and romantically with a complimentary 24 hour Hop On Hop Off ticket Wander hand in hand through Chantilly, the elegant town of art, history, and romance Create timeless Paris memories together with a romantic photoshoot at the city’s iconic landmarks Craft your own fragrance in a romantic Paris perfume workshop that leaves a lasting impression Special Gift Hamper.', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'cityCode': 'SXR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bagdogra', 'cityCode': 'IXB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jabalpur', 'cityCode': 'JLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Paris - City Of Love - Honeymoon Special' package is a romantic 6-day tour covering the elegant destinations of Chantilly and Paris. The itinerary offers couples a magical evening with fine French dining on a scenic Seine cruise, a complimentary 24-hour Hop On Hop Off ticket to explore the city at their own pace, and a professional photoshoot at iconic landmarks to capture timeless memories. Additionally, participants will wander hand-in-hand through the historic town of Chantilly, craft a custom fragrance in a romantic perfume workshop, and receive a special gift hamper to complete their unforgettable honeymoon experience.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrive In Paris | The City Of Love |\nWelcome to Paris, City of light is the capital city of France. It is also the center of French economy, politics, traffic and culture. On arrival in Paris, you will have a private transfer to Paris Hotel.\nWelcome to Paris, with its monument-lined boulevards, museums, classical bistros and boutiques are enhanced by a new wave of multimedia galleries, creative wine bars, design shops and tech start ups. Check in at the hotel and rest of the day is free\n\xa0\nDepending on the flight arrival, Savor French cuisine as Paris glows around you\nParis Seine Dinner Cruise\nEnjoy a memorable 2 hour evening cruise along the Seine, departing from Solférino Port near the Musee d’Orsay. Settle into a cozy, intimate setting as you savor a seasonal 3 course French dinner with coffee or tea. Glide past Paris' illuminated landmarks - including the Musee d'Orsay, Notre Dame, the Conciergerie, the Louvre, and the sparkling Eiffel Tower - framed beautifully through panoramic windows. A perfect romantic night out combining fine dining, iconic views, and the magic of Paris by night.", 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) /\xa0Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre\xa0(Value)\xa0OR similar in Paris'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nParis | Effiel Tower With An Entertaining Evening (Moulin Rouge)|\nBreakfast at the hotel. See Paris your way - hop on, hop off, and explore at your own pace.\nDiscover Paris with complete freedom on a 24 hour Big Bus HopOn HopOff tour. Ride aboard an open top double decker bus and explore the city’s iconic landmarks - Eiffel Tower, Notre Dame, Champs Elysees and more - getting on and off as often as you like. Enjoy pre recorded commentary in multiple languages, free onboard WiFi, and a mobile app with live bus tracking. The perfect relaxed, flexible way to experience Paris at your own pace.\n\xa0\nAscend skywards in the lift to the first floor of the Eiffel Tower and step into the contemporary yet cozy atmosphere of the Madame Brasserie restaurant. Indulge in a three course lunch, consisting of a starter, main course, and dessert, made from locally sourced and seasonal products. {*This restaurant is high on demand and strictly subject to availability}\n\xa0\nLater, Get acquainted with Paris\' famous Iron Lady - The Eiffel Tower!\xa0\nAvoid long lines as much as possible thanks to your priority access. With audio guided comments through an audiopen and a map or mobile application to download, brings about a unique touring experience. Enjoy one of the most beautiful views of the capital & visit the monument from all angles without time limit.\xa0\n\xa0\nOptional Activity: A sparkling Parisian night at the Moulin Rouge: Champagne, glamour, and pure magic. Enjoy an unforgettable evening in Paris with the world famous Moulin Rouge "Feerie" show. Travel in comfort with return transportation in an air conditioned vehicle and delight in ½ bottle of champagne per person as you immerse yourself in a dazzling spectacle featuring 100 artists, including the iconic Doris Girls, 1,000 glittering costumes, vibrant sets, and breathtaking performances.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter the show, you’ll be conveniently dropped off in central Paris, near your hotel or a major landmark for easy onward travel. A glamorous, quintessential Paris night out. [Supplement cost of €180/- Per Person]', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) /\xa0Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre\xa0(Value)\xa0OR similar in Paris'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nParis\xa0 - Chantilly | Via Train\nBreakfast at the hotel. You will make your way to the train station or avail of a private transfer at the cost of EUR 60 per person to Paris Train station for your onward journey to Chantilly.\n[The journey time will be approx. 30 – 35 mins with few limited direct train options as well]\nWelcome to Chantilly! Chantilly is famous around the world for many things: its chateau, racecourse, and equine heritage, lace-making and, of course, its whipped cream! Located just to the north of Paris, Chantilly is the ideal place for an excursion outside of the city, or for a dedicated weekend break!\nChantilly is listed as a 'town of art and history'. The Castle will be the first port of call for many visitors here, and indeed many get no further. Have you seen the James Bond film A View to a Kill? The scenes at the villain’s fabulous country estate were filmed at the Chateau de Chantilly, and the chateau’s stables and racecourse also made an appearance.\nCheck-in at the hotel and rest of the day is free for leisure activities and explore the town on your own.\nInsider Tip - Appreciate Chantilly’s Famous Lace\nChantilly lace is world famous, and the art itself is utterly amazing. The intricate knotting and twisting of thin silk strands with dozens of wooden bobbins by hand is, sadly, a dying art. But in the 17th century, it was popular with the rich, who were the only ones who could afford the adornments that took hours and days to complete. Chantilly’s small museum dedicated to the art has some lovely examples of Chantilly lace, from shawls to lace collars to entire dresses.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Best Western Du Parc / Mercure Chantilly\xa0OR similar in\xa0Chantilly'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nExplore Chantilly\nBreakfast at the hotel and get ready uncover the hidden gem of France - Chantilly!\nA beautiful stroll through the Forest\nThe 15,675-acre Chantilly Forest is the reason why the chateau was built here in the first place. In the shade of the oak trees, limes, hornbeams, and pines, you’ll find plenty of hiking and walking trails, none of them strenuous. It is a perfect green oasis\xa0 - so different from the manicured gardens of the chateau, and yet just across the road.\nIf you love nature and cannot get enough of it - Saunter Through The Le Notre Gardens\nThe gardens of the Chateau de Chantilly are actually three gardens stretching across more than 280 acres. The oldest is the French Garden, created by none other than master gardener Andre Le Notre of Versailles and Tuileries fame. Stylized, ornate, and organized, it is a garden where you can easily visualize royalty strolling about.\nMarvel At The Books In The Library\nThe favorite part of the chateau, however, is the library; it’s simply perfect, with its floor to ceiling books, mezzanine level accessed by a wooden staircase, and reading nooks. Make sure to take time to examine the books in the vitrines in the center of the room; they are very old - many of them handwritten and illustrated - and just stunning\nFinally Fathom The Chateau And Its Art\nHenri d’Orleans was a serious collector. His chateau consists of an older part, built in 1358, and a newer part, dating to the 1800s, which has been turned into a museum. The museum holds his art collection, which is second only to the collection at the Louvre in size. Much of the artwork depicts scenes of war, since the duke was a military man, but there is much more to discover', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Best Western Du Parc / Mercure Chantilly\xa0OR similar in\xa0Chantilly'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nChantilly - Paris\xa0 | Photoshoot Tour With Professional Photographer |\nBreakfast at the hotel and head to the train station for the return back to Paris.\nLater get dressed for this privileged activity - Paris Photo shoot Tour with Professional Photographer! Create long lasting souvenirs of your holidays in Paris with a Photoshoot. After your booking for a 1, 2 or 3h photo shoot tour, the agency will contact you to decide in which places you would like to do be captured, depending on the duration you can choose between 1/2 places up to 3/4 places, such as the Eiffel tower, the Louvre, Notre-Dame, Montmartre etc...\nLater make “A Lasting Impression” – Perfume Workshop Activity”\nDiscover the art of French perfumery with a guided visit to the Fragonard Perfume Museum, where you’ll explore the history, origins, and craftsmanship behind iconic fragrances. Then, enjoy a hands on olfactory workshop and create your own 12 ml Eau de Toilette, guided by a fragrance expert. A sensory, creative experience blending culture, tradition, and personal expression\n\xa0\nLater you can opt to Shop, unwind, and return to Paris in comfort\nEnjoy a smooth and relaxing return transfer from the McArthurGlen Paris Giverny Designer Outlet to central Paris. After a full day of shopping, board a spacious air conditioned coach where your bags are welcome onboard. Sit back and unwind as the direct shuttle takes you comfortably back to the city, dropping you off conveniently near the Eiffel Tower - an effortless and stress free end to your day.\n\xa0\nOR Taste France in one lunch, five wines, artisan cheeses, & a sommelier to guide the journey\nEnjoy a relaxed and delicious Wine & Cheese Lunch in Paris led by an expert sommelier. Taste five French wines, beginning with Champagne and exploring major wine regions, while sampling perfectly paired cheeses. Learn how to read French wine labels, understand Champagne production, and discover why certain cheeses complement specific wines. A fun, flavorful, and educational way to experience two of France's greatest culinary traditions all in one elegant lunchtime tasting. [Time: 12:15 hrs - Supplement cost of € 100/- Per Person]", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Opera Lafayette (Standard) /\xa0Mercure Paris Opera Faubourg Montmartre\xa0(Value)\xa0OR similar in Paris'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart Paris\nPost breakfast and check out, free time until you board your private transfer to the airport.\nChoose to add an extra day or even if you have a late evening flight to opt for the below tours.\n“A Magical Day in Disneyland® Paris” (Optional)\nEnjoy this wonderful offer: transportation by a shuttle bus from the center of Paris to Disneyland® Paris, and entrance to the Disney® Parks (Disneyland® Park and Walt Disney Studios® Park).\nOR\xa0 Indulge in a Shopping Spree at “La Vallee Village”\nWith return shuttle Transfers to an open-air village, discover more than 110 boutiques of prestigious French and international brands, at discounted prices* at “La Vallee Village”\nOr Later witness the “Power of Love”\xa0 with a visit to Le Mur Des Je t’aime, The Wall of Love\xa0\nTucked away in Montmartre’s petite Jehan Rictus garden square, Le Mur Des Je t’aime attracts its fair share of lovebirds each day. Artists Federic Baron and Claire Kito created the mural in 2000, adorning it with hundreds of variations of Je t’aime (I Love You) in 250 different languages and dialects. [on your own activity]\nOr Steal a kiss at Pont des Arts “Love Lock Bridge”\nBetter known at Love Lock Bridge, Pont des Arts has been a popular spot for Parisian rendezvous since 2008—when committed couples first began affixing engraved locks on the bridge’s railings, dropping their keys into the Seine below. Though this practice is now banned, visitors are still encouraged to drop by and take photos as they enjoy the view and each other’s company.\nOr Experience 360 degrees View of Paris “Montparnasse Tower Top of the City”\nWitness one of the most iconic views in the world with this panoramic view of Paris. On the 56th floor of the Montparnasse Tower, you are offered a complete view of the city at every angle. Take the fast elevator which travels from the ground floor to the 56th floor in a mind-blowing 38 seconds, travelling at a speed of 6 metres per second.\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ["\n\n\nCITY NAME\nHotel Name - 5*\n\n\nPARIS\nHotel du Collectionneur Arc De Triomphe / The Champs Elysees House / Maison Albar Hotel Paris Champs-Elysées / Square Hotel / Hotel Paris Bastille Boutet - Mgallery By Sofitel / Sofitel Paris Baltimore Eiffel Tower OR similar\n\n\nHotels near Disneyland® Paris\nRelais Spa Chessy / Radisson Blu Hotel Paris, Marne-la-Vallée / Dream Castle Paris / L'Élysée Val D'Europe OR Similar\n\n\n", 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar:\n\n\n\nCity Name\n4*\n\n\nParis\nMercure Paris Opéra Faubourg Montmartre / Novotel Paris Center Eiffel Tower / Novotel Paris Center Gare Montparnasse / Mercure Paris Bercy Bibliotheque Hotel / Hotel Mademoiselle or similar\n\n\nChantilly\nBest Western Du Parc / Mercure Chantilly / Château de Montvillargenne or similar\n\n\n', 'Hotels Envisaged or Similar:\n\n\n\nCity Name\n3*\n\n\nParis\nHotel Opera Lafayette / Color Design Hotel /\xa0 Hôtel Champerret-Elysées /\xa0 Londres Et N