, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage, or passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure as of 1st August 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leads to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink are not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips for guides, hotel waiters, drivers, etc.\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note : The above prices will not be valid for any block out date/ period which is informed during confirmation of the booking; if any change in the price, the same will be applicable for all bookings and to be borne by the customer\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015506/Baku-2.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015506/itinerary/Baku_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015506/itinerary/baku-Ateshgah.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015506/itinerary/Baku_City_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015506/itinerary/Baku_City_view_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015207', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015207', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Mysteries Of The Three Kingdoms  -  Turkey, Jordan And Egypt', 'days': 12, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Istanbul', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amman', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Petra', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dead Sea', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Amman', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cairo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cairo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cairo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cairo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Cairo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 369888, 'packageSummary': "The 'Mysteries Of The Three Kingdoms - Turkey, Jordan And Egypt' package is a 12-day tour covering Amman, Istanbul, Petra, the Dead Sea, and Cairo. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the ancient rose-red city of Petra, the historic Pyramids of Giza and the Great Sphinx in Cairo, and the majestic mosques and bustling bazaars of Istanbul. Participants will enjoy unique experiences like floating in the mineral-rich waters of the Dead Sea, guided sightseeing tours of Amman's Roman ruins, and exploring the rich cultural heritage and archaeological wonders of these three historic nations.", 'images': ['00886_Istanbul753.jpg', '01378_Topkapi_Palace_istanbul_Turkey_753.jpg', '49725_Dolmabahce_Palace_Istanbul753.jpg', 'AdobeStock_135600005_Amman.jpg', 'WadiRum.jpg', 'DeadSea_87120142.jpg', 'DeadSea1.jpg', '2677_Cairo753.jpg', 'Cairo1.jpg', '99521_Bazaar_Cairo_Egypt_753.jpg', '2677_Cairo753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 369888, 'thumbnailImage': '0886_IstanbulSRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG015207 is named \'Mysteries Of The Three Kingdoms  -  Turkey, Jordan And Egypt\' and spans 12 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Istanbul, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Turkey – Where East Meets West Welcome to Istanbul, Turkey. Connecting two continents, Istanbul is a city where Europe and Asia meet, blending centuries of history with modern life. On arrival at Istanbul Airport, you will be greeted by local representative/tour manager outside the baggage hall. Proceed to the hotel and check in. Standard Check in time-1500 hours. Later, explore Taksim Square and have a walking tour of Istiklal Street. Note: Passengers joining directly / NRI passengers may check in at the hotel on their own. Standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. in at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Blue Mosque & Hippodrome - Topkapi Palace – Grand Bazar Today, see the Blue Mosque and the Hippodrome, showcasing Istanbul\'s Ottoman and Byzantine history. Later, visit Topkapi Palace, the residence of Ottoman sultans for nearly 400 years. Next, proceed for a photostop at Hagia Sophia mosque and end your day with free time for shopping at the super Grand Bazaar., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Istanbul, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Bosphorous Cruise – Dolmabahce Palace – Spice Market Today, enjoy a Bosphorus cruise between Europe and Asia, offering views of Istanbul\'s skyline and waterfront landmarks. Next, visit Dolmabahce Palace, the former administrative center of the Ottoman Empire. Later, visit the Spice Market to explore its shops offering spices, sweets, teas, and local products., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Amman, Meals: Breakfast and Local Dinner, Description: Depart Turkey and Welcome to Jordan- ‘The Holy Land’ Welcome to Amman, Jordan. Meet and assist by your tour manager/ airport representative. Proceed to the hotel and check in. Standard Check in time-1500 hours., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Petra, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Proceed to Wadi Rum - known as the valley of the moons; enjoy a thrilling jeep tour of Wadi rum. Onto Petra. Today, proceed to Wadi Rum - a valley cut into the sandstone and granite rock in southern Jordan known for its towering rock formations, slender valleys, and infinite skies (Distance 320km). Enjoy Jeep Safari at Wadi Rum. Later, transfer to Petra., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dead Sea, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Explore Petra . Drive to Dead Sea. Today, proceed to explore Petra. Take a buggy transfer and visit the Petra Treasury area – One of the 7 Wonders of the World. Proceed to the Dead Sea, the lowest point on earth deep in the Jordan Valley. Evening is free to explore the hotel or enjoy a dip in the dead sea and enjoy the sunset. Check in at the hotel in Dead Sea, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Amman, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Dead Sea– Mt. Nebo – Amman After breakfast, free time in Dead Sea. Proceed to Mt. Nebo - a sacred elevated ridge in Jordan, overlooking the Jordan River Valley and Dead Sea. Continue your tour of Amman, see the Citadel -Temple of Hercules ruins etc. Later, see the Roman Amphitheatre., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Cairo, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Depart Jordan and Welcome to Egypt Depart from Amman Airport and arrive at Cairo. On arrival, Transfers to the hotel. (Standard hotel check-in time: 1500 hrs). Enjoy a relaxed evening., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Cairo, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Explore - Pyramids and Sphinx, Papyrus and Perfumery, GEM – The Grand Egyptian Museum Guided tour Transfer to visit the Pyramids of Giza and Sphinx. Entrance inside the Pyramids is not included. Stop at perfumery & papyrus shops. Enjoy a guided tour of the GEM – The Grand Egyptian Museum., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Cairo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Coptic and Islamic Cairo This morning explore Coptic Cairo - Hanging Church - a unique church that has a wooden roof in the shape of Noah\'s ark, Saints Sergius and Bacchus Church (Abu Serga); Explore Islamic Cairo - Citadel of Saladin, Al-Azhar Mosque – the first mosque established in a city that eventually earned the nickname "the City of a Thousand Minarets", Khan El Khalili Bazaar., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Cairo, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Coptic and Islamic Cairo Day trip to Ain Sokhna including Semi-Sub Tour + Porto Sokhna Cable Car Ride. Today, we drive towards Ain Sokhna a premier Red Sea coastal town on the Gulf of Suez. Enjoy Red Sea with a semi-sub tour from Ain Sokhna - experience the Wonders of the Red Sea coral reefs through the windows of the observation decks. Next, depending on weather conditions and maintenance schedules take the Porto Sokhna Cable Car ride to enjoy Panoramic views of the Red Sea. Evening back to Cairo and overnight in Cairo., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Cairo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Drive to Cairo airport. Departure After breakfast, transfer to Cairo airport. Flight back home. Check out time is 1000 hrs. Distances: Wadi rum to Petra: 102km Petra to dead sea: 200km Cairo to Ain Sokhna: 131km, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 369888.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n3 night accommodation in Istanbul at Four Sides Lion Hotel or similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Petra At Hotel P Quattro/Petra Moon Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Hyatt Zaman Hotel And Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Dead Sea At Hotel Ramada Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Dead Sea Spa Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n\xa04 Nights’ Accommodation At Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo\xa0\n\nFree Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast (Except Day 01)\xa0\n01 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian lunches\n05 local / international lunches\n06 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian dinners\n02 local / international dinners\n. Inclusions: Cost of Visa & Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour up to the age of 68 years Return economy class Airfare ex Royal Jordanian, Egypt Air, Kuwait Airways, Oman Air, Air Arabia, Gulf Air or similar airlines. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary All transfers & excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by air-conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly & multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 25 customers) or a local Representative. All local taxes and services as of 31st January 2026. Jordan and Egyptian Visa on arrival. Exclusions: If you want to travel before the tour starts or return after the tour ends (a deviation), there will be an extra charge. This is subject to seat availability and ticket rules, and the price will be shared by our staff. Note: This change can only be made starting 30 days before your original departure date. Applicable GST and TCS are additional. Tipping in Egypt is expected from anyone providing services e.g., Coach Driver, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of USD 5 per person/per day. For the entire duration of the tour which is to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. POE charges & passport charges and No porterage included. Registration fees at Cairo Airport for passengers between the age of 16 years to 60 years staying in Egypt for 7 nights or more. Any expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, food & drink that are not a part of the package. Additional Meals that are not mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees & local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions. Cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 31st October 2025). Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The routing of the itinerary may change as per flight & hotel availability Please DO NOT issue any tickets without confirming with the sales team. Does not include any flights i.e. International, internal or domestic. 04 passengers in one room are not allowed. Maximum capacity is 03 passengers. Standard Hotel check-in time will be 1500 hours and check out at 1000 hrs. Distances: Wadi rum to Petra: 102km Petra to dead sea: 200km Cairo to Ain Sokhna: 131km Important Note For Egypt: Early Starts for Better Experiences: To ensure you see Jordan and Egypt’s world-famous monuments in the best possible light and avoid the peak midday warmth, many of our tours and domestic flights are scheduled for the early morning. Starting your day early allows you to enjoy the sites while they are quieter and more comfortable. Brisk Itineraries: Jordan and Egypt are home to an incredible density of historical treasures. To help you experience as many of these wonders as possible, our daily schedules are designed to be efficient. While this means time at individual temples may be structured, it ensures you don\'t miss any of the highlights on your itinerary. Please visit the dedicated registration office at Terminal 1, 2, or 3 immediately upon arrival to obtain your triangle-shaped registration stamp if your stay in Egypt is more than 7 days. A fee of USD 15 per person is payable directly to travellers aged 16 to 60. Note: To avoid a fine of 900 EGP (plus the $15 registration fee), please ensure you register upon arrival at Cairo airport. NRI and JD (Joining Direct) passengers arrive in Jordan as per the departure dates above i.e. Day 1 Airport-to-group hotel and group hotel to airport transfers are included in JD / NRI guests arriving between 07 AM and 09 PM on the arrival and departure day only. For transfers not falling within these timings a surcharge may apply. Internal flight transfers are included in JD/NRI passengers. Kindly check with us for more details. Early check and / or late check out is not included. Note that Amman to Cairo are not considered as Internal flight as it’s an international flight and not included for any JR or NRI client. Important Notes: Airline And Airfare The Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 31st January 2026. Any Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers. Passengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves. For Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents. Passengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To/ From The Hub City At Their Own Expense. Hotels / Cruise Most Hotels In Jordan And Egypt Have Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size. As A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room. For Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room. A Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult. Functioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority. Due To International Events And Trade Fairs In Jordan And Egypt Such As The Eid Holidays, Air Show, Marathons, Music Festivals, Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City. Any Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Cruise Cabins / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers. We Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel / Cruise Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary. Some Cities Don’t Have Buffet Breakfast In Hotels. If This Continues When Tours Begin, We Will Provide Breakfast Or Take The Groups To An Indian / Local Restaurant. It Is Important To Note That Hotel Rooms In Egypt Especially The Nile Cruise May Be More Compact / Smaller In Size Than What You Are Accustomed To. Coaches Coaches Are An Important Part Of Your Journeys & We Request Our Guests To Keep The Coach Clean. Due To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives. Eating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach. Due To Limited Boot Space In The Coach, We Suggest You Carry One Check-In Bag & One Handbag Per Person Only In Major Egypt Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop. Coaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach. Meals Meals Are Pre–Set & A–La Carte Is Not Possible. On Certain Days Packed Lunch/Breakfast Will Be Provided. Water Bottles Will Be Provided By Your Guide And Tour Manager As Per Itinerary. Certain Meals Are By Walking During Your Tour. Water Is Not Included During Any Meals. Sightseeing On Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same. Panoramic / Orientation Tours Are Scenic Drives Conducted Primarily From The Coach. Only Specific, Pre-Determined Locations Are Visited On Foot Or Include A Photo Stop. Guests Should Note That The Itinerary Requires Early Morning Wake Up Calls, Early Morning Flights, Significant Walking Distances At Various Locations, Including Attractions, Temples And Airports. This Is An Inherent Part Of The Tour Experience. We Recommend You Bring A Reliable, Comfortable Pair Of Sports Shoes. Your Tour Manager And Driver Will Attempt To Minimize Walking By Getting You As Close To The Entry Points As Regulations Allow, But Ultimate Responsibility For Navigating The Walking Portions Rests With The Guest. Every Site / Monuments Has Its Own Set Of Rules & Regulations. We Need To Respect This & Ensure That We Follow The Same. All Our Visits Are Booked In Advance To Avoid Delays, At The Same Time There May Be Delays Caused Due To Overcrowding, Local Regulations, Security Checks Etc. Most Of The Tours In Jordan And Egypt Will Commence Early And Are Generally Scheduled To Conclude In The Early Evening. These Schedules Are Based On Weather Conditions, Local Tourism Operating Norms And Coach Hours. Furthermore, Guests Are Advised That Local Establishments, Including Restaurants And Retail Stores, Often Operate With Shorter Evening Hours Than In Other Countries. General For Nri Customers Visa Fees, International Flights And Insurance Are Not Included. For Jd – Joining Direct Customers International Flights Are Not Included. If You Are A Jd Or Nri Passenger While Your Internal Flights Are Included, Make Sure Your Internal Flights Match The Tour Group\'s Schedule If You Want Seamless Transfers And Guarantee You Don\'t Miss Any Sightseeing. No Transfers Can Be Arranged For Different Flight Timings And No Refunds For Any Missed Sightseeing. Note That Amman To Cairo Are Not Considered As Internal Flight As It’s An International Flight And Not Included For Any Jr Or Nri Client. On Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members. A Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour. Arrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary, To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer About The Group Flight Timings. Security Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary. Please Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Sotc Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage. Disabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client. Sotc Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour. Normal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges. The Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services. The Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same. There Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour. Any Tours Or Activities Curtailed Or Cancelled Due To Weather Or Traffic Conditions Which Are Beyond The Control Of Sotc Cannot Be Refunded. All Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Local Currencies Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted). Optional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non-Cancellation Policy. Any Optional Tours Not Listed By Sotc On Their Website, Sim Cards Purchased From Local Guides Are Not A Responsibility Of Sotc As These Will Be Considered A 3rd Party Transaction. Gst And Tcs Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India. In Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed. The Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only. Tours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Usd Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange. Please Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”. Weather in Turkey, Jordan and Egypt General Overview Istanbul Weather (October – March 2026/27) Istanbul experiences pleasant autumns and cool winters, offering comfortable weather for exploring historic landmarks, museums, bazaars, and Bosphorus cruises. Amman Weather (October – March 2026/27) Amman experiences mild autumns and cool winters, with comfortable daytime temperatures that make it an excellent base for sightseeing, cultural experiences, and excursions to Petra, Jerash, the Dead Sea, and Wadi Rum. Cairo Weather (October – March 2026/27) Cairo enjoys warm autumns and mild winters with abundant sunshine, offering ideal conditions for sightseeing, exploring ancient monuments, and experiencing the city\'s cultural attractions. Month Avg. High Temp Conditions October 29°C (84°F) Warm and sunny across Turkey, Jordan, and Egypt; ideal for sightseeing and outdoor activities. November 24°C (75°F) Mild with pleasant daytime temperatures; excellent for cultural tours and historical sites. December 19°C (66°F) Cool to mild with comfortable weather for exploring cities, monuments, and archaeological sites. January 17°C (63°F) Coolest month with generally pleasant daytime temperatures and occasional rainfall. February 18°C (64°F) Mild with increasing sunshine; comfortable for sightseeing throughout the region. March 23°C (73°F) Warm and dry as spring begins; ideal for exploring historic landmarks and natural attractions. Note: These are representative daytime temperatures for the principal touring regions of Istanbul (Turkey), Amman (Jordan), and Cairo (Egypt). Coastal destinations such as the Red Sea, Dead Sea, and Mediterranean coast are generally warmer during this period. All weather information is approximate only. Please check weather information before your travel.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTK100', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Mysteries Of The Three Kingdoms - Turkey, Jordan And Egypt' package is a 12-day tour covering Amman, Istanbul, Petra, the Dead Sea, and Cairo. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the ancient rose-red city of Petra, the historic Pyramids of Giza and the Great Sphinx in Cairo, and the majestic mosques and bustling bazaars of Istanbul. Participants will enjoy unique experiences like floating in the mineral-rich waters of the Dead Sea, guided sightseeing tours of Amman's Roman ruins, and exploring the rich cultural heritage and archaeological wonders of these three historic nations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWelcome to Turkey – Where East Meets West\nWelcome to Istanbul, Turkey. Connecting two continents, Istanbul is a city where Europe and Asia meet, blending centuries of history with modern life. On arrival at Istanbul Airport, you will be greeted by local representative/tour manager outside the baggage hall. Proceed to the hotel and check in. Standard Check in time-1500 hours.\nLater, explore Taksim Square and have a walking tour of Istiklal Street.\nNote: Passengers joining directly / NRI passengers may check in at the hotel on their own. Standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. in at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Four Sides Lion or similar in\xa0Istanbul (Free Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nBlue Mosque & Hippodrome - Topkapi Palace – Grand Bazar\nToday, see the Blue Mosque and the Hippodrome, showcasing Istanbul's Ottoman and Byzantine history. Later, visit Topkapi Palace, the residence of Ottoman sultans for nearly 400 years. Next, proceed for a photostop at Hagia Sophia mosque and end your day with free time for shopping at the super Grand Bazaar.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four Sides Lion or similar in Istanbul (Free Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nBosphorous Cruise – Dolmabahce Palace – Spice Market\nToday, enjoy a Bosphorus cruise between Europe and Asia, offering views of Istanbul's skyline and waterfront landmarks. Next, visit Dolmabahce Palace, the former administrative center of the Ottoman Empire.\xa0 Later, visit the Spice Market to explore its shops offering spices, sweets, teas, and local products.\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four Sides Lion or similar in Istanbul (Free Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart Turkey and Welcome to Jordan- ‘The Holy Land’\nWelcome to Amman, Jordan. Meet and assist by your tour manager/ airport representative. Proceed to the hotel and check in. Standard Check in time-1500 hours.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Toledo or similar in\xa0Amman (Free Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nProceed to Wadi Rum - known as the valley of the moons; enjoy a thrilling jeep tour of Wadi rum. Onto Petra.\nToday, proceed to Wadi Rum - a valley cut into the sandstone and granite rock in southern Jordan known for its towering rock formations, slender valleys, and infinite skies (Distance 320km). Enjoy Jeep Safari at Wadi Rum. Later, transfer to Petra.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel P Quattro/Petra Moon Or Similar in Petra (Free Upgrade To Hyatt Zaman Hotel And Resort 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExplore Petra . Drive to Dead Sea.\nToday, proceed to explore Petra. Take a buggy transfer and visit the Petra Treasury area – One of the 7 Wonders of the World. Proceed to the Dead Sea, the lowest point on earth deep in the Jordan Valley. Evening is free to explore the hotel or enjoy a dip in the dead sea and enjoy the sunset. Check in at the hotel in Dead Sea', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ramada Or Similar in\xa0Dead Sea (Free Upgrade To Dead Sea Spa Resort 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDead Sea– Mt. Nebo – Amman\nAfter breakfast, free time in Dead Sea. Proceed to Mt. Nebo - a sacred elevated ridge in Jordan, overlooking the Jordan River Valley and Dead Sea. Continue your tour of Amman, see the Citadel -Temple of Hercules ruins etc. Later, see the Roman Amphitheatre.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Toledo Or Similar in\xa0Amman (Free Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*)'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart Jordan and Welcome to Egypt\nDepart from Amman Airport and arrive at Cairo. On arrival, Transfers to the hotel. (Standard hotel check-in time: 1500 hrs). Enjoy a relaxed evening.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo (Free Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo)'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExplore - Pyramids and Sphinx, Papyrus and Perfumery, GEM – The Grand Egyptian Museum Guided tour\nTransfer to visit the Pyramids of Giza and Sphinx. Entrance inside the Pyramids is not included. Stop at perfumery & papyrus shops. Enjoy a guided tour of the GEM – The Grand Egyptian Museum.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo (Free Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo)'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nCoptic and Islamic Cairo\nThis morning explore Coptic Cairo - Hanging Church -\xa0 a unique church that has a wooden roof in the shape of Noah\'s ark, Saints Sergius and Bacchus Church (Abu Serga); Explore Islamic Cairo - Citadel of Saladin, Al-Azhar Mosque – the first mosque established in a city that eventually earned the nickname "the City of a Thousand Minarets", Khan El Khalili Bazaar.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo (Free Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo)'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nCoptic and Islamic Cairo\nDay trip to Ain Sokhna including Semi-Sub Tour + Porto Sokhna Cable Car Ride.\nToday, we drive towards Ain Sokhna a premier Red Sea coastal town on the Gulf of Suez. Enjoy Red Sea with a semi-sub tour from Ain Sokhna - experience the Wonders of the Red Sea coral reefs through the windows of the observation decks. Next, depending on weather conditions and maintenance schedules take the Porto Sokhna Cable Car ride to enjoy Panoramic views of the Red Sea. Evening back to Cairo and overnight in Cairo.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo (Free Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo)'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive to Cairo airport. Departure\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Cairo airport. Flight back home. Check out time is 1000 hrs.\n\xa0\nDistances:\n\nWadi rum to Petra: 102km\nPetra to dead sea: 200km\nCairo to Ain Sokhna: 131km\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n3 night accommodation in Istanbul at Four Sides Lion Hotel or similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Petra At Hotel P Quattro/Petra Moon Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Hyatt Zaman Hotel And Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Dead Sea At Hotel Ramada Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Dead Sea Spa Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n\xa04 Nights’ Accommodation At Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo\xa0\n\nFree Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n3 night accommodation in Istanbul at Four Sides Lion Hotel or similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Petra At Hotel P Quattro/Petra Moon Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Hyatt Zaman Hotel And Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Dead Sea At Hotel Ramada Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Dead Sea Spa Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n\xa04 Nights’ Accommodation At Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo\xa0\n\nFree Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 2, 'countryCode': 'JO', 'countryName': 'Jordan', 'continentName': 'Africa'}, {'continentId': 2, 'countryCode': 'EG', 'countryName': 'Egypt', 'continentName': 'Africa'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'TR', 'countryName': 'Turkey', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 369900.0, 'hotels': ['\n3 night accommodation in Istanbul at Four Sides Lion Hotel or similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Crown Plaza Harbiye 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Petra At Hotel P Quattro/Petra Moon Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Hyatt Zaman Hotel And Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Dead Sea At Hotel Ramada Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Dead Sea Spa Resort 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n1 Night Accommodation In Amman At Hotel Toledo Or Similar\n\nFree Upgrade To Amman Rotana Tower 5* Or Similar 5*\n\n\n\xa04 Nights’ Accommodation At Hotel Marwa Palace Or Similar In Cairo\xa0\n\nFree Upgrade To Ramses Hilton Or Similar 5* In Cairo\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily breakfast (Except Day 01)\xa0\n01 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian lunches\n05 local / international lunches\n06 Indian Jain/vegetarian/non-vegetarian dinners\n02 local / international dinners\n'], 'visa': ['\nJordan and Egyptian Visa on arrival\n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers & excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Istanbul\n\nTaksim Square & Istiklal Street Walking Tour\nTopkapi Palace\nBlue Mosque\nHippodrome\nGrand Bazar And Spice Bazar\nBosphorus Cruise\nDolmabahçe Palace\n\nAmman\n\nGuided City Tour Of Amman\nVisit The Citadel\nVisit The Amphitheatre\nVisit Mount Nebo\n\nPetra & Wadi Rum\n\nVisit The Nabatean Red Rose City Of Petra\nPhoto Stop At ‘The Treasury’ – One Of The Seven Wonders Of The World\nWadi Rum Desert - Enjoy Jeep Safari\n\nDead Sea\n\nSee The Jordan Valley And The Dead Sea\n\nCairo\n\nGuided Tour Of The Pyramids And Sphinx Of Giza Area\nPapyrus And Perfumery\nGem – The Grand Egyptian Museum Guided Tour\nVisit Coptic Cairo Including Hanging Church\nSaints Sergius And Bacchus Church (Abu Serga)\nCitadel Of Saladin\nAl-Azhar Mosque And Khan El Khalili Bazaar\n\nDay Trip From Cairo To Ain Sokhna\n\nVisit Ain Sokhna, A Premier Red Sea Coastal Town On The Gulf Of Suez\nEnjoy A Semi-Sub Ride In The Red Sea\nPorto Sokhna Cable Car Ride (Subjected To Maintenance Schedules, Weather Conditions)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class Airfare ex Royal Jordanian, Egypt Air, Kuwait Airways, Oman Air, Air Arabia, Gulf Air or similar airlines.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nCost of Visa & Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour up to the age of 68 years\nReturn economy class Airfare ex Royal Jordanian, Egypt Air, Kuwait Airways, Oman Air, Air Arabia, Gulf Air or similar airlines.\xa0\nSightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary\nAll transfers & excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by air-conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly & multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 25 customers) or a local Representative.\nAll local taxes and services as of 31st January 2026.\nJordan and Egyptian Visa on arrival\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you want to travel before the tour starts or return after the tour ends (a deviation), there will be an extra charge. This is subject to seat availability and ticket rules, and the price will be shared by our staff. Note: This change can only be made starting 30 days before your original departure date.\nApplicable GST and TCS are additional.\nTipping in Egypt is expected from anyone providing services e.g., Coach Driver, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of USD 5 per person/per day. For the entire duration of the tour which is to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nPOE charges & passport charges and No porterage included.\nRegistration fees at Cairo Airport for passengers between the age of 16 years to 60 years staying in Egypt for 7 nights or more.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, food & drink that are not a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals that are not mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees & local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 31st October 2025)\n', 'termsAndConditions': "Important Note:\n\nThe routing of the itinerary may change as per flight & hotel availability\nPlease DO NOT issue any tickets without confirming with the sales team.\xa0\nDoes not include any flights i.e. International, internal or domestic.\n04 passengers in one room are not allowed. Maximum capacity is 03 passengers.\nStandard Hotel check-in time will be 1500 hours and check out at 1000 hrs.\n\nDistances:\n\nWadi rum to Petra: 102km\nPetra to dead sea: 200km\nCairo to Ain Sokhna: 131km\n\n\xa0\nImportant Note For Egypt:\n\nEarly Starts for Better Experiences: To ensure you see Jordan and Egypt’s world-famous monuments in the best possible light and avoid the peak midday warmth, many of our tours and domestic flights are scheduled for the early morning. Starting your day early allows you to enjoy the sites while they are quieter and more comfortable.\nBrisk Itineraries: Jordan and Egypt are home to an incredible density of historical treasures. To help you experience as many of these wonders as possible, our daily schedules are designed to be efficient. While this means time at individual temples may be structured, it ensures you don't miss any of the highlights on your itinerary.\nPlease visit the dedicated registration office at Terminal 1, 2, or 3 immediately upon arrival to obtain your triangle-shaped registration stamp if your stay in Egypt is more than 7 days. A fee of USD 15 per person is payable directly to travellers aged 16 to 60. Note: To avoid a fine of 900 EGP (plus the $15 registration fee), please ensure you register upon arrival at Cairo airport.\n\nNRI and JD (Joining Direct) passengers arrive in Jordan as per the departure dates above i.e. Day 1\nAirport-to-group hotel and group hotel to airport transfers are included in JD / NRI guests arriving between 07 AM and 09 PM on the arrival and departure day only. For transfers not falling within these timings a surcharge may apply. Internal flight transfers are included in JD/NRI passengers. Kindly check with us for more details. Early check and / or late check out is not included.\nNote that Amman to Cairo are not considered as Internal flight as it’s an international flight and not included for any JR or NRI client.\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:\nAirline And Airfare\n\nThe Airfare Is Based On The Fare Structure Existing As On 31st January 2026.\nAny Further Increase In The Airfare Due To An Increase In The Fuel Price, Change In Government Regulations, Taxes, Etc., Charged By The Airline Will Have To Be Borne By The Passengers.\nPassengers Missing Flights Note That The Entire Ticket Gets No Show And New Return Ticket Needs To Be Bought By The Passengers Themselves.\xa0\nFor Prices And Departure Dates From Your Hub City Please Contact Our Local Sales Offices/Travel Agents.\xa0\nPassengers Joining This Tour Must Travel To/ From The Hub City At Their Own Expense.\n\nHotels / Cruise\n\nMost Hotels In Jordan And Egypt Have Twin Beds. The Double Bed Will Be Queen Size And Not King Size.\xa0\nAs A 3rd Person In A Triple Room, Most Hotels Use Rollaway Beds And Room Size May Be The Same As The Double Room.\xa0\nFor Child With Bed: At Times Hotel Don’t Have Enough Roll Away Beds, In That Case They Might Give A Double And A Separate Single Room.\xa0\nA Person 11.99 Years And Below Is Considered A Child And 12 Years And Above, An Adult.\nFunctioning Of Air Cooling / Air Conditioning In Hotels Is Subject To Official Declaration Of Summer By The Local Authority.\xa0\nDue To International Events And Trade Fairs In Jordan And Egypt Such As The Eid Holidays, Air Show, Marathons, Music Festivals, Etc., You May Have To Stay In Hotels Further Away From The City.\nAny Damage Caused To The Hotel Rooms / Cruise Cabins / Coach During Your Stay Shall Be Payable By The Passengers.\xa0\nWe Also Reserve The Right To Substitute A Hotel / Cruise Of Similar Class If It Is Deemed Advisable Or Necessary.\xa0\nSome Cities Don’t Have Buffet Breakfast In Hotels. If This Continues When Tours Begin, We Will Provide Breakfast Or Take The Groups To An Indian / Local Restaurant.\nIt Is Important To Note That Hotel Rooms In Egypt Especially The Nile Cruise May Be More Compact / Smaller In Size Than What You Are Accustomed To.\n\nCoaches\xa0\n\nCoaches Are An Important Part Of Your Journeys & We Request Our Guests To Keep The Coach Clean.\nDue To Hygienic Reasons, It Is Not Permitted To Use Toilets On The Coach. However, The Tour Manager Will Make Comfort Stops During Long Drives.\xa0\nEating & Drinking Is Not Permitted On The Coach.\xa0\nDue To Limited Boot Space In The Coach, We Suggest You Carry One Check-In Bag & One Handbag Per Person Only\xa0\nIn Major Egypt Cities, There Are Parking Restrictions For Coaches, And It May Not Be Possible To Stop At All The Places During The City Tour. Tour Manager Will Try His/Her Best To Stop Coach Wherever Possible For A Photo Stop.\nCoaches Are Non-Wheelchair Compliant. There Are Steps To Board / Alight From The Coach.\n\nMeals\xa0\n\nMeals Are Pre–Set & A–La Carte Is Not Possible.\nOn Certain Days Packed Lunch/Breakfast Will Be Provided.\nWater Bottles Will Be Provided By Your Guide And Tour Manager As Per Itinerary.\nCertain Meals Are By Walking During Your Tour.\nWater Is Not Included During Any Meals.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn Certain Departures, We May Sometimes Amend / Reverse The Itinerary. However, All The Services / Inclusions Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nPanoramic / Orientation Tours Are Scenic Drives Conducted Primarily From The Coach. Only Specific, Pre-Determined Locations Are Visited On Foot Or Include A Photo Stop.\nGuests Should Note That The Itinerary Requires Early Morning Wake Up Calls, Early Morning Flights, Significant Walking Distances At Various Locations, Including Attractions, Temples And Airports. This Is An Inherent Part Of The Tour Experience. We Recommend You Bring A Reliable, Comfortable Pair Of Sports Shoes. Your Tour Manager And Driver Will Attempt To Minimize Walking By Getting You As Close To The Entry Points As Regulations Allow, But Ultimate Responsibility For Navigating The Walking Portions Rests With The Guest.\nEvery Site / Monuments Has Its Own Set Of Rules & Regulations. We Need To Respect This & Ensure That We Follow The Same.\nAll Our Visits Are Booked In Advance To Avoid Delays, At The Same Time There May Be Delays Caused Due To Overcrowding, Local Regulations, Security Checks Etc.\nMost Of The Tours In Jordan And Egypt Will Commence Early And Are Generally Scheduled To Conclude In The Early Evening. These Schedules Are Based On Weather Conditions, Local Tourism Operating Norms And Coach Hours. Furthermore, Guests Are Advised That Local Establishments, Including Restaurants And Retail Stores, Often Operate With Shorter Evening Hours Than In Other Countries.\xa0\n\nGeneral\xa0\n\nFor Nri Customers Visa Fees, International Flights And Insurance Are Not Included.\nFor Jd – Joining Direct Customers International Flights Are Not Included.\nIf You Are A Jd Or Nri Passenger While Your Internal Flights Are Included, Make Sure Your Internal Flights Match The Tour Group's Schedule If You Want Seamless Transfers And Guarantee You Don't Miss Any Sightseeing. No Transfers Can Be Arranged For Different Flight Timings And No Refunds For Any Missed Sightseeing.\nNote That Amman To Cairo Are Not Considered As Internal Flight As It’s An International Flight And Not Included For Any Jr Or Nri Client.\nOn Some Occasions You May Have To Join Another Group In Case The Group Does Not Have Adequate Members.\xa0\nA Local Representative Or A Driver May Only Be There To Assist You During Your Initial Part Of The Tour.\xa0\nArrival And Departure Flights Should Be Booked According To The Group Flight Timings. In Case There Is Any Sightseeing Involved On The First Or Last Day Of The Itinerary, To Avoid Missing Any Of The Services. Please Check With Your Sales Officer About The Group Flight Timings.\nSecurity Alerts And Random Closures Might Affect The Itinerary.\xa0\nPlease Take Extra Care Of Your Personal Belongings While On The Tour, Every Country You Travel To Is Prone To Thefts And Bag Snatching. Sotc Will Not Be Liable For Any Loss Of Belongings / Baggage.\xa0\nDisabled Clients Should Carry Their Own Wheelchair And Should Be Accompanied By A Qualified Companion Who Is Able To Provide Assistance To The Disabled Client.\xa0\nSotc Shall Not Accept Any Liability Or Responsibility For Any Damages, Loss, Baggage Loss, Theft, Injury, Accident, Death, Breakdown Or Irregularity, Which May Occur In Carrying Out The Tour Arrangement, Weather Conditions, Strikes, War, Quarantine And Any Other Cause Whatsoever And All Such Loss Or Expense Must Be Borne By The Passengers. Insurance Policies Must Be Carried While On Tour.\xa0\nNormal Insurance Charges For The Duration Of The Tour Are Included In The Tour Price. However, Any Passenger Above The Age Of 60 Years And Those Who Wish To Extend Their Stay Will Be Required To Pay Additional Charges.\xa0\nThe Management Reserves The Right To Claim Any Additional Expenses Incurred Due To Delays Or Changes In Schedules Of Train, Airplane, Bus, Ship Or Other Services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager And The Company Reserves The Right To Amend The Itinerary, Alter, Vary Or Withdraw Any Particular Departure, Excursion Advertised. For The Convenience Of Our Passengers, We Will Sometimes Amend The Itinerary. However, All The Services Will Remain The Same.\xa0\nThere Are No Refunds For Any Services I.E., Meals, Sightseeing Etc. Not Utilized On Your Tour. Any Tours Or Activities Curtailed Or Cancelled Due To Weather Or Traffic Conditions Which Are Beyond The Control Of Sotc Cannot Be Refunded.\nAll Optional Activities Will Have To Be Booked And Paid To The Tour Manager On Day 01 Of The Tour. Payments To Be Made By Cash In Local Currencies Only. (Credit Or Debit Cards Not Accepted).\nOptional Tours Are Booked & Paid On 100% Non-Refundable & Non-Cancellation Policy.\xa0\nAny Optional Tours Not Listed By Sotc On Their Website, Sim Cards Purchased From Local Guides Are Not A Responsibility Of Sotc As These Will Be Considered A 3rd Party Transaction.\nGst And Tcs Will Be Applicable For All Optional Activities Pre-Paid In India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn Case You Decide To Change The Date Of Your Return Reservation Once Confirmed The Exact Amount Payable To The Airline Will Be Advised Once The Same Is Confirmed.\xa0\nThe Images Used In This Brochure Are For Representation Purposes Only.\xa0\nTours Operated Are Subject To Rbi / Goi Regulations. Part Of The Tour Cost Will Be Paid In Usd Out Of Your Btq At Prevailing Rate Of Exchange.\xa0\nPlease Refer To The Booking Form For Detailed “Terms And Conditions”.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nWeather in Turkey, Jordan and Egypt General Overview\nIstanbul Weather (October – March 2026/27)\n\nIstanbul experiences pleasant autumns and cool winters, offering comfortable weather for exploring historic landmarks, museums, bazaars, and Bosphorus cruises.\n\nAmman Weather (October – March 2026/27)\n\nAmman experiences mild autumns and cool winters, with comfortable daytime temperatures that make it an excellent base for sightseeing, cultural experiences, and excursions to Petra, Jerash, the Dead Sea, and Wadi Rum.\n\nCairo Weather (October – March 2026/27)\n\nCairo enjoys warm autumns and mild winters with abundant sunshine, offering ideal conditions for sightseeing, exploring ancient monuments, and experiencing the city's cultural attractions.\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nMonth\n\n\nAvg. High Temp\n\n\nConditions\n\n\n\n\nOctober\n\n\n29°C (84°F)\n\n\nWarm and sunny across Turkey, Jordan, and Egypt; ideal for sightseeing and outdoor activities.\n\n\n\n\nNovember\n\n\n24°C (75°F)\n\n\nMild with pleasant daytime temperatures; excellent for cultural tours and historical sites.\n\n\n\n\nDecember\n\n\n19°C (66°F)\n\n\nCool to mild with comfortable weather for exploring cities, monuments, and archaeological sites.\n\n\n\n\nJanuary\n\n\n17°C (63°F)\n\n\nCoolest month with generally pleasant daytime temperatures and occasional rainfall.\n\n\n\n\nFebruary\n\n\n18°C (64°F)\n\n\nMild with increasing sunshine; comfortable for sightseeing throughout the region.\n\n\n\n\nMarch\n\n\n23°C (73°F)\n\n\nWarm and dry as spring begins; ideal for exploring historic landmarks and natural attractions.\n\n\n\n\nNote: These are representative daytime temperatures for the principal touring regions of Istanbul (Turkey), Amman (Jordan), and Cairo (Egypt). Coastal destinations such as the Red Sea, Dead Sea, and Mediterranean coast are generally warmer during this period.\nAll weather information is approximate only. Please check weather information before your travel.\n\xa0", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/0886_IstanbulSRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/00886_Istanbul753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/01378_Topkapi_Palace_istanbul_Turkey_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/49725_Dolmabahce_Palace_Istanbul753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/AdobeStock_135600005_Amman.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/WadiRum.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/DeadSea_87120142.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/DeadSea1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/2677_Cairo753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/Cairo1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/99521_Bazaar_Cairo_Egypt_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015207/itinerary/2677_Cairo753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014957', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014957', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Iceland Highlights', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Borgarnes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Borgarnes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Reykjavik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014957_0_20260917163732.pdf', 'price': 631641, 'packageSummary': "The 'Iceland Highlights' package is a 7-day tour covering the stunning destinations of Reykjavik, Vik, and Borgarnes. The itinerary includes visits to iconic natural wonders such as the famous Golden Circle, the dramatic black sand beaches of Reynisfjara, and the majestic Seljalandsfoss and Skogafoss waterfalls. Participants will enjoy guided sightseeing tours of the vibrant capital, relaxing dips in geothermal hot springs, and scenic explorations of the volcanic landscapes and historic valleys of Borgarnes.", 'images': ['Reykjavik1.jpg', 'VIK_NEW.jpg', 'VIK.jpg', 'borgarnes11.jpg', 'Reykjavik-1.jpg', 'Blulagoon.jpg', 'Gullfoss.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 631641, 'thumbnailImage': 'Lights.bmp', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014957 is named 'Iceland Highlights' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Reykjavik, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Reykjavik Transfers: Upon arrival in Keflavik Airport, you will meet the representative and get transferred to the hotel on private basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Vik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Reykjavik – Vik Transfers: Today you will travel from Reykjavik to Vik on private basis. South Coast tour: Stops include Seljalandsfoss and Skogafoss waterfalls - Seljalandsfoss fed by Eyjafjallajokull, Skogafoss marking the start of the Fimmvorauhals trek. You also see Reynisfjara’s reshaped coast and the blue ice of Solheimajokull glacier. Special Note: 1. Reykjavik downtown has restrictions for bigger vehicles. For pick ups and drop offs, the nearest authorised stops near the hotel will be used if the hotel is located in the downtown area. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on Private basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Vik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vik - Icebergs & Glaciers Towards Icebergs & glaciers: Drive across Myrdalssandur floodplains and Eldhraun lavafield to Kirkjubaejarklaustur. Visit Skaftafell National Park, shaped by ice and fire, then explore Jokulsarlon Glacier Lagoon and Diamond Beach. Enjoy an amphibian boat ride among floating icebergs. (Amphibian boat ride is valid only till 01 November’26) OR Ice Cave Tour from Jokulsarlon Glacier Lagoon - Explore a stunning natural ice cave hidden within Vatnajökull glacier, famous for its shimmering blue ice formations. Departing from Jokulsarlon, this guided adventure takes you deep into Iceland’s frozen heart for a truly unforgettable experience. (Optional Tour @ Supplement of € 130/- Per Person) {Operational all year around} Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on Private basis, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Borgarnes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vik - Borgarnes Transfers: Today you will travel from Vik to Borgarnes on Private basis. Golden circle tour: Visit three iconic sights: Pingvellir National Park, the Geysir geothermal area - home to the highly active Strokkur - and Gullfoss waterfall, where massive volumes of water plunge into a dramatic, winding gorge. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on Private basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Borgarnes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Borgarnes West Iceland tour: Explore Snaefellsnes peninsula, a mini Iceland with black beaches, Mountains, volcanic craters, cliffs, birdlife, caves, and glaciers. Visit Arnarstapi, see Kirkjufell, Djupalonssandur bay, and the iconic Saefellsjokull glacier. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on Private basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Borgarnes - Reykjavik Transfers: Today you will travel from Borgarnes along the shores of Hvalfjooour Fjord towards Reykjavik. Blue lagoon: Enjoy a classic Icelandic spa experience at the Blue Lagoon or Sky Lagoon. Soak in mineral rich geothermal waters amid dramatic scenery, from Reykjanes lava fields to an ocean edge infinity pool near Reykjavik. [Please note that this activity operates as a shared experience alongside other participants] Special Note: Entrance to Blue Lagoon or Sky Lagoon will be on shared basis inclusive of other guests., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Reykjavik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: From Reykjavik hotel to the Keflavik Airport in private transfer. Special Note: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 631641.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\nHotel Details :\n\xa0\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nReykjavik\xa0(2N)\nGrand Hotel Reykjavík or Similar\n\n\nBorgarnes\xa0(2N)\n\xa0Hotel Vesturland or Similar\n\n\nSelfoss\xa0(1N)\nHotel\xa0Selfoss\xa0or similar\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0, \n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard Category\n\n\n\n\nReykjavik\n\n\nHotel Klettur or similar\n\n\n\n\nVik\n\n\nHotel Eyjafjallajokull or similar\n\n\n\n\nBorgarnes\n\n\nHótel Borgarnes or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n, \nBreakfast daily and up to half of your evening meals\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ Split accommodation in Reykjavik based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Night accommodation in Vik area based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Night accommodation in Borgarnes based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Private airport transfer upon arrival at KEF Airport Private airport transfer upon departure from KEF Airport Sightseeing: (Sightseeing on private basis as per slab booked) South Coast tour on shared basis Towards Icebergs & glaciers tour on shared basis Golden circle tour on shared basis (SIC - Tour) West Iceland tour on shared basis (SIC - Tour) Entrance to Sky lagoon *(Comfort Entrance Tickets) Jokulsarlon glacial amphibian boat tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees - To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.Blackout Period: 15th December 2026 - 10th January 2027 Optioanl Activities Tour Name Per Person Price In Euro Easy Glacier Hike 110 Lava Tunnel Tour 75 Ice Cave Tour 130. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Costing given is subject to change and availability. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltIt