ykjavik, and traversing the serene eastern fjords around Egilsstadir and Hofn. Participants will enjoy guided sightseeing of Iceland's iconic waterfalls, volcanic landscapes, and coastal wonders, making for an unforgettable journey through the country's diverse natural beauty.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Reykjavik\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon arrival in Keflavik Airport, you will meet the representative and get transferred to the hotel on private basis.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Berjaya Natura\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nMagnificent Snæfellsness\nTransfers: There will be a pick-up from the scheduled meeting point near the hotel starts between 07:30-08:00 a.m.\n\xa0\nMagnificent Snæfellsness: Enjoy the scenic guided drive to the Snæfellsness Peninsula (the most popular area because it was a part of the famous web series locations, often referred to as mini-Iceland). Visit Arnarstapi, Kirkjufell Mountain and waterfall (most photographed location), Black Sand Beach, Fishing Villages.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nReykjavik downtown has restrictions for bigger vehicles. For pick-ups and drop-offs, the nearest authorised stops near the hotel will be used if the hotel is located in the downtown area.\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Berjaya Natura\xa0or similar\xa0in\xa0Reykjavik'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nScenic Journey To North Iceland\nTransfers: Pick-up from the scheduled meeting point near the hotel starts at 08:45 a.m.\n\xa0\nScenic Journey to North Iceland: Start your scenic drive towards North Iceland. Visit Hvalfjörður tunnel, Skagafjörður, Glaumbær - a preserved turf farm offering a quiet look into Icelandic rural life from centuries past. After the visit, the drive continues over the Öxnadalsheiði plateau and into Akureyri.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nReykjavik downtown has restrictions for bigger vehicles. For pick-ups and drop-offs, the nearest authorized stops near the hotel will be used if the hotel is located in the downtown area.\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Berjaya or similar in\xa0Akureyri'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nLake Myvatn Area\nMyvatn Area: En route to Lake Mývatn, stop at Goðafoss. Explore volcanic and geothermal sights, including Námaskarð’s bubbling mud pits. Visit Dettifoss, then cross the Mödrudalsöræfi highlands to finish the day in Egilsstaðir.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\n\xa0\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Berjaya Hérað or similar in Egilsstaðir'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nEast Fjords\nEast Fjords: The road trip continues from Egilsstaðir to the fairly isolated and very beautiful East Fjords. Scenic drive via the rugged mountains overlooking the dramatic coastline of the mighty North Atlantic.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Berjaya or similar in\xa0Hofn'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGlacier Lagoon & South Coast\nGlacier Lagoon & South Coast: Visit Jökulsárlón Glacier Lagoon to see drifting icebergs and Diamond Beach, with an included amphibious boat ride. Continue to Skaftafell in Vatnajökull National Park, then visit Vík’s black sand Reynisfjara, plus Skógafoss and Seljalandsfoss.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\nSightseeing will be on shared basis and will be operated as a part of Multi-City Small Group', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Selfoss or similar in South Coast'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nGolden Circle & Blue Lagoon\nGolden Circle, Blue Lagoon: En