ices quoted. Certain Activities are subject to weather conditions and protocols.\n\nImportant Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 20 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: Fixed Dates only\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nTCS & GST would be levied as applicable\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs , conventions , and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/SRP_Kirkjufell-mountain.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/reykjavik_Iceland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/Snaefellsness.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/329451_Akureyri_city_Iceland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/LakeMyvatn.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/EastFjords.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/Jokulsarlon.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/BlueLagoon.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014722/itinerary/Reyjavik_753.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015184', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015184', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Scandinavia Citybreaks', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Helsinki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Stockholm', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Oslo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 279779, 'packageSummary': "The 'Scandinavia Citybreaks' package is an 8-day tour covering the vibrant northern capitals of Helsinki, Stockholm, and Oslo. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic overnight ferry cruises across the Baltic Sea, and visits to iconic landmarks such as Stockholm's historic Gamla Stan and Oslo's famous Vigeland Sculpture Park. The itinerary offers a perfect blend of cultural exploration, modern Nordic design, and breathtaking coastal landscapes, making it an unforgettable Scandinavian adventure.", 'images': ['Helsinki2.jpg', 'Helsinki1.jpg', 'Helsinki3.jpg', 'Stockholm2.jpg', 'Stockholm1.jpg', 'Oslo1.jpg', 'Oslo2jpg.jpg', 'Stockholm4.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 279779, 'thumbnailImage': 'Norway1.avif', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015184 is named 'Scandinavia Citybreaks' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Helsinki, Meals: NA, Description: Arrive Helsinki Transfers: Upon your arrival at Helsinki Airport you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour: Join a small group walking tour of Helsinki covering key landmarks Helsingin Tuomiokirkko Market Square Temppeliaukio Church Uspenski Cathedral and Sibelius Park plus historic quarters between Market and Senate Squares with cafes and restaurants., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Helsinki, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Helsinki to Stockholm by Cruise Transfers: You will be transferred from Helsinki hotel to the port on private basis for the overnight cruise. Helsinki to Stockholm Overnight Cruise: In the evening take overnight cruise to Stockholm and enjoy live entertainment duty free shopping sightseeing. Special Notes: In Helsinki it will be day free at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Visit Skansen Transfers: Upon reaching Stockholm you will be transferred from Stockholm port to the hotel on private basis. Early check in is subject to hotel discretion. Visit Skansen: Skansen on Royal Djurgarden offers stunning views of Stockholm. Known as Sweden in miniature it is the worlds oldest open air museum with music dance traditions historic buildings and Nordic animals all in one place. Special Note: You will check in at the hotel post completing the sightseeing., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Stockholm, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm Walking City Tour Stockholm Small Group Walking Tour: Small group walking tour of Stockholm covering City Hall Sergel Square and Gamla Stan one of Europes best preserved medieval centers. Visit the Nobel Museum Royal Palace with changing of the guards and the Vasa Museum., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Stockholm to Oslo by Train Transfers: You will be transferred from the Stockholm hotel to the train station. Upon arrival at the Oslo train station you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15.00 hrs or at the discretion of the hotel management., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour: Visit Oslos Royal Palace Vigeland Sculpture Park and Opera House. Explore the Kon Tiki FRAM and Maritime museums Akershus Fortress and its history museums then stroll Karl Johans Gate filled with shops cafes bars and nightlife., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Oslo, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will be transferred from Oslo hotel to the airport on private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport three to four hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 279779.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\n\n\nHOTELS ENVISAGED OR SIMILAR\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCITIES\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVALUE CATEGORY\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHELSINKI\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScandic\xa0Hotel\xa0or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSTOCKHOLM\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClarion hotel or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOSLO\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClarion hotel\xa0or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\n. Meals include: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1). Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Helsinki based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation on Cruise from Helsinki to Stockholm 2 Nights’ accommodation in Stockholm based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Oslo based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point-to-Point Basis] Arrival Transfers from Helsinki Airport to the Hotel Private Transfer from Helsinki hotel to the Port Private Transfer from Stockholm Port to the hotel Private Transfer from Stockholm hotel to the train station Private Transfer from Oslo Train station to the hotel Departure Transfer from Oslo hotel to the Airport Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis & from a designated point) Helsinki Small Group Walking Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Entry tickets – Vasa Museum, Skansen Stockholm Small Group Walking City Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Oslo Small Group Walking City Tour (On Shared basis/SIC) Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of EUR 10 per person per day is not included City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES • The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together • The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events • Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room • Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. • WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed • (Supplement charges may apply for such services) • Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. • Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned • At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability • TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost TERMS AND CONDITIONS • Travel Validity: 1 July 2026 – 15 December 2026 • Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ • The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times • Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room • The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses • Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking • To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour • Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly • The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing