Includes Privates service s on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from London Airport to London Hotel\nDeparture Airport Transfer from Rome Hotel to Rome Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Tickets: [Cost is subject to vary until Ticketed]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket London – Paris (Eurostar): – Subject to availability until ticketed\n2nd Class Train Ticket Paris – Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver\nLucerne – Zurich Airport: – Subject to availability until ticketed.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nLondon Hop On Hop Off Bus tour.\nLondon Eye (Entrance Only).\nMadame Tussauds (Entrance Only).\nTower of London (Entrance Only)\nInteractive City Tour, Seine Cruise and Eiffel Tower 2nd Floor with Priority Access (SIC)\nMt Titlis Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nJungfraujoch Excursion (in conjunction with Swiss Pass)\nVenice: Venice Gondola Ride (30 Mins) and Serenade.\nVenice: Murano, Burano and Torcello Half-Day Sightseeing Tour\nFlorence: Pisa and the Leaning Tower Tour from Florence\xa0\nRome: Hop on Hop off in Rome\n\n\xa0\nIntercity travel by Train (Second Class):\n\nLondon – Paris (Eurostar).\nParis – Geneva / Basel (TGV).\nSwiss Pass 4 Days Consecutive Saver.\nLucerne – Venice.\nVenice – Florence.\nFlorence – Rome.\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\n\n\xa0\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/Rome_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/London7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/LondonTowerBridge7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Paris75390.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/EiffelTowerParisFrance7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Interlaken2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/89366_Mt._Titlis_Engelberg_Switzerland_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Jungfraujoch75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Glacier.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/VeniceRialtoBridgeItaly75312.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/71702_Venice_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Florence_1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/rome.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Rome-Colosseum.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014527/itinerary/Rome789.jpg']}, 'score': 1.395028, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015156', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015156', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan With Georgia - Winter', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Baku', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Sheki', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Tbilisi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 190944, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan With Georgia - Winter' package is a 9-day tour covering Baku, Tbilisi, and Sheki. The itinerary includes visits to the historic Old City of Baku, the iconic Flame Towers, the ancient petroglyphs of Gobustan, and the majestic Sheki Khan's Palace. Participants will enjoy guided city tours of Tbilisi, scenic cable car rides to Narikala Fortress, relaxing sulfur bath experiences, and opportunities to witness the stunning winter landscapes of the Caucasus mountains while savoring traditional Azerbaijani and Georgian cuisine.", 'images': ['Baku_753.jpg', '753_NizamiStreet.jpg', 'baku-Ateshgah.jpg', 'Nohur-Lake.jpg', 'Tbilisi_753.jpg', 'Mtshekhta_753.jpg', 'Ananuri-Castle.jpg', 'Kakheti_Church_Georgia_753.jpg', 'Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 190944, 'thumbnailImage': 'Tiblisi267Georgia.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015156 is named 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan With Georgia - Winter' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Baku, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome Azerbaijan - Arrival - Check in Welcome to Baku, Azerbaijan. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500 hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. NOTE All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Baku, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Baku - Walking tour of Old Town – Visit Hyder Aliyev Center - Free time at Nizami Street This morning after buffet breakfast, visit the Heydar Aliyev Center, a building complex in Baku, Azerbaijan designed by Iraqi-British architect Zaha Hadid. Later visit to Highland Park and Alley of Martyrs followed by photo-stop at the National Assembly and the Flame towers - the tallest skyscraper in Baku. Post lunch, we proceed on walking tour of Old City - the historical core of Baku. Photo stop at the Shirvanshahs Palace and Maiden Tower. Later enjoy some free time at Nizami Street., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Baku, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Ateshgah ( Fire Temple) - Visit Yanar Dag ( Fire Mountain) - Free time at Deniz Mall This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed towards Ateshgah (Fire Temple) - a temple used as a Hindu and Zoroastrian place of worship. The pentagonal complex, which has a courtyard surrounded by cells for monks and a tetra pillar-altar in the middle, was built during the 17th and 18th centuries. Later proceed to Yanar Dag (Fire Mountain)- a natural gas fire which blazes continuously on a hillside on the Absheron Peninsula. Free time at Deniz Mall., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Sheki, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion to Gabala - Visit Tufandag Ski Resort - Photo stop at Lake Nohur This morning after buffet breakfast, checkout and depart towards Gabala, the north-west of Azerbaijan. On arrival proceed on a Cable Car ride to Tufandaq Winter-Summer Tourism Complex located at 1920 meters above sea level. Enjoy free time at the top. Later we stop at Nohur Lake - one of the most beautiful lakes surrounded by mountains. Drive to Sheki and Check-in to hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive to Tbilisi, Georgia - Arrival - Check in After buffet breakfast check out and drive to Tbilisi, Georgia. Proceed to the hotel. Check into your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. Note: There will be Border Crossing today with a walk involving approx. 800 meters with your luggage followed by immigration formalities Minimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Tbilisi - Visit Chronicles of Georgia - Visit Mtskheta This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed for an orientation tour. On arrival proceed for an orientation tour. Visit Metekhi Cathedral.Take a cable car ride to Narikala Fortress. Walk across the Bridge of Peace & continue to explore underground sulphur baths the district of naturally hot mineral waters. Walk pass the cafe street - Shardeni, Synagogue, Sioni Cathedral and the most ancient Anchiskhati Basilica.Visit Chroniclesof Georgia. Drive to Mtskheta - Visit the Jvari Monastery and Svetitskoveli Cathedral Walk along the narrow streets of Mtskheta for some souvenir shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion - Visit Ananuri Fortress – Visit Zhinvali Reservoir – Gudauri Ski Resort – Visit Georgia - Russia Friendship Monument - Visit Kazbegi & Gregeti Trinity Church This morning after buffet breakfast, we will drive on the Georgian Military Highway, to the border with Russia. Throughout the route you will be surrounded by dramatic mountain scenery. Visit Ananuri Fortress. Stop at the Zhinvali Water Reservoir and see an amazing view of the Gudauri Ski Resort. Later we visit Stepantsminda known as Kazbegi, small town in the north-east Georgia. Visit the Gergeti Trinity Church located 2200 meters above sea level. Return to Tbilisi. Note: The route to Kazbegi passes through high altitude mountain passes; driving pass the route is subject to weather conditions that are affected by heavy snowfall. In case of heavy snow fall the tour routing will be altered, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion - Visit Kahheti Wine Region - Visit Old Town of Sighnaghi - Visit Bodbe Monastery This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Kakheti Wine Region, renowned as the cradle of winemaking. Begin your day with a wine tasting at a local Kakheti Winery, where you can savour some of Georgia's finest wines. Later, visit the picturesque hilltop town of Sighnaghi, located in the heart of Georgia's wine-growing region. Admire its charming pastel-coloured houses, narrow cobblestone streets, and breathtaking views of the Alazani Valley and the majestic Caucasus Mountains. Continue to the Bodbe Female Monastery, the final resting place of Saint Nino, the enlightener of Georgia. After the visit, return to Tbilisi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. Note : The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 190944.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n04 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott or similar in Tbilisi\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Local / Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian Lunches\n05 Indian Jain/ Vegetarian/ Non-Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n01 Packed Dinner\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B – Breakfast/ L- Lunch/ LC- Lunch coupon/PL – Packed Lunch/ D – Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodations at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same has to be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Thomas Cook Tour Manager/ local representative. (subjected to minimum 25 customers) Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st July 2026. Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary VISA REQUIREMENTS: Visa on Arrival It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Visa On arrival Exemptions applicable in case of Valid Visa Holders to specified countries.. Exclusions: Airfare not included for Joining Direct passenger Compulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 3/guest/day Minimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia. The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Visa charges for NRI passengers. Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July, 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Thomas Cook will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. Meals other than what is mentioned in itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passenger other than those included in your itinerary.. Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Udaipur', 'cityCode': 'UDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'cityCode': 'SXR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAG650', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Azerbaijan With Georgia - Winter' package is a 9-day tour covering Baku, Tbilisi, and Sheki. The itinerary includes visits to the historic Old City of Baku, the iconic Flame Towers, the ancient petroglyphs of Gobustan, and the majestic Sheki Khan's Palace. Participants will enjoy guided city tours of Tbilisi, scenic cable car rides to Narikala Fortress, relaxing sulfur bath experiences, and opportunities to witness the stunning winter landscapes of the Caucasus mountains while savoring traditional Azerbaijani and Georgian cuisine.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome Azerbaijan - Arrival - Check in\nWelcome to Baku, Azerbaijan. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500 hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nNOTE\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Baku - Walking tour of Old Town – Visit Hyder Aliyev Center - Free time at Nizami Street \nThis morning after buffet breakfast, visit the Heydar Aliyev Center, a building complex in Baku, Azerbaijan designed by Iraqi-British architect Zaha Hadid. Later visit to Highland Park and Alley of Martyrs followed by photo-stop at the National Assembly and the Flame towers - the tallest skyscraper in Baku. Post lunch, we proceed on walking tour of Old City - the historical core of Baku. Photo stop at the Shirvanshahs Palace \xa0and Maiden Tower. Later enjoy some free time at Nizami Street.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Ateshgah ( Fire Temple) - Visit Yanar Dag ( Fire Mountain) - Free time at Deniz Mall\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed towards Ateshgah (Fire\xa0 Temple) - a temple used as a Hindu and Zoroastrian place of worship. The pentagonal complex, which has a courtyard surrounded by cells for monks and a tetra pillar-altar in the middle, was built during the 17th and 18th centuries. Later proceed to Yanar Dag (Fire Mountain)- a natural gas fire which blazes continuously on a hillside on the Absheron Peninsula. Free time at Deniz Mall.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Wyndham\xa0or similar in Baku'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay Excursion to Gabala - Visit Tufandag Ski Resort -\xa0 Photo stop at Lake Nohur\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, checkout and\xa0 depart towards Gabala, the north-west of Azerbaijan. On arrival proceed on a Cable Car ride to Tufandaq Winter-Summer Tourism Complex located at 1920 meters above sea level. Enjoy free time at the top. Later we stop at\xa0 Nohur Lake - one of the most beautiful lakes surrounded by mountains. Drive to Sheki and Check-in to hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive to Tbilisi, Georgia - Arrival - Check in\n\xa0\nAfter buffet breakfast check out and drive to Tbilisi, Georgia. Proceed to the hotel. Check into your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nNote:\n\nThere will be Border Crossing today with a walk involving approx. 800 meters with your luggage followed by immigration formalities\nMinimum USD 500 per person in cash on hand is required for the tour for border crossing into Georgia.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Tbilisi\n\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Tbilisi - Visit Chronicles of Georgia -\xa0 Visit\xa0 Mtskheta\n\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed for an orientation tour. On arrival proceed for an orientation tour. Visit Metekhi Cathedral.Take a cable car ride to Narikala Fortress. Walk across the Bridge of Peace & continue to explore underground sulphur baths the district of naturally hot mineral waters. Walk pass the cafe street - \xa0Shardeni, Synagogue, Sioni Cathedral and the most ancient Anchiskhati Basilica.Visit Chroniclesof Georgia. Drive to Mtskheta - Visit the Jvari Monastery and Svetitskoveli Cathedral Walk along the narrow streets of Mtskheta for some souvenir shopping.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion -\xa0 Visit Ananuri\xa0 Fortress – Visit Zhinvali Reservoir –\xa0 Gudauri Ski Resort\xa0 – Visit Georgia - Russia Friendship Monument - Visit Kazbegi & Gregeti Trinity Church\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, we will drive on the Georgian Military Highway, to the border with Russia. Throughout the route you will be surrounded by dramatic mountain scenery. Visit Ananuri Fortress. Stop at the\xa0 Zhinvali Water Reservoir and see an amazing view of the Gudauri Ski Resort. Later we visit Stepantsminda known as Kazbegi, small town in the north-east Georgia. Visit the\xa0 Gergeti Trinity Church located 2200 meters above sea level. Return to Tbilisi.\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0The route to Kazbegi passes through high altitude mountain passes; driving pass the route is subject to weather conditions that are affected by heavy snowfall. In case of heavy snow fall the tour routing will be altered', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion - Visit Kahheti Wine Region - Visit Old Town of\xa0 Sighnaghi - Visit Bodbe Monastery\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Kakheti Wine Region, renowned as the cradle of winemaking. Begin your day with a wine tasting at a local Kakheti Winery, where you can savour some of Georgia's finest wines. Later, visit the picturesque hilltop town of Sighnaghi, located in the heart of Georgia's wine-growing region. Admire its charming pastel-coloured houses, narrow cobblestone streets, and breathtaking views of the Alazani Valley and the majestic Caucasus Mountains. Continue to the Bodbe Female Monastery, the final resting place of Saint Nino, the enlightener of Georgia. After the visit, return to Tbilisi.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Courtyard by Marriott or similar in Tbilisi'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd of\xa0 Tour - Fly Back\n\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\nNote :\n\nThe itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n04 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott or similar in Tbilisi\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n03 night’s accommodation at Hotel Wyndham Baku or similar in Baku\n01 night’s accommodation at Hotel Sheki Palace or similar in Sheki\n04 night’s accommodation at Hotel Courtyard By Marriott or simila