lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG013661_0_20260830182045', 'price': 61203, 'packageSummary': "The 'Simply Georgia' package is a 5-day tour dedicated to exploring the historic and vibrant city of Tbilisi. The itinerary includes visits to the iconic Narikala Fortress, the stunning Holy Trinity Cathedral, the ancient sulfur baths, and the charming, cobblestone streets of Old Tbilisi. Participants will enjoy guided walking tours, scenic cable car rides, traditional Georgian wine tastings, and delicious local culinary experiences throughout their stay.", 'images': ['georgia_753.png', 'narikalafortress.png', 'Sighnaghi.jpg', 'Gudauri_C.jpg', 'Georgia_Tbilis_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 61203, 'thumbnailImage': 'Tibilisi_SRP_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG013661 is named 'Simply Georgia' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Tbilisi, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival Tbilisi Welcome to Georgia! Known as the “Cradle of Wine” and nestled at the crossroads of Europe and Asia, Georgia is a land of breathtaking landscapes, ancient history, and warm hospitality. From the snow-capped Caucasus Mountains to lush valleys and vibrant cities, Georgia offers a unique blend of culture, tradition, and modern charm. Upon arrival at Tbilisi International Airport, you will be greeted and transferred to your hotel. Check-in at the hotel (standard time approx. 14:00 hrs.). The rest of the day is free for you to relax and explore the city at your own pace., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi City Tour Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel. After breakfast, embark on a full-day exploration of Tbilisi, a city that beautifully blends history and modernity. Begin your journey at the iconic Metekhi Church and admire the monument to King Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi. Stroll through Rike Park and cross the striking Bridge of Peace, a contemporary architectural marvel. From here, take a scenic cable car ride up to Narikala Fortress, where you’ll enjoy panoramic views of the city and see the imposing statue of Mother Georgia overlooking the old town. Descend into the historic district of Sulphur Baths, passing by Tbilisi’s only mosque, and wander through the charming streets of Meidan Square, lined with cozy cafés, wine bars, and souvenir shops that echo the city’s rich past. Later, visit Mtatsminda Park, a popular amusement park perched on a hill offering breathtaking views of Tbilisi’s skyline. Conclude the day at the impressive Chronicles of Georgia, a monumental sculpture overlooking the Tbilisi Sea, before returning to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Bodbe – Sighnaghi – Tbilisi Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Today, set out on a scenic journey to the Kakheti region, Georgia’s renowned wine country. Begin with a visit to a traditional Georgian winery in Patardzeuli, where you can experience the rich heritage of winemaking and sample local varieties. Continue to the serene Bodbe Monastery, a spiritual site functioning as a nunnery since 1889 and believed to be the burial place of St. Nino, the saint who brought Christianity to Georgia in the 4th century. Next, explore Sighnaghi, famously known as the “City of Love.” This charming hilltop town, once a key point on the Great Silk Road, is surrounded by impressive defensive walls with 23 towers and offers stunning views of the Alazani Valley and the Caucasus Mountains. Stroll through its picturesque streets, enjoy local cuisine, and soak in the romantic atmosphere. On the way back to Tbilisi, you may choose to stop at Badiauri village, where you can taste freshly baked Georgian bread and even participate in a traditional bread-making activity. Return to Tbilisi for an overnight stay., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Tbilisi - Ananuri – Gudauri – Tbilisi Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Today, embark on a scenic drive along the famous Georgian Military Highway, heading north toward the majestic Caucasus Mountains and the Russian border. The journey begins with a stop at the stunning Jhinvali Water Reservoir, a turquoise lake created during the Soviet era, surrounded by picturesque landscapes. Continue to the historic Ananuri Fortress, a former residence of the Argveti Dukes, featuring 16th–17th century churches and towers overlooking the reservoir. Admire the intricate stone carvings and ornaments symbolizing Georgia’s rich cultural heritage. As you ascend further into the mountains, witness the unique confluence of two rivers that retain their distinct colours even after merging, and taste refreshing mineral springs along the way in Mleta. Arrive in Gudauri, a popular mountain resort known for its breathtaking views and thrilling activities. Here, visit the iconic “People’s Friendship Monument”, a Soviet-era structure perched on a cliff, offering panoramic vistas of deep gorges and snow-capped peaks. Enjoy leisure time to soak in the beauty of the Caucasus before returning to Tbilisi for an overnight stay., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Tbilisi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice Travel Validity: 01 OCT - 15 DEC 2026 CATEGORY HOTELS PACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD SGL DBL TPL CWB (6-11 Yrs) CNB (2-6 Yrs) 4-6 PAX 7-10 PAX Standard Hotel Astoria Tbilisi or Similar 400 288 288 275 115 269 275 Value Novotel Tbilisi Center or Similar 475 350 350 300 140 331 338 Premium Radisson Blu Tbilisi or similar 600 375 375 325 150 356 363 Travel Validity: 01 APR 2026 - 26 SEP 2026 & 06 Jan - 13 Mar 2027 CATEGORY HOTELS PACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD SGL DBL TPL CWB (6-11 Yrs) CNB (2-6 Yrs) 4-6 PAX 7-10 PAX S